dbbd2f18-3dec-4f00-926b-06eb44f681e3	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	955ba081-869d-444d-aebf-4ad4d2a3758d	Weekly project planning	{"body":"Rosemary Lynch has started the weekly planning process and alerted the team that she will be introducing new project schedules using Gantt charts.\\n\\nThis update marks the beginning of the team's weekly coordination efforts. The focus will be on mapping out project tasks and deadlines for the upcoming period.","headline":"Weekly project planning has begun with a focus on project timelines.","action_items":["Rosemary Lynch: Provide the team with the updated project schedule and Gantt charts."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	131
e044b4d5-4dd6-4a1f-9395-be90e5ef1748	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	71c6926d-18db-4f7c-b8d3-dd4a9c997025	Meeting technical troubleshooting	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull reached out to pdelashe to confirm that their microphone was active. The message serves as a status update to ensure the participant is audible during the meeting.","headline":"Communication check performed to confirm audio status for pdelashe.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	132
577b35e3-af93-4cb6-92f3-1c59331dd197	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	e03010ec-09c8-4add-bfb5-3062b1b5f1f0	Apology	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia posted a short message expressing an apology. The thread contains no additional information regarding the reason for the apology or any impact on current project work.","headline":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia sent a brief apology message.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	133
355d0445-edfc-429b-9e77-b192c64ffc87	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	7446d1f6-999b-4bf9-9fe7-7b04315e4704	POC Phase 2 Architecture	{"body":"Philip Jones shared the updated plan for the second phase of the project. The team will set up two interconnected computing environments, using specialized networking software from Isovalent to manage how these systems communicate.\\n\\nTo ensure stability and reliability, the setup will be spread across three different locations. Two of these locations will handle the primary computing tasks, while the third location will act as a tie-breaker to keep the system running smoothly if issues arise.","headline":"Plan established for the second phase of the technical proof-of-concept project.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":["The project will proceed with a two-cluster setup using Isovalent technology.","The infrastructure will be distributed across three physical or logical sites."]}	\N	\N	standard	134
f360b05c-3f51-440f-bb16-3542bc6513ca	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	7880cb6d-a895-442e-8b64-16ba4d2b67a6	VM migration failure triage	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia announced that the second group of server migrations encountered errors, resulting in 18 machines failing to move as expected. \\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia has asked Petros, Janine, and Rydekull to meet immediately to investigate the issue and resolve the migration problems.","headline":"Eighteen virtual servers failed to move during the latest migration update.","action_items":["Petros, Janine, and Rydekull to meet with Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to troubleshoot the migration failures."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	135
949ff4f3-a593-434c-a5db-d2381b26d663	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	b82eb3de-678e-43af-8fbc-b73256cf56f6	OpenShift cluster deployment configuration	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull has asked the team to confirm the current setup process for new OpenShift clusters. He observed that the settings used to grant remote access (SSH keys) to the system administrator account appear to be disabled in the project's configuration files.\\n\\nRydekull is asking the project team to clarify whether this is a deliberate security choice or if the configuration needs to be updated to allow for proper system access.","headline":"Clarification requested on security access settings for new OpenShift clusters.","action_items":["The engineering team needs to confirm if the current method for accessing the cluster is intentional or requires a change."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	136
5cdaf6d1-f621-4393-8ea4-c5e08048a164	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	d4e2e550-18af-4594-a768-f7d917b239bb	VM IP migration challenges	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli reported that changing the network addresses for virtual machines in Hong Kong will be difficult. Based on recent challenges faced in the New York office, the team has realized that simply updating the server addresses causes several other connected systems to stop working.\\n\\nKey services like shared network storage, secure remote access (VPNs), and web traffic handlers are all linked to these specific addresses. Because these systems rely on the current setup, the team must carefully plan how to update them to avoid service disruptions.","headline":"Planned server address changes in Hong Kong are more complex than anticipated.","action_items":["Review all connected systems and services before proceeding with the Hong Kong server address changes."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	137
0651d00c-ea07-43d2-a972-6d06aee39ac8	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	121cff90-110a-46a3-8446-c2c5b84c367b	ACM and Cluster Infrastructure Updates	{"body":"Philip Jones announced that the cluster management software (ACM) has been updated to the latest version, 2.16.0. The team has also cleaned up the automated deployment configurations across all systems to ensure consistency, though some minor adjustments in the OpenShift configuration area are still required. A new cluster, 106, has been added to the lab environment.\\n\\nPhilip Jones has submitted several updates to the system code to fix existing issues and align settings across the board. The team is now preparing to upgrade the Dell storage management software, which is currently waiting on the delivery of required software files.","headline":"Infrastructure updates completed for cluster management and software readiness.","action_items":["Finalize remaining configuration adjustments (Philip Jones)","Complete preparation for Dell storage software upgrade (Philip Jones)"],"key_decisions":["Upgraded cluster management software to version 2.16.0","Added new cluster 106 to the lab environment"]}	\N	\N	standard	138
9aba71c3-8f97-43c4-956f-4eb93442898e	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	d2d278dd-b0e8-4ee4-8a69-10705bc9fb6b	Observability infrastructure configuration	{"body":"Ricardo Gregorio is working on upgrading how we monitor our system's health, specifically by setting up alerts to track the performance and stability of our data collection tools.\\n\\nFurthermore, Ricardo Gregorio is establishing new security measures to scrub sensitive information from our activity logs before they are sent to our storage platform. He is also reviewing our current setup to ensure we are capturing all the necessary data points to keep the system running smoothly.","headline":"Improving system monitoring and ensuring secure data handling for logs.","action_items":["Ricardo Gregorio: Set up automated alerts for system monitoring.","Ricardo Gregorio: Create a process to remove sensitive data from logs before storage.","Ricardo Gregorio: Update the system configuration to include missing performance data."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	139
1506d4a4-a68d-4c56-b909-82e9ae170004	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	01f4cb4a-df16-4fca-a04e-d02b57066e96	Weekly Delivery Reporting	{"body":"Rosalia Suarez Mejias has requested that the team add their project progress updates from the past week into the shared presentation template. This information is necessary to compile the weekly delivery report.\\n\\nAll updates must be completed by the end of the day today. Rosalia Suarez Mejias plans to send out the final report to the team tomorrow morning at 11:00 AM.","headline":"Team requested to provide weekly project updates by end of day.","action_items":["All team members: Add project updates to the shared slide deck by the end of today."],"key_decisions":["The weekly delivery report will be sent out tomorrow at 11:00 AM."]}	\N	\N	standard	140
2225607a-0d7c-4962-be47-e90a5c07e6dc	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ef5296b9-b09f-473b-afde-e990494d4512	Issue tracking and assignment	{"body":"Carina Almeida is asking for an update on who is responsible for the tasks currently assigned to the 'RH' group. This is part of an effort to track project progress and ensure that all work is being handled by the correct team members.\\n\\nThe goal is to clarify current responsibilities so that project management can maintain an accurate view of who is working on which specific items.","headline":"Request for clarification on staff assignments for pending project tasks.","action_items":["Team members to provide updates on their specific responsibilities for the tasks assigned to RH."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	141
58e8afed-b5a5-4e22-8acd-b62c22660cf1	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ffada008-fe4c-47a9-b7b7-49292595dc7b	OAuth proxy backport planning	{"body":"Kevin Rizza shared an update regarding the project to update the OAuth proxy system. The team is currently reviewing the technical requirements and potential issues to ensure a smooth rollout. The current plan is to complete the update for the upcoming 5.0 version first, and then apply those changes to the older 4.22 version.\\n\\nProgress is being tracked in a central project management ticket, OCPSTRAT-3174. Kevin Rizza will post regular weekly updates there so stakeholders can monitor the progress and timeline.","headline":"Plans to update the security login system for older software versions.","action_items":["Kevin Rizza to provide weekly progress updates in the project tracking system."],"key_decisions":["The team will update the security login system for version 4.22 after the 5.0 release is finished."]}	\N	\N	standard	142
c4c4ed72-a0ea-434c-9278-9e58a590abbe	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	87be2cc6-1a02-449e-a6c9-9926ec60f475	Delivery report finalization	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has requested that all team members review the project delivery report one last time. The document is currently available for final comments before it is officially sent out.\\n\\nPlease ensure you check the presentation and add any necessary feedback promptly, as this is the final opportunity to make changes before the report is finalized.","headline":"Final call for feedback on the project delivery report.","action_items":["Team members to provide final feedback on the delivery report presentation."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	143
