72dddd12-c337-4772-90bd-d3413f692512	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	85919912-4e8e-4494-af5a-85e382a7209c	Meeting scheduling and coordination	{"body":"Carina Almeida noted that today's internal team meeting conflicts with important calls involving the TAM team and the NY/MX group. To avoid these scheduling issues, she suggested canceling the live meeting and sharing status updates in the chat instead.\\n\\nCarina Almeida also encouraged the team to reach out if they need any assistance or support today. This change allows the team to stay updated while managing their other professional commitments.","headline":"Internal meeting canceled to resolve scheduling conflicts with external calls.","action_items":["Team members to post their daily updates in the Slack thread.","Team members to contact Carina Almeida if they require help with any tasks."],"key_decisions":["The internal team meeting is canceled for today.","Team members will post their status updates directly in the Slack thread."]}	\N	\N	standard	145
ef8cbd0f-c1d6-4545-bb20-b4afaf616123	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	0c26fc95-9d0e-43ab-977f-e500f9b3d08a	Software version upgrade	{"body":"James Force reported that the necessary background components are now ready, clearing the way for the planned software update. \\n\\nJames Force plans to perform the upgrade tomorrow morning to ensure the system is running on version 26.1.1.","headline":"Software upgrade to version 26.1.1 scheduled for tomorrow morning.","action_items":["James Force to perform the software upgrade tomorrow morning."],"key_decisions":["The team is ready to move forward with the software upgrade to version 26.1.1."]}	\N	\N	standard	146
3b87722e-44bb-45c4-b6c9-a4da31bc97b3	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	f97b02c9-d5f5-485e-8a63-983c815bd937	Production feature governance	{"body":"Jens Feind has raised a concern regarding a request from the customer's team (Nitesh and Srinath) about using experimental or early-access software features in their live production system. This requires a formal agreement between our company and the customer to ensure it meets project standards.\\n\\nJens Feind is asking if this has already been discussed or decided, as the customer is waiting for a formal written confirmation before proceeding.","headline":"Clarification needed on using experimental software features in the customer's live environment.","action_items":["Determine if a decision has been made regarding the use of experimental features.","Draft a written response for the customer confirming the governance policy."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	147
591c8c9a-a203-479d-b88f-cfc187591641	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	d2721090-e300-4f37-b93a-0e735b220fd8	Delivery report update	{"body":"Rosalia Suarez Mejias has requested that the team update the project delivery report. This document needs to be completed and ready to send out by 12:00 PM today.\\n\\nSeveral team members, including Rydekull, rspazzol, Shebi, janine, Philip Jones, James Force, ricardo gregorio, Petros, and pdelashe, have been tagged to contribute their updates to the shared presentation file to ensure the report is accurate and ready on time.","headline":"Team requested to update the project delivery report before noon today.","action_items":["Rydekull, rspazzol, Shebi, janine, Philip Jones, James Force, ricardo gregorio, Petros, and pdelashe must update their sections of the report.","Complete the report by the 12:00 PM deadline."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	148
d556daac-f0c6-4c94-81aa-d572b7240a2f	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	5492806b-52a5-4563-8ab7-71b86cebb907	System Migration Execution	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia announced that the latest phase of the system upgrade, specifically Bundle 3a, has passed all necessary preliminary checks. As a result, the team has started the migration process.\\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia will monitor the progress and provide another update in about an hour to share the current status of the work.","headline":"The system upgrade process has officially begun following successful initial testing.","action_items":["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to report back on progress in one hour."],"key_decisions":["The team has moved forward with the system upgrade."]}	\N	\N	standard	149
92e36c2c-de8d-4bec-a604-0b65747de375	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	2f5b4afc-4f5b-45d5-ba2d-5632e2572e25	Migration project status update	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that the second phase of the migration pilot is moving forward as planned. \\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that a new, higher-priority project is now competing for the attention of the IT support staff. To manage this, she is documenting this potential bottleneck in the project's risk tracker to ensure leadership is aware of the impact on team capacity.","headline":"Migration project is on schedule, but staff availability poses a new risk.","action_items":["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to document the staffing conflict in the project risk tracker."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	150
1956032e-cc82-4935-9290-0ae849fe0ce6	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	8436f3bd-42e4-4363-9578-fbfea6b33909	Infrastructure and Remote Access	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli raised concerns about the current method of securing the system's database, noting that storing security keys on the same drive as the data is not ideal. He is looking into modern, more secure ways to manage these keys using external services to better protect sensitive information.\\n\\nOn the operational side, Raffaele Spazzoli announced that all previous issues preventing remote worker testing have been cleared. Testing is set to restart this coming Monday, and he has requested that James Force dedicate his full attention to this high-priority task.","headline":"Security review of database encryption and restart of remote access testing.","action_items":["Raffaele Spazzoli to research improved security methods for database encryption.","James Force to lead the remote worker testing effort starting Monday."],"key_decisions":["Remote worker testing is scheduled to resume this Monday."]}	\N	\N	standard	151
148e464d-1138-4765-9d74-b3f5055fadd0	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	891d777d-d694-4310-b962-bbdef6f5d025	DMZ network architecture documentation	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli is asking for the original, editable files used to create the network security diagrams (DMZ). Accessing these source files is necessary for the team to review or update the current network setup.\\n\\nCurrently, the request is pending a response from the relevant team member to share the requested documentation.","headline":"Request for original network diagram files.","action_items":["Rydekull to share the original network diagram files with Raffaele Spazzoli."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	152
12af23ac-2768-489f-b109-3d177a9a2139	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	bfc63f06-a87f-477b-973a-d44610b7ec2a	Client communication response	{"body":"Anne Maskell is working on an official reply to Frank regarding his request to speed up the project. She is currently turning notes from previous conversations and meetings into a professional document that can be shared with the client.\\n\\nAnne Maskell has asked the team to add any additional feedback or important points directly into the draft document. She plans to review these updates and send the final response to the client by the end of the day tomorrow.","headline":"Preparing a formal response to the client's request for a faster project timeline.","action_items":["Team members to add feedback and project details to the shared draft document.","Anne Maskell to send the final response to Frank by end of day tomorrow."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	154
ec8b035c-d687-4863-b859-2c81c2d74cad	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	51669db1-ec38-4b16-8322-2865daf1585f	Migration error tracking	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has created a shared document to keep track of all errors occurring during the migration process. This system is designed to ensure that different teams are not accidentally working on the same problems at the same time, which helps prevent confusion and wasted effort.\\n\\nBy using this central list, the team can clearly see who is responsible for each issue and where the fixes need to be applied. This will help keep the project organized and ensure that everyone is working from the same information.","headline":"New shared tracking system launched to coordinate migration error fixes.","action_items":["Team members are requested to add, update, or remove migration errors in the shared spreadsheet as they work."],"key_decisions":["A shared spreadsheet will now serve as the official tool for tracking migration errors."]}	\N	\N	standard	155
1dcd8ef3-56d1-46b7-923b-d32af1c1ba23	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	bda1b95b-0bc8-49fd-90a5-e3c691858ef4	Time Reporting Compliance	{"body":"Rosalia Suarez Mejias has sent a reminder to the team regarding the deadline for submitting time-tracking information. To ensure payroll and project billing are processed correctly, all staff must complete their entries in the required systems today.\\n\\nSpecifically, please ensure your time sheets are updated in the Clarity system and Consulting Cloud by noon. Additionally, Red Hat time cards must be finalized before the end of the business day.","headline":"Reminder to submit all time sheets and hours by end of day.","action_items":["All team members: Submit time sheets in Clarity and Consulting Cloud by 12:00 PM.","All team members: Submit Red Hat time cards by the end of the day."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	156
242cfc7a-2137-4aa2-9c47-28e76eb92fc3	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	c559155b-5faf-4bc3-9b1c-b1b1701e3f1a	AI-assisted software development	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli shared insights on new 'vibe coding' techniques, which involve using AI to help write and refine code. The team is moving toward a 'spec-driven' approach, where clear project requirements are established before AI tools are used to generate the actual software.\\n\\nTo test these new methods, Michael P. will build a specific software tool (an operator), which Vinay will then test to ensure it meets project standards. Raffaele encourages the team to take advantage of current company-provided access to these AI tools to learn these new, more efficient ways of working.","headline":"Team shifting to AI-assisted development practices to improve software creation speed.","action_items":["Michael P. to build the new software tool.","Vinay to test the tool created by Michael P."],"key_decisions":["The team will adopt a new, requirement-focused development process supported by AI tools.","The team will test these new methods by building and evaluating a new software tool."]}	\N	\N	standard	157
eeaaedcb-b02c-4e51-ac45-f70e61ec6560	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	359e3467-1f43-427f-b9cc-6c2b50398856	Customer support case escalation	{"body":"Sam Marland has flagged a new customer support case that appears to be related to a recurring problem with migrating machines that have a large number of disks. Due to the urgency of the situation, Sam is moving this to a dedicated channel to ensure the engineering team prioritizes it.\\n\\nBecause many team members will be traveling for the upcoming Summit, Sam has asked Rydekull to share their notes and findings from previous troubleshooting sessions. This will help the engineering team resolve the problem faster despite the limited availability of staff.","headline":"Urgent support case escalated regarding migration issues for complex systems.","action_items":["Sam Marland to share the case in the migration-blockers-nda-customer channel.","Rydekull to provide background information on the technical issues identified so far."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	158
a3d189a8-7ee2-48a9-b793-dede484d1c2c	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	a7b5f218-c456-4884-aeef-15d6399918f9	Priority & Expectation Alignment and TAM Integration	{"body":"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported on a recent project meeting, noting that the team needs to better align their internal work priorities with the bank's actual business needs. By syncing these expectations, the team aims to ensure they are focusing their efforts on the most impactful tasks.\\n\\nAdditionally, the team is working to better utilize the Technical Account Managers (TAMs). To help them be more effective, the team plans to provide them with more detailed background information on the project. They also decided to hold regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests to ensure nothing important is overlooked.","headline":"Improving Project Alignment and Team Collaboration for the EOSBank Account","action_items":["Carina Almeida: Organize a meeting for next week to brief the TAMs on the project's technical background.","Nikos and Rspazzol: Review the meeting notes and add any missing details."],"key_decisions":["Set up regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests.","Improve the training process for new TAMs to help them understand the project better."]}	\N	\N	standard	159
f4adfcbf-f551-4924-8eec-ccbea0931920	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	406a9fe3-e99e-4ad3-a3be-fa9d85b1b9ad	Alert icon inquiry	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged an unfamiliar alert icon appearing in this channel. He is seeking clarification on why this icon is visible and what it signifies for the team.\\n\\nCurrently, there is no explanation for why this icon is appearing. The team is looking into the cause to determine if it requires any action.","headline":"Inquiry regarding the appearance of an alert icon in the Slack channel.","action_items":["Determine why the alert icon is appearing in the channel (Raffaele Spazzoli)"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	160
36c20b5e-a291-4d41-a063-6f34b21493ea	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	13100af7-8afa-4791-8c26-b2c6bd844e24	Migration event incident	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reported that the migration pilot encountered unexpected software errors on the second day. After attempting to resolve the issues directly, the team determined that the fix was taking too long and decided to revert the system to its previous state to ensure stability.\\n\\nThe team believes the issue stems from the software being outdated and incompatible with the new system. The Windows team will now investigate the root cause to determine why the old software failed to run on the new platform.","headline":"Migration pilot paused to perform a system rollback following application errors.","action_items":["Windows team to investigate the cause of the software incompatibility."],"key_decisions":["Roll back the system to the previous version after the fix-forward attempt failed."]}	\N	\N	standard	161
d7935458-10c1-43ca-85c8-1eff44febbd2	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	c7eeb88b-f40b-4198-95b7-ba62bd4ef814	Helm binary access	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull is looking for a specific software tool called 'Helm' that is needed to manage applications on the company's Linux server. He is currently checking if the tool is already installed and ready for use.\\n\\nAt this time, there has been no confirmation on whether the tool is available or if it needs to be installed by the technical team.","headline":"Request for tool access on the company's secure server.","action_items":["Determine if the Helm tool is available or needs to be set up for Alexander Rydekull."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	162
022d61d7-ff20-455d-a5f3-49e30fb85578	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	fccaa7d9-514e-44ac-adb3-1f40e6ee74a1	System Crash Issue	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged a serious issue where customers are experiencing system crashes (Blue Screen of Death) when using our virtualization software. This problem is affecting multiple clients, and the severity has already caused at least one customer to stop using our product.\\n\\nOur engineering team is currently working to identify the source of the problem to determine if it is a fault in our software or an issue related to Windows updates.","headline":"Urgent investigation underway for system crashes affecting Windows virtual machines.","action_items":["Engineering to investigate the cause of the system crashes and report findings."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	163
f794c4cd-c05d-467a-aff5-889c589a7788	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	cb9ec78e-3d82-41d6-b5eb-5f07b1761fd3	VM Migration Pilot Planning	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has identified the requirements for the second phase of the virtual machine migration pilot. The team is narrowing down a list of 230 machines to those that are independent, not shared across multiple services, and located on specific network segments.\\n\\nThis phase will include both Windows and Linux systems. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that the final list of machines to be moved must be reviewed and confirmed by the IT Service Owners (ITSOs) to ensure accuracy before proceeding.","headline":"Planning the next phase of the virtual machine migration project","action_items":["Collaborate with IT Service Owners to finalize the list of machines for migration (Assigned: Patricia de las Heras Granaglia)"],"key_decisions":["Established specific criteria to filter which virtual machines are eligible for the migration pilot."]}	\N	\N	standard	164
ba9ee264-b481-4969-a1a1-13cb24814875	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	427da0ca-34da-402b-8c44-efae8675400b	Pre-validation documentation review	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has shared a new batch of documents that need to be checked before the project can move forward with its validation process. These documents are available for review via a shared link.\\n\\nShebi is expected to evaluate these materials to ensure everything is in order. This step is a standard part of the quality assurance process to confirm that all requirements are satisfied.","headline":"New validation documents submitted for team review.","action_items":["Shebi to review the documents shared by Raffaele Spazzoli."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	165
68f9e1ac-59d8-439e-ab93-ef348bafa9c8	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	669bfdf1-878d-4597-b61d-bd85595cf0f8	Windows automation support request	{"body":"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga is seeking help with a customer support ticket (04425376) related to automating a Windows build process. The standard support team has clarified that they cannot provide the specific scripts needed to fix the customer's issue.\\n\\nSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga has requested that a team member with Windows expertise take over this task, as he does not have the capacity to investigate or resolve the issue this week.","headline":"Assistance needed for Windows automation support request.","action_items":["Find a team member with Windows expertise to assist with support case 04425376."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	166
32e89452-7f1e-4f72-84ed-ff0d581bad0c	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	cb5d4a19-4439-4725-a8cc-3c3567c65889	Vault secret management	{"body":"Ricardo Gregorio is working on a request to allow one Splunk system to communicate with another. To do this securely, a digital access token needs to be stored in the company's centralized secret management system, known as Vault.\\n\\nRicardo Gregorio has requested assistance with this task, as they do not currently have the necessary permissions or experience to manage secrets within the Vault platform.","headline":"Assistance requested to securely store a Splunk access token in the company's secret manager.","action_items":["Identify a team member with Vault access to help Ricardo Gregorio complete the setup."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	167
