ce89a20d-6864-4c86-be90-e6c9ecc36634	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	10590965-e2d4-4473-ab09-578723a915b0	VIB migration issue	{"body":"Carina Almeida shared an update from the morning build meeting, noting that the planned fix for the VIB migration issue did not work. As a result, 18 virtual machines scheduled for migration on the 13th are currently at risk.\\n\\nTo resolve this, Carina Almeida has asked Sam Marland and Nikos to meet with Roy to discuss the next steps. Janine is the designated contact person for any questions regarding the build process moving forward.","headline":"Technical issues with VIB migration affecting 18 virtual machines.","action_items":["Sam Marland and Nikos to coordinate with Roy to resolve the migration delay.","Team to review the status of the 18 affected virtual machines."],"key_decisions":["The initial plan to fix the migration issue was unsuccessful."]}	\N	\N	standard	169
fc21963c-a494-428b-8f82-8546cae1a73f	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	99a9ce24-c86c-4c69-a907-d6590235b70f	Availability inquiry	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reached out to @atolani to confirm if they are currently working. This is a routine check to see if the team member is available to assist with project tasks.\\n\\nThere has been no response yet, and no further details regarding specific project work were discussed in this thread.","headline":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia is checking if @atolani is available to work today.","action_items":["@atolani to respond to Patricia de las Heras Granaglia regarding their availability."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	170
6798c040-9109-4e0f-a810-690abdf92a77	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	e9d8a216-b620-4860-a59f-1dc59981dbc8	Version update for 104	{"body":"Jens Feind is pushing for an update to system 104 to version 4.21 to help resolve persistent problems with shared storage in Windows clusters. This update is seen as a necessary step to fix current technical bugs and provide a positive path forward for the project.\\n\\nJens Feind is currently waiting for confirmation from the build team to proceed. Because there is significant pressure from leadership to resolve these issues, Jens is preparing a status update for stakeholders to explain the proposed solution and next steps.","headline":"Updating system 104 to version 4.21 to fix shared storage issues.","action_items":["Jens Feind to send a status update email to Vinay and Narender.","Rushikesh to respond to the build team regarding the readiness of the 4.21 update."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	171
d7e55f51-738f-4b3a-bdab-eb1d19fe53d6	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ea651e64-a7cc-4af5-9bef-5db1960969d7	Stretched cluster workload preferences	{"body":"Janine Eichler has asked for an explanation regarding why our system currently prefers specific sites when distributing workloads across our stretched cluster setup. This information is needed to better understand our current infrastructure configuration.\\n\\nAt this time, there has been no response or explanation provided. The team is waiting for further details to understand the reasoning behind these site-specific settings.","headline":"Request for clarification on how workloads are assigned to specific sites in our cluster.","action_items":["Shebi and Rydekull to explain the reasoning behind the current site preference settings."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	172
7cf9c731-79aa-4610-8d59-749c6fbecdb4	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	fa63acf2-9d24-44d3-a797-c8b503724ad9	Windows machine troubleshooting	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli reached out to ask if work has begun on fixing a Windows computer that is currently not working.\\n\\nThis is a follow-up to ensure that the necessary repairs or investigations are underway to resolve the system issue.","headline":"Status check requested for a broken Windows computer.","action_items":["Shebi to report on the progress of the computer repair."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	173
055a938d-1c79-4129-b6b6-3062b3b68654	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	df6f34a1-f98a-475f-9575-07fdfc4d7b9c	Delivery report finalization	{"body":"Rosalia Suarez Mejias has requested that the team review the delivery report and fill in any missing information. This task is urgent, as the report is scheduled to be sent out in 20 minutes.\\n\\nPlease ensure all necessary updates are completed immediately so the final document is accurate and ready for distribution.","headline":"Immediate action required to finalize the delivery report before it is sent.","action_items":["All stakeholders: Fill in missing information in the delivery report within 20 minutes."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	174
ee6ff489-1621-4a2b-ab5f-85641678a2a6	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	484803bb-966a-469b-8238-a4ea77e44c67	RCA process delay	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has informed the team that the investigation into the recent issue is on hold. The initial support ticket was set up incorrectly and needs to be replaced with a new one.\\n\\nOnce the ticket is fixed and sent to the correct technical team, the investigation will begin. This ticket will then be used as the central place to share updates and track progress.","headline":"The Root Cause Analysis process is delayed while a ticket is corrected.","action_items":["Correct and re-submit the support ticket to the proper team."],"key_decisions":["The investigation is paused until the support ticket is fixed."]}	\N	\N	standard	175
26bbd408-889c-437d-8ed9-d2a9fab8d767	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ec7065ca-2fc1-48c0-bdca-362a3a8ee1f9	CAP and OCP release planning	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli confirmed his attendance at the upcoming US/MX meeting to help coordinate project schedules. He is focusing on ensuring that the release plans for CAP and OCP are properly aligned.\\n\\nTo support this, Raffaele Spazzoli has asked the technical account managers (TAMs) to prepare a visual timeline. This document will show exactly when current project issues will be resolved and how that timing fits into the broader release schedule for OCP.","headline":"Planning release schedules for CAP and OCP projects.","action_items":["Technical account managers to create a timeline slide showing when project blockers will be fixed in relation to OCP releases."],"key_decisions":["Raffaele Spazzoli will attend the US/MX meeting to discuss release planning."]}	\N	\N	standard	176
1c2e694c-2983-41bb-ae8b-1cc7e4c6ca1c	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	995d10dd-d1a2-4fd4-a345-ba5252a6b2eb	Internal communication protocols	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has relayed a message from Vinay requesting that @rspazzol stop working on migration-related problems. The team has already identified the root cause of these issues and is currently working with the IT security office to resolve them.\\n\\nAdditionally, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has instructed that any feedback or concerns regarding how these migrations are being handled must be kept strictly within the company and not shared with outside parties.","headline":"New communication policy established for migration-related project issues.","action_items":["@rspazzol to stop addressing migration issues.","@rspazzol to keep all project feedback internal to Red Hat."],"key_decisions":["External parties are no longer to be involved in migration troubleshooting.","All concerns regarding migration processes must remain internal."]}	\N	\N	standard	177
3bf6e488-3283-44ca-be65-77d6769a93d1	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ff1e8694-0b77-4831-a521-5cb1743a01f3	Delivery report status update	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has requested that everyone add their project updates to the shared presentation file. This information is necessary to finalize the current delivery report.\\n\\nPlease ensure all relevant updates are entered into the document by the end of the day to meet the reporting deadline.","headline":"Team members must update the project delivery report by the end of today.","action_items":["Add project status updates to the shared Google Slides presentation by EOD today (All team members)"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	178
7d1e3245-b16a-4614-8666-b7198b15ab29	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	4980a008-9c3a-499d-8ff2-e8243987b880	Migration Pilot Update	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia announced that the second migration pilot project began today at 10:00 AM UK time and will conclude this Thursday.\\n\\nTo keep everyone updated on the project's progress, Patricia has set up a shared spreadsheet. You can use this link to view the latest statistics and see how the migration is moving along in real time.","headline":"The second migration pilot has officially started and is being tracked online.","action_items":["Team members should check the provided spreadsheet to stay updated on migration status."],"key_decisions":["The second migration pilot will run from May 5th until Thursday.","A shared spreadsheet will serve as the official record for tracking migration progress."]}	\N	\N	standard	179
bce8dce3-2547-4331-a3da-d44c2b9505cf	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	7902f6bc-cc96-4048-acd7-04f5ce7a0d0d	Training material review	{"body":"Carina Almeida has asked the team to review the latest training materials to ensure everything is correct and up to date. She shared images of the documents to facilitate this process.\\n\\n@Rydekull, @janine, and @jfeind have been tagged to provide feedback on these materials. The goal is to confirm that the training content is ready for use.","headline":"Request for team review of updated training materials.","action_items":["@Rydekull, @janine, and @jfeind to review and provide feedback on the training materials."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	180
a5de2ce4-fe78-4e05-bc1e-d9f892e67c0c	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	b6ccd481-acb2-4177-9a6a-0e1aa1de8df9	RBAC and Secret Management	{"body":"Rosemary Lynch is following up on a pending project update regarding how the team manages system access and secure password updates using the HashiCorp Vault tool. This information was requested by Praveen to ensure the project remains on track.\\n\\nBecause Shebi will be away from their desk for most of the week, Rosemary Lynch has asked Janine to take over this task to ensure the project continues moving forward without delay.","headline":"Update requested on security access and password management project.","action_items":["Shebi to share the project update and proposed plan.","Janine to take over the project responsibilities from Shebi."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	181
