aca433bf-830d-4986-a494-6b31dbf7f7a1	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	e99a4a57-a2af-466f-af60-83e8cd49f80a	Root Cause Analysis	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has determined that the system errors are caused by a software component that does not work with the processors used in the new environment.\\n\\nThis means the software needs to be updated or replaced to match the requirements of the new hardware before the migration can proceed successfully.","headline":"Migration issues identified due to software being incompatible with new computer hardware.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":["Identified that the software is not compatible with the new system's hardware."]}	\N	\N	standard	183
02b2815f-0eca-4759-b6de-3404c4170dfd	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	d2639dd7-39b3-4dfb-8d31-6008eb2758d4	Delivery report status update	{"body":"Rosemary Lynch is asking for help to finish the Delivery Report, which is scheduled to be sent out at noon. Because Rosemary was away yesterday, there are missing pieces of information that need to be filled in before the final version is ready.\\n\\nRosemary has requested that a large group of team members review the shared presentation link and add their updates by 11:00 AM to ensure the report is completed on time.","headline":"Team input needed to finalize the Delivery Report by noon today.","action_items":["Team members (Rydekull, rspazzol, Shebi, janine, Philip Jones, James Force, ricardo gregorio, Petros, pdelashe) to update the report by 11:00 AM."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	184
2ea6adac-0655-4d5b-baa8-f6d3605e4562	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	b43833a0-1f9e-43c3-8576-851d2974b449	Software frustration	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull shared a general complaint regarding the use of Microsoft Outlook. The comment highlights a negative user experience with the current email software.\\n\\nThere were no specific details provided about what is causing the frustration, nor were any solutions proposed during this brief exchange.","headline":"User reports dissatisfaction with the Microsoft Outlook email application.","action_items":["Follow up with Alexander Rydekull to identify the specific issues causing frustration with Outlook."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	185
3250729e-62fc-4b64-a283-9c34a542790b	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	c7d5c318-ed8b-417c-baad-c2b295184d01	SSL certificate management	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull has started a conversation to address how the team handles 'wildcard' security certificates. This is a follow-up to previous discussions involving @rspazzol, @Philip Jones, and @James Force.\\n\\nThe goal is to ensure the team is aligned on how these security tools are managed. The discussion is currently in the early stages, with no specific changes or new plans finalized yet.","headline":"Team beginning discussion on managing shared security certificates.","action_items":["Alexander Rydekull to follow up with @rspazzol, @Philip Jones, and @James Force to discuss security certificate management."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	186
e173ae7b-be89-454b-b781-906be8fefd42	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	4c8177f0-4adc-4ffd-80ce-4fe56df3a5af	Driver issue investigation	{"body":"Jens Feind reached out to Shebi to see if the driver problems they are currently investigating are the same as those being handled in an existing support case. \\n\\nJens Feind is currently working with Devdatt on that specific support case and is looking to coordinate efforts to ensure the teams are not working on the same technical issues separately.","headline":"Checking for overlap between current driver troubleshooting efforts.","action_items":["Shebi to confirm if the driver issues are related to the case identified by Jens Feind."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	187
4479a6d8-0723-4cd2-bc48-bf62feaaaaf4	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	9656ca56-24b1-4f82-a42c-0a1f16710310	Project delivery reporting	{"body":"Rosalia Suarez Mejias notified the team that all necessary updates were collected and the final project delivery report has been distributed to the appropriate parties.","headline":"The project delivery report has been completed and sent.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":["The delivery report is complete and has been sent out."]}	\N	\N	standard	188
2e7a8a20-06c5-4ab3-8fde-185ac793b1f9	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	92eb024e-d4d1-4ede-81b2-baf5630701ec	GitOps Operator Lifecycle Management	{"body":"James Force raised a concern regarding how the GitOps software is currently installed. Because it is set up manually to help start the system, it automatically updates to the newest version without oversight, which differs from how we manage our other software tools.\\n\\nTo fix this, James Force suggested moving the GitOps software under our standard management policy after the initial setup is complete. This would allow the team to control exactly when updates happen, ensuring the software remains stable and consistent across our systems.","headline":"Improving how we manage and update the GitOps software tool.","action_items":["Investigate a plan to bring the GitOps software under standard management policies","Determine how to lock in specific software versions to prevent automatic, unmanaged updates"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	189
4d926b13-4403-478d-9c3a-646e3b62d478	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	59ff1f5e-e8b3-4004-8349-b6b929596534	HIC project status update	{"body":"Anne Maskell has reached out to schedule a call to provide the latest updates on the HIC project. This meeting will serve as a touchpoint to ensure all stakeholders are aligned on current progress.\\n\\nBy moving the update to a live call, the team aims to streamline communication and address any outstanding questions regarding the project's status.","headline":"Anne Maskell has requested a meeting to discuss the HIC project status.","action_items":["Anne Maskell to organize a meeting to review HIC project updates."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	190
240bd87f-ffdc-4bcf-b831-179870518d46	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	e26b7c3e-2836-4ab6-adea-241802ff5c53	VIB memory failure resolution	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged that the team is still experiencing memory errors on host servers, which are preventing the successful migration of data storage. This issue was brought to his attention by Abhishek.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli is coordinating with the relevant team members to address the problem. He has requested that Roy Golan oversee the fix, while @pdelashe and @janine have been identified as the key staff members responsible for investigating the root cause.","headline":"Ongoing memory errors are preventing successful data storage migrations on host servers.","action_items":["Roy Golan to manage the resolution process.","@pdelashe and @janine to investigate the server memory errors."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	191
573535b9-abf0-4422-a08b-2825996decad	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	c9ee7a7f-f2e3-45ad-a6b8-c1b7b56fb1ae	USA-Mexico data migration	{"body":"Rosemary Lynch has opened a new discussion thread to begin planning the transfer of data between the USA and Mexico. This project involves moving information across international borders and updating the necessary infrastructure to support the transition.\\n\\nAt this time, the project is in the very early stages of planning. No specific timelines or operational details have been finalized.","headline":"Project kickoff for the USA to Mexico data migration initiative.","action_items":["Determine project scope and next steps for the USA-Mexico migration (Owner: Unassigned)"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	211
8c43c79e-10d8-4c44-8d44-2dcab1de95c5	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	7584e75d-2aab-4709-8586-7a08e831f9e1	VM migration IP issue	{"body":"Jens Feind is coordinating the investigation into a technical problem where virtual machines lose their network addresses after being moved to a new system. The team is currently reviewing diagnostic logs from the migration software to identify the root cause.\\n\\nTo streamline the resolution process, Jens Feind has requested that all team members contribute any new information or evidence to an existing support ticket. This will ensure that everyone is working from the same set of data.","headline":"Centralizing support efforts for virtual machine migration connectivity issues.","action_items":["Team members to share any relevant findings or evidence regarding the migration issue in the designated support case."],"key_decisions":["Use the existing support case as the single point of truth for tracking this migration issue."]}	\N	\N	standard	192
4f2990d3-39a1-4a63-914a-14ed79306593	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	5c6303b6-8ebb-474b-9dd2-67b674461cc1	VM migration failure	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reported that the recent move of virtual machines encountered problems. One machine failed to move entirely, and three others did not pass the final quality checks after the move.\\n\\nTo resolve these issues, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has joined a conference call to investigate the cause and fix the errors.","headline":"Issues identified during virtual machine migration process.","action_items":["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to troubleshoot migration and validation issues on the conference call."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	193
31feb254-625b-46fd-95d0-089c7f5d1361	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	63333dd0-942c-41c8-bea9-94a55e5547b1	Pilot project status update	{"body":"Anne Maskell provided an update on the pilot project during the steering committee call held today. \\n\\nNote that the file previously attached to this update has been deleted, so the document is no longer available for viewing in this thread.","headline":"The pilot project status was shared at the steering committee meeting.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	194
6f2a34e7-b8a5-48b3-8c9e-e492af359148	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	b05d9bd6-312f-4722-b4ce-d018af8c8cd1	VM migration failure	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull reported that a specific virtual machine could not be moved as intended. The machine in question is unusually large, containing 37 separate storage disks, which likely contributed to the error.\\n\\nThis issue is currently being treated as a technical problem that needs to be solved before the migration can proceed. No further details on the cause or a timeline for a fix have been provided at this stage.","headline":"A virtual machine failed to move to a new server due to its large storage size.","action_items":["Troubleshoot and resolve the migration error for the large virtual machine (Alexander Rydekull)"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	195
eb05565d-eb11-4454-95b3-684b10b418ff	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	253af41d-7520-4b35-b791-de92658eab8c	Project feasibility inquiry	{"body":"Nick Evans has reached out to Sam Marland to confirm if the project goals are actually achievable as currently planned. The team is looking for assurance that the proposed approach will work.\\n\\nAt this stage, the project is waiting for confirmation from Sam Marland to ensure the plan is realistic before moving forward.","headline":"Request for confirmation on project feasibility.","action_items":["Sam Marland to confirm project feasibility to Nick Evans."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	196
be5790fc-74cd-44ea-833d-a8dcd092634e	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	fa2be7e7-a21f-491e-9e31-0de5b78ca74b	Task notification follow-up	{"body":"Carina Almeida confirmed that she has tagged a team member in the project management system to ensure they are aware of a pending task. This action serves as a direct follow-up to ensure visibility on the item.\\n\\nThe notification is intended to prompt the recipient to review the task and continue the necessary collaboration required to move the work forward.","headline":"Carina Almeida has notified a team member regarding a specific task update.","action_items":["Recipient to check their notifications and review the tagged task."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	197
a9e328cf-8803-4f3b-b04e-fa795e761bed	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	2da819a7-152a-4f78-ab52-0a740f06dc42	VM performance degradation analysis	{"body":"Jens Feind has flagged that two database servers are running slower than expected after being moved to a new hosting environment (Cluster 104). The team is currently reviewing a report that highlights these performance gaps compared to the previous setup.\\n\\nSudhir is leading the investigation to identify why these systems are underperforming. The team plans to meet later this week to discuss the report and decide on a plan to restore normal performance levels.","headline":"Investigation underway for speed issues on migrated database servers.","action_items":["Sudhir to investigate the cause of the slow performance.","Jens Feind to distribute the performance report to the team.","Team to hold a meeting this week to review the issue."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	198
fb92dd75-741b-4707-8a5f-b8a5cf000898	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	1c2444bf-52a7-44e9-8fad-4e76d5a97ec3	Alerting configuration best practices	{"body":"Ricardo Gregorio is reviewing a request from the SRE team to stop sending low-priority system alerts to the team. The goal is to reduce the volume of unnecessary notifications, but there are concerns about whether this will make it harder to track system history or meet official reporting requirements.\\n\\nRicardo is currently investigating whether this is a safe and standard way to manage system alerts. He is looking into whether this approach will cause problems for future troubleshooting or if there are better ways to manage these notifications without losing important data.","headline":"Reviewing a proposal to reduce notification noise by silencing low-priority system alerts.","action_items":["Ricardo Gregorio to determine if silencing low-priority alerts will negatively affect system auditing.","Ricardo Gregorio to identify if there are better ways to manage alert volume than the proposed method."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	199
44d9891f-d178-445e-8ea1-bb53a545e79b	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	65b88d46-b1ec-4d59-a835-83a32ab3a205	Bank service protection periods	{"body":"Rosemary Lynch has started a new conversation to address the rules and policies surrounding Bank Service Protection periods. This discussion is categorized under banking compliance and service policy.\\n\\nAt this stage, the thread is in its early planning phase. No specific details or policy changes have been proposed yet, but the topic is now open for review and future development.","headline":"New discussion opened regarding bank service protection timeframes.","action_items":["Determine the scope and requirements for Bank Service Protection periods (Owner: Unassigned)"],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	200
25f149da-834f-4ec6-a8e2-d6327cdca896	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	c918ebf5-0101-46e9-ba32-28c4af31548e	Network egress configuration	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull has started a discussion to verify how the system currently handles outgoing network traffic. He is asking the team to confirm if specific security rules, known as EgressIPs or EgressFirewalls, are currently being used.\\n\\nThis request is aimed at identifying the current setup to ensure the team has a clear understanding of the existing network configuration. There have been no responses or updates from the team yet.","headline":"Reviewing current network traffic controls and security settings.","action_items":["The team needs to confirm with Alexander Rydekull whether any network traffic restrictions are currently in place."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	201
bab85235-c2b8-4b3b-97e4-1b6bd7ffc984	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	3881fb60-521b-47af-af26-574dd2c09bcd	US/MX migration documentation	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has requested that the team create new presentation slides for the US/MX migration project. These slides need to clearly explain how Red Hat support will function during the transition, including details on specialized support teams and extra assistance periods.\\n\\nFurthermore, Raffaele Spazzoli has asked for an overview of the training program to be included in the project materials. Carina Almeida, Anne, and Shebi have been notified to assist with preparing this information.","headline":"New documentation requested for US/MX migration support and training materials.","action_items":["Carina Almeida and Anne to create slides explaining Red Hat support and the training program for the US/MX migration."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	202
92a95f27-2acc-488f-bcb9-674ba2d92f56	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	caae1dd8-0156-4503-a6b9-87e5b9905c0b	Project retrospective planning	{"body":"Anne Maskell has requested that the team make the project review session a top priority. She noted that completing this review is essential for making necessary improvements before starting the next phase of the project, known as Pilot 2.\\n\\nBy focusing on this review now, the team aims to learn from recent work and apply those lessons to ensure the next stage of the project runs more smoothly.","headline":"Team requested to prioritize project review for upcoming Pilot 2 phase.","action_items":["Team to prioritize and complete the project retrospective."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	203
0ecd44f1-7311-4896-afd5-4c8806b59dbb	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	2ccadeb8-8aef-41e1-9a8e-06483e6c5841	VM migration status	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that while most virtual machines showed an error message during the move, these errors do not affect the system and can be disregarded. One machine failed to move successfully and will be attempted again.\\n\\nOnce the final machine is moved, the technical team will begin testing the service in the user acceptance testing (UAT) environment to ensure everything is working correctly.","headline":"Update on virtual machine migration progress and upcoming testing phase.","action_items":["Technical team to retry the migration for the one failed machine.","ITSO team to perform service testing in the UAT environment."],"key_decisions":["The error messages received during the migration will be ignored."]}	\N	\N	standard	204
4b89edae-514b-4a13-8381-fc6656bebdc1	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	dd52ecfd-de3b-4f2a-8129-2012f319fd44	RCA process alignment	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia noted concerns regarding how the team handles Root Cause Analysis (RCA). She clarified that the team must follow the client's established procedures rather than creating a new internal process at this stage.\\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia plans to discuss these procedures during the next meeting with the client. Once she has a better understanding of how the client operates, she will determine if there are any opportunities to suggest improvements to their current workflow.","headline":"Reviewing and aligning our incident investigation process with the client.","action_items":["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to discuss the RCA process with the client during the next retrospective.","Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to report back to the team with updates and next steps."],"key_decisions":["The team will use the client's existing process for investigating issues instead of creating a new one."]}	\N	\N	standard	205
b11c3b3c-29dc-409b-b859-747d9a157507	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	ba83853c-24e7-46a0-9ea0-1097a3a138bb	Architecture documentation completion	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli has requested that the team prioritize and finish several key project documents over the next two weeks to improve our delivery standards. The focus is on finalizing designs for computing, security, data organization, and the Tertiary Vault system.\\n\\nSeveral team members have been assigned specific sections to write or review. This includes ensuring that data labeling guidelines are actually being applied to the virtual machines currently being moved to the new system, and confirming that security and vault documents are updated and ready for use.","headline":"Team must finalize project architecture documentation within the next two weeks.","action_items":["Michele, Raffaele, and Janine: Finish the computing design document.","Rydekull: Update and refine the security documentation.","Shebi: Review data organization plans and check that they are being used on current virtual machines.","Rydekull: Create the documentation for the Tertiary Vault."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	206
56567ad3-5605-4abc-8f33-78a2efee56aa	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	87c390ec-f5df-40b6-82f9-007b367c24a1	Live migration network configuration	{"body":"James Force is asking for an update on whether the team decided to set up a separate, dedicated network for handling system migrations. This was a topic of earlier discussions, but it is currently unclear if the work was ever completed or if a final decision was made.\\n\\nJames Force has reached out to @rspazzol and @Rydekull to confirm the current status and ensure the team is aligned on how these migrations should be handled moving forward.","headline":"Clarification requested on the setup of a dedicated network for system migrations.","action_items":["@rspazzol and @Rydekull to clarify the current status of the migration network setup."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	207
f78dede2-5b9d-474a-8ed6-dc7cbc9787a6	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	86074525-4f11-479b-9148-64a1d56523dd	VM failure technical analysis	{"body":"Sam Marland has requested an update on the recent technical issues affecting one of our virtual machines. The team is looking for a clear explanation of why the system failed, specifically focusing on software library errors that were previously identified.\\n\\nSam Marland is asking for a summary of the current investigation progress and the steps being taken to fix the problem to ensure the system is stable.","headline":"Inquiry regarding the cause and status of the recent virtual machine failure.","action_items":["Sam Marland: Provide an update on the investigation and repair status of the failed virtual machine."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	208
b63244e2-fade-442d-9a9f-cd9895740a88	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	3a920f12-d855-4567-ba8d-05f9b3422a8b	Meeting efficiency and resource management	{"body":"Raffaele Spazzoli expressed frustration regarding a recent meeting where four architects were present with Michele without a clear purpose. He noted that this represents an inefficient use of the team's time and requested that the group find a way to prevent similar situations in the future.\\n\\nThe team is looking to improve how they manage client interactions to ensure that staff time is spent productively. The focus is on ensuring that only necessary personnel attend meetings and that there is a clear reason for every session.","headline":"Improving meeting efficiency and preventing unnecessary staff attendance.","action_items":["Raffaele Spazzoli, Rydekull, and Shebi to create a process to better manage meeting attendance and ensure clear agendas."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	209
44a2b997-0311-42ad-90de-4e5c79920fe2	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	423ace56-9b2c-4934-a542-0bb40b71d5fe	OCP image synchronization metrics	{"body":"Alexander Rydekull is asking for a breakdown of how many software images are currently being synchronized within our OpenShift environment. He is looking for both the number of images handled during a single software release and the total number of images managed across all version history.\\n\\nThis information is intended to help the team better understand the scale of our current environment and the workload associated with our release management processes.","headline":"Request for data on how many software images are being updated in our system.","action_items":["Philip Jones and James Force to report on the volume of images synced per release and in total."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	210
169956db-3498-4f16-bef2-746fb59ce588	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	b7d1504f-427b-48fe-ad89-4e19b64b1d1e	Infrastructure and Storage Maintenance	{"body":"Philip Jones completed necessary updates to the Dell storage software on system 104, ensuring all required components are correctly installed. Philip Jones also fixed a search tool issue on system 101 and submitted a request to add new storage capacity on the Pure Storage system.\\n\\nPhilip Jones is currently working on setting safety limits for how much storage can be assigned to individual servers. Additionally, Philip Jones is assisting with an ongoing investigation into identity management issues on system 301.","headline":"Updates on storage system maintenance and ongoing troubleshooting tasks.","action_items":["Philip Jones: Document current system issues.","Philip Jones: Set storage capacity limits for servers.","Philip Jones: Resolve identity management issues on system 301."],"key_decisions":["Updated Dell storage software to the latest version.","Requested additional storage space for the search function."]}	\N	\N	standard	212
a0fa164e-4f36-4e40-9b8f-1102f40f4bcd	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	51efbb33-6c08-4b28-8d6d-ad1c652d1611	Network infrastructure configuration error	{"body":"James Force alerted the team to a setup error in the new network infrastructure located outside of the lab. Because a specific communication setting between devices was missed, the network is currently only using a fraction of its intended capacity.\\n\\nMichael and Rushi are aware of the situation and are working to fix the configuration. This update is intended to keep stakeholders informed should any performance questions arise during the build process.","headline":"Network connectivity issues identified due to configuration errors in the new build.","action_items":["Michael and Rushi to resolve the network configuration error."],"key_decisions":[]}	\N	\N	standard	213
12bba620-d700-4802-94b3-a1b3f0c7b260	095e378b-965f-40ac-b706-6a2102ec70ef	5385496f-47c0-4869-869a-50512d1cdaf9	Migration Pilot Update	{"body":"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has informed the team about changes to our migration plan. The project now starts later than planned because there's less work happening right before it begins. To make sure everything runs smoothly, we have added two new people named Janine and Alex to help out when someone is on call while Shebi will continue working as usual.","headline":"Migration Pilot Update: Changes made, including a rescheduled start date and updated on-call members.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":["Reschedule migration start date","Include new members (Janine & Alex) in the 'on call' team"]}	\N	\N	standard	214
8f361b9b-79a2-443a-a928-4963a8e3363a	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	85bf7097-66fc-4d45-836b-b703c23d2c4e	Increase readiness probe delay	{"body":"In our project management channel on Slack, Alice from Engineering noticed that it takes quite some time for our application to start up in real-world situations. She thinks this might be causing delays and wants us all to wait a bit longer before we know if the app is ready after updates are made (from 10 seconds now to 30). This change could help make sure things run more smoothly when it's time for our application to start up again. Alice has brought this suggestion forward, but as of yet no decisions or tasks have been assigned.","headline":"Alice proposes a longer wait before checking if the app is ready to go, aiming for smoother production starts.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	0
7e50bae2-54c7-4362-ad0b-5606e1edeceb	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	c6add2de-5588-49d6-ac16-60e413b76238	Build Optimization	{"body":"Bob suggested two main improvements to speed up the software development process. First, he plans to save frequently used files (specifically project dependencies) so they do not need to be downloaded every time the system builds. Second, he proposed running the build and testing tasks at the same time rather than one after the other.\\n\\nThese changes are intended to make the development workflow faster and more efficient, allowing the team to get feedback on their work more quickly.","headline":"Improving software build speeds through smarter resource management and task scheduling.","action_items":["Bob: Configure the system to cache project dependencies.","Bob: Update the build process to allow simultaneous testing and building."],"key_decisions":["Enable file caching for project dependencies.","Run build and testing tasks simultaneously instead of sequentially."]}	Engineering	\N	standard	1
2fbda5cf-fd89-4406-a50f-1ef4615e5f40	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	ab63bd62-6a1d-4b19-9fff-292c365ffb29	Deployment Pipeline Issue	{"body":"Alice shared that the team's automated system for deploying code isn't working as expected in their testing area, which is like a full-scale version of production. The main trouble seems to happen when trying to create container images using Docker commands before setting up project dependencies with npm install. This problem keeps halting progress and stops the team from moving forward.","headline":"Staging environment deployment pipeline failing due to issues with building Docker containers and installing npm packages.","action_items":["Find out why building containers is taking too long","Look into problems that might be occurring during package installation"],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	2
10236545-512a-4ae1-8412-0cd990865310	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	b99458b0-f389-44c7-8337-0f83a10c188a	Pipeline Cache Fix and Kubernetes Update	{"body":"Bob announced plans to update our system's background processes to improve efficiency. These changes focus on how the system stores temporary data and how it checks if new software is ready to run.\\n\\nThese improvements are expected to cut our deployment wait time by two-thirds, reducing the process from 15 minutes down to less than 5 minutes.","headline":"Upcoming updates will significantly speed up our software deployment process.","action_items":["Bob to submit the necessary code changes for review"],"key_decisions":["Initiate updates to deployment and system check processes"]}	Engineering	\N	standard	3
cb100eef-dc88-468a-a5b5-f2abe569726d	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	8dbc269c-8b88-4248-a1d5-279f5b6b8d70	Build Cache Issue	{"body":"Bob noticed that the team's build process was slowed down because someone updated a file called package.json, which is needed for installing dependencies with npm (a tool used by developers). Without using some sort of saved cache from previous builds, this update takes about 8 minutes to complete.","headline":"Build Cache Issue Due to Package Update","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	4
3b0cb7e9-9115-4083-bed4-812abc3d5e4d	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	1859e155-4b2a-4aaf-9552-56a462210d5b	Kubernetes Deployment Issue	{"body":"Charlie informed the team that a recent deployment of their application into Kubernetes failed. The problem was due to health check endpoints timing out which means they are not working correctly.","headline":"Kubernetes Deployment Failed, Need to Fix Health Check","action_items":["Adjust pod readiness probe configuration"],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	5
defd7f6d-b4cb-4411-8f17-270918721cf7	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	65d65b9f-cdac-473a-aff7-2f0e9cac9675	Docker layer cache implementation	{"body":"Alice brought up the idea of using caching in their project's build process, which would save time and resources. By storing 'node_modules', they can avoid reinstalling dependencies for every change made during development on identical branches or pull requests when nothing has changed with respect to those packages.","headline":"Talk about adding a Docker cache to speed up our GitHub workflows by keeping node modules around between builds.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	6
cbf32b8e-74c3-47b7-8fac-a6d2d0efa64f	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	8caa6aba-d479-429c-8da1-372ffdc8c84c	Migration and caching implementation	{"body":"In this conversation, Eve has agreed to make some updates that will improve how quickly our system can find data. She's going to add a special kind of index called 'partial', which helps speed things up when we look for specific information in the large amount of data we have stored on computers.","headline":"Eve plans database changes and cache setup.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":["Add partial index","Implement Redis caching"]}	Engineering	\N	standard	7
830f709e-2b4d-49c3-9917-81aebaed800b	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	2ee65712-6640-4ce7-b7f2-7d1b434ea559	Database Performance Optimization	{"body":"Dana, who works on databases for our team, has done some work to make a query faster. By putting in something called an 'index', Dana expects the time it takes for certain queries will go from 45 seconds down to less than half a second after moving everything over (migration). Now we need to keep track of this and see if our expectations are met.","headline":"Improving database speed by adding an index and checking results.","action_items":["Keep an eye on how fast the queries run now that Dana has made changes"],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	8
36e523f5-3ced-4e39-88f6-f95feae6d3bf	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	c4ed34d8-44c8-49e5-9967-485c219a8cc8	Database Optimization	{"body":"Eve highlighted a performance issue with a large data table that currently holds 50 million records. Because the table is not properly organized for quick searching, it is causing system slowdowns.\\n\\nTo resolve this, Eve recommended adding a specific search tool (an index) to the database. This will allow the system to find information much faster, improving overall speed and efficiency for users.","headline":"Database performance improvement planned for large data table.","action_items":["Add a new index to the database to speed up data searches (Assigned to: Eve/Engineering)."],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	9
070da1c1-b9fc-41e5-9833-af249c09883b	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	fbb5b99d-5f4f-430b-8f04-fcda828eb9ac	Database Performance Issue	{"body":"Dana informed the team that users are experiencing delays when accessing data through an analytics tool. The problem seems to be because our database software is scanning every row in a large table, which takes too long and makes things slow for everyone using it.","headline":"Database slowdown affecting analytics dashboard performance needs attention.","action_items":["Dana will look into ways of making the data access faster","The team will discuss how to improve response times"],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	10
4f6b0f89-c2a5-4a33-bbab-e96dcb1a94c4	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	273d9578-dbc9-4149-80d8-aa54f70bbfe0	Database Optimization	{"body":"Frank, a member of our engineering team, has come up with an idea to speed up the majority of dashboard-related searches. He suggests creating an index that only includes records from the last 90 days - this is because most users are looking at these recent entries and it will make finding them much faster without taking too much space on disk.","headline":"Optimizing database queries by focusing on recent data.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	11
296cbd50-e475-4fc7-9a45-0d195cb3ac4a	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	ef33387b-05ab-4f2c-a743-7844d353d63e	Database Performance Issue	{"body":"In our Slack conversation, Dana discovered why some reports are taking too long to generate. By running an analysis tool called EXPLAIN ANALYZE on a database query meant to create these reports, it was found that instead of quickly finding just what's needed for the report dates requested (which is like using our 'user_id' index), the system goes through every single user record in the entire table. This means we need to find another way to make this process faster.","headline":"Dana found out that a database query is slow because it scans all user data instead of just picking relevant records for the report date range.","action_items":[],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	12
90d552d2-f10e-4704-9e3e-013faa4c9866	b582e346-3983-4888-a50f-647ae9c954f8	e28e9551-034b-41df-89a0-2fe26aa297bd	Sales Demo Feedback	{"body":"U_TEST3 shared that the customer demo was well received and they are particularly interested in how our product can assist with role-based briefings. This means customers want to see features tailored for different job functions within their team, which could help them understand better what we offer.","headline":"Sales Demo Feedback: Customers Interested in Role-Based Views","action_items":["U_TEST3 and U_TEST1 will work together on a follow-up demo that includes role-based views to cater specifically to the needs of different sales team roles."],"key_decisions":[]}	Engineering	\N	standard	13
