5d9b9b0d-7dcf-4029-b5a1-cbdb4f5219c0	e0147672-6cc7-462a-b14c-df52101fef22	Migration failure management process	["SLA definition", "Incident triage optimization", "Operational collaboration"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia led a workshop to refine the Miox migration failure management process, specifically addressing ambiguities in SLA adherence and initial triage responsibilities. The team reviewed the ACN-drafted process, resulting in modified accountability matrices and updated SLA thresholds for incident response.\\n\\nKey architectural and operational improvements include ensuring Splunk-based Miox logs are accessible to the triage team and formalizing a Confluence-based knowledge base for error-to-resolution mapping. Furthermore, the team is establishing escalation protocols for ITSO non-responsiveness, evaluating whether to trigger automated rollbacks or transition to hypercare.", "headline": "Optimization of Miox migration failure triage, SLA definitions, and cross-functional operational workflows.", "action_items": ["Ensure all Miox logs in Splunk are accessible to the triage team.", "ACN to develop/review a Confluence knowledge base mapping Miox errors to solutions or points of contact.", "Program-level escalation to define protocols for unresponsive ITSOs (rollback vs. hypercare).", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia (Red Hat) to submit a proposal for collaboration with the Command Center and support triage."], "key_decisions": ["Modified responsibilities and SLA definitions for Miox migration failure management.", "Established escalation criteria for ITSO response delays (30-minute threshold)."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia held a workshop to fix confusion regarding who is responsible for handling migration failures and how quickly they must respond. The group updated the current process to ensure everyone knows their role and that response times are clearly defined.\\n\\nTo improve efficiency, the team decided to centralize technical logs and create a 'cheat sheet' for common errors to help the support team resolve issues faster. They are also setting up a plan for what to do if specific support staff do not respond within 30 minutes, ensuring projects do not stall during critical migration phases.", "headline": "Improving the process for handling migration errors and clarifying team responsibilities.", "action_items": ["Make system error logs available to the support team.", "ACN to create a reference guide for common migration errors and solutions.", "Define a backup plan for when support staff are unavailable.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to propose a new way for the team to work with the Command Center."], "key_decisions": ["Updated the process for managing migration failures to clarify roles and response time requirements.", "Set a 30-minute response time expectation for technical support staff."]}	2026-05-09 13:24:35.258959+00	\N
