aa0f3bde-0553-4eef-bb4a-ecc8a10939ca	6ce8e077-1d45-478e-804a-bf3f6a4fac9f	Migration Retrospective and Troubleshooting	["Incident Management", "Access Control", "Root Cause Analysis"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia identified critical bottlenecks in the migration incident response process, specifically regarding attendance at the Incident Bridge and the over-allocation of resources for troubleshooting. She highlighted a significant lack of administrative access for the SRE team across OCP and VCenter environments, which hindered immediate remediation efforts.\\n\\nTo address systemic issues, Patricia is pursuing a formal integration with Red Hat via a dedicated SNOW group for incident assignment. Furthermore, she is conducting a root cause analysis (RCA) regarding potential platform incompatibilities and has engaged proactive support, with Shebi currently aggregating historical data on similar incidents to expedite resolution.", "headline": "Migration retrospective identifies access control gaps and incident management process improvements.", "action_items": ["ACN to confirm with Vinay regarding the creation of a Red Hat SNOW group.", "Shebi to compile a list of similar platform issues and documented solutions.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to continue RCA and engage proactive support."], "key_decisions": ["Establish a strict time-bound attendance policy for the Incident Bridge, defaulting to a rollback if stakeholders fail to join.", "Initiate a review of SRE access permissions across OCP and VCenter."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia led a review of the recent migration, noting that the team needs a more efficient way to handle emergency calls. She proposed setting a strict time limit for meetings; if the necessary people do not join on time, the team will revert the changes to avoid further delays. She also noted that the support team was slowed down because they lacked the necessary permissions to access key systems.\\n\\nTo prevent future delays, Patricia is working to improve how the team coordinates with external partners like Red Hat. She is also investigating the root cause of the technical problems and working with Shebi to gather information from past issues to help solve the current situation faster.", "headline": "Team reviews migration issues and plans to improve access and incident response processes.", "action_items": ["ACN to verify with Vinay if a new support ticketing group can be created for Red Hat.", "Shebi to gather data on previous similar problems to help find a solution.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to lead the investigation into the root cause of the migration issues."], "key_decisions": ["Implement a 'no-show' policy for emergency calls that triggers an automatic rollback of changes.", "Review and update system access rights for the support team."]}	2026-05-09 13:06:30.64971+00	\N
fc4ce9dd-e43b-4d5c-a888-858d193e0b3b	1d759c1e-271b-40d9-89c2-d37a2fb8390d	Migration Automation and Integration	["IP Address Management", "Ansible Automation", "Infrastructure Provisioning"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga confirmed the integration of Windows golden image configurations—specifically restricting qemu-agent RPC calls and VirtIO driver settings—directly into the migration automation pipeline to mitigate post-migration failures. Additionally, the team has established an IP change matrix to manage network reconfigurations across various OS variants and multi-NIC scenarios.\\n\\nFollowing a sync with Janine, Jfeind, and Rydekull, Ansible was selected as the primary orchestration tool for post-migration IP updates. Srinath is currently provisioning the necessary Windows and Linux test VMs to validate the Ansible playbooks. Sebastian has requested support from Petros or Jfeind to execute the validation once the infrastructure is provisioned.", "headline": "Migration automation strategy finalized with Ansible integration and Windows golden image hardening.", "action_items": ["Srinath: Provision Windows and Linux test VMs for automation validation.", "Petros or Jfeind: Execute validation of Ansible playbooks upon VM delivery."], "key_decisions": ["Hardening Windows golden images by baking qemu-agent RPC restrictions and VirtIO configurations into migration automation.", "Adopting Ansible as the standard automation framework for post-migration IP address updates.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga designated as the owner for the US Migration Workstream."]}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga provided an update on the migration project, noting that the team is embedding specific system settings directly into the migration process to prevent common technical errors. They have also developed a plan to manage how computer network addresses will be updated during the move to the new data center.\\n\\nTo ensure these updates happen smoothly, the team decided to use the Ansible automation tool. Srinath is currently setting up test computers so the team can verify that the new automation works correctly for both Windows and Linux systems. Sebastian has asked Petros or Jfeind to assist with testing once the equipment is ready.", "headline": "Team aligns on automation tools and testing plans for upcoming data center migration.", "action_items": ["Srinath: Prepare the test computers for the migration team.", "Petros or Jfeind: Test the new automation process once the computers are ready."], "key_decisions": ["Incorporating system settings directly into the migration process to reduce errors.", "Selecting Ansible as the official tool for managing network address updates.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga appointed as the lead for the US Migration Workstream."]}	2026-05-09 13:15:27.832133+00	\N
661df2a4-753b-4967-b126-a0f43df1fe7f	3a570333-32a9-439e-8986-d40353e94468	Migration Project Management	["Workload Assessment", "Communication Planning", "Infrastructure Readiness"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on the migration project, noting the transition into the third migration event and the initiation of Pilot Phase #2. A critical challenge involves identifying legacy workloads within the installed base, prompting a request for Red Hat to quantify the legacy-to-installed-base ratio based on historical engagement data. The current scope is finalized at 230 VMs across 93 services, with a hierarchical mapping structure defined as Fabric -> Services -> VM.\\n\\nRegarding infrastructure and tooling, the team is evaluating the prioritization of MIoX development, specifically weighing Comms Integrations against pattern expansion. Due to current MIoX limitations, ITSO communications will be handled manually to manage message sequencing. Additionally, the UK Country Pilot plan is being baselined with a cutoff date scheduled for Monday, contingent on Vimal providing a comprehensive view of Fabric readiness.", "headline": "Migration Project Update: Phase 2 Pilot, Infrastructure Readiness, and MIoX Integration Strategy.", "action_items": ["Red Hat: Quantify legacy workload percentage based on prior engagement data.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Attend tomorrow's meeting to baseline the plan.", "Vimal: Provide a report on Fabric readiness for the UK pilot."], "key_decisions": ["Scope finalized at 230 VMs across 93 services.", "ITSO communications will be managed manually due to current MIoX functional limitations.", "UK Pilot start date set for two weeks post-completion of Phase 2."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia shared a status update on the migration project, confirming that the second pilot phase is underway. The team is currently working to identify older, undocumented applications, and has requested that Red Hat analyze past projects to help estimate how much of the current environment consists of these legacy systems. The project scope has been officially set at 230 virtual machines across 93 services.\\n\\nTo keep stakeholders informed, the team will manage communications manually for now, as the current project management tool does not yet support automated notifications. The team is also prioritizing tool improvements that will help streamline these communications. A detailed plan for the UK pilot is being finalized for release on Monday, pending a final check on infrastructure readiness from Vimal.", "headline": "Update on Migration Project Phases, Scope, and Communication Planning.", "action_items": ["Red Hat: Estimate the amount of outdated software based on previous project data.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Join the meeting tomorrow to finalize the project schedule.", "Vimal: Confirm that the infrastructure in the UK is ready for the migration."], "key_decisions": ["The project scope is confirmed at 230 virtual machines and 93 services.", "Manual communication processes will be used for IT staff to prevent inbox overload.", "The UK pilot will begin two weeks after the second phase is completed."]}	2026-05-09 13:15:46.250148+00	\N
