b8ec43ce-dc73-4a74-ac5b-640748a219b9	0acc7785-d98f-493b-9c49-b27fb915d177	Infrastructure and Build Engineering	["Container Storage Modules", "Image Mirroring", "OpenShift Maintenance"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Philip Jones reported a blocker regarding the latest Dell Container Storage Module (CSM) deployment. The module is failing to pull images due to incorrect pathing, specifically a mismatch between the expected 'dell' namespace and the mirrored 'dell-emc' registry path, compounded by an unexpected appended folder name. Philip has confirmed that the mirrored images align with the official support matrix, necessitating a potential vendor-side fix.\\n\\nIn parallel, Philip confirmed the successful merge of the updated oc-mirror documentation. The mirroring process is now restricted to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, with plans to execute 'oc-mirror delete' to prune version 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces. Additionally, Philip has escalated an investigation into OpenShift machinesets and machines to Durga.", "headline": "Dell CSM deployment blocked by image pathing issues and oc-mirror cleanup progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate issues regarding OpenShift machinesets and machines.", "Execute 'oc-mirror delete' to remove 4.19 images from Nexus and local storage."], "key_decisions": ["Restricted oc-mirror scope to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Initiated pruning of OpenShift 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces."]}	{"body": "Philip Jones provided an update on infrastructure maintenance, noting that the latest Dell storage software cannot be installed because it is looking for files in the wrong location. Despite following the official documentation, the software is unable to locate the necessary images in our mirrored storage. Philip indicated that this is likely a vendor issue that will require a fix from Dell.\\n\\nOn the maintenance front, Philip successfully updated the documentation for the image mirroring process. The team is now focusing on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, and they are preparing to delete older version 4.19 files to free up space. Additionally, Philip has requested that Durga look into problems involving the management of virtual machine sets.", "headline": "Updates on storage module deployment issues and OpenShift maintenance progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate reported issues with virtual machine sets.", "Philip Jones to proceed with deleting outdated 4.19 files once ready."], "key_decisions": ["The team will focus mirroring efforts on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Old version 4.19 files will be removed from the system to save space."]}	2026-05-09 13:23:30.96894+00	\N
