a6db0934-d35d-469d-8477-3e4e0172be02	ea8f3a4a-6867-49be-aa2e-dbe51edef118	Training Curriculum Gap Analysis	["GitOps Operational Alignment", "OpenShift Virtualization Enablement"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga highlights a critical disconnect between Red Hat DO156/DO316 labs and the bank's production environment. Current training emphasizes standard Web Console and CLI usage, which contradicts the bank's strict GitOps-driven operational model. Furthermore, the reliance on etcd-resident configurations for VM scheduling, labeling, and affinity rules creates an architectural gap where trainees lack visibility into the required YAML-based infrastructure deployment patterns.\\n\\nSebastian proposes a custom bridging session to reconcile these discrepancies. By involving Architects and Consultants to map vanilla OpenShift concepts to the bank's specific GitOps architecture, the team aims to ensure that VM management, networking, and backup strategies (e.g., Commvault) are correctly contextualized for the trainees' daily operational requirements.", "headline": "Gap analysis identifies misalignment between standard OpenShift training and bank-specific GitOps operational workflows.", "action_items": ["kibrahim to evaluate the feasibility of injecting a custom bridging session into the training curriculum.", "Architects and Consultants to prepare a walk-through mapping Red Hat training concepts to the bank's GitOps architecture."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reports that students are struggling to apply standard OpenShift training to the bank's actual work environment. Because the bank uses specialized automated deployment tools and specific backup systems rather than the standard tools taught in the course, trainees are finding it difficult to translate their learning into practical, day-to-day tasks.\\n\\nTo resolve this, Sebastian suggests adding a custom training session led by internal experts. This session would bridge the gap between the generic course material and the bank's unique setup, ensuring that staff are trained on the specific tools and processes they will actually use on the job.", "headline": "Current technical training requires customization to match the bank's specific operational standards.", "action_items": ["kibrahim to review the training plan and determine if a custom bridging session can be added.", "Internal experts to prepare a presentation connecting training concepts to the bank's specific operational workflows."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:11:00.405001+00	\N
9f9b49cc-99a5-494f-9f38-0d61d4d3c678	b6a551ce-db39-4f14-ae2a-0ffe25018f35	Migration Support and Hypercare	["ITIL Process Compliance", "SLA Management", "RCA Documentation"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has initiated a centralized thread to consolidate migration support and hypercare strategies ahead of a proposal deadline. The approach must strictly adhere to the client's existing ITIL-compliant framework, ensuring all proposed operational procedures align with established governance.\\n\\nRegarding technical constraints, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia highlighted a critical 15-minute SLA window for VM migration rollback decisions. Consequently, all proposed contingency measures and technical optimizations are to be documented within the Root Cause Analysis (RCA) section of the project documentation to maintain process integrity.", "headline": "Migration support strategy alignment with ITIL processes and strict VM rollback SLAs.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to finalize the proposal by the end of the week.", "Team members to contribute ideas to the shared Google Doc while respecting the 15-minute VM rollback SLA."], "key_decisions": ["All migration support proposals must strictly adhere to the client's existing ITIL-compliant processes.", "Proposed technical optimizations and contingency ideas must be documented within the RCA section of the project documentation."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has started a discussion to gather all project ideas into one place before the proposal deadline at the end of the week. Because the client is a bank, all plans must follow their existing internal rules and standard operating procedures rather than creating new ones.\\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia also noted a very tight 15-minute time limit for deciding whether to cancel a server migration if something goes wrong. To stay organized, all suggestions for handling these issues should be added to the official project document under the section dedicated to analyzing past problems.", "headline": "Consolidating migration support plans to meet strict client deadlines and service standards.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to complete the final proposal by the end of this week.", "Team members to add their feedback and ideas to the provided Google Doc link."], "key_decisions": ["The team will follow the client's existing internal rules instead of creating new processes.", "All migration-related suggestions will be stored in the shared project document under the RCA section."]}	2026-05-09 13:25:08.952419+00	\N
c79e6e72-9be0-47a1-9caf-b8f159d5d899	6e907dfb-5bfa-4900-af5f-90553efa4488	Auth proxy feature prioritization	["Release planning", "Customer requirement tracking"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sam Marland initiated a discussion regarding the prioritization of the auth proxy feature, specifically referencing RFE-7054. The requirement is driven by a customer deployment (HSBC) currently targeting OpenShift 4.22, with a migration path to 5.2 scheduled for the following year.\\n\\nSam Marland posits that the auth proxy feature is a prerequisite for the 4.22 release. Wallace Lewis (Engineering Director) is seeking confirmation on the timeline to align the RFE-7054 delivery with the 4.22 dev-complete status and the subsequent 5.2 roadmap.", "headline": "Prioritization of Auth Proxy feature for OpenShift 4.22 release cycle.", "action_items": ["Sam Marland to confirm if auth proxy is required for 4.22 or if it can be deferred to 5.2.", "Engineering team (@rspazzol, @Rydekull, @Nikos, @Nick Evans) to review RFE-7054 requirements."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Sam Marland is coordinating with the engineering team to determine if a new security feature (authentication proxy) must be ready for the upcoming 4.22 software release. This feature is a specific request from a key customer, HSBC, who is currently using the 4.22 version.\\n\\nWallace Lewis, an Engineering Director, is looking for clarity on whether this feature needs to be finished for the current version or if it can wait until the 5.2 release next year. The team is currently assessing the schedule to ensure the feature is delivered in time to meet the customer's needs.", "headline": "Reviewing the timeline for the new authentication proxy feature.", "action_items": ["Sam Marland to confirm the final deadline for the authentication proxy feature.", "Engineering team to evaluate the development timeline for the requested feature."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:25:20.927341+00	\N
