c15682df-bb80-4fd2-84f7-8a833fc38d60	481cbe07-3b95-4628-b4b4-e7b131ad3ffa	Bulk Migration Testing	["Performance Optimization", "Capacity Planning", "Migration Strategy"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported that Magnus has validated a 400ms latency threshold for the AAP platform, negating the need for immediate architectural modifications. Infrastructure scaling is underway, with the UK database CPU count increased to 18 and Red Hat’s performance tuning parameters applied. The migration strategy is finalized with a 45–75 minute SLA, targeting an 80/20 split between storage offloading and cold migration.\\n\\nTesting will shift to the UK environment due to Hong Kong lab delays, with Nitesh and Abhishek tasked to profile CPU, memory, and disk I/O metrics for Linux and Windows workloads. Janine noted that migrations requiring re-IP will necessitate extended automation workflows; consequently, the team will benchmark both standard and re-IP patterns to establish appropriate safety buffers. Abhishek confirmed that recent migration failures were non-Ansible related and are currently being remediated.", "headline": "Bulk Migration Testing Update: AAP Latency, Resource Scaling, and Migration Strategy Refinement", "action_items": ["Nitesh and Abhishek to conduct resource consumption testing in the UK environment.", "Abhishek to remediate non-Ansible migration failures and exclude problematic VM scenarios from upcoming tests.", "Team to benchmark and establish safety buffers for re-IP migration automation tasks."], "key_decisions": ["Maintained current AAP architecture based on 400ms latency validation.", "Established migration SLA of 45 to 75 minutes.", "Defined migration strategy ratio: 80% storage offloading, 20% cold migration."]}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga provided an update on the bulk migration project, confirming that the current system performance is acceptable and no major technical changes are needed. To support the migration, the team has increased the processing power of the UK database and applied recommended performance improvements. The team has also set a goal to complete each virtual machine migration within 45 to 75 minutes, using a mix of storage-based and standard transfer methods.\\n\\nBecause the Hong Kong testing facility is not yet ready, Nitesh and Abhishek will move their testing to the UK site to measure how much computing power and memory are required for different types of systems. Janine highlighted that migrations requiring network address changes will take longer, so the team will build in extra time to account for these complexities. Abhishek is currently addressing minor errors from previous tests to ensure smoother results moving forward.", "headline": "Progress Update on Bulk Migration Testing and Infrastructure Capacity Planning", "action_items": ["Nitesh and Abhishek to perform resource testing in the UK lab.", "Abhishek to fix recent migration errors and prepare for the next round of testing.", "The team to calculate extra time needed for complex network address changes."], "key_decisions": ["The current system is fast enough to proceed without major changes.", "Migration goals are set for 45 to 75 minutes per machine.", "The team will use a specific mix of transfer methods to optimize speed."]}	2026-05-09 13:25:27.045013+00	\N
df1b8ed3-f8df-4017-886b-892ac532ed65	d02b1a8e-85e2-420d-b910-d94bfd5f20c0	EntraID proxy configuration issue	["Change management", "Network infrastructure"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Philip Jones confirmed that the EntraID connectivity issue on segment 301 is caused by a misconfigured proxy. The current egress policy is blocking traffic to graph.microsoft.com, which is a mandatory endpoint for EntraID operations. The discrepancy appears to stem from a failure to replicate existing proxy configurations from the legacy infrastructure.\\n\\nPhilip Jones noted that remediation is now subject to formal change management protocols. Consequently, the required firewall or proxy policy update must be submitted through the Change Advisory Board (CAB) process, precluding an immediate hotfix.", "headline": "EntraID connectivity failure on node 301 identified as proxy egress restriction.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to initiate a change request for proxy configuration updates to allow traffic to graph.microsoft.com."], "key_decisions": ["The resolution path is mandated to follow the formal Change Advisory Board (CAB) process."]}	{"body": "Philip Jones reported that the recent connection problems with EntraID on system 301 are due to a configuration error in the network security settings. Specifically, the system is currently blocked from communicating with the necessary Microsoft services, likely because the settings were not correctly copied over from the previous system.\\n\\nPhilip Jones indicated that this cannot be fixed immediately. Because of company policy, the necessary adjustments must now go through a formal review and approval process before they can be implemented.", "headline": "EntraID access issues caused by incorrect network security settings.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to submit a formal request to change the network settings."], "key_decisions": ["The fix must undergo a formal review process before implementation."]}	2026-05-09 13:11:05.890017+00	\N
