365dab11-ba18-4ac4-94d9-69020e2495d3	cd33e312-f3de-4c01-9dda-29b46e053970	Migration Support Engagement Strategy	["Pilot vs Production Workflow", "Incident Management Process", "Cross-functional Collaboration"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga has proposed a bifurcated support engagement strategy for US/MX migration workshops. For Pilot Migrations, the model is Consulting-led, utilizing proactive support cases and a proposed 'Quarantine/Triage' environment for VMware rollbacks and RCA. Failed OpenShift VMs are isolated for analysis, with fixes applied to the underlying automation before rescheduling.\\n\\nFor Volume/Production Migrations, the model shifts to a Support-led execution. This phase leverages TAMs for follow-the-sun coverage and the ESS team for immediate break/fix resolution. Sebastian is soliciting documentation and workflow feedback from Anne, Carina Almeida, pdelashe, and Nikos to formalize these processes for upcoming workshops.", "headline": "Defining support engagement models for Pilot versus Production migration workflows.", "action_items": ["Anne, Carina Almeida, pdelashe, and Nikos to provide slides, workflows, and documentation for the migration support strategy.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to synthesize feedback into a formal presentation for the US/MX workshops."], "key_decisions": ["Proposed transition from Consulting-led pilot support to Support-led production migration support.", "Proposed implementation of a 'Quarantine/Triage' environment for failed VM migration analysis."]}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga is working to define how our support teams will handle migration projects. During the initial testing phase (pilots), our consultants will lead the process, focusing on troubleshooting and refining our automation. If a migration fails, the plan is to move the affected virtual machine into a separate 'triage' area to fix the issue before trying again.\\n\\nOnce we move to full-scale production, the responsibility will shift to our dedicated support teams. They will provide 24/7 coverage to handle any issues immediately. Sebastian is currently gathering input from Anne, Carina Almeida, pdelashe, and Nikos to ensure these processes are clear and well-documented for our upcoming workshops.", "headline": "Clarifying how our teams will support migration projects from testing to full launch.", "action_items": ["Anne, Carina Almeida, pdelashe, and Nikos to share relevant documents and ideas with Sebastian.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to create a final presentation slide based on team feedback."], "key_decisions": ["The team will move from a consultant-led model during testing to a support-led model for full production.", "The team plans to propose a dedicated 'triage' area for fixing failed migrations during the upcoming workshops."]}	2026-05-09 13:25:55.910384+00	\N
d649ec2e-f0c0-404e-96c3-7742169c933a	33f87bfa-ab21-4b07-a6dd-65a5960ecd0e	Cluster Infrastructure Maintenance	["Compliance Reporting", "Isovalent POC", "Storage Troubleshooting"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Philip Jones reports progress on cluster automation, specifically providing guidance to Kuldeep on silencing alerts during cluster provisioning. Compliance reporting support is ongoing for Vinayak regarding XML-to-CSV conversion. Network troubleshooting continues for three nodes failing to join cluster 307. Regarding storage, Pure has provided scripts for cluster 102 cleanup and 104 volume re-mapping; however, the 104 script requires modification to support FC connections rather than the current iSCSI-based logic. James is developing an alternative contingency script.\\n\\nThe Isovalent phase 2 POC is initiating, with the team standardizing on version 4.20. This decision avoids potential compatibility issues with operators on 4.21 and 4.22, aligning with the customer's potential upgrade path.", "headline": "Cluster infrastructure maintenance, storage remediation, and Isovalent POC progression updates.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to test cleanup script on cluster 102.", "Pure to provide revised volume re-mapping script for cluster 104 (FC support).", "James to finalize contingency scripting for cluster 104.", "Philip Jones to continue network troubleshooting for cluster 307 nodes."], "key_decisions": ["Standardize Isovalent POC on version 4.20 to ensure operator compatibility."]}	{"body": "Philip Jones provided updates on several infrastructure tasks, including automating alert management for new clusters and assisting with compliance report formatting. Technical teams are currently investigating connectivity issues preventing three nodes from joining cluster 307.\\n\\nStorage repairs are underway for clusters 102 and 104. While a fix for cluster 102 is ready for testing, the repair script for cluster 104 requires adjustments to match the specific hardware configuration. Additionally, the team is starting the second phase of the Isovalent testing project, choosing to use version 4.20 to ensure stability and compatibility with existing tools.", "headline": "Updates on system maintenance, storage repairs, and new software testing plans.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to test the cleanup process for cluster 102.", "The storage vendor to provide an updated repair script for cluster 104.", "James to prepare a backup plan for cluster 104 repairs.", "Philip Jones to continue working with the network team to fix cluster 307 connectivity."], "key_decisions": ["The team will use software version 4.20 for the Isovalent testing project to avoid compatibility risks."]}	2026-05-09 13:26:03.647904+00	\N
