0780e7b5-6d12-4268-a3ae-bf4f66658bd1	c446a609-0bc4-476e-ad3b-dff23ac60ce8	Storage offload compatibility	["NetApp integration", "Customer support"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported a failed attempt by a customer to utilize native storage offload functionality within a NetApp-based infrastructure. The architecture is fundamentally incompatible with the current offload implementation.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli confirmed that the customer has been advised to utilize the NetApp-specific 'Shift Toolkit' as the designated alternative for managing these storage operations.", "headline": "Incompatibility identified between native storage offload and NetApp storage environments.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Native storage offload is officially unsupported for NetApp environments.", "Direct customers to the NetApp Shift Toolkit for storage migration/offload tasks."]}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli notified the team that a customer attempted to use our built-in storage offload feature with their NetApp storage system, which resulted in a failure due to technical incompatibility.\\n\\nTo resolve this, Raffaele Spazzoli has informed the customer that they must use NetApp’s own software, known as the 'Shift Toolkit,' to handle these tasks instead of our platform.", "headline": "NetApp storage systems are not compatible with our standard offload feature.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Our storage offload feature will not be used for NetApp systems.", "Customers should use the NetApp Shift Toolkit as the approved workaround."]}	2026-05-09 13:11:21.422596+00	\N
1b0acaf5-359a-43c4-b00d-a15efbcb1863	0695dc1b-ff8c-4c0b-8c9c-d2837e0940b5	VM Migration Technical Issues	["Windows Failover Clusters", "Shared Disk Migration", "Bug Tracking"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Jens Feind identified a critical limitation in the Migration Toolkit for Virtualization (MTV) where VMs utilizing shared disks must be powered off to initiate migration, resulting in the failure to preserve static IP configurations. This dependency has been formally documented as bug MTV-5235 in Jira. Jens has consulted with Martin Necas regarding the architectural implications of this constraint.\\n\\nAdditionally, Jens Feind is providing ongoing support for Red Hat support case 04432578 and assisting with the VMware Tools cleanup initiative. Until a permanent solution or workaround is engineered, affected VMs are restricted from current migration plans.", "headline": "Addressing Windows Failover Cluster IP migration failures for VMs with shared disks.", "action_items": ["Jens Feind to draft a statement for Narender regarding the migration exclusion.", "Jens Feind to share the draft statement for team feedback."], "key_decisions": ["Exclude VMs with shared disks from upcoming migration plans until a workaround is implemented.", "Formalized the IP migration issue as Jira bug MTV-5235."]}	{"body": "Jens Feind reported an issue where virtual machines using shared storage lose their network settings during the move because they must be turned off before the transfer. This prevents Windows Failover Clusters from restarting correctly after the migration is complete.\\n\\nTo prevent further issues, the team has decided to pause the migration of these specific machines until a fix is developed. Jens is currently coordinating with the support team and documenting the problem to ensure it is resolved properly.", "headline": "Migration of specific virtual machines paused due to network configuration issues.", "action_items": ["Jens Feind to write a status update for Narender regarding the migration pause.", "Jens Feind to share the update with the team for review."], "key_decisions": ["Pause migrations for virtual machines with shared storage to avoid network errors.", "Officially track the migration issue in the bug reporting system."]}	2026-05-09 13:26:22.385708+00	\N
70b3934e-fda0-45bc-88c3-2d1d42fc604d	f79942ba-525a-4bd0-b85d-5022bfc74418	Windows VM driver migration	["Ansible automation", "OCP infrastructure patching"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Arpit Tolani is developing an Ansible automation workflow to standardize display drivers to 'virtio' for Windows Server VMs following migration. The proposed logic involves querying the VMI status for 'prettyName' and executing an 'oc patch' command to update the VM spec. \\n\\nArpit Tolani has identified architectural dependencies regarding OCP connectivity, module selection, and the requirement for VM post-patching reboots. He is currently seeking a mechanism to dynamically retrieve the list of migrated Windows VMs to integrate into the automation pipeline.", "headline": "Automating post-migration Windows VM display driver patching via Ansible and OCP CLI.", "action_items": ["Arpit Tolani to define OCP connectivity and module strategy for Ansible.", "Arpit Tolani to identify a data source for the list of migrated Windows VMs."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Arpit Tolani is creating an automated process to ensure that all Windows virtual machines are correctly configured with the right display software after they are moved to the new cloud infrastructure. This automation aims to save time by automatically updating the settings for every Windows machine identified in the system.\\n\\nTo move forward, Arpit Tolani needs to determine the best way for the automation tool to connect to the system and how to generate a list of the specific machines that have been moved. He is also planning for the necessary system restarts required to finalize these updates.", "headline": "Streamlining the setup of Windows virtual machines after moving them to the new system.", "action_items": ["Arpit Tolani to determine the technical method for connecting the automation tool to the system.", "Arpit Tolani to find a way to track which specific machines have been moved so they can be updated."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:26:28.668057+00	\N
