7c1d1b87-fd6e-44bb-b278-994932913cbf	0738be78-06e9-477c-950d-e896be4dbd5f	Migration risk assessment	["Infrastructure rebuild", "Project velocity", "Stakeholder coordination"]	\N	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Anne Maskell has raised concerns regarding the migration risk assessment, specifically highlighting the transition from legacy source VM hardware to an OpenShift-based infrastructure. The primary technical risks identified include the lack of validation for the rebuild process and the absence of a coordinated decommissioning strategy for the source hardware.\\n\\nAnne Maskell has requested clarification from James Force regarding the build stream's current status on these rebuilds, noting that these architectural dependencies could negatively impact overall migration velocity.", "headline": "Risk assessment regarding VM hardware decommissioning and OpenShift migration velocity.", "action_items": ["James Force to provide status update on build stream coordination regarding VM to OpenShift rebuilds."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Anne Maskell has flagged a potential risk to the project timeline due to the plan to replace old server hardware with a new platform. She noted that the team has not yet tested this new setup, and there is no clear plan for how to retire the old equipment.\\n\\nAnne Maskell is seeking input from James Force to determine if the team responsible for building the new system is aware of these issues and if they have a plan to prevent these technical hurdles from slowing down the overall migration progress.", "headline": "Concerns raised about potential delays in the server migration project.", "action_items": ["James Force to confirm the status of the server replacement plan and address coordination concerns."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:11:23.738641+00	\N
42ffd150-66c3-465e-a1a3-6d829ea8d02e	a84c821a-ae5d-41d4-ac93-04b23267c768	Weekly Delivery Reporting	["Status Updates", "Deadline Management"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias has initiated the weekly delivery reporting cycle, requiring all stakeholders to populate the designated Google Slides template. The scope of the update covers the period from the previous Thursday through the current date.\\n\\nTo ensure the final report is ready for distribution by 11:00 AM tomorrow, Rosalia Suarez Mejias has mandated that all content updates to the main body of the presentation be finalized by close of business today.", "headline": "Weekly Delivery Report submission deadline established for project status synchronization.", "action_items": ["All team members: Update the delivery report template by COB today."], "key_decisions": ["Report distribution scheduled for 11:00 AM tomorrow.", "Update window defined as last Thursday to current date."]}	{"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias has requested that the team provide their progress updates for the past week in the shared project presentation template. This information is necessary to compile the weekly delivery report.\\n\\nTo keep the project on schedule, Rosalia Suarez Mejias has asked that everyone complete their entries by the end of the day. This will allow for the final report to be sent out tomorrow morning at 11:00 AM.", "headline": "Team requested to provide project status updates for the weekly report.", "action_items": ["All team members: Add project updates to the Google Slides template by the end of the day."], "key_decisions": ["The weekly report will be sent out tomorrow at 11:00 AM.", "Updates must cover work completed since last Thursday."]}	2026-05-09 13:11:32.098434+00	\N
3ba684a5-3f1d-4164-bba9-4880d9b528b6	e6d70d7f-5c75-4792-99da-fbd563c46fb8	Migration issue resolution	["Infrastructure troubleshooting", "VIB version upgrade", "VMWare tooling"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sam Marland has identified four primary failure vectors impacting current migrations: residual VMWare tooling preventing VM restarts, XFS filesystem corruption detected by MTV, and two distinct VIB versioning issues. The VIB issues include a lack of HSBC certification for v0.3.0 and host resource contention during the 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 upgrade path. Additionally, an LVM-related failure and an unrelated MioX incident were noted.\\n\\nSam Marland is requesting validation of this incident list and immediate remediation strategies for reporting to leadership. Coordination is underway with Roy Golan via Nikos to clarify the specific technical constraints surrounding the VIB upgrade.", "headline": "Analysis of migration failures involving VMWare tooling, VIB versioning, and filesystem integrity.", "action_items": ["Validate the list of migration issues for accuracy (Team)", "Define proposed solutions for each identified failure point (Team)", "Provide additional technical information regarding the VIB issue (Roy Golan)"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Sam Marland has summarized four main technical problems causing current migration failures. These include issues with software removal, file system errors, and problems related to a recent software update that caused system performance issues and certification conflicts. A separate, unrelated issue with the MioX system was also identified.\\n\\nSam Marland is asking the team to confirm these findings and provide clear solutions as soon as possible to update project leadership. The team is currently working with Roy Golan to better understand the software update issues.", "headline": "Review of current migration issues and request for resolution plans.", "action_items": ["Confirm the accuracy of the reported migration issues (Team)", "Develop and document solutions for each migration issue (Team)", "Provide further details on the software update problems (Roy Golan)"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:27:14.739424+00	\N
232cc1fb-8584-4f0d-9b14-48137da4e026	2451cdb5-902b-45e9-89ef-e45ccaabb5ba	OS driver issue resolution	["Windows driver troubleshooting", "Project status update"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has initiated an inquiry regarding ongoing OS driver failures on Windows, citing an external email thread involving Abhishek as evidence of stalled progress. The current status of the driver stack is under scrutiny due to lack of resolution.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli is requesting a technical summary of the root cause analysis and the remediation roadmap from @atolani and @jfeind. The request aims to identify specific blockers or resource requirements necessary to stabilize the driver implementation.", "headline": "Escalation regarding persistent OS driver instability on Windows platforms.", "action_items": ["@atolani and @jfeind to provide a summary of the OS driver issues and the resolution plan.", "@atolani and @jfeind to identify any additional resources or support required to resolve the driver failures."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged concerns regarding ongoing problems with Windows drivers, noting that recent communications suggest the team is not making sufficient progress toward a fix.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli has asked @atolani and @jfeind to provide a clear update on the current situation, the plan to fix it, and any help they might need to get the project back on track.", "headline": "Request for status update on unresolved Windows driver issues.", "action_items": ["@atolani and @jfeind to summarize the current driver problems and the plan for fixing them.", "@atolani and @jfeind to list any support or resources needed to resolve these issues."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:11:39.683292+00	\N
477b62a4-1cee-4119-adbc-bc5c22bfd4fd	5ae678ff-93a3-4b67-841e-f953179d3cd4	VM Affinity Rule Management Gap	["Data Protection Limitations", "Externalized Configuration Management"]	\N	0.95	gemini-2.5-flash	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga identified a critical architectural gap where VM affinity and anti-affinity rules are stored exclusively within the OpenShift etcd database, leading to data loss upon VM deletion. Currently, these rules lack a declarative source of truth, necessitating manual intervention by administrators for both initial configuration and post-recovery scenarios. The current backup solution exhibits limitations, as label-based affinity rule recovery is inconsistent across clusters, often requiring manual reconciliation.\\n\\nTo remediate this, Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga, in consultation with Michele, Jakob, Phil, and Rydekull, has proposed transitioning to a GitOps-based externalized configuration management system. This architecture will serve as the authoritative source of truth, enabling automated reconciliation of placement rules across OpenShift clusters. This requirement has been categorized as a future architectural enhancement rather than part of the current project scope.", "headline": "Addressing VM Affinity Rule Persistence and Externalized Configuration Management Gaps", "action_items": ["Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to update 'Data Protection and Data Recovery' documentation with current backup/restore limitations.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to add the externalized configuration management requirement to the 'Data Architecture' documentation."], "key_decisions": ["Adopt a GitOps-based externalized configuration management system as the future source of truth for VM affinity rules.", "Classify the implementation of programmatic affinity rule management as a net-new requirement for the platform."]}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga highlighted a challenge regarding how virtual machines (VMs) are managed after they are moved to our new system. Currently, the rules that dictate where a VM should run are stored only inside the system itself. If a VM is deleted or needs to be restored from a backup, these rules are often lost, requiring manual work by administrators to fix them. This creates a risk of human error and increased downtime during recovery.\\n\\nTo solve this, Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga and the project team have decided to move toward a new system that stores these rules in a central, external location. This will allow the system to automatically keep track of and apply these rules, ensuring they are never lost during a migration or recovery. While this is not part of the current project, it has been officially documented as a necessary future upgrade.", "headline": "Improving how we manage and recover virtual machine placement settings", "action_items": ["Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to update project documentation to reflect current limitations in data recovery.", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga to add the new centralized management system to the project's future requirements list."], "key_decisions": ["The team will eventually move to a centralized system to automatically manage VM placement rules.", "The current manual process for restoring VM settings will remain in place until the new system is developed."]}	2026-05-09 13:01:39.727518+00	\N
c54fb0a4-5f38-448f-b62f-e8c68aceb28e	e449132b-113e-4ef6-9076-35223f0cb201	VM migration triage process	["troubleshooting", "infrastructure migration"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	\N	\N	2026-05-25 12:54:17.194239+00	\N
0e69eeef-53fb-4b62-b36e-399eb08a0ad0	dd7635d0-7b56-494e-a958-87d46d46eb3b	Observability infrastructure updates	["Logging configuration", "Alerting rules"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Ricardo Gregorio reported progress on observability infrastructure, specifically the integration of new alert rules into the OpenTelemetry (Otel) Collector, credited to James Force. Additionally, Ricardo updated logging configurations to include extra namespaces and removed existing filters targeting the cyber Splunk instance.\\n\\nRicardo noted a data ingestion volume of 18GB from 104 sources over the last 24 hours while filters were active. Future technical requirements include modifying the Trident configuration to support https-metrics, with a pending consultation scheduled with James Force.", "headline": "Updates to OpenTelemetry collector alerting and logging infrastructure configurations.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to review Splunk filter changes with Rijo.", "Ricardo Gregorio to modify Trident configuration for https-metrics support.", "Ricardo Gregorio to coordinate with James Force regarding Trident configuration updates."], "key_decisions": ["Removed existing filters targeting cyber Splunk for logging.", "Expanded logging configuration to include additional namespaces."]}	{"body": "Ricardo Gregorio provided an update on efforts to improve how the system monitors performance and logs data. This includes adding new automated alerts to the system, thanks to contributions from James Force, and expanding the scope of data being collected into new areas.\\n\\nRicardo also adjusted the settings for how data is sent to the security reporting tool (Splunk) to ensure better visibility, noting that 18GB of data was processed over the last day. Upcoming work involves updating the system's connection settings to support secure metrics, which will be coordinated with James Force.", "headline": "Improvements to system monitoring and data logging processes.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to meet with Rijo to review recent logging changes.", "Ricardo Gregorio to update system connection settings for secure metrics.", "Ricardo Gregorio to sync with James Force on upcoming configuration tasks."], "key_decisions": ["Updated logging settings to capture more data and removed previous restrictions.", "Added new automated alerts to the system monitoring tools."]}	2026-05-09 13:11:45.822266+00	\N
f37e4a0c-8361-4d04-8f77-1f3798abcdf6	19e30323-ab54-458a-affd-82aa1e569285	Software driver update request	["BSOD resolution", "VirtIO-Win driver upgrade"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has identified that MTV 2.11.4-2 effectively addresses BSOD occurrences reported by customers by integrating the latest VirtIO-Win 1.9.57 driver set. \\n\\nSpazzoli has formally requested that Philip Jones initiate the upgrade process to version 1.9.57 to standardize this fix across the environment.", "headline": "Request to upgrade VirtIO-Win drivers to version 1.9.57 for BSOD mitigation.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to evaluate and implement the upgrade to VirtIO-Win 1.9.57."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli noted that a recent software release (MTV 2.11.4-2) includes updated driver files that successfully resolve system crash issues experienced by other customers. \\n\\nSpazzoli has asked Philip Jones to update the current system to this newer version to ensure better stability and prevent further crashes.", "headline": "Proposed software update to fix system crashes.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to review and perform the requested software update."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:11:50.981904+00	\N
25a4462a-f3a8-4a5f-a0f7-8957c790601f	ad850b5b-cc68-4faf-a688-b05b49768db8	High Availability Strategy	["OpenShift Infrastructure", "Disaster Recovery", "Service Priority Modeling"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga outlined a dual-phase strategy for OpenShift High Availability. The initial design utilized node and VM labeling across Country, Data Center, and Fabric dimensions, integrated via GitOps, MIOX, and Ansible to enforce strict Affinity/Anti-Affinity rules. This approach aimed to model physical failure domains for automated scheduling constraints.\\n\\nHowever, Rushi identified significant operational risks, noting that strict Anti-Affinity constraints could impede rapid recovery during outages due to scheduling conflicts. Consequently, the team is pivoting toward a Service Class (Priority Level) model. This shifts the architecture from static placement constraints to dynamic resource management, where high-priority workloads are live-migrated during failures, while low-priority workloads are preemptively terminated to reclaim capacity.", "headline": "Transitioning from Affinity-based HA to Service-Class Priority Modeling for OpenShift Infrastructure.", "action_items": ["Define service priority levels for application workloads.", "Implement logic for aggressive evacuation and live-migration of high-priority VMs."], "key_decisions": ["Abandon strict Affinity/Anti-Affinity rules in favor of Service Class-based priority modeling.", "Adopt a capacity-reclamation strategy where low-priority VMs are powered down during failure events."]}	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga shared a plan to improve system reliability by tagging servers based on their physical location. While this would help organize where applications run, the team realized it would be too complex to manage during an emergency, as it could prevent systems from restarting quickly when things go wrong.\\n\\nTo simplify this, Rushi suggested a new approach based on service importance. Instead of managing complex rules for every server, owners will simply label their services as high or low priority. If a major failure occurs, the system will automatically move important services to healthy servers and turn off less important ones to make sure the critical work continues without interruption.", "headline": "Moving to a priority-based system to ensure critical services stay online during outages.", "action_items": ["Assign priority levels to all existing services.", "Develop the automated process to move critical services and stop non-essential ones during outages."], "key_decisions": ["Shift from complex location-based rules to a simple priority-based system for system recovery.", "Decided to prioritize critical services by shutting down non-essential services during major failures."]}	2026-05-09 13:11:54.824736+00	\N
8164a902-6a28-46ef-b331-28af0a982551	ba54d886-764e-4d53-b8d6-9cc50f63de11	Observability and Logging Configuration	["Infrastructure Monitoring", "Storage Metrics Integration"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Ricardo Gregorio updated the log-forwarder filter to include the netapp-trident namespace and implemented specific regex patterns for message filtering. Additionally, he prepared a Kustomize patch definition for region-based endpoints to facilitate upcoming live environment transitions.\\n\\nRicardo Gregorio is currently collaborating with Onkar to integrate PowerMax storage metrics into the storage team's monitoring infrastructure.", "headline": "Updates to log-forwarder filters and storage metrics integration for NetApp and PowerMax.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to finalize PowerMax metrics integration with Onkar.", "Ricardo Gregorio to deploy Kustomize patch for region-based endpoints next week."], "key_decisions": ["Included netapp-trident namespace in log-forwarder filter configuration.", "Applied regex patterns to message filtering logic."]}	{"body": "Ricardo Gregorio has updated the system's logging tools to better capture data from the NetApp storage environment. He also created a plan to manage regional settings, which will be implemented next week to ensure smooth system updates.\\n\\nAdditionally, Ricardo Gregorio is working with Onkar to ensure that performance data from the PowerMax storage system is properly shared with the storage team for better oversight.", "headline": "Improvements to system monitoring and storage data tracking.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to complete the PowerMax data integration project with Onkar.", "Ricardo Gregorio to execute regional configuration updates next week."], "key_decisions": ["Updated logging filters to include NetApp storage data.", "Standardized message filtering using new pattern rules."]}	2026-05-09 13:12:03.534623+00	\N
24828d48-0b73-40c2-829b-5ae281ca35e8	42531c45-cd86-4263-80e4-208df96a85c1	System migration execution	["Migration status update", "Technical deployment"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that all migration prechecks have been executed successfully, validating the environment's readiness for the transition. Consequently, the migration process has been officially launched.\\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia estimates a total execution window of approximately 60 minutes. A follow-up status report is scheduled to be provided upon the conclusion of this deployment phase.", "headline": "System migration initiated following successful completion of pre-deployment validation checks.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Provide status update in approximately 60 minutes."], "key_decisions": ["Initiation of system migration following successful precheck validation."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia announced that the system has passed all necessary safety checks and the migration process is now in progress.\\n\\nThe team expects the migration to take about one hour to complete. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia will provide another update once this time has elapsed.", "headline": "The system migration process has officially started and is currently underway.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Provide a progress update in one hour."], "key_decisions": ["The migration process has been started."]}	2026-05-09 13:09:26.613546+00	\N
fe728e6d-2485-4456-a9a8-1fef4824e11c	86b0b131-18cf-41e3-a01a-185cca2abedd	Node drain failure	["Live migration issues", "VM management"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported that node drain processes are exceeding expected time thresholds, resulting in live migration failures for virtual machines. The current behavior necessitates manual intervention to migrate VMs, which indicates a failure in the automated migration orchestration even under conditions of high storage latency.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli has requested that Balamurugan open a formal support case to investigate the underlying cause. Shebi and James Force have been tagged to provide additional context and technical insights into the migration failure patterns observed during the drain process.", "headline": "Node drain operations failing due to live migration timeouts on VMs.", "action_items": ["Balamurugan to open a formal support case regarding node drain and live migration failures.", "Shebi and James Force to provide technical context on the migration issues."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli highlighted a problem where moving virtual machines from one server to another during maintenance takes too long, causing the process to fail. This forces the team to move these machines manually, which is not the intended automated behavior, regardless of storage speed.\\n\\nTo resolve this, Raffaele Spazzoli has asked Balamurugan to document the issue through an official support ticket. Shebi and James Force have been brought into the conversation to help troubleshoot and provide more information on why these automated moves are failing.", "headline": "Issues with moving virtual machines during server maintenance.", "action_items": ["Balamurugan to submit a formal support request.", "Shebi and James Force to assist with the investigation."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:12:05.481419+00	\N
0c89f9c2-81b2-43ff-9cb3-9df0b7a5879c	32607395-5d92-4180-85f4-58a893a881b2	Client meeting follow-up	["Pure account status"]	\N	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Sam Marland initiated a status check regarding the recent client interaction with Pure. The thread currently lacks any technical architectural updates or project-specific deliverables.\\n\\nNo further technical context or documentation has been provided by the participant at this time.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding the status of the Pure account engagement.", "action_items": ["Sam Marland: Provide update on the Pure client call."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Sam Marland is asking for a summary of the recent conversation with the client, Pure. There has been no response or information shared regarding the outcome of that meeting yet.\\n\\nThis remains an open request for information to understand the current status of the account.", "headline": "Request for an update on the recent meeting with Pure.", "action_items": ["Sam Marland: Follow up to receive a report on the Pure meeting."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:07:55.623055+00	\N
2fcb3274-d671-4f4e-bea3-5bd7c7c08bd8	c61d9f22-9991-418d-b73e-305a0cab47cd	Infrastructure Migration Planning	["Project Scheduling", "Resource Management"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on Pilot Phase 2, confirming a scope adjustment to 212 VMs. The reduction from the initial 230 VMs is attributed to decommissioning paths, inventory reconciliation, and pending responses from 23 ITSOs. The migration execution is scheduled across three days, May 5th through May 7th, with specific hourly batching for the 212 VMs.\\n\\nRegarding the UK Pilot, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that cluster provisioning remains on schedule. The deployment lifecycle is mapped from May 13th through June 15th for Dev, UAT, and OAT environments, followed by a transition to contingency and production phases from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Infrastructure Migration Pilot Phase 2 scheduling and UK cluster deployment roadmap finalized.", "action_items": ["Follow up with 23 non-responsive ITSOs regarding VM inventory."], "key_decisions": ["Finalized Pilot Phase 2 scope at 212 VMs.", "Established migration execution window for May 5th-7th.", "Defined UK Pilot deployment timeline from May 13th through July."]}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia shared an update on the second phase of the server migration. The total number of servers to be moved has been adjusted to 212, down from the original 230, due to some servers being retired and others requiring further clarification from the IT support teams. The migration work is scheduled to take place over three days, from May 5th to May 7th.\\n\\nAdditionally, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that the UK project is on track. The team will focus on testing and development environments from mid-May through mid-June, with the final production rollout scheduled to run from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Update on server migration plans and upcoming project timelines.", "action_items": ["Contact the 23 IT support staff members who have not yet responded to confirm their server details."], "key_decisions": ["Reduced the number of servers in the current migration phase to 212.", "Confirmed the migration schedule for early May.", "Confirmed the timeline for the UK project through the end of July."]}	2026-05-09 13:08:01.193954+00	\N
