cc99813f-00a4-4f9e-8c4e-095646fead41	f97b02c9-d5f5-485e-8a63-983c815bd937	Production feature governance	["Architectural decision making", "Customer communication"]	\N	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Jens Feind has flagged an inquiry from Nitesh and Srinath regarding the formal governance policy for utilizing DevPreview or Upstream features, specifically citing the 'MTV-wait-hook', within production environments. The current architectural stance requires a joint decision between HSBC and Red Hat.\\n\\nJens Feind is seeking clarification on whether this topic is currently under active deliberation or if a formal consensus has already been reached, as the customer is requesting a written conclusion to validate the supportability of these features in production.", "headline": "Governance requirements for deploying DevPreview and Upstream features in production environments.", "action_items": ["Clarify current status of governance discussions regarding DevPreview/Upstream features with the customer.", "Provide a written conclusion to Nitesh and Srinath regarding production usage of non-GA features."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Jens Feind has raised a concern regarding a request from the customer's team (Nitesh and Srinath) about using experimental or early-access software features in their live production system. This requires a formal agreement between our company and the customer to ensure it meets project standards.\\n\\nJens Feind is asking if this has already been discussed or decided, as the customer is waiting for a formal written confirmation before proceeding.", "headline": "Clarification needed on using experimental software features in the customer's live environment.", "action_items": ["Determine if a decision has been made regarding the use of experimental features.", "Draft a written response for the customer confirming the governance policy."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:17:09.440089+00	\N
fe437153-9b1f-4b89-a6ee-3586832fc6c9	2f5b4afc-4f5b-45d5-ba2d-5632e2572e25	Migration project status update	["Resource constraints", "Risk management"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reports that the migration project is currently on track for Pilot Phase 2, with planning activities currently underway. \\n\\nHowever, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia identified a resource constraint regarding ITSO availability. Due to a competing high-priority program, dedicated resources are being diverted, necessitating an update to the project's RAID (Risks, Assumptions, Issues, Dependencies) log to reflect this impact on project velocity and delivery timelines.", "headline": "Pilot Phase 2 remains on schedule despite emerging resource contention risks.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to update the RAID log regarding ITSO resource availability constraints."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that the second phase of the migration pilot is moving forward as planned. \\n\\nPatricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that a new, higher-priority project is now competing for the attention of the IT support staff. To manage this, she is documenting this potential bottleneck in the project's risk tracker to ensure leadership is aware of the impact on team capacity.", "headline": "Migration project is on schedule, but staff availability poses a new risk.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia to document the staffing conflict in the project risk tracker."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:17:13.127611+00	\N
2d018f21-9b33-456f-95a0-7917292f26da	8436f3bd-42e4-4363-9578-fbfea6b33909	Infrastructure and Remote Access	["KMS integration", "etcd security", "remote worker testing"]	\N	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli initiated a discussion regarding the implementation of encrypted etcd, questioning the security efficacy of local key storage. He is investigating Kubernetes native support for KMS-based key management to mitigate risks associated with co-located key and database files, noting a lack of documentation on current implementation status.\\n\\nAdditionally, Raffaele Spazzoli confirmed that all blockers for remote worker testing have been resolved. Testing is scheduled to resume on Monday with high priority, requiring dedicated focus from the assigned personnel.", "headline": "Evaluation of etcd encryption at rest via KMS and resumption of remote worker testing.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli to investigate Kubernetes KMS integration for etcd encryption.", "James Force to prioritize and execute remote worker testing starting Monday."], "key_decisions": ["Remote worker testing will resume on Monday with high priority."]}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli raised concerns about the current method of securing the system's database, noting that storing security keys on the same drive as the data is not ideal. He is looking into modern, more secure ways to manage these keys using external services to better protect sensitive information.\\n\\nOn the operational side, Raffaele Spazzoli announced that all previous issues preventing remote worker testing have been cleared. Testing is set to restart this coming Monday, and he has requested that James Force dedicate his full attention to this high-priority task.", "headline": "Security review of database encryption and restart of remote access testing.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli to research improved security methods for database encryption.", "James Force to lead the remote worker testing effort starting Monday."], "key_decisions": ["Remote worker testing is scheduled to resume this Monday."]}	2026-05-09 13:17:22.786806+00	\N
7af4ccf3-f95c-43b7-bbe1-63a7d95a7179	ba83853c-24e7-46a0-9ea0-1097a3a138bb	Architecture documentation completion	["Technical documentation", "Project tracking"]	\N	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has mandated the completion of several critical architecture documentation workstreams within a two-week timeframe. The scope includes the compute design for non-HIC, security documentation, data architecture (specifically labels and annotations), and the Tertiary Vault configuration.\\n\\nKey dependencies involve cross-team reviews and implementation verification. Specifically, Shebi is tasked with validating data architecture labels against current VM migration status, while Rydekull is responsible for filtering security docs and populating the Tertiary Vault documentation based on existing internal resources.", "headline": "Urgent two-week deadline set for completion of outstanding architecture documentation.", "action_items": ["Michele, Raffaele, and Janine: Complete compute design for non-HIC.", "Rydekull: Review, lean, and filter security documentation.", "Shebi: Review and approve data architecture (labels/annotations) and verify implementation on migrated VMs.", "Rydekull: Populate Tertiary Vault documentation."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has requested that the team prioritize and finish several key project documents over the next two weeks to improve our delivery standards. The focus is on finalizing designs for computing, security, data organization, and the Tertiary Vault system.\\n\\nSeveral team members have been assigned specific sections to write or review. This includes ensuring that data labeling guidelines are actually being applied to the virtual machines currently being moved to the new system, and confirming that security and vault documents are updated and ready for use.", "headline": "Team must finalize project architecture documentation within the next two weeks.", "action_items": ["Michele, Raffaele, and Janine: Finish the computing design document.", "Rydekull: Update and refine the security documentation.", "Shebi: Review data organization plans and check that they are being used on current virtual machines.", "Rydekull: Create the documentation for the Tertiary Vault."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-09 13:17:27.516368+00	\N
