89f4c962-d5d0-4d98-a48c-367773498fe1	6f61d945-422e-4e7b-9e63-a3d21f2c8b3a	Nexus repository mirroring discussion	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_JAMES_F3856179 initiated a discussion on setting up Nexus repository mirrors from the UK instance (nexus3.uk) to multiple endpoints, including those in Hong Kong and by Shwetali et al., with environment substitution for each cluster's endpoint.", "headline": "Nexus repository mirroring setup for UK to HK clusters discussed", "action_items": ["Prerana will draft a pull request (PR), as per U_JAMES_F3856179, to implement the proposed repository mirroring setup using environment substitution for Nexus endpoints.", "The team needs to add Helm variables and modify Helm charts accordingly."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_JAMES_F3856179 brought up the idea of creating Nexus repository mirrors from their main instance located in the United Kingdom to clusters that are based elsewhere, including one proposed by Shwetali et al. This setup would use environment substitution for specifying which NeXUS endpoint a cluster should pull data from.", "headline": "Team discusses setting up a backup UK-based NeXUS repository mirror in Hong Kong", "action_items": ["Prerana is tasked with creating and submitting the necessary changes as PR to implement this repository mirroring strategy using Helm charts, following U_JAMES_F3856179's proposal.", "The team acknowledges that they need additional variables in their Helm configurations."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 02:11:30.66494+00	\N
043d7d45-59a9-44c1-bf31-2618b28e0e75	362cd99a-3756-49e0-bade-a8edaa000067	Database VM Performance Test Discussion	["VM Migration/Automation", "Testing"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The engineering team, including Sudhir (VM Migration/Automation), Devdatt (Testing), Alex, Shebi, U_JENS_9E9831E8, gathered to analyze performance gaps in RHEL 8.10 VMs running Oracle DB on Vsphere clusters within the Lab and at site #104.", "headline": "Database VM Performance Test Discussion with HSBC and Engineering Team", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Set up the Lab\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"Alex\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Create two VMs on Vsphere and 104, configure them to use DELL storage arrays as primary DB provider.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Synthetic data setup\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Implement synthetic data generation tool and ensure visibility of test results within the team.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Performance tuning on OCP VM\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"Devdatt\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Adjust performance settings to measure, analyze, and mitigate identified gaps between Lab and 104 environments.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Proceed with Testcase 1 setup: Create a lab environment mirroring production, ensuring both are using DELL storage arrays for consistency in performance testing."]}	{"body": "The team discussed the performance differences in Oracle DB running on RHEL VMs across two locations. Sudhir, Devdatt, Alex and Shebi from engineering joined with HSBC representatives to understand why some virtual machines are slower than others.", "headline": "Database VM Performance Test Discussion", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Create similar VMs\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"Alex\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Set up two virtual machines, one on Vsphere and another at site #104 to mirror production as closely as possible.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Use the same storage for both environments\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"Devdatt\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Ensure that DELL is used consistently across all VMs in different locations, which will be our main DB provider's hardware.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Generate and use synthetic data\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Use a tool to create test data that will help in measuring the performance of our VMs.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Tune and optimize DB on OCP\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"Devdatt\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Make adjustments to improve database speed, aiming to close any identified gaps between environments.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Plan Testcase 1: Set up a test environment in the lab that closely matches production for accurate performance testing."]}	2026-05-26 03:16:24.415499+00	\N
7f9d0798-211d-4caf-b98a-d04f9e3b2077	89423714-415e-4027-b5fb-0a258947bcf1	Migration Status and Rollbacks Discussion	["XFS File System Corruption", "Cgroup / Sysroot Filesystem Mounts Issues", "Fix-Forwards Resolution"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The engineering team, led by Arpit Tolani (U_SEBAST_AC383055), reported a largely positive outcome from the day's migrations. A total of 113 virtual machines were processed with an approximate success rate of 89%, including those remediated via Fix-Forward/Retry mechanisms, as noted in Bundle 1C which had zero rollbacks.", "headline": "Engineering team reports successful VM migration with minor rollbacks and ongoing issues.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Investigate and resolve XFS File System Corruption on source VMs before migration\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Red Hat Support\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Address Cgroup / Sysroot Filesystem Mounts issues in Bundle 1B, specifically related to LUKS encrypted filesystem.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Follow provided instructions for requesting internet access on VDI and Bank Laptop if allowed by the business unit\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Arpit Tolani\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The engineering group, including Arpit Tolani (U_SEBAST_AC383055), had a mostly successful day with 113 virtual machines moved. However, they encountered problems leading them to revert changes in about 9% of the cases - this includes issues related to file system corruption and encrypted filesystem mounts.", "headline": "Engineering team successfully migrated most VMs but faced some issues that led to rollbacks.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Resolve XFS File System Corruption on source VMs before migration\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Address Cgroup / Sysroot Filesystem Mounts issues in Bundle 1B, specifically related to LUKS encrypted filesystem.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Request internet access on VDI and Bank Laptop if allowed by the business unit\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Arpit Tolani\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:37:33.745749+00	\N
ac76293d-c10a-46dc-8a20-6f98fcf9a51f	3251777b-6fec-45ae-ba8d-f73732bd2ac1	XFS Corruption Root Cause Analysis and Testing Strategies	["Engineering Kernel Mismatch Issue"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The Engineering team, led by U_SEBAST_AC383055, is addressing a series of failures caused by an XFS filesystem corruption during the conversion process from RHEL 7 to RHEL 10. The root cause appears to be linked with kernel mismatches between source VMs and target appliance environment wherein on-disk format repairs are hindered due to read-only mounting of filesystems.", "headline": "Investigating XFS Corruption due to Kernel Mismatch in RHEL Conversion", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Upload customized virt-v2v image to Nexus for Forklift integration\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@U_SEBAST_AC383055\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Option A: Utilize a modified virt-v2v image that excludes the XFS repair step."]}	{"body": "The Engineering team, including U_SEBAST_AC383055 and Philip Jones, is trying to fix errors with the file system during an upgrade from one version of Red Hat Linux (RHEL) to another. They found that a mismatch between kernels in their testing VMs and conversion appliance caused these issues because they couldn't make changes needed for repair while converting.", "headline": "Fixing XFS File System Errors in RHEL Upgrade Process Discussed", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Option A: Use an image without the XFS file system fix step."]}	2026-05-26 04:21:16.943692+00	\N
