632779ba-58c0-49a5-a594-4d472286dfc4	215173c3-3fba-4973-93d5-3eedecbd5d93	Bulk VM migration testing	["Infrastructure migration", "System performance testing", "Compliance and configuration"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	1	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_JENS_9E9831E8 reports that the first iteration of bulk migrations has been completed, but only around 60 out of promised available VMs are ready for use due to compliance-related deletions. The migration is executed using MIO-X with a focus on realism and includes cold direct migration scenarios as test cases since storage offloading isn't currently supported in the tool.", "headline": "Bulk VM migration testing progress with infrastructure and performance considerations", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Restore the 128 deleted VMs as soon as possible to meet promised availability\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"unknown internal team responsible for compliance issues resolution\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Implement storage offload feature in MIO-X with coordination from Abhishek, after resolving the identified configuration issue on VMware\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Abhishek and Srinath's team for testing environment setup\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Share official Confluence page detailing bulk migration test results with Red Hat Teams channel participants\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8 and Srinath's team for documentation sharing\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Continue working with available VMs while awaiting restoration of deleted ones", "Implement MIO-X for a more realistic testing environment"]}	{"body": "U_JENS_9E9831E8 informs the team that although they started migrating some virtual machines (VMs), only about 60 are ready due to internal rules removing others. They're using a tool called MIO-X for testing, which mimics real migration scenarios as closely as possible.", "headline": "Progress update on bulk VM migration testing with a focus on performance, compliance, and infrastructure", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Get back the 128 removed VMs quickly, as they were taken down due to internal compliance issues. The responsible team is not specified.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Fix a configuration issue on VMware that caused some migrations to fail and ensure it doesn't happen again in production or testing environments, as identified by Srinath\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Srinath\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Share detailed migration test results with the Red Hat Teams channel for broader team awareness.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8 and Srinath's team\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Work with the VMs that are currently available", "Use MIO-X and adapt it to simulate actual migrations more accurately"]}	2026-05-25 14:44:40.322769+00	\N
a41bff5e-1078-44ea-8bc7-232f78338537	8fc01cfd-3cb3-4203-8893-1716391c67d7	HIC Design Workshop documentation	["Knowledge management", "Design collaboration"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_SEBAST_AC383055 initiated the request in Sheffield, emphasizing the importance of capturing all details from their recent workshops. The suggestion was to compile these into an extensive document on Google Docs for structured knowledge management and design collaboration within the Engineering team.", "headline": "Request for comprehensive documentation of HIC Design Workshop notes with visual aids.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Compile all HIC Design Workshop notes with visual aids\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\",\\"reference\\":\\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_SEBAST_AC383055 asked the team in Sheffield for all workshop information, including any visuals or diagrams. The goal is to have this compiled into one big Google Doc so everyone involved can easily access and contribute to it later on.", "headline": "Request to create a detailed document of HIC Design Workshop notes.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Compile all HIC Design Workshop notes with visual aids\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\",\\"reference\\":\\"\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 18:00:58.352256+00	\N
45fd0a04-73c3-4859-ad7e-d1c217fd7b3a	bc7ac5c9-2d47-4244-ad91-9d114134f9bb	Migration support and hypercare	["ITIL process compliance", "SLA management", "RCA documentation"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Engineer U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB initiated a critical discussion on the Migration Support and Hypercare Thread, emphasizing adherence to predefined Bank processes following ITIL standards. The thread highlights that within 15 minutes of VM migration initiation, decisions must be made regarding continuation or rollback due to Service Level Agreements (SLAs). U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB suggests segregating Root Cause Analysis documentation for each proposed idea into a separate section. The thread also references an ongoing Google Document where all ideas are consolidated, accessible via the provided link.", "headline": "Urgent thread for migration support proposal with ITIL compliance and SLA considerations.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB started a thread to gather ideas for migrating VMs in line with the bank's existing processes, which follow industry-standard guidel092651347. The team must decide quickly (within 15 minutes) whether migration is successful or if they need to roll back due to strict SLA rules.", "headline": "Discussion about urgent migration proposal with ITIL and SLA constraints.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 14:55:33.849449+00	\N
52271698-3c9a-4089-b4df-10e35566d394	7029f740-3d03-4587-a954-a40d0b77373d	DC Migration Process Integration	["VM Migration Tool Harmonization"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E discussed the necessity to align our virtual machine (VM) migration tool automation processes within a broader data center (DC) migration context. The team is aware that there's an existing DC migration program and synchronizing with it could provide clarity on its methodology, which may involve network device configurations at the systemic level by external parties.", "headline": "Integration of DC Migration with VM Migration Tool Harmonization", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Understand DC Migration Program's Process\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Shebi\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E brought up the need to understand how our virtual machine migration fits into a larger data center move. They learned there's already an ongoing DC migration, but details are unclear at this point.", "headline": "Aligning VM and Data Center Migrations for Better Integration", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Meet with DC Migration Program Team\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Shebi\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 15:04:29.215473+00	\N
06783864-3813-4e6a-8f50-fe5fbc946591	6598f042-3ad9-4a7c-a225-6d9b13769770	VirtIO-Win Driver Issue	[]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The Engineering team led by @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E has identified that the installation of MTV2.11.4-2 appears to mitigate most BSOD occurrences related to VirtIO drivers in their environment, which is a significant improvement from previous versions. The discussion highlights an urgent need for upgrading to 1.9.57 due to its enhanced stability and performance benefits.", "headline": "MTV2.11.4-2 resolves BSOD issues with VirtIO-Win drivers, prompting a request for an upgrade to version 1.9.57.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Evaluate compatibility of MTV2.11.4-2 with existing systems\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Engineering Team\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Upgrade the team's system using MTV2.11.4-2"]}	{"body": "The Engineering department is excited about a new update (MTV2.11.4-2) that seems to fix many of the Blue Screen Of Death issues they've been having with their virtualization software by using updated VirtIO driver versions. The team believes upgrading from this version will further improve stability and performance, which is crucial for smooth operations.", "headline": "MTV version fixes BSOD problems, and the team wants to upgrade drivers for better performance.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Check if the new drivers work well with current systems\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Engineering Team\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Install MTV2.11.4-2"]}	2026-05-25 15:14:28.424902+00	\N
dffbcb7c-9df0-4940-8c11-5d45a4ba23d7	999809b8-7371-4efe-a9f7-89652aed8398	TCs Submission	[]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_ROSALI_5BB9C3D4 initiated the thread to kickstart the Technology Component (TC) submissions. The discussion revolved around ensuring that all engineering teams are aligned with the project's architectural requirements and standards before proceeding.", "headline": "[TCs Submission] Initiating TC submission process", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_ROSALI_5BB9C3D4 started a conversation about the Technology Component (TC) submission for an engineering project. The team discussed making sure everyone understands what's expected before they submit their parts.", "headline": "[TCs Submission] Starting TC submissions", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 15:12:59.344258+00	\N
05f180cc-f272-4646-b0cf-1d0034498e56	195b1177-70c5-4953-8fef-bb6ae753c247	Storage Migration Issue	["Engineering Workload", "Customer Service Request"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "Roy from engineering is aware of the storage migration issue involving offloading between HPE and Dell vendors. The process should be interoperable, but it's currently failing.", "headline": "HPE to Dell Storage Migration Offload Issue", "action_items": ["Janine to take over this project before U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E goes on PTO."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E is facing an issue with moving data from HPE to Dell storage. Roy, who works in engineering, knows about it but hasn't responded quickly because he was on vacation.", "headline": "Storing Data Migration Problem", "action_items": ["Janine should handle this before U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E goes on leave."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 15:27:36.767699+00	\N
9503f674-b224-4362-91ef-33cc1e72e780	f406aa46-e1d2-4c70-b872-39234e1d7792	Bulk Migration Testing	["Infrastructure Performance", "Migration Strategy", "Capacity Planning"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	1	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Magnus confirmed a latency of around 400ms for the Bulk Migration using Ansible Automation Platform (AAP) is acceptable, thus no immediate architectural changes are required. The team has increased UK database CPU capacity to 18 and applied Red Hat’s fine-tuning recommendations as part of infrastructure performance enhancements.", "headline": "Bulk Migration Testing with AAP: Performance and Strategy Updates", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["No AAP platform architecture change needed due to acceptable latency", "Increase in UK database CPU set at 18"]}	{"body": "The team has decided that a migration time of between 45 minutes to an hour and fifteen minutes is acceptable. They plan to do most migrations by moving data over the network (storage offloading) but will also move some VMs directly from one server to another when they're not in use (cold migration). Nitesh and Abhishek are going to test these methods next, using UK equipment because their usual lab is still being built. They need to find out how much of the system’s resources—like CPU power, memory space, and hard drive storage—are used during migrations for Linux or Windows systems.", "headline": "Bulk Migration Testing: Performance and Planning Updates", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Migration time acceptable between 45 minutes - an hour and fifteen minutes", "80% of VM migration via storage offloading"]}	2026-05-25 15:37:37.545095+00	\N
734611c6-32d1-4713-b63e-3fb1056a2b19	3951b76b-ec38-4c80-bb30-706ecdf9315d	Data Architecture and Infrastructure	["High Availability Strategy", "Cluster Troubleshooting", "System Maintenance"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "In a detailed discussion on data architecture, Gareth & Michele presented an aspirational design to model physical failure domains using affinity/anti-affinity rules within the context of high availability. The strategy involved labeling nodes and VMs with three critical dimensions: Country, Data Center, and Fabric - a process facilitated by Unicorn as the primary system of record across various journeys including cluster build (GitOps), VM migration (MIOX), and new VM provisioning (Ansible/ITSP). However, Rushi highlighted that this approach is highly aspirational for day-to-day operations due to operational realities. In the event of an outage, there's a bottleneck as VM admins prioritize immediate service restoration over debugging complex affinity rules imposed by application owners.", "headline": "Exploring High Availability Strategies and Troubleshooting in OpenShift", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Gareth & Michele discussed a plan to ensure high availability of services by using affinity/anti-affinity rules within their data architecture. They proposed labeling different aspects like country, location, or network segments on servers (nodes) and virtual machines (VMs). This would help in keeping critical applications running even if some parts fail. However, Rushi pointed out that this plan might be too complex for the team to manage every day because when something goes wrong quickly with a service, they need to fix it fast without worrying about these detailed rules.", "headline": "Discussing High Availability and Troubleshooting in OpenShift", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 15:47:38.628196+00	\N
b7133fad-5f50-4c0a-ac39-ff70b53b7101	6fe29a5e-fa91-441e-805c-b6bf2d086e67	Infrastructure and Cluster Operations	["Security Compliance", "Storage Troubleshooting", "GitOps Strategy"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "James reported troubleshooting pure Kubernetes-related issues to their root cause. He collaborated with Suhas and Sourav regarding the remaining custom compliance operator rules not derived from CIS or HSBC AI benchmarks but instead invented by HSBC for specific use cases.", "headline": "Progress on infrastructure issues and GitOps strategy, with discussions around security compliance operators.", "action_items": ["James and his colleagues will continue working together towards finalizing the implementation of remaining operator rules."], "key_decisions": ["The team is close to wrapping up work on implementing additional security measures in their Kubernetes setup, with a focus on custom compliance operators."]}	{"body": "James has been troubleshooting some problems with their infrastructure. He's worked closely with Suhas and Sourav to finalize a set of unique operator rules that are specific to the company’s needs rather than widely used benchmarks. They believe they have almost finished this part of work.", "headline": "James and team working on Kubernetes issues, custom compliance rules for security.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["James, along with his teammates, is nearing completion on their custom compliance rule implementation for Kubernetes."]}	2026-05-25 15:57:39.618463+00	\N
2a396af4-ff74-44d4-aea2-abe8f24f1331	984fa56e-8e77-4cd6-961c-4f651d4e55d9	Node drain failure	["Live migration issues", "VM management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "During the Engineering workstream discussion, Balamurugan highlighted an issue where draining nodes is taking a significant amount of time. This prolongation has led to live migrations failing because they cannot complete in time before node failure occurs.", "headline": "Node drain delay causing VM migration failures", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Balamurugan and others in the Engineering team are dealing with a problem where nodes take too long to drain, which is leading to virtual machines (VMs) failing during live migration. This issue persists even when storage speeds aren't causing delays.", "headline": "Drain delay causing VMs not able to move", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 16:07:41.894519+00	\N
fa39744d-7495-4e7f-b2d1-10c5774d7f59	6261ab7e-528c-4be3-aa6d-a655da1a7990	VM Migration Proposal	["Engineering", "Testing"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_JENS_9E9831E8 has initiated a proposal for testing the impact of installing 'qemu-guest-agent' on Windows virtual machines (VMs) as part of an upcoming migration. The installation is seen by Srinath, from Ansell Engineering, to be potentially problematic if performed before VM migration due to rollback concerns.", "headline": "Proposal to test VM migration with and without qemu-guest-agent pre-hook.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Write a proposal\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_JENS_9E9831E8 has brought up the idea of testing if installing a tool called 'qemu-guest-agent' on Windows virtual machines before migration helps reduce reboots. Srinath, who is part of Ansell Engineering team working with U_JENS_9E9831E8, worries that doing this might cause issues during rollbacks.", "headline": "Testing VM Migration with Pre-hook Installation.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Write a proposal\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_JENS_9E9831E8\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 05:48:11.770623+00	\N
1848fbcc-6325-460c-a61b-deac75d7bc4e	0cc0a65d-b706-4ca8-be41-ffc708bbcfb2	ACM secret propagation optimization	["GitOps", "ArgoCD configuration", "Secret management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "In a Slack conversation, @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E brought to attention the current state of secrets being managed within GitOps practices for AcmeCorp's applications. It was observed that only certificates and GitHub credentials are propagated at present.", "headline": "Optimization of ACM secret propagation and ArgoCD configuration discussed.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Develop and propose an optimization mechanism for AcmeCorp's secret propagation.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["To optimize secret management, a method will be developed based on existing mechanisms to prevent ArgoCD from auto-syncing ACM secrets after initial seed."]}	{"body": "James Force, an engineer at AcmeCorp, mentioned in a Slack conversation that the team currently only shares certificates and GitHub credentials with others using GitOps practices. He suggested finding ways to improve this by having ArgoCD pull its own secrets after starting from seed information.", "headline": "Team discusses improving how secrets are shared and managed for AcmeCorp's applications.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Find a way to optimize secret sharing in GitOps practices for AcmeCorp's applications, specifically by having ArgoCD pull its own secrets after starting from seed information.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\"}"], "key_decisions": [""]}	2026-05-25 16:27:50.819364+00	\N
