d9a08b93-9adf-4c9e-b6cc-e9094f277fca	90594646-d6f2-4bf6-9808-0b72679f0916	Kubernetes network security	["API access control", "Infrastructure configuration"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 initiated the conversation by highlighting a critical issue with their internal setup lacking firewalls. This gap in traditional firewall protection has led to concerns about unauthorized communication between nodes and Kubernetes API, which could pose significant security risks within an Engineering workstream.", "headline": "Discussion on enhancing Kubernetes network security, focusing on API access control and infrastructure configuration.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 brought up that their team is facing security issues because they don't have firewalls set up in their network. This means anyone could potentially talk to parts of their Kubernetes setup, which isn't safe or secure.", "headline": "Conversation about improving network safety for a project using Kubernetes and needing to control who can access the system's nodes and API.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 19:08:01.12289+00	\N
