a7348959-497c-4ef0-920c-0df7d00ffae1	a114ed56-e892-4a3a-b4d2-77a567820a89	Migration Errors Summary Creation	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In an effort to streamline the resolution of migration-related issues, U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB has established a centralized repository for logging all identified bugs within their engineering team. This Google Sheets document is accessible at https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/, with a shared edit permission set for the engineering team members (U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB included). The spreadsheet is designed to categorize errors, identify responsible parties for assessment and resolution, as well as pinpoint where each solution should be implemented. U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB invites the team members to contribute by adding new findings or revising existing entries.", "headline": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB creates a shared spreadsheet to track migration errors and assign responsibilities.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Sam Marland, an engineer at the company, has created a Google Sheets document where they can keep everyone updated on any issues that come up during their software's migration. This way, if someone finds something wrong with how things are working after moving to new systems or platforms, it will be recorded in one place for easy access and reference by all team members involved. Sam has shared this spreadsheet so anyone who works closely with the project can add information about what went wrong (if anything), who should take a look at fixing these issues, and where exactly they need work done to make sure everything is running smoothly again.", "headline": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB creates a shared spreadsheet to track migration errors and assign responsibilities.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 22:23:11.876523+00	\N
c53e5bf5-1e0c-4754-b57c-daf41fb45d9c	5a304454-4c79-4815-88a7-51a9f639ce24	Platform Engineering and Operations	["Migration Planning", "Compliance and Security", "Workflow Documentation"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "In a Slack thread among @U_PLEASE_8E4FCE90 (unknown), @U_TC_ACAFE313 (unknown), @U_TIME_3519BFBB, and @U_PATRIC_460B8EAB (unknown), several critical issues were raised. The team discussed the failure of a workaround for VIB in HSBC's migration plan which affects 18 VMs as per Nitesh from yesterday's build call.", "headline": "Discussion on platform tasks, compliance and security concerns for HSBC's migration plan.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to provide an update on the Gitops workflow documentation for remote workers and discuss use cases with Shwetali and Prerana."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The team had a discussion on various topics related to HSBC's platform engineering. They talked about the failed workaround for VIB that impacted several VMs in their plan. There was also talk of Red Hat possibly offering Quay as an SaaS option, and concerns were raised regarding CIS compliance with new OCP checks.", "headline": "Team conversation about migration issues, compliance problems, and work progress.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to update on the Gitops workflow documentation progress."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 22:33:13.27633+00	\N
e2dcd95f-9a77-4d52-b5b2-85530a366350	fee31afb-88af-4f38-8f37-16ba5a1871dd	Infrastructure and Capacity Planning	["Network Architecture", "SRE Operations"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "The conversation among the participants revolves around Mexico's readiness to participate in an unspecified IT-related international collaboration. The discussion highlighted that while there is consensus on following global guidelines for setting up a Demilitarized Zone (DMZ), concerns were raised about capacity and infrastructure alignment, particularly regarding the initial purchases of new kits which did not account for capability fragmentation introduced by DMZ architecture with respect to [customer|utility|non-prod\\\\extranet]x[edmx|idmz]. The misalignment across regions was acknowledged. Philip Jones noted that all clusters, including production (prod), have been inadvertently set up for a tech preview which includes OCP virt and virtio video adapters - potentially impacting future support or upgrade plans.", "headline": "Mexico's participation in ITSO program and DMZ architecture issues", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Review and adjust the number of nodes for each cluster considering 14 clusters as a minimum requirement.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Philip Jones\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Adjustment based on initial purchases misalignment due to DMZ architecture.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Switch off tech preview settings from prod clusters and assess impacts before proceeding with upgrades or support.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Philip Jones\\",\\"detail\\":\\"To avoid future issues related to OCP virt and virtio video adapters in production environments.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Mexico will align with global DMZ guidelines", "Acknowledgment of capacity misalignment due to initial kit purchases"]}	{"body": "The team discussed Mexico joining an international group focused on technology. They found that while there is agreement to follow global standards for setting up a secure network zone (DMZ), they realized their initial equipment purchases didn't match the required capacity due to how these zones were designed, leading to fewer nodes than needed across all regions including production environments.", "headline": "Mexico's IT program participation, DMZ setup concerns, and cluster configuration", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Adjust the number of nodes in each cluster to meet minimum requirements.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"\\",\\"detail\\":\\"To ensure capacity meets DMZ standards.\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Ensure tech preview settings are not applied to production clusters before making any changes or upgrades.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Philip Jones\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Prevent potential issues with future support and upgrade plans in the production environment.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Mexico agrees with global DMZ standards", "Acknowledgment of need for more equipment purchases"]}	2026-05-25 22:53:18.612581+00	\N
3e2d692c-9571-48f6-8574-4e618f918af0	64b7df3d-1cb6-4c74-ad7f-2da5c3e693f0	New Case Alert - HSBC Holdings PLC	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga initiated a case alert for an issue identified within the production cluster of HSBC Holdings PLC, specifically referencing Khyati Tulo's report. The problem appears to be related to engineering concerns that require immediate attention.", "headline": "New Case Alert: HSBC Holdings PLC - Issues in Production Cluster", "action_items": ["Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga needs assistance with the case alert for HSBC Holdings PLC."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "A new issue has been reported by Khyati Tulo at a bank called HSBC. Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga, who is involved with this alert and the engineering team responsible for production clusters within banks like HSBC, needs help because he's going to Sheffield soon.", "headline": "New Case Alert: Problem in Banking Cluster", "action_items": ["Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga requires assistance from colleagues in handling this new case alert."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 07:09:58.090791+00	\N
d9b25cc2-8cd8-4b85-9cae-6b468f892504	fea5757a-f0c8-48c2-bf31-af84a8e9f29b	VIB installation failure investigation	["MTV2.11 migration issues", "Support case escalation"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB reported that the latest status of the VIB issue is not satisfactory. It appears MTV2.11 requires VIB 0.3.0 for installation but encounters failures, potentially due to concurrency problems in ESXs (see thread timestamped at '7777708400.000000'). The issue persists even with the latest VIB version and seems linked not only to VM configurations with numerous disks but possibly other scenarios as well.", "headline": "Investigating VIB installation and migration failures in ESXs, with a focus on concurrency issues.", "action_items": ["Identify all known failure cases for MTV2.11 migration", "Determine if concurrency is a contributing factor"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB brought up that there is an issue where a system called MTV2.11 can’t install or move because of problems with something named VIB 0.3.0, which seems to be needed for it but isn't working right now in some ESXs environments (these are servers). The problem might happen when too many things try to use the system at once. We also found out that this issue can occur even after updating to a newer version of VIB and not just with certain VM setups, which have lots of disks.", "headline": "Exploring issues with installing and migrating to the new VIB in ESXs, focusing on why it's not working.", "action_items": ["Find all different ways in which people are experiencing these issues", "Check if trying too many things at once is causing the problems"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 23:23:29.612769+00	\N
fdfe14e5-b9fe-4b7a-b3a0-d0f805d4ae01	8123db45-b9ba-4c61-99ac-288b5c2f6168	Gantt chart review	["Project scheduling", "Timeline management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.85	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "During the Gantt chart review call, U_CARINA_D5667D0C led a discussion with engineering team members to assess progress on critical path activities. The conversation focused on identifying potential bottlenecks in resource allocation and dependencies between tasks that could affect overall project delivery dates.", "headline": "Gantt chart review for Engineering project scheduling and timeline management.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Conduct a detailed risk assessment of identified critical path activities\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Engineering Team\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Review and optimize resource allocation to mitigate bottl0necks\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Project Scheduler U_CARINA_D5667D0C\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C, representing the engineering team in a recent call about our Gantt chart, discussed how to keep everything on track. They talked about making sure we're not waiting too long for things or running out of resources that could delay us from finishing by when they wanted.", "headline": "Gantt chart review for Engineering project scheduling and timeline management.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Do a thorough check to see where and why delays might happen\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Engineering Team\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Look closely at how we're using our resources so nothing gets held up or runs out too quickly\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Project Scheduler U_CARINA_D5667D0C\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 23:45:43.621318+00	\N
8d27cedc-7d60-4290-b8a2-6b59d117634d	fe75b1c7-b352-4d05-83e6-1299b45b576d	Unicorn IP update necessity	["VM re-IP change", "Project management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6, an engineer at Unicorn, highlighted the necessity of updating Unicorn when a virtual machine (VM) undergoes an internal network address or external public IP change. This is due to Unicorn's role as a central hub for information exchange with other tools that rely on its data sources like ODS.", "headline": "Unicorn IP update required for VM re-IP change", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6, an engineer at Unicorn, reminded the team that whenever a virtual machine's network settings change (its internal or public internet-facing address), it is essential to update our central system called 'Unicorn'. This helps with keeping all connected tools updated too. The changes can happen in any location like Hong Kong.", "headline": "Unicorn IP update needed when VM changes address", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 23:50:30.123764+00	\N
1bc8ab44-8a7d-4d97-b072-7b5ce833d6dc	e46f4c2f-a349-4a99-a74c-1ae9daeb753d	Migration Escalation and Coordination	["Engineering Support", "Project Timeline Alignment", "Automation Development"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_SEBAST_AC383055 reported that four migration-related cases were escalated to Engineering Support Services (ESS) today. These include RHEL-165220, MTV-5368, and two others with IDs 04408443 and 04432578 related to different issues but impacting the migration timeline due to discrepancies in disk geometry. A case (ACE escalation) was created for attention from engineering before next week's migration, emphasizing the need for clear documentation of project impacts and exact dependencies on these cases.", "headline": "Migration issues escalated, with a focus on timeline alignment and automation development.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Document project impact and exact dependencies in the support cases.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_SEBAST_AC383055\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Gather logs proactively for failing scenarios, request them directly in the case to familiarize customers with process\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Kathinka and Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Escalate four issues to ESS with a focus on timeline alignment", "Create an ACE escalation case before next week's migration"]}	{"body": "U_SEBAST_AC383055 brought up that there are four migration problems affecting the project's progress. These include a mix of integration and copy-offload issues with different cases linked to various system components like sun partition tables, Veritas storage, etc., which need fixing before migrating again next week.", "headline": "Migration issues escalated; timeline alignment needed, plus new automation for complex VM setups.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Explain to customers about the escalation process and how it affects them.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Kathinka and Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Escalate migration problems for urgent attention", "Create a case specifically aimed at gathering necessary information quickly"]}	2026-05-26 00:00:31.338415+00	\N
b0245ac6-fd27-47b5-9993-fee9efe4265e	3d5a8944-1ac8-4aee-b654-b2ab00cc4581	Client relationship and project updates	["Open source strategy", "Team culture"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.9	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "Vinay from engineering expressed his preference for working with Red Hat due to its transparency. The client is considering releasing the codebase of MIO-X once a non-disclosure agreement (NDA) expires in about three weeks, as they plan to share this project widely within ITSO.", "headline": "Discussion on NDA lifting and open-sourcing MIO-X, team culture via Spotify playlist.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Continue working with Red Hat due to its transparency", "Lift the NDA for MIO-X and consider open sourcing post expiration"]}	{"body": "Vinay, an engineer at the company, has been enjoying working closely with Red Hat and appreciates their open approach. The client is thinking about letting go of a legal agreement that currently keeps MIO-X confidential once it's no longer needed because they want to share this project widely within ITSO.", "headline": "Client plans on sharing project code after contract ends; team culture initiative with Spotify playlist.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Continue working with Red Hat due to its transparency", "Lift the NDA for MIO-X and consider open sourcing post expiration"]}	2026-05-26 00:40:08.460894+00	\N
