7338dd5d-9a5e-4363-bbdd-f4d74cb80539	a2cca23d-67c7-4543-93c1-7439cc4ab121	[Build Git Ops Strategy]	[]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The engineering team, led by @U_ROSEMA_0749D041, discussed the implementation of a Build-independent Continuous Deployment (GitOps) strategy. The conversation highlighted concerns about maintaining infrastructure as code principles and ensuring seamless integration with existing CI/CD pipelines.", "headline": "[Build Git Ops Strategy] - Engineering Discussion", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The engineering team, including @U_ROSEMA_0749D041, had a conversation about how to use version control for deploying applications. They talked about keeping the code that sets up their systems in sync with changes made and making sure it works well within their current workflows.", "headline": "[Build Git Ops Strategy] - Engineering Discussion", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 01:22:20.777965+00	\N
7edbb2df-2a77-4312-8565-8630299086ae	33e582ab-6be1-45a5-99a2-9e4853c6e420	Migration issues and VM patching post-migration	["Windows OS type identification"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "Arpit Tolani, a member of the Engineering workstream in Slack, initiated a discussion about migration failures. He asked for assistance to join an existing bridge conversation where he seeks resolutions for VIB issues as well as identifying patterns that might be causing XFS problems.", "headline": "Discussion on VM patching and Windows OS type identification post-migration.", "action_items": ["Arpit Tolani is working on an Ansible script to patch Windows VM video devices post-migration and seeks validation for the logic, particularly regarding OS type identification which should be in line 295 of `post_migration_run.yaml`."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Arpit Tolani, from the Engineering team, started a conversation about some problems encountered during migration. He's looking for help to join an existing group chat where there are talks around solving known VIB-related issues and finding patterns in XFS errors that may have occurred post-migration.", "headline": "Team discusses fixing migration issues and ensuring correct video drivers on Windows VMs after migrating.", "action_items": ["Arpit Tolani is creating a script to update the video device driver on Windows VMs after migration. He's also checking if there should be any changes in identifying different operating systems within this context."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:05:29.481862+00	\N
8e7d9e44-5838-4f32-bb37-400e613ef621	606e3f36-0ee7-4e4a-a712-b8b99852e031	Migration Test Case Discussion	["Network Configuration", "System Compatibility"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_ARPIT_8F539902 initiated a conversation regarding the migration of Multi Homing Virtual Machines (VMs) from vmware to Open Compute Project (OCP), focusing particularly on TC-13 & 14. The primary concern is ensuring that network interface names and IP addresses remain unchanged post-migration, which involves maintaining MAC address consistency across the migration process.", "headline": "Discussion on Migration Test Case for VMs and Network Configuration", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_ARPIT_8F539902 discussed a test case to ensure that migrating virtual machines (VMs) from one system, vmware, won't change the network settings like interface names and IP addresses. This is important because these VMs use specific MAC IDs for their connections in Windows boxes which are tied to adapter assignments with assigned IPs.", "headline": "Migration Test Case for VMs: Ensuring Network Stability", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:09:04.557744+00	\N
a4c97d36-6cf0-4ed2-ad3b-b8b82f9b6852	0ab7ab44-dbf4-4327-a8f0-a021221f3c48	MTV Upgrade and Migration Blockers Resolution	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In the recent meeting, U_SEBAST_AC383055 discussed a recap of today's session focused on resolving blockers encountered during our last cluster migrations and planning ahead with an update from MTV 2.11.6.", "headline": "MTV Upgrade and Migration Blockers Resolution: Plan for VIB upgrade to facilitate MTV migration", "action_items": ["Re-run failed migrations on VIB 3.0 hosts", "Upgrade impacted ESXi hosts to VIB 3.0 over the weekend"], "key_decisions": ["Immediate Retry: Re-run failed migration batches using VIB 3.0 hosts to validate fixes", "Weekend Upgrades: Escalate request for host upgrades from Abhishek, Dennis will handle the upgrade process"]}	{"body": "U_SEBAST_AC383055 shared an update about our plan to fix issues from past migrations before moving forward with updating all clusters. The team is working on fixing migration problems by re-running failed attempts using a newer version of VIB, which should already be installed in some hosts.", "headline": "MTV Upgrade and Migration Blockers Resolution: Next steps for a smoother upgrade process discussed in the meeting", "action_items": ["Run migration attempts again on some hosts with VIB 3.0 installed", "{\\"descriptions\\":\\"Dennis will upgrade certain ESXi servers to VIB 3.0 this weekend, after getting approval from Vinay\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Dennis\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Re-run the previous week's unsuccessful migrations to check if fixes work", "If successful, plan for an upgrade this coming weekend"]}	2026-05-26 02:31:29.897094+00	\N
35680495-59b2-47a3-b405-ee455e7da04e	c7affcc1-05e0-4cfc-a81e-9787ba70421c	Cross Cluster Live Migrations in Kubernetes	["Kubernetes Networking"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In a recent Slack thread, @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E brought up the latest findings regarding cilium's capabilities in handling cross cluster live migrations and its comparison with ovnk. The conversation included insights from Nikos and Sam Marland about potential networking challenges when using CILUM for Cross Cluster User Datagram Protocol (CUDN) and Network Service Extension Bridging (NSX). It was suggested that a deeper technical discussion on this topic would benefit the engineering team, specifically with input from network engineers. The consensus leaned towards involving @Brandon_Marlow to facilitate an in-depth conversation due to his expertise.", "headline": "Discussion on Cilium vs OVNK for Cross Cluster Live Migrations", "action_items": ["Invite Brandon Marlow for a technical discussion on CILUM and ovnk capabilities"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "A team member, @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E, shared concerns about the ability of cilium to move applications across different clusters effectively. They mentioned a newer technology called ovnk as an alternative and asked for input from network experts like Nikos and Sam Marland on this matter. The team discussed some networking issues that might arise with using these technologies in real-world scenarios, particularly when dealing with complex user data movement (CUDN) across clusters protected by NSX bridging.", "headline": "Comparing Technologies for Moving Applications Between Clusters", "action_items": ["Set up a meeting to discuss the pros and cons of cilium vs ovnk for cross cluster migrations"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:12:35.195667+00	\N
3415882e-94aa-4731-b9c1-d92ce4abda6e	892aa2a7-f975-49ac-82e3-98cf24abc811	Migration automation scaling issues and AAP box capacity planning	["VM pre-flight checks sequentiality", "Ansible playbook execution optimization"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The Engineering team, led by @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E, is working on scaling the number of virtual machines (VMs) migrated per day from one to 350 in each active data center. They are exploring ways for MIOX's migration plans involving multiple VMs and have identified sequential pre-flight checks using roles and blocks as a bottleneck, along with the post-flight process which also relies on similar mechanisms leading to slow playbook execution times when AAP is used. The team acknowledges that their current Automation Application Platform (AAP) can only handle 50/70 concurrent jobs at best and seeks solutions for this limitation.", "headline": "Scaling up VM migration automation while addressing sequential pre-flight and post-flight checks.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Configure AAP to handle more concurrent jobs\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Nikos\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Create a document addressing the identified issues.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Petros\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Investigate the feasibility of creating migration plans with multiple VMs."]}	{"body": "The Engineering team, including @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E, is working to scale up the number of virtual machines they migrate each day from one per host in an active data center. They're currently facing delays because every VM has to go through a series of checks before and after migration which takes time when done sequentially with their current tools.", "headline": "Improving VM migration speed and efficiency for increased daily volume", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Look into increasing AAP's ability to handle more jobs at once\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Nikos\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Write a document that outlines the problems and potential solutions.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Petros\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Investigate the feasibility of creating migration plans that include multiple virtual machines."]}	2026-05-26 03:19:39.354591+00	\N
474a3c3e-608f-44ba-a34a-ebe23b76e557	e6e5c5b4-a152-42cc-8e8a-869f9afc8654	VM Migration Workstream discussion for support cases related to RDM and VCS migrations.	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In a recent Slack thread, @U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB sought clarity on the current status of support cases pertinent to Veritas Clusters migration and other virtual machine (VM) migrations. The request was directed towards engineers like @jfeind, @Shebi, and @Petros with expertise in RDM (Release Delivery Management) and VCS (Virtual Customer Systems). These individuals are expected to provide insights during the upcoming VM Migration Workstream call scheduled for tomorrow. The discussion aims at understanding which cases need immediate attention post-migration completion, thereby assisting @U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB in prioritizing tasks effectively.", "headline": "Request for VM Migration Support Cases Prioritization", "action_items": ["@jfeind to provide insights on RDM and VCS migration support cases during the VM Migration Workstream call."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB, a member of the team involved in migrating Veritas clusters and other virtual machines (VMs), wanted to understand which support cases are critical after these migrations. They asked @jfeind, @Shebi, and @Petros for their input during an upcoming VM Migration Workstream meeting tomorrow. The goal is to prioritize tasks effectively once the most urgent ones have been resolved.", "headline": "Seeking Clarity on Prioritizing Support Cases for Cluster & VM Migrations", "action_items": ["@jfeind to provide insights on RDM and VCS migration support cases during the VM Migration Workstream call."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:23:06.612126+00	\N
543daec9-c49f-4576-9421-de701d05c282	b3ef66e3-e3c9-49b0-8b61-9935c300ac31	Day Cover Swap Confirmation	["Project Management Coordination", "Team Communication"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The engineering team is coordinating a day coverage exchange to accommodate the migration on Friday. U_CARINA, Shebi, and ATOLAI are confirmed participants in this change.", "headline": "Confirmation of day cover swap for Recharge Day", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Finalize the day coverage exchange logistics and notify all relevant stakeholders.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_CARINA\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Day cover swap for Recharge Day", "Confirmation of team members participating"]}	{"body": "The engineering team is working together to make sure everyone can take time off on the same day, which will be next Friday. U_CARINA asked if this was still okay with all involved parties.", "headline": "Team swap for Friday's migration", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["", ""]}	2026-05-26 03:29:12.790451+00	\N
c817d4f3-68fc-4146-99c1-f4461b1bb25e	676ca122-67ea-45d6-9a1a-6a1d4ae5558f	Migration issues and support actions	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB, a member of the Engineering workstream on Slack, reported issues encountered during software migrations. The thread indicates that common error patterns are being identified to streamline troubleshooting (triage). To facilitate immediate resolution and knowledge sharing among team members facing similar challenges, U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB has updated the Proactive Support case with Zoom links for each migration bundle. This approach aims at reducing downtime by providing direct access to expert guidance.", "headline": "Engineering team addresses migration errors with triage and support enhancements.", "action_items": ["{\\"responsible\\":\\"U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB\\",\\"task\\":\\"Continue identifying common errors and updating the Proactive Support case with Zoom links for each migration bundle.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Implement triage process", "Provide immediate support through live sessions"]}	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB from the Engineering department shared that they're working on fixing some errors found during a recent migration. They are currently sorting out these mistakes to understand them better, which is called 'triage'. To help solve problems faster and share solutions with others in similar situations, U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB has added links for live support sessions using Zoom on the Proactive Support case.", "headline": "Engineering team tackles software migration problems by finding patterns in issues.", "action_items": ["{\\"responsible\\":\\"U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB\\",\\"task\\":\\"Keep working on sorting errors and adding Zoom links for live support.\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Start a process to sort out migration issues", "Set up quick help options through video calls"]}	2026-05-26 03:33:54.096819+00	\N
561f2d53-9c3a-45a8-97ff-75446b108481	e698334d-462b-45a7-a34b-dfea6930ec64	HSBC onboarding new joiners	["team communication", "OTP and ID sharing"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C initiated the process of HSBC's engineering team members being onboarded. The conversation began by acknowledging that out-of-band communication channels, such as SMS for OTP delivery and secure document sharing platforms for ID dissemination, are in place to facilitate this sensitive information exchange.", "headline": "HSBC onboarding new joiners with OTP and ID sharing", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C informed the team that three of them had received their One-Time Passwords (OTPs) and IDs necessary for joining HSBC. These were shared via secure methods to ensure confidentiality, like text messages for OTP delivery and a safe way to share documents containing personal information.", "headline": "HSBC onboarding new joiners with OTP and ID sharing", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:41:54.879807+00	\N
f6e3e26b-feb8-4bc5-9d0c-efd2e24b6d8a	27becdec-71c1-41e4-88e9-1edbea1dda4e	Migration Strategy Discussion	["Time Zone Consideration", "Personal Assignment"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The engineering support for migrations has evolved into assigning specific individuals to manage each migration event. This approach is expected to enhance efficiency and experience by considering the global distribution of time zones among Red Hat team members. Arpit, Sebastian, and Jens have been allocated dedicated tasks based on their respective timezone availability at different times throughout the day in UK Time.", "headline": "Engineering team to adopt a 'person assigned to migration bundle' strategy with timezone optimization.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Adopt a 'person assigned to migration bundle' strategy", "Dedicate specific individuals for each time-sensitive task"]}	{"body": "The engineering support group has agreed to a new approach where each person is responsible for one migration task. This method should help everyone work better together and finish faster, especially since some members are in different time zones across the UK and India. Arpit will handle early morning tasks when it's still dark outside in London but daytime elsewhere; Sebastian takes on mid-morning duties while Jens is assigned to later afternoon responsibilities.", "headline": "Engineering team decides on personalized assignment of migrations tasks.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Personalized assignment of migration tasks"]}	2026-05-26 03:45:47.214645+00	\N
88f398fe-03c0-4d48-b50b-c0420e3e0f1a	a1c4951b-4400-4234-88cf-ce2d1cd6b471	storage cluster utilization in phase 2 design	["CSI topologies"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In the phase two design conversation, @U_JANINE_71F80BBD raised a question about best practices for integrating different types of storage into one cluster without stretching across multiple pods. The options discussed were to create either a single storage cluster with various arrays or employ CSI topologies while still determining the appropriate storage class at provision time, as facilitated by @rspazzol and others in the Engineering workstream.", "headline": "Discussion on optimal utilization of storage arrays in non-stretched cluster setup.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The team, including @U_JANINE_71F80BBD and others in the Engineering department of Phase Two Design project discussed how to use various kinds of storage together efficiently within one big group (or 'cluster') that doesn't stretch over multiple pods. They talked about two main ideas: either setting up a single cluster with different types of storages or using something called CSI topologies, which is another way for the system to manage where data goes.", "headline": "Exploring best practices for integrating different storage types into a single cluster setup without stretching across pods.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:49:26.389642+00	\N
b16638a2-f46c-4bbe-9ca3-1fdae746107f	bb6fd514-cac5-42db-bb89-45ae40dcb895	VM Migration Plan Discussion	["cilium vs ovnk"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The team discussed the migration of virtual machines (VMs) to three OCP clusters linked with Fabrics 111, 113, and 122. Raffaele Spazzoli mentioned that these are cluster IDs: Cluster-0 for 111 is [Clusters 301,302,303], Cluster-1 for 113 is [Clusters 311 and 312], and Cluster-4 for 122 is cluster ID 314. The migration plan includes meetings with engineering to discuss ovnk features in India involving BGP expertise, potentially implicating @Nikos's role as a participant.", "headline": "Discussion on VM Migration Plan and cilium vs ovnk", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The team is planning to move virtual machines (VMs) into three different Open Compute Project (OCP) cluster environments. These are linked with specific network fabrics, identified as 111, 113, and 122 for clusters numbered 301-303, 311-312, and 314 respectively. There's growing interest in ovnk (Open Virtual Network), a networking technology that could be used to connect these VMs across different data centers or geographic locations.", "headline": "Discussion on moving VMs to new clusters and comparing technologies", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 03:53:40.751122+00	\N
65f824fe-967c-4942-95cb-4de14b20b978	4f44fad3-e85d-4e63-810a-0b1149c0427a	Engineering testing of rawio solution with unisphere VM	["HSBC Testing"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In a recent Slack thread discussion involving U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E and other team members including Abhishek Wand Devdatt and Devdatt A. Patel (a.k.a devdatt), the Dell engineering team reported successful testing of rawio solutions integrated with unisphere VMs, as stated by U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E in a message timestamped at 7:57 PM UTC on March 16th (ts '7777712100.000000'). The Dell team expressed satisfaction with the outcomes, indicating readiness for broader deployment despite not being GA yet.", "headline": "Dell tests rawio solution with unisphere VM, HSBC to start testing", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Dell engineering satisfied with rawio solution testing", "HSBC to commence HSBC-specific testing"]}	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E shared a Slack message with team members Abhishek Wand Devdatt (also known as devdatt) and Devdatt A. Patel, indicating that the engineering team at Dell has successfully tested new software called rawio when used together with another tool named unisphere VM on their computers. The testing went well according to U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E's report sent out in a Slack thread timestamped March 16th, and now they are ready for the next phase of work.", "headline": "Successful test of new tool for banking, next steps planned by Dell and HSBC teams", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Dell engineering team is satisfied with testing results", "HSBC will start their own tests"]}	2026-05-26 03:57:17.872864+00	\N
601860df-cedb-4ceb-8fbd-c4e0e05bf6ac	44932932-f15c-4564-a7b0-9ea6b067e4a6	Migration Update Discussion	["Engineering Workflows", "Customer Feedback Integration"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "During the last Retro, U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB gathered data on migration failures as reported by the Customer Site Reliability Engineer (SRE) team. The aim was to understand and categorize errors using a consistent terminology adopted by customer's SRE for ease of statistical analysis.", "headline": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB summarizes migration failure reasons captured by customer's SRE team for statistical analysis.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "In a recent Retro, U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB talked about why some migrations didn't work out as planned. The Customer Site Reliability Engineer (SRE) team gave reasons for these failures which are now being looked at to see what types of errors happened most often.", "headline": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB discusses migration issues and plans to analyze them with the customer's SRE team.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 04:51:07.196447+00	\N
feb42d81-6a61-406c-af4e-4f033dfb3388	626c56c3-d2da-46ec-a986-b2dafcdc8fcd	Storage Migration Issue	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB reported a failure in migrations involving Dell as either the source or destination, with an error message indicating 'Copy Offload failed to add the ESX HBA UID. Source Pure Target DELL'. The specifics of whether Miox or MTV is involved were not confirmed by @U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB and further investigation into which side caused the issue was suggested.", "headline": "Dell storage migration failures due to HBA UID copy offload issues", "action_items": ["Determine if migrations are failing due to Miox or MTV. This requires technical analysis of migration logs."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "A user on the team, @U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB, has noticed that when trying to move data from or to Dell-based systems within our network, it's not working. They received an error message saying something about a 'Copy Offload failed', which is related to how we connect and transfer files between different types of storage devices.", "headline": "Dell storage transfer problems", "action_items": ["Identify the root cause of migration failures for Dell systems."], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 04:48:55.171202+00	\N
a44aec4f-50b9-4bdd-be2e-0fc1d9331915	3165e2cc-2af5-4873-95f8-30c693769bd4	Bug Report and Version Management Discussion	["Support Communication", "Version Control"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_GOOGLE_64E3F7FD initiated a conversation with @U_GOOGLE_64E3F7FD regarding the pvc / pv uid mismatch issue reported in https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04426565, seeking confirmation on which Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) version introduced this bug.", "headline": "Discussion on bug introduction and version rollback", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_GOOGLE_64E3F7FD is trying to find out which version of Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) introduced a bug causing mismatches between PVCs/PVs. This information will help decide whether reverting back to an earlier, stable version might be necessary until the issue can be fixed.", "headline": "Bug report and potential rollback discussion", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 04:54:43.509187+00	\N
573f780d-e88a-49ef-beb1-4f11a59cbb3a	f378b82b-830c-4d30-be0e-4c47111ca8bc	KDD Decisions and Cluster Strategy	["Engineering", "Cluster Management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "During today's KDD discussion led by @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E from the engineering workstream on Slack, several key decisions were made regarding cluster architecture. The consensus was to configure HIC clusters with 24 nodes for non-stretched scenarios and expandable up to 48 when stretching is required due to varying demands or resource constraints.", "headline": "KDD Decisions and Cluster Strategy: Engineering team discusses HIC clusters, namespace approach, node firewall operator.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["HIC clusters will be configured as either 24 or 48 nodes based on the need", "Continuation with two namespace approach for cluster management"]}	{"body": "The engineering group, led by @U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E on Slack today discussed the setup for their decision-making cluster (HIC). They decided that these clusters will have 24 or up to 48 nodes depending on how much work we expect them to handle. This way they can manage more if needed without stretching too thin.", "headline": "KDD Decisions and Cluster Strategy: Engineering team finalizes details about our clusters.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Clusters set at either 24 or expandable to 48 nodes", "Continuation with the two-namespace approach for cluster management"]}	2026-05-26 04:57:40.342589+00	\N
