7b56a64e-54fc-4e19-81f6-ef4dd5c2cfeb	8eaf5529-4f9e-4a37-8d63-9e73dd03b138	Migration Issues in Kubernetes Cluster	["Resource Management", "System Health"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_PHILIP_740C6823 reported an issue with a significant number of Persistent Volume Claims (PVC) being stuck in the 'Terminating' state, despite corresponding persistent volumes existing. This situation is causing disk space consumption and potential data loss concerns due to each PV consuming resources without releasing them back into the system.", "headline": "Investigating stuck PVC's and LOST PV states in Kubernetes cluster.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Investigate failed migrations leading to stuck 'Terminating' state of PVCs and LOST persistent volumes (PV).\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_PHILIP_740C6823\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "A team member, U_PHILIP_740C6823, noticed that a lot of persistent storage requests (volume claims) are not releasing the disk space they're using. This is causing problems because these unused spaces aren't being freed up and could lead to running out of room for new data.", "headline": "Kubernetes cluster experiencing issues with stuck volume claims and lost volumes.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Help investigate the cause behind persistent storage requests not releasing disk space, potentially leading to a 'Terminating' state without resolution and resulting in lost volume states. This issue needs immediate attention due to its impact on available resources.\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"U_PHILIP_740C6823\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 12:36:01.054441+00	\N
3225bf2b-d4d7-44c5-bab7-150f8d25828f	bef86497-7d4f-421e-b8ca-ccd7df3bd882	MTV Bug Escalation Request	["Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_SAM_F28235E5, a member of the Engineering team at Red Hat, has escalated an issue regarding orphaned storage resources after failed virtual machine (VM) migrations. The ticket is currently active with reference number #04426565 and marked as 'Escalation Pending'. U_SAM_F28235E5 seeks updates on the status of this bug, which has been acknowledged by Red Hat's support team.", "headline": "Escalated Bug MTV-5546: Orphaned Storage Resources Post VM Migration", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_SAM_F28235E5, a Red Hat employee working in the Engineering department, has brought up an issue where certain storage resources are left unused after attempts to move virtual machines (VMs) fail. This problem is causing concern and needs attention from higher-ups within the company as it's currently labeled 'Escalation Pending'. U_SAM_F28235E5 has requested an update on this matter.", "headline": "Escalated Bug MTV-5546: Orphaned Storage Resources After Failed VM Migrations", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 12:38:40.68844+00	\N
