b88cf3dd-09c3-4905-bf77-535c40a55ef3	39f5297d-ba21-4263-8b0c-5eb93398adc5	Automated Secret Management Strategy	["Engineering", "Infrastructure"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In a recent build standup call, @Philip Jones and the team discussed issues related to Automated Secret Management (ASM) in their engineering workflow. The main concern is that secrets are getting refresed unpredictably during new clusters' creation with AWS CloudFormation templates using ACM credentials for InfraEnv variables and ISO image generation, leading to frequent 'ISO not ready' errors.", "headline": "Discussing automated secret management strategy for cluster builds with unexpected ISO refreshes.", "action_items": ["Finalize an automated secret management strategy that includes pulling secrets from a centralized source like Vault for password rotation and replication downstream to managed clusters without disrupting the deployment flow."], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The team, including @U_SEBAST_AC383055 and others in the engineering department, are facing problems with their current method of creating new clusters. The Automated Secret Management system isn't working as expected because secrets keep getting updated without warning during ISO image generation for these builds.", "headline": "Team discusses need for a better secret management plan due to ISO image issues during cluster builds.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 11:52:42.532959+00	\N
56a09844-d970-41c5-bac5-896d23e7f711	9593e551-b537-4eca-b44f-e6ad21289da8	Engineering Update on POC Phase 2 Clusters	["POC Documentation Assistance"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "Philip Jones, representing the Engineering team in a Slack thread discussing Project Management Intelligence updates on 'Engineering Update on POC Phase 2 Clusters', confirmed that they will install an agent-based version for this iteration of the Proof of Concept (POC). The decision was made to build one ACM cluster and construct the second from it, aiming to mirror HSBC's majority cluster deployment process. Philip highlighted a need for additional information in POCDOC related to assisting with Agent-Control Module (ACM) installation.", "headline": "Confirmation of agent-based installation for POC phase 2 with ACM cluster build", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Provide info in POCDOC for assisting with ACM installation\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"Philip Jones, Engineering team member\\"}"], "key_decisions": ["Install agent-based version of the clusters", "Build one ACM cluster and construct second from it"]}	{"body": "In a recent Slack conversation among the engineering group, Philip Jones shared that for their upcoming project management update on 'POC Phase 2 Clusters', they'll be using an agent-based installation approach. This is different from before when all clusters were based on agents and will now involve creating one cluster with Agent Control Module (ACM) first to replicate how HSBC usually builds their own systems, which should give a clearer picture of the final product.", "headline": "Engineering confirms agent-based cluster setup and build process changes in POC phase 2", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["Switching installation approach from agent-based clusters", "Build process change for POC phase 2"]}	2026-05-26 08:08:27.172645+00	\N
fb4e0d39-ef76-4140-ab2b-ac3bb3d4f0eb	e449132b-113e-4ef6-9076-35223f0cb201	VM Triage Process Proposal	["Security Input Requested", "Linux VM Troubleshooting", "Windows VM Troubleshooting"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E proposed a triage process to handle failed migrations from the production environment. The idea involves moving the problematic virtual machine (VM) into a separate namespace using MTV and virtctl guestfs for OS manipulation, ensuring compatibility with the new environment by changing its IP address within an appropriate range and setting up root access via local account creation.", "headline": "Proposal for VM Triage Process in Case of Migration Failures", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Confirm VM start-up capability post triage\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Shebi\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Validate root account functionality within the local context of the new environment\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Janine\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Delete original migrated VM upon successful troubleshooting and resolution confirmation\\",\\"responsible\\":null}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E suggested a new plan to deal with virtual machines that can't migrate successfully. The idea is to move these VMs into a separate testing area, make sure they work there and then fix any issues before deciding if we should keep them or not.", "headline": "New Plan for Handling Failed Virtual Machine Migrations", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Make sure the new environment works for our problem VM\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Shebi\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Check if we can access and fix issues with root privileges in this separate area\\",\\"responsible\\":\\"@Janine\\"}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Decide whether to keep or delete the VM after fixing it, based on its performance in the new environment.\\",\\"responsible\\":null}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 12:43:32.942199+00	\N
43b9ccb3-290d-4ba5-9155-3bca4e269fda	930dbd62-8c70-4329-8f76-62784a9b6901	Migration Issues and Solutions Discussion	["VMWare Tooling Issue", "XFS Filesystem Issue", "VIB Version Upgrade Pressure", "LVM Related Failure"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "U_SAM_F28235E5 outlined multiple technical challenges faced during migrations. One machine encountered a restart failure due to improper removal of the underlying VMware tooling which is critical for virtualization management.\\n\\nAnother issue was detected by MTV, indicating potential integrity problems with XFS filesystems that could affect data reliability and performance in Linux environments where this file system type is utilized. Additionally, there are concerns regarding VIB version 0.3.0 not being certified by HSBC which may impact deployment stability.\\n\\nThe upgrade from v0.2.0 to v0.3.0 of the VIB has put pressure on host resources leading to migration failures due to resource contention or configuration mismatches that could have been anticipated during planning phases.", "headline": "Identified migration issues related to VMWare, XFS filesystems, VIB version upgrades and LVM.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Validate list accuracy\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"U_SAM_F28235E5\\"]}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Understand proposed solutions for each issue to report back promptly.\\",\\"responsible\\":[]}"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_SAM_F28235E5 has brought up several migration problems that are causing delays. One machine couldn't restart because the tools needed for running virtual machines weren't removed properly afterward.\\n\\nThere were also issues with how data is stored on certain Linux computers, which could affect speed and safety of access to information.", "headline": "Migration issues identified across VMWare, filesystems, VIB versions and LVM configurations need resolution.", "action_items": ["{\\"task\\":\\"Confirm the accuracy of identified migration problems\\",\\"responsible\\":[\\"U_SAM_F28235E5\\"]}", "{\\"task\\":\\"Come up with and understand proposed fixes for each issue to report back quickly.\\",\\"responsible\\":[]}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 09:29:04.797568+00	\N
