aa2d80b0-ded2-4bc5-98e6-4b8f3a3a8afa	49039253-65ea-4d1f-9e23-e3ee1a5497a3	Migration failure process improvement	["Observability integration", "Operational triage", "SLA management"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "During the thread, Ricardo Spazzoli highlighted concerns about unclear responsibilities within SLAs during failures. Vinay requested ACN to be more proactive with initial triage processes. The team decided on making all Miox logs available for immediate access by those conducting triages and review of a Confluence Knowledgebase containing error solutions or contacts, as per Ricardo's suggestion.", "headline": "Review and modify Miox Logs process for better observability in migration failure management.", "action_items": ["Review Confluence Knowledgebase of Miox Errors for solutions or contacts.", "Escalate unresolved ITSO responses to Program with clear instructions on rollback, hypercare, and importance of timely response.", "Red Hat (me) to present collaboration proposal with Command Center and triage support for Raffaele."], "key_decisions": ["All Miox Logs posted in Splunk should be accessible to the team doing triage", "ACN will update responsibilities and SLAs based on feedback"]}	{"body": "The team discussed issues with unclear roles during system migrations, particularly regarding SLA management. Ricardo Spazzoli suggested making logs accessible to those triaging problems immediately after a failure occurs. Vinay asked ACN (Alberto Consulting Network) for more proactive initial responses in such events.", "headline": "Improve processes for handling migration failures and SLAs.", "action_items": ["Make logs accessible for immediate triage after failures.", "Escalate unresolved responses from ITSOs to Program with clear instructions on rollback, hypercare, and timely response importance.", "Present collaboration proposal with Command Center and triage support for Raffaele."], "key_decisions": ["Making Miox Logs available post-failure", "Review and adjust responsibilities and SLAs"]}	2026-05-25 13:55:53.373705+00	\N
dd09d727-1eba-4a60-8e98-61d77e40a6d4	f3c8eedd-6866-4948-80a6-f6576da29589	Project Completion Reflection	["Emotional Response to Project Ending"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.75	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "In this Slack thread, U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 shares their personal reflection regarding the end of an engineering project. They express anticipation for leaving behind Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI) assets that they feel will be destroyed post-project completion. The sentiment conveys a sense of finality and loss, as well as relief at having contributed to something substantial in what is perceived as their 'cruel world.' This emotional response suggests the project had significant personal value for U_ALEXAN_D03599F6.", "headline": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 reflects on the completion of a VDI project and its impact.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "In this Slack conversation, U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 talks about how they feel after completing an engineering project. They are looking forward to the day when everything related to Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI) is gone because it's a part of their work that has been important to them, and its end feels like losing something valuable. U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 seems sad about this but also happy for the project being done.", "headline": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6 shares feelings about finishing a project and its effects on their work environment.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 10:53:24.127078+00	\N
a317b3d2-6edd-4039-86dc-4c1c785a7347	2c71d014-e2a1-4818-acb2-69c188e7e727	Proxy RFE release planning	["API development", "Release scheduling", "Quality Engineering"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	gemini-3.1-flash-lite	classify-v1	{"body": "U_NICK, Rydekull, and Nikos engaged with OAuth PM and Engineering regarding the no-proxy Requested by Field Engineer (RFE) issue. The consensus is to target General Availability (GA) in version 5.1 due to branch closure constraints and extensive testing requirements for a full suite of tests development.", "headline": "Discussion on Proxy RFE release planning for API changes in versions 5.0 and potentially 4.2x.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["The no-proxy RFE will be released as GA in the next major release, which is currently scheduled after July with potential shifts depending on prioritization fluidity."]}	{"body": "U_NICK, Rydekull, and Nikos talked about when to release a change that affects how proxies work in the system. They've decided it should go live with everyone after July 1st because they need time for testing everything thoroughly before releasing.", "headline": "Planning for Proxy RFE Release and Version Scheduling.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["The no-proxy RFE is scheduled to be released as GA following version 5.0, which might shift due to workload prioritization."]}	2026-05-25 14:25:31.121214+00	\N
eb4abb07-85b9-4d76-9aba-6432b9994aa9	4aabf1b6-978d-4c70-b93d-dfa62d1e9831	ClusterVersion resource discussion	["Image specification in ClusterVersion", "OpenShift Container Platform documentation"]	\N	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli initiated a conversation about whether specifying 'image' in the `ClusterVersion` YAML configuration is necessary, pointing to documentation that suggests using only version parameters. He mentioned specific lines from an example and questioned their relevance given current handling of cases by ESS (Enforcement System). Carina Almeida responded with insights into how unhandled cases are currently managed within the system.", "headline": "Discussion on the necessity of an image specification within ClusterVersion resource for OpenShift Container Platform.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli asked if the image details specified within a certain line of their cluster version configuration were needed, as they felt it might be redundant. He referred to official documentation that recommends using only versions instead and questioned why this detail was still in place when cases related to these configurations are not being fully addressed by ESS (Enforcement System). Carina Almeida replied with information about how unhandled situations were currently managed, leaving the team without a clear decision on whether or not to remove image specifications from their configuration.", "headline": "Team discusses whether to keep or remove 'image' specification in ClusterVersion YAML for OpenShift Container Platform updates.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 11:06:10.938647+00	\N
