,\\"responsible\\":[\\"James Force\\",\\"@Anne\\"],\\"details\\":\\"Submit the required work logs to ensure a timely report can be prepared by noon, as requested.\\"}"], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 23:03:19.501446+00	\N
030d2a7f-1ddb-438e-b173-fab2b19f8a77	e29e9493-a62c-4105-8697-33ecb6b15843	Project Management Issue - Memory Error during Migration	["Technical Support"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "James Force initiated a discussion about the migration issue, where Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga referenced an article on Red Hat Customer Portal regarding similar issues. James mentioned that despite MutatingAdmissionPolicy being available in TechPreviewNoUpgrade mode as per docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.21/, it's not yet GA and the migration is failing with an out-of0 memory error, invoking oom-killer during VM to OpenShift Virtualization conversion.", "headline": "Migration of Virtual Machine to OpenShift fails with out-of-memory error.", "action_items": ["James Force will post KCS solution", "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga provided a link for reference"], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "The team encountered an issue while trying to migrate from virtual machines (VMs) to the new OpenShift system. James Force asked for a solution, and Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga suggested looking at Red Hat's Customer Portal where similar problems were discussed in 2018.", "headline": "Migration of Virtual Machine to OpenShift fails due to memory issues.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-26 12:26:15.996367+00	\N
