bd622c52-273c-492f-aacb-8aa969ca6518	4ca72493-46a8-4f3a-9f52-bb365c2cb5a5	Descheduler Affinity And Taints Issue	["RFE-7370 Discussion", "Site A/B Rebalancing"]	89544343-b14b-4504-944b-463ad88bb59a	0.95	phi3:mini	classify-v1	{"body": "The thread initiated by U_GOOGLE_3D5CDFC0, a member of the Engineering team at Google, discusses an issue with the descheduler's AffinityAndTaints Profile. The profile does not account for preferred scheduling but only required during scheduling as per RFE-7370 discussion thread on Atlassian.", "headline": "Discussion on descheduler's AffinityAndTaints Profile and RFE-7370 to rebalance workloads post HIC scenario.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	{"body": "U_GOOGLE_3D5CDFC0 from Google brought up that the descheduler doesn't consider preferred sites when rescheduling tasks. This is a problem because sometimes specific servers are better for certain jobs (like heavy computation or data storage). The team discussed this issue while referring to an open request on Atlassian, RFE-7370.", "headline": "Google's Engineering team discusses a problem with workload scheduling after site loss and recovery in HIC scenario, seeking non-automated solutions.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}	2026-05-25 21:45:39.064037+00	\N
