c4ed34d8-44c8-49e5-9967-485c219a8cc8	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778675581.000001	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778675581.000001", "text": "That table has 50 million rows without proper indexing. We need to add a compound index on user_id and created_at columns immediately.", "type": "message", "user": "Eve"}]	{Eve}	2026-05-13 06:32:53.239661+00	2026-05-25 11:13:35.308377+00	delivered	2026-05-22
fbb5b99d-5f4f-430b-8f04-fcda828eb9ac	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778675400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778675400.000000", "text": "We have a critical database performance problem. The user query on the analytics dashboard is taking 45 seconds. PostgreSQL is doing a sequential scan on the events table.", "type": "message", "user": "Dana"}]	{Dana}	2026-05-13 06:32:53.208898+00	2026-05-25 11:13:35.3156+00	delivered	2026-05-22
273d9578-dbc9-4149-80d8-aa54f70bbfe0	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778675883.000003	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778675883.000003", "text": "The fix is a partial index with a WHERE clause for the last 90 days. That would cover 95% of dashboard queries and reduce the index size dramatically.", "type": "message", "user": "Frank"}]	{Frank}	2026-05-13 06:32:53.281801+00	2026-05-25 11:13:35.321288+00	delivered	2026-05-22
8caa6aba-d479-429c-8da1-372ffdc8c84c	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778676064.000004	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778676064.000004", "text": "Agreed. I'll write the migration to add the partial index. We should also add query result caching in Redis for this specific dashboard endpoint.", "type": "message", "user": "Eve"}]	{Eve}	2026-05-13 06:32:53.296723+00	2026-05-25 11:13:35.286581+00	delivered	2026-05-22
ef33387b-05ab-4f2c-a743-7844d353d63e	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778675702.000002	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778675702.000002", "text": "I ran EXPLAIN ANALYZE and confirmed the sequential scan. The query planner isn't using the existing user_id index because the date range filter is too broad.", "type": "message", "user": "Dana"}]	{Dana}	2026-05-13 06:32:53.259518+00	2026-05-25 11:13:35.326966+00	delivered	2026-05-22
92d53b78-0741-42a3-a6c9-f3b1d8666ef3	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778204723.000023	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778204723.000023", "text": "[Migration Pilot Phase#1 -  Retrospective]\\nCustomer has scheduled a retro session today to improve the incident management process, with what we've learned from yesterday. Mi idea is to schedule an internal one today, before tomorrow's migration event, to gather your feedback as well. I know that squeezing a new meeting is difficult, but how about today after our Standup? I just need 30' or less. @Shebi @Petros @Rydekull @rspazzol?", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.790381+00	2026-05-12 05:07:53.992793+00	delivered	2026-05-09
38a926a0-ae1c-49b0-a5b3-400930d42739	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778213540.000140	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778213540.000140", "text": "[metrics and acm] Enterprise architecture and the run team are starting to take a look at the otel integration and are raising some objections (the same I was raising at the beginning: not all metrics are being forwarded). next steps: a demo of what exist today will be given. Onkar will demo the otel piece, redhat will demo in platform observability. I volunteered, but I have some travel time in front of me and I might have to delegate. @Shebi @Shebi. in the horizon there is the fact that the run team and the Enterprise architecture team bith like the idea of using the product feature when it comes to operationalization. so we might be asked to enabled ACM observability. This was a hard no from Vinay, so we'll se how the conversation evolves. Aside from @ricardo gregorio who has been following this we need and architect to follow this.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.168153+00	2026-05-09 14:56:00.459072+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
5c62cac9-91c5-45a4-b55b-ec384f48ad6b	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778222356.000016	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778222356.000016", "text": "[USA/Mexico site visit] (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Rosemary Lynch"}]	{"Rosemary Lynch"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.632258+00	2026-05-12 05:07:53.999784+00	delivered	2026-05-09
244db115-79fc-45ff-8907-e287cec9ab52	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227459.000019	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227459.000019", "text": "[observability]\\nwe've added three new metrics to the otel-collector on 104 (data stream flow validated otel-collector-gw-lb>kafka>splunk))\\ncustomer removed a transform filter from otel-collector-gateway-lb in DEV (they have not confirmed validation that prometheus label has been re-added > will confirm tomorrow)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.718467+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.013623+00	delivered	2026-05-09
60616049-ab45-47a0-833b-129f2eca47ea	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778218575.000015	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778218575.000015", "text": "@Rosemary Lynch are we meeting today? Review Work stream distribution", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.612274+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.024475+00	delivered	2026-05-09
e28e9551-034b-41df-89a0-2fe26aa297bd	T_SMOKETEST	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	9999900020.000000	9999900021.000000	2	[{"ts": "9999900020.000000", "text": "Customer demo went well. They are interested in the briefing feature — specifically the role-based views. Sales team should follow up with a tailored demo for their architects.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST3"}, {"ts": "9999900021.000000", "text": "Great feedback. The intelligence report layout resonated most. Let us make sure the deep links to Slack threads work correctly for the demo environment.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST1", "thread_ts": "9999900020.000000"}]	{U_TEST3,U_TEST1}	2026-05-21 13:16:36.416582+00	2026-05-27 08:23:25.440245+00	delivered	2026-05-22
362cd99a-3756-49e0-bade-a8edaa000067	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711000.000000", "text": "[Database VM Performance Test]\\nToday we had a session with HSBC (Devdatt, Sudhir and guests from the DB Team) aswell as Alex, Shebi and me,\\nregarding the measured db performance gaps of VMs (RHEL 8.10 running Oracle DB) on the current Vsphere cluster in  the Lab and 104.\\nWe got a clear picture of the current state (clusters, vms and tools used) as well as we plan to proceed. The topic will move from Sudhir (VM Migration/Automation) to Devdatt (Testing) and we decided on the following two testcases shouldering this:\\nTestcase 1: Setup the Lab (1 VM on Vsphere and 1 on 104) make sure both are on the same storage array (DELL as this will be the main storage provider DBs are running on), make sure the tool which creates the synthetic data is in place and how to get the results visble.\\nTestcase 2: Start tweaking (tuneD etc) the VM on OCP to measure and close the performance gap.Carina Almeida  [1:16 PM]\\n@channel To all members of the migration squads\\n\\n Please note that if a PM requests your attendance on a migration call, this must take priority over all other activities.\\nThese calls are critical for unblocking live migrations, so your prompt attendance is essential.\\n:thank_you_smile:", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.952865+00	2026-05-26 21:12:26.889881+00	summarized	2026-05-26
a7af5e4c-965c-47cb-9d3b-1fee5f3ae6f6	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778198363.000083	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778198363.000083", "text": "[Naming Conventions & DataSource Management] We had a meeting with @janine, JD, Nitesh, Ryan, and Samuel.\\nWe started with a discussion on VM image naming conventions, which quickly transformed into an architectural conversation about how we manage DataSources, image versioning, and exceptions for specific OS requirements (especially for the Windows team).\\nCurrently, clusters pull container images from Nexus, tag them as “latest,” and make them available as a DataSource. While this works for HIC environments, it does not meet the requirements for Non-HIC environments. The Windows team requires vendor-driven compatibility and the ability to use specific older image versions (N-1, N-2, etc.). Relying purely on the “latest” tag breaks the audit trail, making it difficult to track exactly which patch or build a VM was spun up from. More info in the thread --> :threeeyedfish:", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.416131+00	2026-05-09 19:28:00.553088+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
ab8f673c-9969-4823-94a0-0a527965b0ec	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778203827.000087	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778203827.000087", "text": "[Testing 17/04/26]\\nSolved some long running issues today\\nFencingAgentRemediation is now resolved. Updating the proxy config allowed the FAR Operator to flow and fencing was tested successfully today at Cluster 104. :white_check_mark:\\nOS Driver issue: the Video Driver was put in place following the kubeVirt upstream documentation and tested with Devdatt and Balaji. :white_check_mark:\\n@Nick Evans Nitesh from the Migration Workstream asks for updates on this, if an implementation of the currently Ansible post-hook driven disk mapping is to be implemented as an feature inside MTV. Do you follow this up?\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04329870", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.467936+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.030367+00	delivered	2026-05-09
4f84a9c1-4623-4da6-b881-4c4ad2df04cf	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778207907.000027	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778207907.000027", "text": "[incident retrospecive] @pdelashe let's propose to add a check after the VM is migrated to see if all the windows service have started.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.885031+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.040749+00	delivered	2026-05-09
5dfa65ce-14b0-450b-a3d8-125ddfea110d	T_SMOKETEST	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	9999900010.000000	9999900012.000000	3	[{"ts": "9999900010.000000", "text": "Sprint velocity is tracking well — we completed 34 points last sprint. For Q3 planning, we should allocate capacity for the observability epic and the OpenShift migration.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST2"}, {"ts": "9999900011.000000", "text": "The OpenShift migration is critical. We need to move from Docker Compose to proper deployments by end of July. Can we get the infra team involved early?", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST1", "thread_ts": "9999900010.000000"}, {"ts": "9999900012.000000", "text": "I will coordinate with the platform team. They have capacity starting next week.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST4", "thread_ts": "9999900010.000000"}]	{U_TEST2,U_TEST1,U_TEST4}	2026-05-21 13:16:36.311704+00	2026-05-27 08:23:25.431064+00	delivered	2026-05-22
aa100117-718f-440d-85e6-3752ef652a21	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778216612.000032	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778216612.000032", "text": "[EOS gantt review]\\nNote that - Gantt is supposed to be baselined next week (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.462908+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.052784+00	delivered	2026-05-09
eb2048d9-5162-4965-959e-ab830c7a5504	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778216733.000033	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778216733.000033", "text": "Only PMs can get excited with a gantt review @pdelashe :upside_down_face::rolling_on_the_floor_laughing:", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.483713+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.060294+00	delivered	2026-05-09
2eeeb51b-6b20-4f23-8052-b46ceee45377	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778238878.000038	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778238878.000038", "text": "[Design Workstream - OpenShift Control Plane with Michele]: Hey team, Here is a summary of today’s meeting with Michele, @Rydekull, and @janine regarding the OpenShift Virtualization Control Plane architectures and our strategy for the bank’s infrastructure.\\n1. Control Plane Topologies in Scope\\nMichele outlined the architectural patterns we are considering, categorized by site constraints and stretching requirements:\\n• Non-stretched, non-constrained sites (local pattern):\\nStandard cluster (3-node dedicated control plane)\\nCompact cluster (3-node converged control plane + workloads)\\n• Stretched patterns, non-constrained sites:\\n2-Node Arbiter (1 CP per main site + arbiter in a 3rd site)\\nSite Affinity CPs (Stretched OSV cluster across Primary + Secondary DC, pinning CPs to 1 site; etcd on active/active storage)\\nCluster stretched across 3 sites (Control plane distributed in each site - dedicated or converged)\\n5-Node Control Plane (3 CPs in Primary and 2 CPs in Secondary DC)\\n• Non-stretched, constrained sites (edge/small footprint):\\nSingle Node OpenShift (SNO)\\nHosted Control Planes / HyperShift (Per-site management cluster hosting multiple HCPs)\\nDC-hosted HCP for constrained sites (workers at the edge site, control plane hosted in a hub DC)\\n2-Node arbiter in a third site (exception-based)\\nRemote Worker Nodes\\n2. VMware “Single/Double Clusters” vs. OpenShift Reorganization\\nWe discussed the bank’s current VMware deployment model, which strictly relies on “Single” and “Double” clusters. We agreed that this legacy pattern does not apply to OpenShift. Because OpenShift does not mandate a two-node minimum for a cluster (e.g., we can use SNO or 3-node compact), we have the opportunity to completely reorganize the infrastructure to maximize resource efficiency rather than mirroring the VMware footprint 1:1.\\nFor context, here is the bank’s current VMware footprint that we will be reorganizing:\\nAmerica: 5 Double Clusters (Total: 5)\\nAsia: 54 Double, 3 Single Clusters (Total: 57)\\nEurope: 24 Double, 10 Single Clusters (Total: 34)\\n3. Action Items (Documentation)\\n@janine will take the lead on documenting two architectural topics:\\nControl Plane Protection: How OpenShift safeguards the control plane in scenarios involving memory compression or Pod eviction.\\nSNO Disaster Recovery: The exact recovery process for migrating VMs from one Single Node OpenShift instance to another SNO instance in the event of a catastrophe, specifically leveraging a shared storage backplane between the two instances.\\nI wanted to give created some diagrams about each scenario, I started to use the deck created by @rspazzol for it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1pzeLapP79fwMHs1KosbonrhNaL4ka62rTKFt4TeKaVE/edit?slide=id.g3d5d185d837_0_946#slide=id.g3d5d185d837_0_946 (edited) \\nGoogle Slides", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.601923+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.065531+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8ffb9ba8-b83c-4aab-b56d-eac8224fe512	T_SMOKETEST	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	9999900001.000000	9999900003.000000	3	[{"ts": "9999900001.000000", "text": "We need to refactor the authentication module to support OIDC. The current JWT validation is too tightly coupled to our custom provider and will not work with Keycloak.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST1"}, {"ts": "9999900002.000000", "text": "Agreed. I looked into the Keycloak adapter and we can use passport-openidconnect. The main risk is session handling — we should keep stateless JWT but add token refresh support.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST2", "thread_ts": "9999900001.000000"}, {"ts": "9999900003.000000", "text": "Action item: create a spike branch to test Keycloak integration with our NestJS guards by end of sprint.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST3", "thread_ts": "9999900001.000000"}]	{U_TEST1,U_TEST2,U_TEST3}	2026-05-21 13:16:36.218449+00	2026-05-27 08:23:25.41882+00	delivered	2026-05-22
c962504c-2366-4c30-9d4e-86e1838c2fee	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209469.000029	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209469.000029", "text": "can't join the standup... still in the retro call", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.176657+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.070888+00	delivered	2026-05-09
06af814f-b428-4691-8e3e-d900d6280836	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778218354.000034	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778218354.000034", "text": "@Carina Almeida do we have a channel for the TAMs? cc @Nikos", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.520575+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.075896+00	delivered	2026-05-09
38a84f05-ac1a-44bf-8b8d-5d3f1c0485de	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228034.000294	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228034.000294", "text": "[Migration team cover for the next two weeks]\\n@pdelashe – I  mentioned we would address this on Monday, but I’ve moved it up as I realised there is a bank holiday in Germany next week.\\nTeam,\\nNext week, the bank is planning to migrate approximately 230 VMs across Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. Since Thursday is a bank holiday in Germany, we need to ensure coverage. @atolani @ricardo gregorio @rspazzol @Rydekull do you have availability to cover for @Shebi and @jfeind? We need one arch and one Consultant for Thursday.\\nMay 22nd is a Red Hat Recharge Day. We are currently coordinating with ESS to see if they can cover migrations that day. However, I would like to know if anyone is interested in a day swap: working on the 22nd and taking your Recharge Day at another date. This would help us with coordination.\\nPlease let me know your availability for the cover and the swap by lunch time tomorrow. :pray:\\nTagging who's not tagged yet: @janine @James Force @Philip Jones @Petros\\nShebi-Openshift-Alerting\\nAPP  18:11\\nwas added to proj-eos-mvp by Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga\\n.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:26.007123+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.081668+00	delivered	2026-05-09
476a5793-e6c5-46dc-b71c-cf336d1afe41	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778221861.000181	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778221861.000181", "text": "[acm secret propagation] @James Force there is a meeting on Monday on this, I added you to it so you can explain the mechanism. from what I can see from the gitops repo, we propagate only the certs and the github credentials. in both instance we should find a way to cut the cordon from ACM and have argocd pull its own secrets after the initial seed. I have an idea on how to do it based on the same mechanism on how we can set the root app to not auto-sync. cc @Shebi .\\nPer similar concept we should also find a way to have ArgoCD deploy its own operator after the initial seed.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.694909+00	2026-05-09 21:06:59.976602+00	embedded	2026-05-09
d03cde6a-07f4-409a-a9d8-86e3a3532563	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227468.000268	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227468.000268", "text": ":alert:Team - please keep an eye on your HSBC training and make sure it is up to date. I know its a pain from a time commitment- but its also part of what gives us the access to hsbc emails and systems etc. and is part of their governance so needs to be maintained", "type": "message", "user": "Anne Maskell"}]	{"Anne Maskell"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.721071+00	2026-05-09 21:07:00.071629+00	embedded	2026-05-09
3c4c2d95-626e-429f-b8fb-6e258c4cc151	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778221539.000279	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778221539.000279", "text": "[copy fail CVE] this seems important and urgent. @Nikos are you taking care of the  needed communication to the customer?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.821736+00	2026-05-09 21:07:00.20462+00	embedded	2026-05-09
c92ebc14-d18f-470e-8a76-cf74f31682a4	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778218455.000075	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778218455.000075", "text": "@jfeind, @James Force, @ricardo gregorio please can you check my message in Teams (Red Hat chat) and let me know if you're currently working on any of the out-of-sync argo apps / services. We've been asked to get them all green, in sync etc. If there are any apps supporting non-git managed config, we will need to look into merging these changes into the code base.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.259565+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.112753+00	delivered	2026-05-09
5e244209-4da3-4285-9bf6-da06e73a3ac0	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778197300.000040	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778197300.000040", "text": "Regarding GitOps: Can we please establish a system where a PR is to be reviewed by one Red Hatter and one HSBC Team member? Also I saw that on my recent PR the Reviewer just added 3 more Commits putting in some extra values which then merged outside the feedback loop.\\nThat is in my humble opinion not a recommended practice of a Review process. :expressionless:", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.636224+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.118955+00	delivered	2026-05-09
f84b9248-17f6-4cc7-b0be-1e8d18811612	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778197662.000042	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778197662.000042", "text": "@Shebi the US Migration Workstream is an \\"official\\" workstream? With different people and diffrerent meetings? Because if YES, we need to add it to our workstream planner, at least to keep track of it and include it in reporting", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.668745+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.125222+00	delivered	2026-05-09
1d759c1e-271b-40d9-89c2-d37a2fb8390d	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778239899.000039	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778239899.000039", "text": "[Migration Workstream - update]:\\nWindows Golden Image Integration: The team is taking the configurations we developed for the Windows golden image (such as restricting qemu-agent RPC calls and configuring the VirtIO drivers via the VM YAML) and baking them directly into the migration automation to prevent post-migration issues.\\nCurrent Status: They are implementing these features now and will report back if they need further assistance or troubleshooting from our side.\\nUS Migration Workstream & IP Updates (Today’s Sync), we had a meeting with @janine , @jfeind, @Rydekull with the team about this topic.\\nRole Update: Narender officially designated me as the owner from our side for the US Migration Workstream. Was this discussed with you @pdelashe?\\nIP Change Matrix: The Migration team is creating a testing matrix to handle IP address changes during the datacenter moves, covering every OS variant and scenarios with single or multiple network interfaces.\\nAutomation Strategy: We agreed that Ansible is the best path forward to automate these post-migration IP updates. We offered our help to develop and refine this automation.\\nAction Items & Next Steps\\nTo build and validate the Ansible playbooks, we need live test environments.\\nSrinath is currently taking the task to provision the test machines. I explicitly requested at least one Windows VM and one Linux VM so we can validate the automation logic across both OS variants. He will notify us as soon as they are ready for us to begin testing. I will need someone to pick this up once they deliver the VMs to test @Petros or @jfeind are you up for this one?", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.622294+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.134697+00	delivered	2026-05-09
cd3cddb3-9693-4188-9837-eeb724a9d297	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700300.000000", "text": "[Weekly Planning Review] (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ROSEMA_0749D041"}]	{U_ROSEMA_0749D041}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.60476+00	2026-05-26 21:23:37.986165+00	summarized	2026-05-26
ecfc96d2-ef67-4982-ae6d-55b4d5052b5a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700500.000000", "text": "[helm binary] Looking for a helm binary in the environment that I can use from the linux bastion, any suggestions are helpful :slightly_smiling_face:", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.635726+00	2026-05-26 21:28:36.589676+00	summarized	2026-05-26
