09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700600.000000	7777700607.000000	8	[{"ts": "7777700600.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nadded couple of namespaces and a message keyword to the existing filter setup in the logforwarder resource;\\nteam work with @Philip Jones to get the dell powermax metrics available;\\nadded couple of powermax metrics to the otel configuration on 104. observability team with validate data flowing into splunk tomorrow.\\nenabled, manually on 104, servicemonitor to make Trident-metrics available. At quick glance could not work out array capacity;\\nthanks @Philip Jones for pulling metrics list from 104 manually;\\nraised PR to enable custom alerts to monitor OTEL Collector health, message queue usage and failure of messages not queuing locally or not sending to the OTEL Collector Gateway.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D"}, {"ts": "7777700601.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nPR to add alert rules to Otel Collector - thank you @James Force \\nPR to add extra namespaces in logging\\nRemoved filters in CLF targetting cyber Splunk. Will review this with Rijo tomorrow. Last 24h with filters in place: data ingestion of 18G from 104\\nNeed to mod. Trident config to allow for https-metrics. Might have a catch up with @James Force if/when available next.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700602.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nadded netapp-trident namespace to log-forwarder filter + added regex patterns to message filter\\nsimulated a kustomize patch definition for the region based endpoints in anticipation for live changes next week\\nworking with Onkar to provide powermax metrics to stor team", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700603.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n- customer wants to find a way of 'observing' the cluster build lifecycle, i.e., capturing/monitoring the build phases/progress/failures. This is because over the weekend 4x worker nodes out of 48x did not join a cluster that was built. Unsure how this can be done, so currently researching this. Thank you for helping @janine\\n- checked with Cyber team. Cluster 104, last 24h ingested 33.6 million events ~ 59.2G. It seems that they have not checked the contents in regards of what is useful, what is sensitive, etc\\n- reviewing Confluence doc in regards to OCP-V Security Requirement Matrix (defined by customer)Carina Almeida  [5:54 PM]\\n[Migration velocity]\\n\\n@janine @Shebi @Rydekull iIn our call with ACN today, we agreed to document the specific challenges and constraints that can impact migration velocity.\\n\\nWhile the document @Anne prepared outlines our advice to achieve velocity, we now need to explicitly list the challenges and constraints. Could you please add your input to that document? - Go Faster ideas\\n\\nACN also raised a question regarding potential Miox restrictions. They were informed that Miox can only migrate 40 VMs in parallel. Are you aware of this limitation, or do you have a views on whether this is accurate?\\n\\nThank you so much.\\n\\nPS. @Nikos  and @rspazzol for info.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700604.000000", "text": "[Observability] Seems the initial sizing calculation they did for storing (filtered) metrics in splunk (which was an order of magnitude higher than what we saw in overall disk usage in OpenShift) wasn't the storage consumed in splunk, but kafka. in splunk it actually looked okay today from what they showed us, got to ask for the specific number, but Onkar was not concerned at all anymore, they'll doublecheck, but looks like it's not actually an issue.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JANINE_71F80BBD", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700605.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ninvestigating whether info from the assisted-service pod logs can help with monitoring the managed-cluster build progress. I will share some findings with @janine \\nworking on SIEM log requirements (will catch up with @Rydekull tomorrow)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700606.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ntemporarily forwarding infra/audit logs to SIEM Splunk Pre-Prod instance, via 102;\\nshared intentional ssh attempt failures and selfsubjectaccessreviews resource events with the SIEM team;", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}, {"ts": "7777700607.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ncreated changes (with new staff) for logging & otel configs to target GB/HK lab clusters;\\nworking on of alert rules for logging to eal with silent failures, etc\\nworking on SIEM use cases for tomorrow's PM meeting", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}]	{U_RICARD_02F5C49D,U_JANINE_71F80BBD}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.642941+00	2026-05-26 21:37:57.007206+00	summarized	2026-05-26
79fea343-0bb2-4e1e-aa93-93701e4deda7	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700800.000000", "text": "[netapp and storage offload] just a heads up, customer tried to do storage offload with netapp. this of course does not work. netapp has its own tool called shift toolkit. We have communicated the situation,", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.681664+00	2026-05-26 21:45:23.678002+00	summarized	2026-05-26
70296ee0-af61-4ea8-af53-b0eb59e691bb	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700700.000000", "text": "[hyper-care] we need a slide on how the hyper-care works at a high level (for us/mx deck). We also need a low-level description of the process in agreement with the customer. @Anne @Carina Almeida @pdelashe I expect this to come from you but do let me know if I am wrong. We need clarification on the following:\\n\\nhow does the customer engage with us when a migration fails\\nwho is available and response time. Is the OS a matter in this decision.\\ntroubleshooting environment (we cannot/should not access production) and level of collaboration with the migration team and service owners.. (RACI)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.665439+00	2026-05-27 08:26:12.570335+00	summarized	2026-05-27
