05bba4d3-2151-4f69-8e49-af5ba53a7fbe	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777701700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777701700.000000", "text": "[audit logs to SIEM] the pipeline is proved, thanks @ricardo gregorio. security team now has to verify they understand what they get (@Rydekullassigned to help), provide feedback on whether it is too much or too little, write security breach detection rules. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.770445+00	2026-05-26 22:06:06.693777+00	summarized	2026-05-26
f58dc0ad-f627-4553-9e4f-f60e9f452f5a	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778235842.000062	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778235842.000062", "text": "@janine is my understanding right that you are going to suggest the customer a strategy to increase the isolation between control plane and workloads on schedulable master nodes?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.025999+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.222133+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3d8250e2-15bd-433c-9fe1-0c2c2e427cde	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778224792.000292	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778224792.000292", "text": "[Build Update]:\\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel.\\n421 channel work is underway as well.\\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully.\\nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.981811+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.226798+00	delivered	2026-05-09
e8628613-e516-4708-957d-57523f658a89	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778221548.000108	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778221548.000108", "text": "@ricardo gregorio just an FYI that the Dell CSM driver has been successfully updated on 104 now. Hopefully everything needed is there and working.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.754374+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.231366+00	delivered	2026-05-09
1fd7ea35-cdf1-4909-8366-2a96f0cc4429	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778215544.000104	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778215544.000104", "text": "@janine :point_up_2:", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.716225+00	2026-05-09 13:32:55.81002+00	pending_retry	\N
8c4c71ae-600b-425f-bc41-bf17e1ed968c	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702000.000000", "text": "[OS drivers] @atolani @jfeind there is an email thread from Abhishek to which I am being added about issues that we are still having with the OS drivers for windows. This typically means that we are not making progress. Can you summarize the issue and the plan to resolve it. Also anything you need?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.796654+00	2026-05-26 22:12:35.741371+00	summarized	2026-05-26
bc7ac5c9-2d47-4244-ad91-9d114134f9bb	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702300.000000", "text": "[Migration Support and Hypercare Thread]\\nI am opening this thread to keep all ideas together as I need to send our proposal by end of this week. Bear in mind that we can't invent a new process and need to adapt to what they have already defined (remember this is a Bank and they follow ITIL proceses), and their SLAs: While migrating a VM there are only 15minutes limit to decide to roll back, so all the ideas you are proposing IMO should be in a separate section of RCA . I'm putting everything together here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vYMFbZpGRjLOltrKqecQh06cpCp-8tkKLprEdCQwUAo/edit?tab=t.1q40s08up9xd#heading=h.wd3rd5djgvwy", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.823425+00	2026-05-26 22:23:00.41367+00	summarized	2026-05-26
7029f740-3d03-4587-a954-a40d0b77373d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702400.000000", "text": "[US DC migration] we learned that there is a program level DC migration and we need to sync with them to understand what the process is. The VM migration tool/automation with need to be harmonized with that process. likely they will take care of the network devices (DNS, Loadbalacer, firewall) configuration at the program level, but teh modalities are unknown at this point. Next week there will be a meeting with the DC migration program team to get some insight. @Shebi will follow this part and create a proposal on how the VM migration process will integrate with the larger DC migration process.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.829158+00	2026-05-26 22:26:56.046425+00	summarized	2026-05-26
6598f042-3ad9-4a7c-a225-6d9b13769770	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702500.000000", "text": "[bsod] MTV 2.11.4-2 seems to solve most of teh bsod-related problems that other customers have been experiencing by installing the latest VirtIO-Win 1.9.57 drivers. It would be grate if we could upgrade top this version. @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.837984+00	2026-05-26 22:29:08.212867+00	summarized	2026-05-26
c353832b-3022-4167-a2f5-426b136c2055	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777701900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777701900.000000", "text": "[Resourcing call with Vinay and Programme team]\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nAnne and I met with Vinay and the Programme Team today. While the objective was to position the new staff, the discussion evolved into a broader conversation regarding team allocation.\\n\\nWe walked them through our Governance and Work Distribution slides, which have now been shared with them for reference.\\n\\nA key request from Vinay is that our team maintains an 80% dedication to ENG work. This means ENG tasks take priority over all other activities. In case you have a conflict in priorities, please notify Rose, Patricia, or myself immediately so we can coordinate with ENG for prioritisation. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.78879+00	2026-05-26 22:11:12.166293+00	summarized	2026-05-26
da84b8f5-7088-49fc-815f-187d8989fbaa	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702100.000000	7777702101.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777702100.000000", "text": "[VM Migration]\\nSrinath and Abhishek are interested in NUMA aware VMs regarding their high performance applications.\\nMain question is how their current NUMA mappings on VMware would be translated to OCP+V.\\nI am currently go through the docs and sources regarding the current state of kubeVirt\\nhttps://kubevirt.io/user-guide/compute/numa/\\netc\\nIf anyone of you is deep in the matter, a short exchange would be appreciated.\\nOverall I asked that this would be perfect match for a testcase, they agreed and would need to organize such a VM into the current environment for us to migrate. (edited) \\nkubevirt.ioNUMA - KubeVirt user guideDocumentation for KubeVirtRaffaele Spazzoli  [10:32 PM]\\na bit of good news, today HSBC deployed three more clusters. minor non blocking automation issues reported, they will be addressed.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}, {"ts": "7777702101.000000", "text": "[VM Migration]\\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\\n\\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \\n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.Added by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerPhilip Jones  [6:18 PM]\\n[build]\\n\\nWe have restored cluster 104 this morning. It's now at least as good as it was before the storage update :wink:\\nCluster 102 pure storage update now successfully completed after we ran a cleanup script to remove stale entries in the pure storage cluster kvdb. \\nTake away from this is that the storage cluster had a lot of volume snapshots it thought it was managing that didn't actually exist on the flasharray. This was likely triggered by stress testing back in Feb.\\nWe still see a LOT of volume snapshots associated with non-existent, previously deleted pvc's. These are for the most case the same stale volumes the script removed from kvdb. We will need to create our own script to remove them and complete the cleanup.\\n\\nIssues impacting hkoclu307 and the three nodes that refused to register now tracked to a Cisco switch issue. A ticket is being raised with Cisco to debug. \\nIsovalent call postponed for today.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8", "thread_ts": "7777702100.000000"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.804819+00	2026-05-26 22:16:16.359385+00	summarized	2026-05-26
215173c3-3fba-4973-93d5-3eedecbd5d93	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702200.000000", "text": "[Bulk Migrations] :books:\\nAlso from me a bit of good news.\\nFirst iteration of bulk migrations was done.\\nBefore I share some numbers, I share one issue: from the 200 VMs they promised we have just around 60 available now, because 128 have been deleted due to some internal compliance issue on how those VMs have been deployed internally. Bit of a nuisance, I got promised they will bring them back asap, I hope so, until then we have to work with what we got.\\nThe Bulk Migration itself is run over MIO-X to get it as real as possible.\\nTest Case No 1 was done as cold and direct migration (storage offloading is currently not available as a feature in MIO-X, due it can not make sure that both source and target storage maps are the same and storage offload activated. I had a conversation with the team and Abhishek is now taken care of this to be implemented.)\\n\\nSo, now some numbers:\\n\\n61 VMs Migrated with 1 VM per Migrationplan :arrow_forward:\\n59 VMs with disksize of 100-150 GB, mix of Linux and Windows OS\\n- 52 VMs migrated successfully within a total timeframe of 43 (earliest) to 120 min (latest). :white_check_mark:\\n- 7 VMs failed through a freak configuration on VMware which said: 2 sockets and 1 cpu, this translates into 0.5 sockets, while the manifest actually expects an integer >=1 for the sockets value. :x:\\nThis has been identified and fixed, also Srinath mentioned this happend when the testing VMs have been created and should not re-occur within the production VMs. :check:\\n- 2 running into a MIO-X timeout (currently set to approx 3 hours) but those had 1,5 TB disk which took 5 hours and finished successfully :white_check_mark:\\n\\nI will share in the Red Hat Teams channel the official Confluence page on this bulk migration test.\\nA lot more to come, especially looking forward to have 200 VMs with storage offload and various migration plan sizings. Good thing is that VM Migration and Testops Team works now together really well. We plan to have a bulk migration status call now two times a week.\\n\\nObservability while we migrate is in the making by Srinath and will hopefully be gathered on the next iteration. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.816757+00	2026-05-26 22:20:54.704084+00	summarized	2026-05-26
21426b22-78fa-4fd1-a7ed-fb6a667b7227	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778216844.000144	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778216844.000144", "text": "[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?", "type": "message", "user": "Nick Evans"}]	{"Nick Evans"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.215282+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.239717+00	delivered	2026-05-09
11ee8c1c-1804-4a42-a51f-371adf38fe62	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778213743.000103	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778213743.000103", "text": "[wildcard certificates] Currently in a meeting where the need for wildcard certs are being discussed and Natti is arguing the facts and defending the approach. Will update here with more infor", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.704628+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.246121+00	delivered	2026-05-09
195b1177-70c5-4953-8fef-bb6ae753c247	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702800.000000", "text": "[any to any storage offload migrations] any to any means between different storage vendors. This should work, but it seems not to. I have involved Roy from engineering but he has be slow to answer as he was on PTO. Customer is attempting migration from HPE to Dell. There is a certain urgency on this and I am about to go on PTO. @janine can you pick this up? Let's sync on this today before I disappear.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.862061+00	2026-05-26 22:32:12.330523+00	summarized	2026-05-26
3951b76b-ec38-4c80-bb30-706ecdf9315d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703000.000000", "text": "[Labels - Data Architecture - Affinity and Anti-Affinity Discussions]:\\n\\nPart 1: The Aspirational Design (Gareth & Michele)\\nWe successfully validated a strategy to model our physical failure domains in OpenShift to enable High Availability via Affinity/Anti-Affinity rules. This relies on tagging OpenShift nodes and VMs with three critical dimensions: Country, Data Center, and Fabric.\\n\\nWe mapped out exactly how to inject these labels across three journeys using Unicorn as the primary System of Record:\\n\\nCluster Build (GitOps): Querying Unicorn via bare-metal hostnames to label OpenShift nodes.\\nVM Migration (MIOX): Pulling metadata to inject labels into the VM manifests during migration.\\nNew VM Provisioning (Ansible/ITSP): Having Ansible query Unicorn to label net-new VMs at creation.\\n\\nPart 2: The Reality Check (Rushi)\\n\\nWhen I reviewed this with Rushi, he rightly pointed out that while this looks great on paper, it is highly aspirational for our day-to-day operations.\\nThe Bottleneck: Strict Affinity/Anti-Affinity requires heavy coordination with Application Owners to define these rules properly.\\nThe Operational Reality: In the event of an outage, VM Admins are solely focused on restoring services immediately. They will not have the time to debug why a VM isn’t scheduling due to Anti-Affinity constraints.\\n\\nPart 3: The Alternative Proposal (Service Classes)\\n\\nTo solve this, Rushi proposed a much more pragmatic, DR-focused approach: Service Classes (Priority Levels).\\nInstead of forcing App Owners to define complex affinity rules, we simply ask them to define the priority of their service.\\nIn the event of a massive failure (e.g., node, rack, or hall), the platform aggressively evacuates and live-migrates the High Priority VMs to healthy nodes.\\nLow Priority VMs are simply stopped/powered down to free up capacity for the critical workloads.Philip Jones  [6:14 PM]\\nPJ - Build:\\n\\nMore investigation of Pure Storage Issue\\nPulled into a call with SRE team who want to have a solution for silencing all alerts for maintenance windows or during cluster build / deployments.\\nJoined a called regarding new cluster hk307. Three nodes not joining the cluster correctly. One registered as a node, but showing as not available. Two are just awol. I couldn't find any issues with the nodes or config, the HK networking team are claiming no issues there side either, but I think we need to get on a call with them to resolve. I've also adding the toolbox container to oc-mirror so we can run more troubleshooting on nodes as required.\\nAttended a call (along with Raffa) with Dell to discuss CSM Operator issues. The call was positive and they've acknowledged some problems with the existing operator. Hopefully future operator versions will work out of the box (so to speak).\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.880315+00	2026-05-26 22:38:19.788882+00	summarized	2026-05-26
6fe29a5e-fa91-441e-805c-b6bf2d086e67	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703100.000000	7777703101.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777703100.000000", "text": "[build]\\n\\ntroubleshooted the pure issues making progress root cause, session with pure on monday\\nspent the majority of my time today time with Suhas and Sourav on going over the remaining custom compliance operator rules, the final remaing things are not from the CIS KubeVirt benchmarks but custom HSBC AI invented ones so some not relevant/unclear, but think we're close to wrapping this piece of work up\\nwent over next steps for the remote worker piece with Vinayak - it's a bit slow going but the priority on this has seemed to get lower so somewhat expected\\nclarified the kubeletconfig changes required for the SRE team ... again, but the point/approach has stuck now as they've raised a PR for it now\\nbonus: there is a bit of traction again on getting LACP link aggregation metrics for node exporter after prompting it... fingers crossed as this would be a nice addition and with a prom alert this could be quite informative and useful https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/issues/1604#issuecomment-4299123571 \\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}, {"ts": "7777703101.000000", "text": "[build]\\n\\nSpoke with Mike on the LACP issue we came accross recently, they will add some checks on their side to mitigate this, but  he was curious if there was anything we can do on our side, I mentioned the lack of metrics in this area but he seemed happy about the upstream conversation and was curious to know if something did get added to node_exporter upstream when would that land in openshift\\nQuick call on the ACM prorogation policies and then created an issue on the backlog to attempt to remove dependency on ACM after the initial seed... I will try to pick this up when I get some time\\nRuishi dragged me into a call to discuss security policies and then went around the circles of gatekeeper, kyverno VAPs etc..  I circ led it back to the point of that VAPs were decided and work was already started here,,, I think there is a clear need for a proper backlog and planning of work as things feel a bit all over the place \\nRushi called me again on the gitops approach and his want to move to something completely different (this binary artefact approach). I told him again this won't work, but he wants to allign with some 'deploycontol' approaches of their... @janine I've pinged you on the links in the teams chat.. maybe can you help me here? I think we just need to educate here on our controls for gitops and route to live process. IIRC you were working on something around this area?\\nMTU... all our clusters MTU is just at 1400 (default)... this is probably a driver in the why live migrations are 'slow'....  @Rydekull I your help tomorrow on this to understand your last comment on the jump frames GH issue on upping this value to 9000 \\nPure upgrade troubleshooting \\nSnapshot issue (102) - I've just sent the operator log to pure for 102 on the pending failed upgrade due to snapshots... hopefully they can script up something to address that ... however.... if their approach is to manually delete records out of etcd using etcdctl... not sure I really like that, doesn't exactly feel elegant!\\nVolume mapping (104)  - unfortunately the horrible idea I had the other day to manually remap volumes looks like it is a reality and the only way forward... albeit they provided us with a more elegant way to get the required info we need, and also let us know we don't need to define the targets in the purevolume resource", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179", "thread_ts": "7777703100.000000"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.963034+00	2026-05-26 22:49:11.729346+00	summarized	2026-05-26
999809b8-7371-4efe-a9f7-89652aed8398	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702600.000000	7777702601.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777702600.000000", "text": "[TCs Submission]\\nHI team!", "type": "message", "user": "U_ROSALI_5BB9C3D4"}, {"ts": "7777702601.000000", "text": "[TCs Submission]\\nHI team!", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_F60D95C9", "thread_ts": "7777702600.000000"}]	{U_ROSALI_5BB9C3D4,U_GOOGLE_F60D95C9}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.845694+00	2026-05-26 22:30:36.564515+00	summarized	2026-05-26
984fa56e-8e77-4cd6-961c-4f651d4e55d9	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703200.000000", "text": "[node drain] Balamurugan is saying that draining nodes takes so long that the VMs eventually fail to live migrate and they have to be manually moved. This should not be happening even if storage is slow. I asked him to open a case and to involve @Shebi . @James Force you are also in that conversation so perhaps you can add more color.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.980114+00	2026-05-26 22:50:38.40515+00	summarized	2026-05-26
6261ab7e-528c-4be3-aa6d-a655da1a7990	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777714500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777714500.000000", "text": "@Rydekull I followed up on your idea which you mentioned to Ansell regarding installing qemu-guest-agent on Windows VMs as a pre-hook to reduce the number of reboots. Srinath sees it as a red flag currently installing anything on the VMs before the migration in case of a rollback. Nevertheless I think the idea is not bad, we agreed that I write a proposal to Abhishek to create a new testcase with a VM being migrated that has qemu-agent installed and a vanilla one to see what the time difference would make.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.27816+00	2026-05-26 22:52:46.149081+00	summarized	2026-05-26
a998ae29-3336-4367-8c10-315b85e5fc7b	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778217622.000262	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778217622.000262", "text": "[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.66023+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.253554+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3d09f8fa-e733-4553-baef-6e1c82998774	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778196243.000063	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778196243.000063", "text": "@Petros @Shebi can you plz forward to my hsbc email the daily migration meetings? I have the weekly ones, but not the standups..", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.035709+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.26656+00	delivered	2026-05-09
0de681bd-aed0-4382-9919-d76e07cf3942	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778198614.000214	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778198614.000214", "text": "[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.15289+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.276544+00	delivered	2026-05-09
b6d6d770-c7ed-45f9-93dc-0f1bc4ff8c78	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778203766.000086	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778203766.000086", "text": "Hi all, if you don't mind sharing:\\nwhich AI tool(s) are you (if) using outside the cust. environment? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.457106+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.283227+00	delivered	2026-05-09
0cc0a65d-b706-4ca8-be41-ffc708bbcfb2	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703400.000000", "text": "[acm secret propagation] @James Force there is a meeting on Monday on this, I added you to it so you can explain the mechanism. from what I can see from the gitops repo, we propagate only the certs and the github credentials. in both instance we should find a way to cut the cordon from ACM and have argocd pull its own secrets after the initial seed. I have an idea on how to do it based on the same mechanism on how we can set the root app to not auto-sync. cc @Shebi .", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.018619+00	2026-05-26 22:55:03.679084+00	summarized	2026-05-26
5ae678ff-93a3-4b67-841e-f953179d3cd4	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778216311.000031	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778216311.000031", "text": "[Affinity and Anti-Affinity rules] As @Petros recently highlighted, we currently have a gap regarding VM management post-migration. Right now, when a VM is migrated via MTV, its definition and affinity rules live exclusively inside the OpenShift cluster’s etcd database. If a VM is deleted, those placement rules are permanently lost because we currently lack a central source of truth outside of the hypervisor to manage them declaratively.\\nIn a meeting with Michele, Jakob, Phil and @Rydekull we agreed that addressing this gap and programmatically managing these rules represents a net-new requirement for the platform. Here is the breakdown of our current process, the future state, and the impact on backups.\\nCurrent State (Manual):\\nA user submits a ServiceNow request specifying their Anti-Affinity needs.\\nA VMware Admin (OpenShift Admin in future) takes that request and manually updates the target Virtual Machines with the specific rules.\\nData Protection & Label Recovery:\\nAutomated Recovery: The backup solution will only be able to automatically restore VM labels (used for Anti-Affinity) in environments where the workflow explicitly backs up the VM Object, Jakob confirmed this is not the case for all clusters.\\nManual Recovery: For any other setup, the recovery process falls back on the VM Admin to restore the VM (From the golden image + restore from Netbackup) and manually reapply the labels (Using ServiceNow tickets regarding the Virtual Machine to be recovered).\\nFuture State (Data Architecture):\\nTo solve this, the target design is to build an externalized config management system (leveraging GitOps). This will serve as the central source of truth for Anti-Affinity rules data, which will then automatically push updates and reconcile the state down to the OpenShift clusters. This is not part of our current project, and it will be discussed at a later stage.\\nNext Steps:\\nI am going to add the backup/restore limitations to the “Data Protection and Data Recovery” section of our documentation, and I will add the externalized config management system to the “Data Architecture” section as a future requirement.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.4326+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.288712+00	delivered	2026-05-09
e2f0d369-730e-47cb-b747-7a518407d0d3	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227879.000079	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227879.000079", "text": "[observability]\\n- meeting with SRE to discuss alertmanager receiver usage/filtering\\n- PR to update otel config 104\\n- capacity planing meeting with kafka team. Obs team provided forecast data ingestion based on a span of 100 clusters being built within the next 3-6 months across the 3x regions. Follow up meeting Tue next week. Will catch up with Obs team to understand how much contingency has been allocated  within this calculation (including addition of extra metrics and filter (removal) adjustments if/when required that might increase data volume).", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.348601+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.293908+00	delivered	2026-05-09
