a28201c7-555f-4a51-9059-c45e4a137462	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778212351.000091	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778212351.000091", "text": "[RH Gov & WOW]\\nTeam, thanks to everyone who got excited with me today during propose Gov & WOW slide run-through\\nIf you need a good bed time reading tonight, you can find here the link to the slides and the Miro board.\\nPlease let me know if you have comments by Monday 10am GMT. I plan to review this with Anne after that, then send info to the customer.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.516666+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.320853+00	delivered	2026-05-09
6004aa6f-8afc-4391-ba23-b03c3d9faf4a	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228180.000080	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228180.000080", "text": "[build]\\nSpent some time this morning with Sourav updating the tlsSecurityProfile on cluster102. Awaiting his feedback on whether we proceed with custom profiles or not. This likely gives a little more control to the customer, but will require manual maintenance. Config will be managed centrally from Git.\\nInvestigated an Image Stream issue for Prerana. This appears be a badly defined dataimportcron on 105.\\nReviewed all the argo apps across Lab clusters. Now have a list of issues to fix and will work through this tomorrow.\\nOC mirror sync updated to pull missing Dell CSM images.\\nCustom dell csm configmap now ready to utilise above images.\\nRaised a request to enable crowdstrike through proxy as there's several images we're unable to mirror for the operator.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.362448+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.326149+00	delivered	2026-05-09
17033358-4349-481a-8d3b-bdce08e8b16f	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778226538.000238	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778226538.000238", "text": "[Isovalent Update]\\nLargely just confirming the version that we'll be installing for the POC phase 2.\\nLast time all the clusters were agent based installations so I've suggested that this time we build one ACM cluster and build the second cluster from that instead. This should more closely represent the build process HSBC will use for the majority of their clusters.\\nWill need to provide some info in POCDOC to assist with ACM install etc.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.399101+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.343998+00	delivered	2026-05-09
14b3ed4c-b11e-4512-b51b-5bdc805c3633	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219746.000106	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219746.000106", "text": "@James Force @Philip Jones where do we stand with configuring the maximum number of disks per node both in dell and pure?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.736786+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.352828+00	delivered	2026-05-09
ea8f3a4a-6867-49be-aa2e-dbe51edef118	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778230071.000111	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778230071.000111", "text": "[Sheffield’s Training Feedback]: I want to share some valuable feedback I just received from one of our  students regarding the current OpenShift Virtualization training plan. This aligns perfectly with what we have been hearing from others who have gone through the recent sessions @Philip Jones@James Force@Nikos Help me out if I am missing or misinforming something, you were there present on the trainings.\\nWhile the standard Red Hat hands-on labs (DO156/DO316) are excellent for baseline knowledge, there is a significant disconnect between the “textbook” OpenShift platform and the bank’s actual operational reality. The trainees are having a hard time mapping the generic labs to our bespoke environment.\\nThe training assumes standard platform usage (e.g., using the OpenShift Web Console and CLI). In reality, our teams will not be logging into the console. We are strictly driving operations via GitOps, not using OVN Networking for VMs, and Commvault/other tools for backups.\\nArchitectural Vulnerabilities Exposed: Seeing the standard platform behavior actually reinforced a gap we discussed recently: currently, VM configurations (scheduling, labeling, annotations, affinity rules) only live in the OpenShift etcd database. The trainees rightfully pointed out that we need to see how this infrastructure deployment looks in GitOps/YAML format to truly manage it.\\nWe need a shortcut to bridge the gap between what the vanilla platform offers and how we actually build and operate it here.\\n@kibrahim - Given this feedback, what can we do to adapt the upcoming enablement phases?\\nWould it be possible to inject a custom bridging session into the curriculum? The Architects and Consultants could host a walk-through to connect the Red Hat training concepts directly to the bank’s GitOps architecture so the trainees get a realistic view of their day-to-day operations.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.795149+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.359535+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8fc01cfd-3cb3-4203-8893-1716391c67d7	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777704400.000000", "text": "[Sheffield - HIC Design Workshops notes]: Please all the notes here, include screenshots or whatever you want and later we can add structure, is better to have excess in this case: https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/edit?tab=t.0", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.191982+00	2026-05-26 23:13:45.162915+00	summarized	2026-05-26
f4f8e853-ee74-4557-b70f-c2f0ca6bbd0a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777704300.000000", "text": "[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessibleThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.162782+00	2026-05-26 23:11:39.522975+00	summarized	2026-05-26
d8c7d8c5-2a85-40bf-9eec-f4aeedafc3a0	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777704500.000000", "text": "[RFE-7054 - Auth Proxy] - I had a call two people in engineering about the auth proxy last night. I explained to them that we have a workaround at the moment but at some point, we might need to configure a different proxy and the cluster wide proxy doesn't work for us anymore. The proposed solution is to add a new property to the oauth object. THey're not sure if they will be able to backport it to 4.22 but they were confident on a backport to 4.23. @Shebi @Rydekull @James Force @rspazzol @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_2764FAE5"}]	{U_GOOGLE_2764FAE5}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.22103+00	2026-05-26 23:15:33.098402+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e9500400-3225-4491-a082-1a245b9b0f64	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778211834.000054	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778211834.000054", "text": "Hi team - per our stand up today ...Frank has challenged the HSBC project leadership to \\"go faster\\" on the programme as a whole. This involves removing blockers, improving processes,  adding resources etc...\\nQuestion to you all - given what we know of their technical environment are there any platform suggestions that mean they can build faster, migrate faster etc that we know the project isn't taking advantage of.\\nThis is all caveated of course with it being do-able in the HSBC world before you all inundate me on things that they arent dong that most people do as standard! :rolling_on_the_floor_laughing:\\nMentioned on the call Plan to Flow, Building a HIC environment, Run team capability.\\nPlease reply in :thread2: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Anne Maskell"}]	{"Anne Maskell"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.874526+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.374116+00	delivered	2026-05-09
0acc7785-d98f-493b-9c49-b27fb915d177	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228660.000020	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228660.000020", "text": "Build Team Update:\\nCompleted about 50% of the securecodewarrior training HSBC has added to my required courses list.\\nSpent a chunk of time trying to get the latest DELL CSM version working. Sadly it doesn't have the correct paths for the images it needs to pull and there's no easy workaround. It will likely require a fix from Dell. Based on their docs here: https://dell.github.io/csm-docs/docs/supportmatrix/component-version/ the images we've mirrored are where they should be, but the container storage module is looking for them under dell, rather than dell-emc. It's also appending an additional folder name to the requests, which we can't replicate.\\nAlso requested Durga to investigate an issue with machinesets and machines.\\nNew oc-mirror docs now merged.\\noc-mirror is now mirroring 4.20 and 4.21 only. Hopefully we will be running oc-mirror delete to prune away 4.19 from Nexus and the local workspace soon.\\nDell Technologies\\nComponent and Image Details\\nContainer Storage Modules Component Version Component Image Version PowerFlex 2.16.1 PowerStore 2.16.0 PowerMax 2.16.2 PowerScale 2.16.0 Unity XT 2.16.0 Authorization v2.x 2.4.0 Observability 1.14.0 Replication 1.14.0 Resiliency 1.15.0 COSI 1.0.0 Container Storage Modules Certified Operator 1.11.3 Images PowerStore Version/Digest Image 1.11.3 registry.connect.redhat.com/dell-emc/dell-container-storage-modules-operator@sha256:9547300ef7cca3a9e3f33ba43d01b3feb99a78c92bae0838b8f152fa90b80e45 2.16.0 registry.connect.redhat.com/dell-emc/dell-csm-powerstore@sha256:4be94a81d2bfdabacb686d3061ef9b71861f21efd6678b23c418c484dd10d2f9 1.14.0 registry.connect.redhat.com/dell-emc/dell-csm-metrics-powerstor… Show more", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.742126+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.390254+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8fce8875-e0ed-4791-a83a-f6e08c73f11d	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778220527.000107	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778220527.000107", "text": "Hi @rspazzol - what's needed from me (higher up)?", "type": "message", "user": "Khaled Ibrahim"}]	{"Khaled Ibrahim"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.74583+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.410927+00	delivered	2026-05-09
