2e590429-30fb-4e0a-b152-224cd582f105	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705400.000000", "text": "[Virtualization Migration Update]\\n\\n\\nCustomer complains about not being able to migrate floppy disk drives!!! It is more than 30 years ago since I used a floppy but I had to dig further why do we need one at 2026. VMware ships .flp disk images which contain the pvscsi drivers for windows installation. The drivers are not included in the Windows ISO so they have to be somehow available during installation. OCPVirt does not need these drivers so issue resolved.\\nMigration Parallelism\\nThe customer has managed to migrate 70 vms in parallel but by using 70 individual mtv plans each containing 1 vm.\\nI have captured output of one migration in AAP and will inspect the timings of each phase.\\nNeed to consider whether doing parallel pre/post checks will add any benefit in terms of time saving. e.g. Are we saving 10mins, 30 mins, 1 hr? Can we live with without parallelism and do the checks sequentially?\\nNeed to evaluate if the complexity of adding parallelism to the implementation could introduce more issues than the time saving benefit. e.g. We could have saved 1hr, but in some cases all the pre-checks are stucked somewhere and it is hard to con[8:51 PM]\\n[VM Migration Debugging Session]\\nToday Martin Necas from engineering joined us to debug a variety of issues.\\n\\nForemost the topic around migrating VMs with Shared Disks not take over their IP:\\nSuccessful workaround applied to the customer environment by making sure the VM is actually running before migration so the forklift controller can catch its metadata (this is done for all the VMs of the targeted VSphere), it stays in in-memory cache before the controller or its pod restarts (current caveat), a verbose warning is to be implemented to make the user aware of this process pattern.\\nWe migrated the VMs with their IPs preserved then. :check:\\n\\n\\n\\nNext, a constant pita was solved by a new flag in the Migration Plans:\\nspec.rdmAsLun=true\\nThats really great as it was something important pending at the customer, as they do not need change the disks any longer manually, or by a post-hook. :check:\\n\\nAlso, what is currently ongoing is that qemu-guest-agent sometimes not installs on Windows Servers, we gathered logs which have some hot leads to be followed up by engineering. :gear:\\nCase: https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\n\\nRegarding the VMware Tools Cleanup, there is a much more smooth and stable option on the horizon now, its an early dev-preview and therefore no where documented so far, but with 2.11.4 we can enable this featureGate in MTV:\\noc patch ForkliftController  -n openshift-mtv forklift-controller  --type=merge -p '{\\"spec\\": {\\"feature_vsphere_vmware_driver_removal\\": \\"true\\"}}'\\nIt contains most of the famous VMware removal script from Github including other findings from Red Hat to cleanup the VMs. Sudhir and the team agreed to start testing it with the ultimate goals of removing all the post-hook removal scripts currently scrubbing VMware Tools. :check:\\n\\nRegarding the Windows Failover Cluster issue to initialize and consume the shared disks we are still on going, with quite a range of potential error sources. Martin will now take it as priority and investigate in our RH labs. :wrench:\\nAt this point I want to highlight Martins amazing dedication to our HSBC project! He stayed with us in a marathon call for many hours answering and tackling wide range of customer questions until 11:00 pm at night in his timezone. Customer team was really impressed and pleased by that. If you got a few reward zone points to spare, Martin definitely deserves it :slightly_smiling_face: :+1: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PETROS_2EB3D870"}]	{U_PETROS_2EB3D870}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.364069+00	2026-05-26 23:38:27.167206+00	summarized	2026-05-26
8fdea01e-2e24-4270-9276-500e42b9e45c	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777704700.000000", "text": "[Windows restarts] Vinay mentioned they've noticed Windows VMs restarting up to 20 times as part of the migration. Any context on this? Is it expected behavior? Is there something that can be done to improve the situation?", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}]	{U_SAM_F28235E5}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.270147+00	2026-05-26 23:16:55.91611+00	summarized	2026-05-26
be96b70d-c128-4676-901e-3963c0a9eb32	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704800.000000	7777704806.000000	7	[{"ts": "7777704800.000000", "text": "[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\n\\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\\n\\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}, {"ts": "7777704801.000000", "text": "[Migration Update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\n\\nStart date confirmed May 5th\\n4 VMs may drop of scope (due RDM)\\nStill some issues in MIoX integrations with CRQ, may delay a bit the change approval (holidays 1 and 4)\\nTODO: Proactive Support Case\\nPilot Mexico:\\n\\nConfirmed availability dates for Fabric Mid June; Vimal to provide cluster readiness dates \\nTODO: Confirm with ACN the migration window for MX\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}, {"ts": "7777704802.000000", "text": "[Migration Update]\\nMigration prechecks run OK. Migration launched now. More news in 60 min (approx duration time of the migration) (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}, {"ts": "7777704803.000000", "text": "[Migration Update]\\n@atolani @Snehal Lalsare we already have some migraiton failures at \\"allocate disk\\" stage. If you can join the call ant take a look? Jus iin case we are facing a not-known issue like the XFS error or the Encrypted error\\nThey are not asking for us yet, so it is not urgent, but that will give @Snehal Lalsare a view on the Dynamics (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}, {"ts": "7777704804.000000", "text": "[Migration update]\\nAfter yesterday's problem with DELL storage, the scope for today's migration is being changed, removing those VMS, and it will probably delay the start hours. They haven't published the new scope yetRosemary Lynch  [9:44 AM]\\n[Delivery Report] is due to go out at noon GMT. Can the team review and update the Delivery Report before 11am GMT please?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}, {"ts": "7777704805.000000", "text": "[Migration update]\\nFirst Migraiton Bunlde was reduced to 7 VMs, with 2 failures (XFS Issues) and 5 successes\\nSecond Migration Bundle for today has been canceled, as all VMs were on DELL storage\\nNo news on third Bundle yet\\nWar room with Red Hat + HSBC + Dell still in progressPatricia de las Heras Granaglia  [11:42 AM]\\n[MIgration support for Next Week]\\nI am going to propose the same teams as this week. Next week we are only having migrations on 26,27,and 29 as 28 is holiday in India, but there is an additional \\"bundle\\" on 29 (ie, 4 migrations instead of 3)\\n\\nPosting the \\"roster\\" inside the thread, as it is too long to post it here (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_A8EBB692", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}, {"ts": "7777704806.000000", "text": "[Migration Update]\\nTomorrow we are again running migrations with no DEL storage; They haven't publishd the plan yet but it is highly probalme that the 8:00 AM Mingraiotn is cancelled and the other ones will run. I'll post more info as soon as ACN shares the detailed planCarina Almeida  [5:32 PM]\\n:battery: Happy Recharge Day, Red Hatters! :battery:\\nWishing the whole team a fantastic and relaxing long weekend. I hope everyone manage to take some time off to get recharged!\\n\\n:hammer_and_wrench: A massive thank you to the colleagues who is logging on tomorrow to cover migrations and to the ones working on Monday. Thank you for holding down the fort!\\n\\n:flag-in: Finally, safe travels to the team heading off to India this weekend.\\n\\nHave a great weekend, all! :sunglasses:\\nimage.png Carina Almeida  [5:44 PM]\\nand just before we all go.....\\n\\n:training_done:\\nHSBC Season 2 training is now on with all about People and Culture.\\n\\nPlease make sure you have your HSBC training done in time :wink:", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB", "thread_ts": "7777704800.000000"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB,U_GOOGLE_A8EBB692}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.301155+00	2026-05-26 23:27:25.503078+00	summarized	2026-05-26
90594646-d6f2-4bf6-9808-0b72679f0916	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705100.000000", "text": "[Due to their internal network setup missing firewalls...] We're being asked if we can prevent who can talk to the nodes and the kube api. Many ways to skin a cat. Stupid that it is required and not solved with a traditional firewall.\\n\\nAny thoughts?", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.333151+00	2026-05-26 23:31:59.221933+00	summarized	2026-05-26
4a74effd-6f09-474b-b496-056281d5a0f0	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778210802.000102	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778210802.000102", "text": "was added to proj-eos-mvp by Raffaele Spazzoli\\n.", "type": "message", "user": "Khaled Ibrahim"}]	{"Khaled Ibrahim"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.692777+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.418501+00	delivered	2026-05-09
6e907dfb-5bfa-4900-af5f-90553efa4488	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778193343.000163	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778193343.000163", "text": "Had this ping from the PM team for auth proxy as they try and prioritize. My view is we need this feature for 4.22 unless someone else says otherwise. @rspazzol @Rydekull @Nikos @Nick Evans\\nWallace Lewis\\nHi Sam!  I hope this message finds you well.\\nI'm an engineering director in OpenShift and the requirement to provide https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7054 for HSBC is on our list for planning our next release.  I'm trying to gather more details on timeline so we can prioritize this appropriately.  I've been told the plan is to have HSBC on 4.22 (now dev complete for us) until moving to 5.2 next year.  Can you confirm that's the plan and/or do you see a need to have this auth proxy feature available prior to our 5.2 release?  If this would be better to discuss in a short meeting, feel free to grab a time on my calendar that works for you.  Thanks in advance!\\nFrom a private conversation | Apr 23rd", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.457407+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.430535+00	delivered	2026-05-09
dea69be1-e3e1-41c0-be46-7a532bef1220	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778206076.000116	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778206076.000116", "text": "@Shebi were you looking at Windows Failover clustering with someone? There's a message in the VM Migration workstream on teams, mentioned it was\\"quite urgent\\"", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.859259+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.444258+00	delivered	2026-05-09
80517352-3617-4fef-ba50-2cd0b4a92ea7	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227129.000109	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227129.000109", "text": "[Migration Workstream - US]:\\nMoving the estate to the new datacenter requires a massive re-configuration of IP addresses across the board. Currently, the end-to-end automation required to orchestrate this does not exist.\\nI have started a Proof of Concept (PoC) to automate the IP address changes directly at the VM OS level. For now, this PoC operates in isolation, without factoring in the broader external network dependencies (DNS, Load Balancers, etc.).\\nThe Target End-to-End Workflow:\\nUltimately, we need to build and connect automation that handles the full lifecycle:\\nVM Migration -> Firewall Updates -> DNS Changes -> Load Balancer Changes\\nAppliances & Load Balancers:\\nScott J Wright is driving the appliances migrations. Currently, there is some self-service automation for F5 load balancers (for creating and deleting LBs) that a developer is working on. However, how this specifically fits into the  migration  is still unclear.\\nAction Items & Next Steps:\\nI proposed that we work directly with Scott to fully understand the capabilities of the existing F5 automation. (If anyone wants to join tomorrow let me know, 3:30 PM UK)\\nMichael will be collaborating with @rspazzol and me to map out the broader Network automation so we can start putting all these isolated pieces together for the US migration.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.767435+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.451618+00	delivered	2026-05-09
b6a551ce-db39-4f14-ae2a-0ffe25018f35	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778199874.000154	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778199874.000154", "text": "[Migration Support and Hypercare Thread]\\nI am opening this thread to keep all ideas together as I need to send our proposal by end of this week. Bear in mind that we can't invent a new process and need to adapt to what they have already defined (remember this is a Bank and they follow ITIL proceses), and their SLAs: While migrating a VM there are only 15minutes limit to decide to roll back, so all the ideas you are proposing IMO should be in a separate section of RCA . I'm putting everything together here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vYMFbZpGRjLOltrKqecQh06cpCp-8tkKLprEdCQwUAo/edit?tab=t.1q40s08up9xd#heading=h.wd3rd5djgvwy\\nGoogle Docs", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.318729+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.461963+00	delivered	2026-05-09
618714f5-6cae-4aaa-b5cd-adafefdadb9a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705700.000000", "text": "[pure storage driver upgrade issue] @Philip Jones @James Force I am trying to figure out where we are with all the email on the subject. Would it be fair to say that we fixed the issues in 104 and 102? Do we have a plan for future upgrades?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.405213+00	2026-05-26 23:42:41.180863+00	summarized	2026-05-26
9d20bdc2-f28f-4fef-887a-8083006b5653	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705800.000000", "text": "[Consulting Support Model during Migrations]\\nI've put together mi ideas and what I've proposed to ACN and HSBC as our support during migrations & hipercare in a Presentation format here: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1BJE9tmRgpDlAWTAtbRugZffAxIpJP6a7zkQKb75plWA/edit?slide=id.p1#slide=id.p1 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.416542+00	2026-05-26 23:44:25.112542+00	summarized	2026-05-26
53adaf8c-7ef8-4f13-9d89-b81da9e443f3	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705900.000000", "text": "[302 pure storage error] I think James Force is aware of it (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_19CE3B0A"}]	{U_GOOGLE_19CE3B0A}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.425705+00	2026-05-26 23:45:47.547569+00	summarized	2026-05-26
5213aafc-9d3e-4c0c-8f40-933ddbd75c68	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706000.000000", "text": "[Migration Pilot 2 update]\\nStarts today at 10:00 AM UK time and ends on Thursday. I am going to keep the \\"statistics\\" in this spreadsheet so you can check how migrations are progressing\\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0\\nGoogle SheetsPosted in eos-hsbc-virt | May 5th | View messageCarina Almeida  [10:50 AM]\\n@Rydekull @janine @jfeind  can you have a look at your training please? Thanks", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.472418+00	2026-05-26 23:48:19.239896+00	summarized	2026-05-26
46db996a-abea-4384-849e-d19328198d99	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705600.000000", "text": "[WAF and IDS] from reading the minutes of the Sheffield meeting, it looks like cilium will not be able to deliver WAF and IDS in the agreed time. new date seems to be November. @Nikos @Nikos FYI in case you want to make another attempt with OVN. @Shebi please confirm my understanding.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.395441+00	2026-05-26 23:41:10.86502+00	summarized	2026-05-26
d02b1a8e-85e2-420d-b910-d94bfd5f20c0	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778199834.000114	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778199834.000114", "text": "Morning all, just to confirm that EntraID issue on 301 is now confirmed as a proxy config issue. It isn't permitting traffic to graph.microsoft.com which is a requirement. Why they didn't just copy what they had enabled on the old proxies I have no idea. Regardless it will now be a change request that has to go through a CAB apparently so not a quick fix :disappointed:", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.831831+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.47452+00	delivered	2026-05-09
33f87bfa-ab21-4b07-a6dd-65a5960ecd0e	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778229628.000208	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778229628.000208", "text": "[Build update]\\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it.\\nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.083828+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.480996+00	delivered	2026-05-09
967bab08-60b0-4e3f-821b-35e6b8a0fa36	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778231529.000129	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778231529.000129", "text": "And why are you working at this time @atolani? 'go home' and speak to you tomorrow :wink:", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.026695+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.487531+00	delivered	2026-05-09
c446a609-0bc4-476e-ad3b-dff23ac60ce8	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778241371.000131	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778241371.000131", "text": "[netapp and storage offload] just a heads up, customer tried to do storage offload with netapp. this of course does not work. netapp has its own tool called shift toolkit. We have communicated the situation,", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.049655+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.495082+00	delivered	2026-05-09
