32607395-5d92-4180-85f4-58a893a881b2	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778226427.000187	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778226427.000187", "text": "How did the call with Pure go?", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.775579+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.558161+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3cbe94c8-8127-42ad-895b-c5392b00e638	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706200.000000", "text": "[Performance]\\n@Shebi @Rydekull\\nToday I got a preview on a document to be shared with us, which shows performance differences on a VM migrated to 104. It is a Oracle DB on RHEL 9 and there are quit some drops on Cluster 104 vs the Vsphere.\\nThe VMs in question are gbl25239315 and gbl25239316.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.512121+00	2026-05-26 23:53:20.873098+00	summarized	2026-05-26
587e8d0d-d5e1-4e8d-9cc0-e6fd02d76471	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706400.000000", "text": "[HK and re-ip] Vinay yesterday casually dropped that some VMs in HK will need Re-iping. We are learning how hard it is to re-ip here in NY. couple of things that came out yesterday that we didn't think about: OS-mounted NAS, VPNs, proxies. they are all also affected by the VM's IP change. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.54461+00	2026-05-26 23:56:47.989374+00	summarized	2026-05-26
9f06477a-6f8d-429e-a237-e5064b4552df	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706500.000000", "text": "[Weekly Planning] Look away now Gantt charts incoming... (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ROSEMA_0749D041"}]	{U_ROSEMA_0749D041}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.551878+00	2026-05-26 23:58:16.562498+00	summarized	2026-05-26
efe1d390-b09e-4209-a41a-75aceb71c5f1	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777715800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777715800.000000", "text": "Folks. I need to take time off today for some urgent work. I will be joining from tomorrow.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ARPIT_8F539902"}]	{U_ARPIT_8F539902}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.383802+00	2026-05-26 23:59:47.440459+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e420c85e-c022-4389-8449-37efe77b7ec6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706100.000000", "text": "[RBAC (Manifest & VNC Access)] @Shebi in Build status call toady Praveen asked for an update on the proposed solution that you committed to outline. Has this been sent & he missed it? It's around secret management and password rotation on local accounts using Hashi Vault. I've asked @janine if she can take this over from you as you will be away from desk for most of this week.", "type": "message", "user": "U_IMAGE_3227E706"}]	{U_IMAGE_3227E706}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.498786+00	2026-05-26 23:50:51.461833+00	summarized	2026-05-26
9639d4c1-76bd-49a9-b3aa-765747f8e8f7	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706300.000000", "text": "[Build of OpenShift Clusters] @James Force @Philip Jones @rspazzol @janine Question, when we deploy the clusters today, we dont add a ssh-key to the core user, do we? It seems commented out in the git files.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SUDHIR_58B5FB81"}]	{U_SUDHIR_58B5FB81}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.527877+00	2026-05-26 23:55:04.19913+00	summarized	2026-05-26
0738be78-06e9-477c-950d-e896be4dbd5f	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778202616.000136	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778202616.000136", "text": "Hi all - Are we involved in any of the discussions here?\\non the risk call today there is concern that the demise of the source VM hardware and a rebuild as a OpenShift is a risk to the velocity of the migrations as 1 this hasnt been tested and 2 the demise process isnt fully cordinated.  @James Force - is there any discussion in the build stream about these rebuilds? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Anne Maskell"}]	{"Anne Maskell"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.124637+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.573603+00	delivered	2026-05-09
0695dc1b-ff8c-4c0b-8c9c-d2837e0940b5	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778225086.000226	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778225086.000226", "text": "[VM Migration]\\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \\n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.\\nAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.28507+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.593546+00	delivered	2026-05-09
a84c821a-ae5d-41d4-ac93-04b23267c768	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778203997.000137	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778203997.000137", "text": "[Delivery Report]\\nHi team,  Can you all please put in your updates from last Thursday to today to the template: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0#slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0 I will be sending this out at 11am tomorrow. Please ensure that you update the main body by close of business today. Thank you all.", "type": "message", "user": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}]	{"Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.135102+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.601061+00	delivered	2026-05-09
e6d70d7f-5c75-4792-99da-fbd563c46fb8	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778230049.000269	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778230049.000269", "text": "Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.730525+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.607075+00	delivered	2026-05-09
c8c2a450-1834-49e4-8db6-bff4a1e4ff1c	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778223086.000146	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778223086.000146", "text": "Hi @pdelashe, just reviewing the open support cases....can proactive case https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04414181 be closed now? If, so, are you able to close it as you raised it IIRC?", "type": "message", "user": "Nick Evans"}]	{"Nick Evans"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.238706+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.611567+00	delivered	2026-05-09
2451cdb5-902b-45e9-89ef-e45ccaabb5ba	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778231727.000147	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778231727.000147", "text": "[OS drivers] @atolani @jfeind there is an email thread from Abhishek to which I am being added about issues that we are still having with the OS drivers for windows. This typically means that we are not making progress. Can you summarize the issue and the plan to resolve it. Also anything you need?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.248884+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.61921+00	delivered	2026-05-09
7c2b1bee-63bc-4adf-835b-087e8ba09a03	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706700.000000", "text": "[Migration update 2nd Batch] 18 VMs failed. @Petros @janine @Rydekull can anyone join the bridge for triage?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.565502+00	2026-05-27 00:01:43.722093+00	summarized	2026-05-26
2e319409-a626-418f-8a56-b73669ca8239	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706800.000000", "text": "[VIB Version Issue] @Rydekull @janine Abhishek reached out to me to get more help about this. Based on his message, he does not fully understand the need of specific VIB versions and their relation to MTV versions. Can you please help him with a way forward? Roy is also engaged on this in case we need engineering support.\\n\\nLet me know if I can somehow help, I want to give him a clear way for thought Roy was support :grimacing:). (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_8416E06D"}]	{U_GOOGLE_8416E06D}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.574464+00	2026-05-27 00:03:43.193518+00	summarized	2026-05-26
dd7635d0-7b56-494e-a958-87d46d46eb3b	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778229041.000161	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778229041.000161", "text": "[observability]\\nPR to add alert rules to Otel Collector - thank you @James Force\\nPR to add extra namespaces in logging\\nRemoved filters in CLF targetting cyber Splunk. Will review this with Rijo tomorrow. Last 24h with filters in place: data ingestion of 18G from 104\\nNeed to mod. Trident config to allow for https-metrics. Might have a catch up with @James Force if/when available next.", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.430595+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.626661+00	delivered	2026-05-09
19e30323-ab54-458a-affd-82aa1e569285	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778235942.000162	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778235942.000162", "text": "[bsod] MTV 2.11.4-2 seems to solve most of teh bsod-related problems that other customers have been experiencing by installing the latest VirtIO-Win 1.9.57 drivers. It would be grate if we could upgrade top this version. @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.441071+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.633428+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8acb0426-c368-4021-ab56-89939fa588ec	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219582.000002	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219582.000002", "text": "[michele meetings] We have everyday meetings with Michele, who is getting up to speed with all of the architecture design/decisions taken in the last few months. Not very interesting meetings so far. The only real meat in the discussion is how many ACM clusters should we have and where. I think we are moving towards the idea of having as few as possible of these cluster (maybe 2 UK and HCK). There is also a vague idea of using these ACM clusters to consolidate in teh future some other infra functions which have the same granularity, namely the rpm cache server and the AAP instances. Licence issues aside this seems like a good idea to me. As you probably remember one of our design principles is that if ACM dies, the workload clusters should keep working normally. For the consultant/architects, if you see any ACM policy that invalidates our principle, please let me know. This approach reduces the responsibility of ACM to: cluster installation (including gitops kickstart), centralized VM management tool (optional). In general the responsibilities are so limited that one can question the value of having ACM (I certainly am doing that). Michele would also like to activate the centralized observability capability.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.285993+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.639336+00	delivered	2026-05-09
835c0113-cf72-42d8-b54e-174395c7c7a9	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778226558.000018	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778226558.000018", "text": "[Upcoming Recharge days]\\nTeam,\\n:reminder_string: Our upcoming recharge days are booked for the 22nd May and 28th August.\\nPlease note the bank has been informed of those days and that we plan to be off then.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.683207+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.6468+00	delivered	2026-05-09
f9c3f85b-af45-43c8-b1f3-bfb4b2f90374	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778206646.000026	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778206646.000026", "text": "Haha, one of my old customers joined this project from ACN's side last week. I taught him OpenShift (3) :smile: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.835246+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.654883+00	delivered	2026-05-09
ba54d886-764e-4d53-b8d6-9cc50f63de11	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778229235.000175	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778229235.000175", "text": "[observability]\\nadded netapp-trident namespace to log-forwarder filter + added regex patterns to message filter\\nsimulated a kustomize patch definition for the region based endpoints in anticipation for live changes next week\\nworking with Onkar to provide powermax metrics to stor team", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.618885+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.665928+00	delivered	2026-05-09
86b0b131-18cf-41e3-a01a-185cca2abedd	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778237937.000177	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778237937.000177", "text": "[node drain] Balamurugan is saying that draining nodes takes so long that the VMs eventually fail to live migrate and they have to be manually moved. This should not be happening even if storage is slow. I asked him to open a case and to involve @Shebi . @James Force you are also in that conversation so perhaps you can add more color.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.642475+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.674311+00	delivered	2026-05-09
6ce8e077-1d45-478e-804a-bf3f6a4fac9f	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778212290.000030	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778212290.000030", "text": "[Migration Retro Call]\\nSTOP. Waiting for people to show up at the Incident Bridge. Agreed to establish a reasonable time and if no one shows up, decide to roll back\\nSTOP. Bringing so many people to the call to troubleshoot.\\nSTART. SRE Team should have access to OCP, VCenter, etc, etc (some of them did not have)\\nSTART? Shall Red Hat have a SNOW group so they can assign icidents to us? I've asked ACN to confirm with Vinay first\\nRCA and propose a solution (if it ends up being  platform incompatibility). I've updated the proactive support case to see if we can get help from Support, and Shebi is collecting a list of similar issues and solutions", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.345061+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.681988+00	delivered	2026-05-09
ad850b5b-cc68-4faf-a688-b05b49768db8	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778226293.000173	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778226293.000173", "text": "[Labels - Data Architecture - Affinity and Anti-Affinity Discussions]:\\nPart 1: The Aspirational Design (Gareth & Michele)\\nWe successfully validated a strategy to model our physical failure domains in OpenShift to enable High Availability via Affinity/Anti-Affinity rules. This relies on tagging OpenShift nodes and VMs with three critical dimensions: Country, Data Center, and Fabric.\\nWe mapped out exactly how to inject these labels across three journeys using Unicorn as the primary System of Record:\\nCluster Build (GitOps): Querying Unicorn via bare-metal hostnames to label OpenShift nodes.\\nVM Migration (MIOX): Pulling metadata to inject labels into the VM manifests during migration.\\nNew VM Provisioning (Ansible/ITSP): Having Ansible query Unicorn to label net-new VMs at creation.\\nPart 2: The Reality Check (Rushi)\\nWhen I reviewed this with Rushi, he rightly pointed out that while this looks great on paper, it is highly aspirational for our day-to-day operations.\\nThe Bottleneck: Strict Affinity/Anti-Affinity requires heavy coordination with Application Owners to define these rules properly.\\nThe Operational Reality: In the event of an outage, VM Admins are solely focused on restoring services immediately. They will not have the time to debug why a VM isn’t scheduling due to Anti-Affinity constraints.\\nPart 3: The Alternative Proposal (Service Classes)\\nTo solve this, Rushi proposed a much more pragmatic, DR-focused approach: Service Classes (Priority Levels).\\nInstead of forcing App Owners to define complex affinity rules, we simply ask them to define the priority of their service.\\nIn the event of a massive failure (e.g., node, rack, or hall), the platform aggressively evacuates and live-migrates the High Priority VMs to healthy nodes.\\nLow Priority VMs are simply stopped/powered down to free up capacity for the critical workloads.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.591695+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.687009+00	delivered	2026-05-09
db8bbd61-5f55-4a37-b9af-40682111c261	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778276189.000209	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778276189.000209", "text": "[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessible\\nThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.098238+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.696241+00	delivered	2026-05-09
