5a304454-4c79-4815-88a7-51a9f639ce24	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777707900.000000	7777707904.000000	5	[{"ts": "7777707900.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Carina Almeida  [11:26 AM]\\n[VIB - update from the build call this morning]\\n\\nIn this morning's build call, Nitesh mentioned that the VIB workaround did not work and on 13th there are 18 VMs in the migration plan that will be impacted by the VIB.\\n\\n@Sam Marland @Nikos can you help with the sync with Roy - FYI @janine is you point of contact on build re. this.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PLEASE_8E4FCE90"}, {"ts": "7777707901.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Philip Jones  [11:19 AM]\\nHas Red Hat ever considered providing Quay as a SaaS offering? This could be cloud hosted and customers could have their own private VPN or direct connect option to reach it.\\n\\nIt could provide the a full mirror of content for OCP, Operators, etc etc. Customers could have some limited admin capabilities to sync specific additional images, setup their preferred image scanner etc...\\n\\nThat way, they have a performant, reliable solution with all the content available immediately. Something like this might work for many customers who don't want to use a public registry and prefer to have their own image scanning etc in place.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TC_ACAFE313", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}, {"ts": "7777707902.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nIf you have not done so already please log your time sheets in Clarity (was due Friday) and your Red Hat time card in PSA please before 11am.James Force  [9:48 AM]\\nFolks, just gonna be a little late starting today (~1 hour), just need to do some personal admin this morning", "type": "message", "user": "U_TIME_3519BFBB", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}, {"ts": "7777707903.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:08 PM]\\n@pdelashe I'm available for the next 3 hours if you need some coverage in the was room. I assume many other have taken recharge day", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_460B8EAB", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}, {"ts": "7777707904.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nIf you have not done so already please log your time sheets in Clarity (was due Friday) and your Red Hat time card in PSA please before 11am.Raffaele Spazzoli  [9:35 AM]\\n[platform tasks] I have been catching up with Rushi. There are several platform tasks pending. not sure if they have made progress recently. These tasks are being managed by @Rosemary Lynch so perhaps @Rosemary Lynch we should have a stand up dedicated just to these tasks. I'll add here the discussion I had with Rushi on them.\\n\\nEntra and service accounts -- @Shebi -- a final explanation/diagram is missing. In particular something tat shows that a user with certain entitlement can only get the sa token of the cluster they are entitled to.\\nCIS compliance -- not sure who is assigned to this -- hsbc is not apply because the OCP CIS v1.9.0 and the OCP-V CIS v.1.0.0 have been released but the compliance operator is not capable of reporting on teh new checks. HSBC does not want to go the custom checks route. So I believe the only option is to open an RFE to the compliance operator team to get those checks updated. There is also apparently a discrepancy between in the TLS check between what the operator expects and what the suggested configuration does.\\nuse case write up  for remote workers -- @rspazzol \\nVNC access via SA. Additional checks must be added when using this approach. We have to checks that the user has entitlements on that VM and that there is a change request open. @rspazzol to talk with Shwetali and design this.\\nGitops workflow documentation -- @Philip Jones -- the workflow that hsbc wants to use on the gitops repo is still not fully fleshed out. @Philip Jones I'd like to get a status o what you have done so far. I'll also talk to Shwetali and Prerana to understand what use cases they want to support.\\nLab cluster instabilities -- @Philip Jones -- I assume this is a continuous learning task. we need a status update.\\n\\n\\nthere were more open items, but Rushi was not worried about them. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_TIME_3519BFBB", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}]	{U_PLEASE_8E4FCE90,U_TC_ACAFE313,U_TIME_3519BFBB,U_PATRIC_460B8EAB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.765756+00	2026-05-27 00:22:06.338265+00	summarized	2026-05-26
a114ed56-e892-4a3a-b4d2-77a567820a89	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777707800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777707800.000000", "text": "[Migration Errors]\\nRelated to Sam Marland and to prevent same issues being addressed by different teams in parallel , I've created this summary of errors table in my spreadsheet to keep track of those migraiotn errors that are on our side, who is assesing them and where the solution should be applied. Feel free to change/add/remove anything, ok?. But letś keep all errors tracked together to prevent \\"pani\\" mode :slightly_smiling_face: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/edit?gid=422593593#gid=422593593 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.759361+00	2026-05-27 00:15:06.933218+00	summarized	2026-05-26
