f97b02c9-d5f5-485e-8a63-983c815bd937	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778204368.000088	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778204368.000088", "text": "@rspazzol\\nNitesh and Srinath are asking about the handling of using DevPreview or Upstream Features (like the MTV-wait-hook) in production. Current status is that it is considered a governance/architectural decision which needs to made by HSBC and Red Hat, but as you see on the Email thread he is looking for a \\"written conclusion\\" on that.\\nIs this currently being discussed, or has there some common consensus been set with the customer already?", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.4806+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.105436+00	delivered	2026-05-09
ffada008-fe4c-47a9-b7b7-49292595dc7b	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778245662.000282	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778245662.000282", "text": "Update on the plan for oauth proxy.\\nKevin Rizza\\nhey Sam, we are still assessing all the work that needs to happen. at this point we believe that making this change for the oauth stack is something we will target to backport to 4.22. we are still looking at all the edge cases, so we don't have a firm commitment on exactly what date it would land, but we're trying to get this done in the 5.0 release timeframe and then work on a backport once that's done.\\nwe're tracking all that effort here https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/OCPSTRAT-3174, and I'll keep regular weekly updates in that ticket\\nFrom a private conversation | May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.847351+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.066548+00	delivered	2026-05-09
