2f5b4afc-4f5b-45d5-ba2d-5632e2572e25	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778206469.000089	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778206469.000089", "text": "[Migration update]\\nEverything on track for Pilot Phase 2; working on Planning\\nI've just learned today that there seems to be another program/project going on  with higher priority than EOS that has an impact on ITSOs availability and dedication. This is going to be included in the big RAID Log", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.492123+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.118451+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8436f3bd-42e4-4363-9578-fbfea6b33909	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778215052.000092	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778215052.000092", "text": "[build meeting]\\nencrypted etcd. this request came today. This feature never made any sense to me as the key is on the same disk as the etcd database. Can anyone help me figure out the value? @Rydekull @Shebi @janine. Things are improving on that front because kube is starting  to support fetching the key from a KMS, is anyone familiar with that feature (it is not mentioned on our docs)\\nremote workers. all blockers removed, we should continue testing on Monday. This has the highest  priority. So I gace my full availability. @James Force you are assigned to it. please let me know if you cannot give it full attention.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.527886+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.124712+00	delivered	2026-05-09
8123db45-b9ba-4c61-99ac-288b5c2f6168	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708700.000000", "text": "[gantt review call]", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.809531+00	2026-05-27 00:33:01.093329+00	summarized	2026-05-26
fe75b1c7-b352-4d05-83e6-1299b45b576d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708800.000000", "text": "[When / if re-IP of a VM occurs] Unicorn will need to be updated, since its central to so many other tools. I believe Unicorn will be updated without us needing to do anything. But just writing this so you remember that this needs to be done for any VM that changes IP (regardless if its US or HK or wherever).\\n\\nUnicorn is apparently the source of info for IPs for other tools, or in fact, ODS is, that pull from Unicorn.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.814097+00	2026-05-27 00:34:50.043543+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e46f4c2f-a349-4a99-a74c-1ae9daeb753d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708900.000000", "text": "[Issues escalated to ESS - TAM]: We escalated today 4 issues impacting the migration:\\n\\nCase 04408443 and related RHEL-165220\\nCase 04442406 and related MTV-5368\\nCase 04432578 and related MTV-5349\\nCase 04435341\\nI created one ACE escalation to gather attention from engineering to get the issues solved before the next migration next week.\\nOur escalations are currently missing project timelines. We must clearly document the project impact and exact timelines in these cases so Engineering can see the immediate dependencies and prioritize fixes accordingly. @pdelashe I am not sure about this, I think we have communicated timelines with ESS/TAM, but I am not sure.\\nTo bypass support delays, the team is mandated to gather logs proactively for these failing scenarios. I asked them to request the logs directly in the support case, so the customer gets familiar with the process.\\nA new dedicated Slack channel has been created for rapid communication and incident management for these specific EOS critical cases.\\nKathinka created with my help this document to share with engineering about the support cases being escalated: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LACIffqYUWCgC4NtIVyDEcfEWvC0LIPbpu8tjp12fao/edit?tab=t.0\\n:jira: RHEL-165220 [Integration] : virt-v2v with sun partition table and Veritas storage failed with: parted exited with status 1: Warning: The disk CHS geometry reported by the operating system does not match the geometry stored on the disk labelAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler:jira: MTV-5368 [New] : Copy-offload: VMs with many disks fail with \\"failed to get the VIB version\\" due to unthrottled concurrent esxcli callsAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [6:16 PM]\\n[US Migration Workstream]:\\nTimeline Alignment (Project ECB): Srinath is scheduling a sync with Nitesh and the US team to align our remaining development efforts (IP changes, DNS, LB, Firewall, Unicorn, etc) with the official ECB migration dates.\\nMulti-NIC Re-IP Automation: We need Ansible support (@Petros / @atolani) to finalize the automation for VMs with multiple network interfaces. We are looking at using the QEMU guest agent or OS cmdlets to push the IP changes, but we need to validate this against our existing pipelines.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.818287+00	2026-05-27 00:38:52.560572+00	summarized	2026-05-26
51669db1-ec38-4b16-8322-2865daf1585f	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778195097.000297	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778195097.000297", "text": "[Migration Errors]\\nRelated to Sam Marland and to prevent same issues being addressed by different teams in parallel , I've created this summary of errors table in my spreadsheet to keep track of those migraiotn errors that are on our side, who is assesing them and where the solution should be applied. Feel free to change/add/remove anything, ok?. But letś keep all errors tracked together to prevent \\"pani\\" mode :slightly_smiling_face: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/edit?gid=422593593#gid=422593593 (edited) \\nGoogle Sheets", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:26.041102+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.147586+00	delivered	2026-05-09
