8890e384-b556-4b9c-b56a-c08c88bfd3da	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778242439.000179	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778242439.000179", "text": "[architecture documentation] with regards to this thread https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C099TDJDDKL/p1776434503713569 , I hope everyone is making progress. Here is my update:\\n@janine has been helping me creating teh documentation that was assigned by Vijay to Michele, we should be in decent spot enough to keep Vijay happy. @janine will keep working with Michele in my absence.\\n@Carina Almeida please keep people accountable to complete their documentation. the deadline is Friday 5/1\\nPS: I have been in many projects in which red hat has been in defect because we didn't deliver the documentation. Let's make sure this is not one of those.\\nRaffaele Spazzoli\\n[arch documentation] we need to finish the following pieces of architecture docs in two weeks. Please let's sure we deliver on this, as red hatter we are notoriously slow/bad at this part..:\\ncompute design for non-hic, status: empty, assigned: Michele, Raf and now @janine\\nsecurity: status: Natty populated it: @Rydekull to review, lean and filter. This is the piece that concerns Vijay\\ndata architecture (i.e. labels and annotation): populated by Gareth. @Shebi to review and approve. @Shebi since you are also following teh migration track, let';s make sure this guidance is implemented. I have not seen those labels on the migrated VMs. I could be wrong though.\\nTertiary Vault: sta… Show more\\nThread in proj-eos-mvp | Apr 17th | View message", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.669619+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.335114+00	delivered	2026-05-09
c559155b-5faf-4bc3-9b1c-b1b1701e3f1a	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778257915.000295	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778257915.000295", "text": "[vibe coding] it turned out that all the nice tools that Vinay teams is coming out with are partially vibe coded by Vinay himself. So we started talking a bit about spec-driven development and I shared my methodology (bmad) . Michael P. will now develop an operator, Vinay will try it. @Shebi was already coding away. All in all, the world is changing, take a look at what is happening and learn the new methodologies. you can do it for free for now as long as red hat is paying for your tokens... (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:26.017926+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.156035+00	delivered	2026-05-09
359e3467-1f43-427f-b9cc-6c2b50398856	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778193356.000296	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778193356.000296", "text": "Case - https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04442406\\nAbhishek has raised this case over night. It appears linked to the issue from yesterday with the machine with many disks. My intention is to share this ASAP in the migration-blockers-nda-customer channel for focus. It is going to be difficult to get focus with everyone about to travel to Summit. @Rydekull I think you're closest to this from a debug perspective. Can you share any more context you've seen during debugging so we can help engineering?", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:26.028803+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.16265+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3d5a8944-1ac8-4aee-b654-b2ab00cc4581	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709300.000000", "text": "[dinner with hsbc] Vinay has reiterated how much he likes to work with redhat. He likes something about our transparency and openness that he does not get from the other vendors. Let's continue this way.\\nThey also shared that likely n a few weeks the NDA will be lifted. As soon as we get to the point where communication of this project will be given to hundred of ITSO, there is no point in continuing with the NDA.\\nThey also shared that once the NDA is lifted, there is an intention to open source MIO-X. The modalities still have to be defined, stay tuned....Carina Almeida  [1:31 PM]\\n:guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\\n\\nTo help us get through this programme and customer's build/migration blockers, we’ve officially started a team Spotify playlist: https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\\n\\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote tomorrow after our internal stand-up :wink:\\n\\nIn the meantime, keep the beat on! :headphones:", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.843319+00	2026-05-27 00:41:19.834795+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e0147672-6cc7-462a-b14c-df52101fef22	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778207419.000139	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778207419.000139", "text": "[Migration Failure Process Workshop]\\nGoal: Improve the failure management as it is not clear who needs to do what, and in particular SLAs\\nGoal2: Vinay has asked ACN to be more proactive on the initial Triage\\nWe reviewed the process drafted by ACN (Image on Teams) and modified some responsabilities and SLAs\\nActions:\\na) All Miox Logs posted in Splunk should be available for the team that is doing the triage\\nb) ACN to review a Confluence Knowledgebase of Miox Errors = Solutions or whom to call\\nc) Escalate to the Program what to do if ITSOs do not respond in the agreed time (30') either rollback or move to hypercare, or someone to talk to ITSO to clarify the importance of responding in time\\nd) Red Hat (me) to send our proposal on how we want to collaborate with the Command Center and support triage", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.15864+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.403687+00	delivered	2026-05-09
7639d894-7e95-4728-886a-b8278d551f38	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228214.000174	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228214.000174", "text": "PJ - Build:\\nMore investigation of Pure Storage Issue\\nPulled into a call with SRE team who want to have a solution for silencing all alerts for maintenance windows or during cluster build / deployments.\\nJoined a called regarding new cluster hk307. Three nodes not joining the cluster correctly. One registered as a node, but showing as not available. Two are just awol. I couldn't find any issues with the nodes or config, the HK networking team are claiming no issues there side either, but I think we need to get on a call with them to resolve. I've also adding the toolbox container to oc-mirror so we can run more troubleshooting on nodes as required.\\nAttended a call (along with Raffa) with Dell to discuss CSM Operator issues. The call was positive and they've acknowledged some problems with the existing operator. Hopefully future operator versions will work out of the box (so to speak).\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.606855+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.437234+00	delivered	2026-05-09
cd33e312-f3de-4c01-9dda-29b46e053970	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778195282.000182	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778195282.000182", "text": "[US/MX Workshops]: We have a request for the workshop to clarify our support engagement in both pilots (Test Migrations) and production migration (Volume Migrations). I need help from @Anne @Carina Almeida , @pdelashe, even @Nikos if you have any slides, ideas, workflows, screenshots, documents, share it them here and I will create a slide out of this. My understanding is the following about both process:\\nPilot Migrations (Consulting-Led)\\nDuring the pilot phase, Red Hat Consulting will be heavily involved in the execution and troubleshooting. The goal here is to establish our baseline and refine our automation.\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution.\\nExecution: Consulting is involved in the communication structure of the migration (we are passive listeners here).\\nFailure Handling (The New RCA Proposal): If a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back in VMware. The failed OpenShift VM is then moved to an isolated “Quarantine/Triage” environment. (Note: This isolation environment is not currently in place; we will officially propose building this during the upcoming workshops).\\nResolution: Consulting performs Root Cause Analysis (RCA) in the triage environment, finds the issue and ask for the fixes the underlying automation (Narender), and places the VM back into the backlog to be rescheduled for a future migration wave.\\n2. Volume / Production Migrations (Support-Led)\\nOnce we move into bulk production migrations, the execution and issue resolution will shift entirely to our Support organization.\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution to ensure global readiness.\\nExecution & Failure Handling: Handled 100% by Red Hat Support. This will leverage our Technical Account Managers (TAMs) across the different timezones to ensure “follow-the-sun” coverage, alongside the recently onboarded ESS team.\\nResolution: The Support and ESS teams will drive immediate break/fix resolutions and coordinate any necessary escalations directly.\\nPlease review this logic and let me know your thoughts or if you see any gaps.\\nThis message was deleted.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.708745+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.528775+00	delivered	2026-05-09
f79942ba-525a-4bd0-b85d-5022bfc74418	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778276029.000229	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778276029.000229", "text": "{Migration}\\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has \\"Windows Server\\" or not.. If it has, patch it\\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\\n --type merge\\n -p '{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"domain\\":{\\"devices\\":{\\"video\\":{\\"type\\":\\"virtio\\"}}}}}}}'\\nBut with automation i have few questions.\\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...", "type": "message", "user": "Arpit Tolani"}]	{"Arpit Tolani"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.315945+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.56454+00	delivered	2026-05-09
5e6ddf22-45d4-4d14-b038-13edd1c3a9eb	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227799.000239	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227799.000239", "text": "[Virtualization Migration Update]\\nCustomer complains about not being able to migrate floppy disk drives!!! It is more than 30 years ago since I used a floppy but I had to dig further why do we need one at 2026. VMware ships .flp disk images which contain the pvscsi drivers for windows installation. The drivers are not included in the Windows ISO so they have to be somehow available during installation. OCPVirt does not need these drivers so issue resolved.\\nMigration Parallelism\\nThe customer has managed to migrate 70 vms in parallel but by using 70 individual mtv plans each containing 1 vm.\\nI have captured output of one migration in AAP and will inspect the timings of each phase.\\nNeed to consider whether doing parallel pre/post checks will add any benefit in terms of time saving. e.g. Are we saving 10mins, 30 mins, 1 hr? Can we live with without parallelism and do the checks sequentially?\\nNeed to evaluate if the complexity of adding parallelism to the implementation could introduce more issues than the time saving benefit. e.g. We could have saved 1hr, but in some cases all the pre-checks are stucked somewhere and it is hard to continue the migration or troubleshoot!", "type": "message", "user": "Petros Petrou"}]	{"Petros Petrou"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.410904+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.584696+00	delivered	2026-05-09
916a590b-ae74-4761-bba3-bd95c6e2cbd5	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709600.000000", "text": "[wibdows sql server performance] @jfeind I believe you were seeing windows sqlserver performance degradation. Please take a loom at this doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BeJ-eOc4lqpkU-apddFAfekUSxAFKSuVkrC3XHLQPjw/edit?tab=t.0 if it applies, please sanitize jpmc name and share it with the customer.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.861152+00	2026-05-27 00:43:11.085904+00	summarized	2026-05-26
736d4693-2694-4a86-9bab-5585c203354a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709400.000000", "text": "[Maj / Carina sync]\\n\\nUS: The US session was very quiet as most participants joined remotely; only one person attended in person.\\nThe deep dive session re. re-IP was highly successful, though significant work remains. I noted that we are looking into bringing a consultant to help with this.  Maj suggests hiring a consultant who can work UK hours to better align with the majority of the team.\\n\\nMexico: The Mexico team is ready to begin and even attended sessions on their day off.\\nA list of required trainees has been compiled during the visit, including a request for Spanish speakers. Maj has identified 24 names, which match the ATL list. Maj will liaise with ATL and explain the request. Carina needs to double check with GLS about the Spanish speaker instructor.Jens Feind  [3:24 PM]\\n[Bulk Migration]\\nToday we had several runs with Bulk Migration holding approx 57 VMs per Migration Plan.\\n12-16 VMs do migrate successfully while the others fail.\\nIts an interesting topic, as the variation of error says:\\n\\"No VSphereXcopyVolumePopulator CR found - populator may not have been created or was deleted\\"\\nor\\n\\"populator pod failed\\"\\nThe latter error message in the populator pod log actually complains \\"failed to ensure VIB is installed\\"\\nChecked with Devdatt that the ESXi hosts in question are all running on VIB 0.3.0\\n\\nThe second issue might be tackle with 2.11.6 release as it states in its notes:\\nhttps://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/migration_toolkit_for_virtualization/2.11/html-single/release_notes/index#ref_resolved-issues-2-11-6_release-notes\\n\\nDevdatt is creating a support case now, I will highlight it to the TAM team.\\ndocs.redhat.comRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRaffaele Spazzoli  [4:38 PM]\\n@Philip Jones I need your help in understanding something. we were thinking on re-purposing 102 to hic deployment. probably 2 cluster each of 6 nodes. of course the biggest change is the deployment of cilium and teh configuration of BGP. Michael said this is not possible without bringing in new HW (specifically a netscaler router) to handle the VTEP. But my understanding is that the VTEP is only needed when stretching the networks, not strictly when enabling BGP. What is your point of view?", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.849018+00	2026-05-26 01:27:00.267439+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
481cbe07-3b95-4628-b4b4-e7b131ad3ffa	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778224012.000172	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778224012.000172", "text": "[Bulk Migration Testing with AAP]: Latency & AAP Platform: Magnus confirmed that a latency of around 400ms is acceptable, meaning no architectural changes to the AAP platform are required right now. We have also increased the UK database CPU to 18 and applied Red Hat’s fine-tuning recommendations.\\nMigration SLAs & Strategy: The acceptable duration for VM migrations is set between 45 minutes and 1 hour 15 minutes. Our target split is 80% via storage offloading and 20% via cold migration.\\nResource Consumption Testing: Because the Hong Kong lab is still under construction, Nitesh and Abhishek will conduct the next round of testing in the UK environment. We need to measure exact CPU, memory, and disk consumption during both Linux and Windows migrations to accurately calculate capacity needs.\\nFuture Re-IP Scenarios: @janine told that future migrations requiring IP changes will involve additional pre- and post-migration automation tasks, taking longer. We will measure both standard and re-IP migration patterns and add safety buffers for unexpected scenarios.\\nRecent Test Results: Abhishek confirmed that the recent 52 migrations had some failures, but they were not Ansible-related. The team is fixing these issues and will avoid problematic VM scenarios in the upcoming tests.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.576634+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.704279+00	delivered	2026-05-09
a03183ef-2f19-4bdc-909d-751fee6923b4	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219271.000291	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219271.000291", "text": "[US Migrations] @Shebi current status:\\ngenerally: they expect to have to report stauts / progress more often beginning next week. seems they get some mgmt attention.\\nJune got pointed to another repo where he shall put his playbook and where another pb sits that he should invoke. nothing to do from our side here.\\nThey asked if you had started anything on the multi NIC linux use case.\\nThey asked us to kickstart the re-IPing automation for windows VMs. I';ve reached out to the windows team, will need to file a \\"formal\\" request to the program lead so we can get a peek into what the Widnwos team did when they re-IPed VMs. @Carina Almeida pinging you here, if you could let me know how this request to the pgrogram leads works, I'd be eternally grateful :slightly_smiling_face:\\nThey seem focussed on the VM side of things, who's responsible for the other necessary things (LB, DNS, app config, etc.)?", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}]	{"Janine Eichler"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.967815+00	2026-05-12 05:07:54.821995+00	delivered	2026-05-09
a7b5f218-c456-4884-aeef-15d6399918f9	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778230801.000001	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778230801.000001", "text": "[Sync on Engineering Prio CAP-978 EOSBank” meeting]: Overall, it was a productive session, and we identified a few key areas where we need to refine our approach:\\nPriority & Expectation Alignment: Raffaele and I noticed a lack of synchronization between the bank’s priorities/impact and our own. Moving forward, we need to make a conscious effort to ensure our internal priorities are synced with the customer’s expectations so we are always pushing on the right levers.\\nTAM Integration & Architectural Context: The TAMs are a fantastic addition to the team! However, to maximize their impact, we need to fast-track their onboarding. We have established a working dynamic, but it needs refinement. Specifically, we need to proactively provide the TAMs with much deeper architectural context so they can drive more value for the project. @Carina Almeida this is for the call we need for next week, most likely.\\nRFE & Support Case Rhythm: Stepping back to analyze our Support Cases and RFEs in this format was incredibly useful to see what is truly important and what might be missing from our radar. We agreed that we need to establish a regular cadence for these alignment meetings. @Nikos @rspazzol add something if I missed", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.259865+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.167792+00	delivered	2026-05-09
2019a02f-eb80-46d9-96c6-39c5624e5c4d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710000.000000", "text": "[Storage Offload overloading the storage]: On the migrations on Wednesday I saw many  migration-plan* pods on pending state, the error was\\nO/22 nodes are available: pod has unbound immediate PersistentVolumeClaims. preemption: 0/22 nodes are available: 22\\nPreemption is not helpful for schedulingI am assuming we were not doing storage offload and all the migrations went to the regular storage migration path. Has anyone seen that before?\\n2 files Carina Almeida  [10:49 AM]\\n[Migration Bucket 1 ]\\n\\n- Bundle 3A - starting at 10am BST - 46 VMs\\nMigration started at 10:01\\n\\nRH team - @Shebi @jfeind and I\\nI'll ping you if / when needed :wink: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.881378+00	2026-05-26 02:22:00.351378+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
a2cca23d-67c7-4543-93c1-7439cc4ab121	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709800.000000", "text": "[Build Git Ops Strategy]", "type": "message", "user": "U_ROSEMA_0749D041"}]	{U_ROSEMA_0749D041}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.872933+00	2026-05-27 00:44:37.160973+00	summarized	2026-05-26
606e3f36-0ee7-4e4a-a712-b8b99852e031	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710800.000000", "text": "[Migration]\\nFor TC-13 & 14.\\n\\nUsecase talks about Migrating Multi Homing VMs from vmware to OCP & talks about testing if the migrated VM wont change the nic names & IP provided to interfaces will be same as before after migraiton.\\n\\nin Windows Boxes, Specific NIC is mapped to specific adapter using MAC ID. & That adapter is assigned the IP, So chances of migration changing the IP address or swapping goes to zero.\\nSame goes with linux that HWADDR is mapped to interface & even in config file & that preserves the IP address.\\n\\nAll we have to make sure is that we are retaining mac address after migraiton. Local test works perfectly in my env,  How do I prove this test case in cust env?", "type": "message", "user": "U_ARPIT_8F539902"}]	{U_ARPIT_8F539902}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.939202+00	2026-05-27 00:49:12.505708+00	summarized	2026-05-26
868cde2b-a169-44f5-8f81-8cd1d1e103e7	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710200.000000", "text": "[Migration Bucket 1 ]\\n\\n- Bundle 3C - started at 1pm BST with 17 VMs", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.902677+00	2026-05-26 02:53:00.240716+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
9f34243b-5214-4dcf-9e6d-30099c118cd0	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710400.000000", "text": "[build - node labelling]\\nSo it seems that the build team have added a new app node-metadata-configuration to which will add labels to nodes... this is partly my fault as I suggested this approach for the remote worker test, but i didn't realise it'd be taken forward as an approach to the rest of the estate (especially after not being tested properly in the lab) :confused:  I've since informed them the best way to label up nodes which haven't yet been provisioned is to add the bmac.agent-install.openshift.io.node-label. annotation to the BMH resource.. but basically ... I think we have a bit of an issue now.. and I'm a bit stumped on how we elegantly handle day 2 labelling of nodes in a gitops manor. See attached image for what's been done for reference..... so this works and it has to be done through defining resources and not patches as kuztomise basically cannot patch something it doesn't 'own', so you have to define it thorough a resource... the issue here is that if the application is deleted node-metadata-configuration  then because we have pruning enabled in our root app it thus deletes the resources... so in this case it deletes the nodes.. hence potentially bloody destructive here.... so a couple questions:\\n\\n\\nAnyone have any ideas on how to elegantly do day2 labelling via gitops? (day 1 is fine via that bmac BMH annotation)\\nShould we turn off auto pruning in the root app? (it's on atm, and I suppose there are pros and cons for doing this)\\n\\n\\nthoughts @rspazzol @Philip Jones and co?\\nimage.png Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [5:01 PM]\\n[VM Migration Updates (Today’s batches) ]: We processed a total of 92 VMs today across three batches. The majority of the migrations were successful, but we did hit a few consistent issues that we need to keep tracking.\\n\\nOverall Statistics:\\n\\n   * Success (Clean): 62 VMs\\n    * Success (Fix Forward): 11 VMs (Primarily IP assignment/agent issues)\\n    * Rollbacks: 19 VMs\\n\\nKey Failures:\\n\\nXFS / File System Corruption (10 VMs): This was the major driver for our Linux rollbacks today (e.g., gbl20127087, gbl20051434). This is an OS/filesystem issue that is not easily fixable from the MTV side. We are currently working closely with the customer to determine the best approach to handle these XFS corruption issues prior to migration. @rspazzol I am still not sure we can fix this without asking for additional downtime.\\n\\nVIB / Allocate Disks Issue (11 VMs): We saw several rollbacks due to the known VIB / storage populator issue. The good news is that most of these are addressable with the fixes in our latest MTV 2.11.6 release. We tested this now in Cluster 104 and it is working now, I would like to make this update on production ASAP @Carina Almeida can we make sure this is communicated so it takes more priority?\\n\\nMissing IP / Post-Migration (6 VMs): Several Windows VMs successfully migrated but required a “Fix Forward” because OpenShift couldn’t find an IP address or the OCP agent wasn’t running post-migration. We were able to push these through, but it adds manual overhead. I hope this is fixed updated in 2.11.6  or (11.3.6 :wink: )", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.918727+00	2026-05-26 02:55:00.289768+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
601beb55-4fa4-493e-aff1-78d6d7c89ba6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710600.000000", "text": "[Cluster housekeeping] I'm getting small aneurysms when im looking in the cluster and all the events that are just flooding with failures. So I was thinking, how can we improve this situation on a wider scale with some daily maintenance cleanup activities? Of course, what we want to do first and foremost is to fix the rootcause what leaves the litter aro down the clusters with useless activites and failures that consumes way too much resources in total and clutters any logs.\\n\\nSo...\\n\\nAny migration related  items in migration workspaces that are older then 7 days, clean them away\\nAny PVC pending older then ... hmm, a bit unsure here.. I wanna say 3 days, but maybe it needs a bit more logic in it\\nAny pods(not VMs) that are crashlooping, kill them, scale down deployment or whatever it is\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.931652+00	2026-05-26 02:56:00.419129+00	pending_retry	\N
33e582ab-6be1-45a5-99a2-9e4853c6e420	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710700.000000", "text": "[Migration failures !]\\nIf anyone can join the bridge? And verify a) no more VIB issues b) find a patter inf posible for XFS issues?Arpit Tolani  [10:01 AM]\\n{Migration}\\n\\n- name: Patch VM video device to virtio\\n  kubernetes.core.k8s:\\n    host: \\"{{ oc_api_url }}\\"\\n    api_key: \\"{{ oc_token }}\\"\\n    validate_certs: false\\n\\n    state: patched\\n\\n    api_version: kubevirt.io/v1\\n    kind: VirtualMachine\\n\\n    name: \\"{{ vm_name }}\\"\\n\\n    definition:\\n      spec:\\n        template:\\n          spec:\\n            domain:\\n              devices:\\n                video:\\n                  type: virtio\\n\\n  when:\\n    - vm_os_type | default('') == \\"Windows\\"\\n\\nI was working on a ansible script to patch Windows VM just post migration to get correct Video card driver. This script will go in post_migration_run.yaml in line 295.\\nWe already have a task there to identity the OS type.. does it look good?\\n\\nI have a question? Where do I specify namespace? I cant see that in entire logic.. Do we take care of namespace somewhere else, or its something like all VM in a cluster goes to same NS & we are already in that NS, so no need to define it..", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.935322+00	2026-05-27 00:47:15.607064+00	summarized	2026-05-26
0ab7ab44-dbf4-4327-a8f0-a021221f3c48	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710500.000000", "text": "[Update to MTV 2.11.6]:\\nhere is a quick recap of today’s meeting regarding our path forward with the MTV upgrade and resolving our recent migration blockers.\\n\\nThe next batch of clusters slated for migration are still running VIB 2.0 on the ESXi hosts, which conflicts with the updated MTV version.\\nNext Steps:\\n\\nImmediate Retry: We are going to re-run all the failed migrations from our previous batches on the target clusters that already have VIB 3.0 installed to validate the fixes.\\nWeekend Upgrades: Abhishek has requested approval from Vinay, he will escalate to Dennis. Dennis will be upgrading the impacted ESXi hosts to VIB 3.0 over this coming weekend.\\nIf the weekend upgrades go as planned, our new batches for next week will be running cleanly on VIB 3.0 hosts, allowing us to fully upgrade to MTV 2.11.6 without issues.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.926815+00	2026-05-27 00:52:29.521991+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e6e5c5b4-a152-42cc-8e8a-869f9afc8654	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711200.000000", "text": "[Support Cases needed for Veritas Clusters Migration & Others]\\n@jfeind, @Shebi @Petros can we use 5 min of tomorrows VM Migration Workstream call for me to understand which support cases that are in the path to complete RDM and VCS migrations? So I can understand priorization once the most urgent ones are solved?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.963315+00	2026-05-27 01:02:15.924081+00	summarized	2026-05-26
85dd8cb5-0d2a-49a9-b420-f693e71d12f7	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711300.000000", "text": "[build - PJ]\\n\\nPrerana and I are working to tune the oc-mirror jobs. \\nThe wrapper script has been updated to use the default values for --parallel-images (4) and --parallel-layers (5) and incredibly, it's running fine now :slightly_smiling_face:. We are seeing (as expected) a significant speed improvement. We have already got run time down to 6hrs and hope to bring it down to <5hrs. \\nPrerana has asked that we investigate image mirror failures so I've been making some changes after discussions with her.\\nWe have disabled the sync for the falcon-operator (crowdstrike) as it will be very tricky to sync this way given their 30 minute token expiry time.\\nThe Infoscale operator, requested a while back has never sync'd correctly and Prerana isn't aware of the requirement for it, so it's also now disabled.\\nI've created /etc/containers/registries.d/registry.k8s.io.yaml to disable sig-store checks impacting specific images. The signatures of these images are stored on us-central1-docker.pkg.dev which isn't currently allowed through the proxy. \\n\\n\\nIsovalent call is cancelled today as several members of WWT are unavailable.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}]	{U_PHILIP_740C6823}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.999877+00	2026-05-27 01:12:24.292215+00	summarized	2026-05-26
676ca122-67ea-45d6-9a1a-6a1d4ae5558f	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711500.000000", "text": "[Migration update Bundle 08:00 AM]\\nWe already have some errors in the migration. Triage is being done (to recognize common errors). I've updated the Proactive suport case with Zoom links for each migration bundle (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.014163+00	2026-05-27 01:16:38.865806+00	summarized	2026-05-26
c7affcc1-05e0-4cfc-a81e-9787ba70421c	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710900.000000", "text": "[cilium vs ovnk] some more cracks on the cilium capability around cross cluster live migrations came out recently. A little nudge and ovnk may be in the race again. Michael is asking to talk to redhat network engineering around cross cluster CUDNs and NSX bridging. @Nikos @Sam Marland we probably just need Brandon Marlow for that conversation. Is that something you guys can setup?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.948093+00	2026-05-27 00:54:50.62865+00	summarized	2026-05-26
892aa2a7-f975-49ac-82e3-98cf24abc811	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711100.000000", "text": "[scaling the migration automation] As the migration issues are debugged, we are getting ready to scale up the number of VMs being migrated. The objective is to reach 350 per active DC per day. Today MIOX creates N migration plans with one VM in each. There is investigation happening for having miox creating plans with multiple VMs (@jfeindis involved in it). However there are a few obstacles for this to happen:\\n\\nESXi hosts pre-flight checks are sequential (using roles and blocks).\\nVM pre-flight and post-flight checks are sequential (using roles and blocks). In this case the ansible playbook call AAP with an API to trigger another ansible playbook. resulting in very slow execution.\\nthe current AAP box support a maximum of 50/70 concurrent executions.\\n\\n\\n@Petros is putting together a document to address this issues. In proposed actions will be:\\n\\nconfigure the AAP box to be able to handle more concurrent job @Nikos is this a point where we should create more synergy with the redhat team that is looking after ansible?\\nresolve the ansible calling ansible with simple a playbook reusing another playbook\\nrefactor the sequential code to be parallelized by the number of VMs in a plan. This is a job that probably AI could do.\\n\\n\\nI'd like more eyes on this as Ansible is not my domain. Also forgive any in accuracy in the terminology.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.95856+00	2026-05-27 00:59:14.997774+00	summarized	2026-05-26
b3ef66e3-e3c9-49b0-8b61-9935c300ac31	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711400.000000", "text": "[Recharge day cover]\\n\\n@pdelashe @Shebi @atolani @Anne - all of you said you could swap your days and cover migration on Friday - Recharge day. Is this still the case? please let me know so we can get organised for then :thank_you_smile:", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.008376+00	2026-05-27 01:14:09.738225+00	summarized	2026-05-26
bb6fd514-cac5-42db-bb89-45ae40dcb895	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712000.000000", "text": "[New target clusters for migration]\\nAccording to the Migration plan, on May 26th, the VMs will be migrated to 3 different OCP clusters, the ones linked to Fabrics 111, 113 1nd 122.. According to Confluence, 111 is clusters 301,302,303, 113 is clusters 311 and 312, and 122 is cluster 314Raffaele Spazzoli  [4:17 PM]\\n[cilium vs ovnk] increasing interest from hsbc on ovnk, two more meetings to be scheduled with engineering: rodamap session, demo session. @Nikos is on it. I also floated the idea that while we are all together in india we could try some of the ovnk features. We will need someone familiar with BGP. @atolani are you by any chance?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.114651+00	2026-05-27 01:25:37.158215+00	summarized	2026-05-26
4f44fad3-e85d-4e63-810a-0b1149c0427a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712100.000000", "text": "[unisphere and rawio] dell tested out solution for rawio with their unisphere VM. they are satisfied. hsbc will start the testing now even if the solution is not GA yet. @jfeind this my end up with abhishek wand devdatt and therefore eventually with you.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.118563+00	2026-05-27 01:28:13.285349+00	summarized	2026-05-26
dddeeb2a-ce5d-492f-a9e0-1105690d1219	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712200.000000", "text": "[mirroring - cilium]\\n@rspazzol you mentioned yesterday if we had the cilium operator locally yet.. I've checked amd looks like we don't. do you want us to add it in now?\\n\\noc-mirror list operators --catalog=registry.redhat.io/redhat/certified-operator-index:v4.21 --package=cilium-enterprise\\n\\nNAME               DISPLAY NAME  DEFAULT CHANNEL\\ncilium-enterprise                1.16\\n\\nPACKAGE            CHANNEL  HEAD\\ncilium-enterprise  1.16     cilium-enterprise.v1.16.16-xf0717b8@Philip Jones I assume this operator ^ is what we need? can you confirm", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.127117+00	2026-05-27 01:30:20.787485+00	summarized	2026-05-26
f31a26b2-8072-42f6-8630-fe716b20f4a3	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712300.000000	7777712301.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777712300.000000", "text": "[Today’s migration update]\\nWe pushed through a massive volume today, processing 195 VMs (a mix of 105 RHEL and 89 Windows servers). We achieved a high success rate of approximately 95%, with the vast majority migrating cleanly.\\n\\n:large_green_circle: Success (Clean): 176 VMs\\n:large_yellow_circle: Success (Fix-Forward / Retry): 11 VMs (Primarily IPs not present, agent issues, and disk allocation issues)\\n:red_circle: Rollbacks: 8 VMs\\n\\n\\nBlocker Review & Rollback Reasons\\nThe 8 rollbacks were entirely driven by two specific issues during the Convert image to kubevirt stage:\\n\\nXFS Filesystem Corruption / xfs_repair (5 VMs): The underlying filesystem on the source VMs triggered fatal errors during conversion. This is about the Bug I created: https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5561 CC @Nick Evans \\nOut of Memory (OOM) / setfiles (2 VMs): The conversion appliance ran out of memory, causing the setfiles process to crash. @James Force this is the fix using Gatekeeper cc @rspazzol \\n\\n\\nTomorrow’s Troubleshooting Sync: We have an approved change request to use one of the affected production servers for live debugging. Tomorrow at 11 AM CEST, we will have a joint debugging session with the customer, Red Hat Support, and Engineering to isolate exactly when and where the XFS corruption is being triggered. Anyone is welcome to join, I don’t have the zoom link, but I will share it when I get it.\\n:jira: MTV-5561 [New] : virt-v2v fails during migration of RHEL 7 VMs due to XFS filesystem errors, potentially related to RHEL 10.1 xfs_repair running against a RHEL 7 XFS filesystem.Added by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerCarina Almeida  [9:33 AM]\\n:exclamation:[Read me - CONFIDENTIAL] :exclamation:\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nJust a quick but important heads-up regarding current project dynamics.\\n\\nWe are observing some internal tension on the bank's side right now coming from their Engineering. None of this is directed at Red Hat, but it is impacting meeting atmospheres.\\n\\nPlease keep these two rules of thumb in mind:\\n\\nIf bank stakeholders are arguing or there's clear tension, please stay neutral and step back from the debate.\\nIf Red Hat is put on the spot or challenged, do not debate it live. Interject politely, ask to take the subject offline, and immediately bring Anne or myself into the conversation.\\n\\n\\nThank you all for maintaining our usual high standards of professionalism. :pray:", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}, {"ts": "7777712301.000000", "text": "[Today’s Migration update]: Today was a very challenging day on the storage front, but I want to resonate with @Carina Almeida by saying a massive thank you to everyone. Today was one of those days where the true Red Hat spirit shone through. We collaborated across different areas under pressure, maintaining a highly professional and supportive atmosphere.\\n\\nWe processed a total of 118 VMs across three batches today. Unfortunately, we hit massive storage-layer blockers that forced a high number of rollbacks.\\n\\n:large_green_circle: Success (Clean): 41 VMs\\n:large_yellow_circle: Success (Fix-Forward / Retry): 5 VMs\\n:red_circle: Rollbacks: 72 VMs\\n:x: Failed: 0 VMs\\n\\n\\nThe high rollback rate today was almost entirely driven by underlying storage infrastructure issues during the Allocate Disks phase:\\n\\nCopy-Offload ESX HBA UID Errors: A massive chunk of Bundle C failed because copy-offload could not add the ESX HBA UID. \\nPowerMax & LUN Mapping: Several Windows VMs failed to allocate disks due to PowerMax clonner initialization failures (“Service Unavailable”) or failing to map LUNs.\\n\\n\\nThe Good News (XFS Resolved!): I spent the majority of today focused on the persistent XFS repair bug. By implementing Option A (the custom virt-v2v image from Engineering that skips the native XFS repair step), we successfully bypassed the conversion crashes. I will make sure this gets into production quickly so we can reduce the number of failures. Tomorrow I will check more on the Dell issue, to see how I can help.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055", "thread_ts": "7777712300.000000"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.136775+00	2026-05-26 04:39:00.108184+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
e698334d-462b-45a7-a34b-dfea6930ec64	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711700.000000", "text": "[New joiners, HSBC onboarding]\\n\\nTeam,\\nThis morning I got OTP and ID only for three of you. I'll be sharing those with the other colleagues as I get them :wink:", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.032438+00	2026-05-27 01:18:25.006221+00	summarized	2026-05-26
27becdec-71c1-41e4-88e9-1edbea1dda4e	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711800.000000", "text": "[Support to Migrations]\\nWe had a call this morning to get some feedback on how we support migrations, and we've agreed to try a \\"person assigned to a migration bundle\\" strategy for the remaining of this week, to see if it improves our experience and efficiency, considering also our timezones and the fact that we have now another migration event at 8.00 am uk time\\nAs we have Red Hat team members in different time zones, we are thinking on dedicating specific people to handle each bundle to optimize our distribution.\\n\\n\\nArpit will be dedicated to the bundle that runs at 8:00 AM UK Time 12:30 PM India time, \\nSebastian will be dedicated to the bundle that runs at the 10:00 AM, UK Time \\nJens will be dedicated to the bundle that runs at 14:00 UK Time. \\n\\n\\nNew members like Aray and Snehal will be shadowing in whichever bundles they can join.\\n\\nDetails on how the process works can be found here:  I also added to that doc how to involve ESS if we need additional support\\n\\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1yVVRat6To3JSWxPKJZ0Kp-jfDSkN1zPUJz6yVnuQ9xo/edit?tab=t.0", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.039793+00	2026-05-27 01:20:54.891707+00	summarized	2026-05-26
626c56c3-d2da-46ec-a986-b2dafcdc8fcd	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712600.000000", "text": "[Migrations from and to Dell storage] :alarm_flash:\\nFYI, but today migrations were either DELL is the origin or the destination, are failing. The short error is \\"Copy Offload failed to add the ESX HBA UID. Source Pure Target DELL\\" I'm not sure on which side it is (Miox, MTV, ???) but it will porbably start to have lots of visibility (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.153064+00	2026-05-27 01:34:36.801119+00	summarized	2026-05-26
34410998-99f5-4a72-b996-56962e675845	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712500.000000", "text": "[vm migration planning and node re-purposing] at the strategic meeting it turned out that Accenture is planning migration solely based on the IT service level concept. This means that VMs do not come from the same VMware cluster. As a result now that we are at ~700 migrated VMs we still cannot re-purpose any node. A request will be made to Accenture to consider that further requirement in their planning.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.148127+00	2026-05-26 04:47:00.795597+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
f378b82b-830c-4d30-be0e-4c47111ca8bc	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712900.000000", "text": "[KDD] reporting some KDD decisions taken today (for what they are worth)\\n\\nHIC clusters will be 24 nodes when non-stretched,  48 nodes when stretched. still confusing to me if we actually need stretched  clusters.\\nwe will continue with the two namespace approach\\nwe will not implement the node firewall operator for now, it needs to be deeply tested.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.164936+00	2026-05-27 01:38:43.17114+00	summarized	2026-05-26
b4197546-f990-4083-aa54-f002aa89663d	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777713000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777713000.000000", "text": "[Time Card Submission]\\nHi team, as most of you will be out for the quarterly Recharge Day tomorrow & Monday is a bank holiday both in the UK & Germany, please ensure that you log your Time Sheets on Clarity for the bank today and log your Red Hat time cards within the next two hours, so they can be approved on time. Thank you everyone! :sunny:", "type": "message", "user": "U_JOHANN_669B3727"}]	{U_JOHANN_669B3727}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.168845+00	2026-05-27 01:41:20.746465+00	summarized	2026-05-26
ff276b96-0418-42fa-ba50-123438d87d88	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777713100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777713100.000000", "text": "[Migration Bundle Handover]\\nAfter a short retro today, we have agreed that we need an easy way to handover each bundle migration status to the following team, for background and context and to prevent troubleshooting the same issues twice. I've drafted a \\"Tab\\" in this channel rather than creating a separate channel or document, so each team can provide their inputs onthe the bundle once its is completed. Please let me know what do you think of the format and if it is useful. https://redhat.enterprise.slack.com/docs/T027F3GAJ/F0B4VJB90ET\\nCanvas Migration Bundle Handover\\nCanvasNote: We don't need the number of success / failures of each migration as those are tracked here:  \\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0\\n26 May 2026 - Bucket 4 - Bundle 1c\\nObserved Errors:\\nPriority Action Items:\\nCustomer Mood: \\nSupport cases opened:\\nRoot Cause Analysis:\\n26 May 2026 - Bucket 4 - Bundle 1b\\nObserved Errors:", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.173234+00	2026-05-27 01:43:50.509656+00	summarized	2026-05-26
c19e517e-d4fb-4f2a-a933-216f0e505d82	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777713200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777713200.000000", "text": "[Migration Completed]\\nAs all DELL VMs were removed from today's migrations, we migrated 9 VMs today, and 2 of them were rolled back due to XFS Issues.Raffaele Spazzoli  [3:23 PM]\\n[dell migration failures and CSM observability module] I'm getting only partial information but it looks like Dell has indicated that the Unisphere API  was overwhelmed because of the CSM observability module making to many requests. The CSM observability module is now disabled in prod. The observability team was really sorry for that. I tried to reassure that they didn't do anything wrong they had no easy way to know that they were DOSing the Unisphere API (that metric is not reported and can be seen only from the array GUI; ah the irony!!) . @pdelashe @Shebi @jfeind does this correspond with what you are seeing?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.177343+00	2026-05-27 01:45:56.248161+00	summarized	2026-05-26
44932932-f15c-4564-a7b0-9ea6b067e4a6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712700.000000", "text": "[Migration update - Reasons for Failure]\\nAfter our last Retro, we decided to capture the reasons for failure during the migrations; these reasons are provided by the customer's SRE team and may / may not be 100% accurate, but as they use now a consistent terminology, it is easier for me to start getting statistics per error type. Added a new Tab to my spreadsheet with that info: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13zteoVDscXt-TSb0ytvHaXIzFrqnM85K9jSDppxEK1Q/edit?gid=900127641#gid=900127641", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.156863+00	2026-05-27 01:32:25.436749+00	summarized	2026-05-26
3165e2cc-2af5-4873-95f8-30c693769bd4	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712800.000000", "text": "[info] Regarding https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04426565, I've asked support if they can confirm which version this bug (pvc / pv uid mismatch) was introduced in. We may be better off reverting to a prior version until the fix is available.", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_64E3F7FD"}]	{U_GOOGLE_64E3F7FD}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.160792+00	2026-05-27 01:36:25.56096+00	summarized	2026-05-26
406a9fe3-e99e-4ad3-a3be-fa9d85b1b9ad	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778214671.000011	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778214671.000011", "text": "hey do you also see the alert icon in this channel? do we know why it's there?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.538998+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.175714+00	delivered	2026-05-09
13100af7-8afa-4791-8c26-b2c6bd844e24	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778223257.000017	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778223257.000017", "text": "[Migration Event Pilot Phase 1 day #2]\\nThere was an issue with the application; we tried to fix-forward but went way past the 2 hour window, and we have agreed to roll back. Looks like the software running in the machine - very old and out of support - had compatibility issues wth the new platform (team suspects CPU, or very old DLL versions). To be investigated by the windows team after rollback", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.645862+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.184686+00	delivered	2026-05-09
c7eeb88b-f40b-4198-95b7-ba62bd4ef814	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778220484.000124	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778220484.000124", "text": "[helm binary] Looking for a helm binary in the environment that I can use from the linux bastion, any suggestions are helpful :slightly_smiling_face:", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.96456+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.190859+00	delivered	2026-05-09
fccaa7d9-514e-44ac-adb3-1f40e6ee74a1	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778229480.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778229480.000000", "text": "[bsod] bsod as in blue scree of death for windows. This is apparently now affecting several of our customers. Some regression in either our product or windows. A customer pulled out of openshift virtualization for this. Engineering trying to figure out what is it.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:21.230712+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.197652+00	delivered	2026-05-09
