6f61d945-422e-4e7b-9e63-a3d21f2c8b3a	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710300.000000", "text": "[build - nexus repos]\\nTo date, every cluster has been built using the Nexus instance in the UK. We now have repo mirroring set up from the UK to the HK Nexus and Prerana and Shwetali have proposed using environment substitution for the Nexus endpoint for our clusters (i.e., nexus3.uk vs. nexus3.hk) see the image I'll attach for a draft PR Prerana raised. However, we would also need to add a Helm variable for this instance and modify the Helm charts to support it...as there isn't much use in building a cluster in HK that pulls from the UK only to switch repositories later. I'm not sure i'm a huge fan of this.. I was thinking of adding multiple mirrors (as they are supposedly ordered) as I think thats safer and it also gives us additional protection say if an image cant be pulled from 1 geo for some reason it can still be pulled from the other... thoughts? @rspazzol @janine @Philip Jones @Rydekull https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.21/html/config_apis/imagedigestmirrorset-config-openshift-io-v1#spec[…]ors-2\\ndocs.redhat.comChapter 15. ImageDigestMirrorSet [config.openshift.io/v1] | Config APIs | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationChapter 15. ImageDigestMirrorSet [config.openshift.io/v1] | Config APIs | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationJens Feind  [3:18 PM]\\nThanks to everyone who helped pushing out MTV 2.11.6 fast into the Labs, this will help us move forward in both the Migration and Testing Workstreams :+1:", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.909059+00	2026-05-26 21:07:58.728832+00	summarized	2026-05-26
27c72c54-bbe3-4608-8464-f0f948036bb9	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777716800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777716800.000000", "text": "{Migration}\\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has \\"Windows Server\\" or not.. If it has, patch it\\n\\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\\n --type merge\\n -p '{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"domain\\":{\\"devices\\":{\\"video\\":{\\"type\\":\\"virtio\\"}}}}}}}'\\n\\nBut with automation i have few questions.\\n\\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...Rosalia Suarez Mejias  [10:53 AM]\\nDelivery Report]\\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ARPIT_8F539902"}]	{U_ARPIT_8F539902}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.493117+00	2026-05-27 04:32:24.170141+00	summarized	2026-05-26
5a5f5e94-ea77-427e-9191-5e020864af7c	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777723000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777723000.000000", "text": "Hmm, so based on what is being said atm, I need help from someone to help roll out wiz/cs next week.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.85403+00	2026-05-27 04:34:13.949825+00	summarized	2026-05-26
fcf5f04a-b5b1-451c-9b2d-be8aa6b4e9a1	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777723200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777723200.000000", "text": ":green_alert:\\n\\nNDA partly lifted internally in HSBC. Those on the NDA are now allowed to talk \\"carefully\\" about an Infrastructure Modernisation programme with those not on the NDA previously. The \\"why\\" they are doing the programme is still confidential for obvious reasons! External comms DO NOT change at present so from a RH perspective I suggest we stay as is", "type": "message", "user": "U_ANNE_7F9C7274"}]	{U_ANNE_7F9C7274}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.861968+00	2026-05-27 04:38:14.845577+00	summarized	2026-05-26
a210ea9e-9386-40d4-89be-a3b2974b481c	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777723300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777723300.000000", "text": ":helpme:\\n\\nAppliances - who can join this chat with the customer and me - it came as an action out of Stefanie and Franks interlock this week.  \\"The ask would be to support us in understand options whereby our vendor provided appliances are not certified for use with OpenShift\\". Nikos is on holiday next week and i dont want a week of no movement\\nimage001.png Raffaele Spazzoli  [1:37 PM]\\nI can help.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ANNE_7F9C7274"}]	{U_ANNE_7F9C7274}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.866665+00	2026-05-27 04:40:10.824341+00	summarized	2026-05-26
fa63acf2-9d24-44d3-a797-c8b503724ad9	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209018.000118	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209018.000118", "text": "@Shebi were you able to start troubleshooting the failed windows machine?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.902812+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.263157+00	delivered	2026-05-09
89423714-415e-4027-b5fb-0a258947bcf1	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711600.000000", "text": "[Migration status 18.05.2026]:\\n\\nOverall, we had a successful day, processing 113 VMs with an approximate 89% success rate (including those remediated via Fix-Forward/Retry). Bundle 1C was a perfect run with zero rollbacks.\\n\\n    :large_green_circle: Success (Clean & Fix-Forward/Retry): 101 VMs\\n    :red_circle: Rollbacks: 12 VMs\\n\\nPrimary Blockers & Rollback Reasons:\\n\\nXFS File System Corruption: Caused 4 rollbacks across Bundles 1A and 1B. As established, this is an OS-level issue on the source VMs that requires remediation prior to migration. We were having support from Red Hat Support troubleshooting one of the rolled back VMs, and we found something interesting. When we ran medatada dump on the XFS filesystems.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCgroup / Sysroot Filesystem Mounts: Caused 8 rollbacks in Bundle 1B (e.g., “No file system mounted for cgroup”). (This was related to LUKS encrypted filesystem)\\n\\nFix-Forwards (Resolved): Mostly related to missing IPs, QEMU/OCP agent issues, intermittent vCenter connectivity, and VMTools failing to uninstall cleanly post-migration. (edited) \\nimage.png Arpit Tolani  [10:46 AM]\\nany red Hat doc I try to open from VDI gets blocked with error \\"I do not have general internet access right, if our business unit allows that, we can follow the instructions to request the same\\"\\n\\nis it allowed for our team? accessing internet on VDI & Bank Laptop?", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.024514+00	2026-05-26 21:15:56.428876+00	summarized	2026-05-26
39f5297d-ba21-4263-8b0c-5eb93398adc5	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700000.000000", "text": "[Build Standup Call]: @Philip Jones keep me honest here, so we give more context to @janine before joining the call. For building new clusters with ACM the secret is getting refreshed unexpectedly, causing the InfraEnv variables and the ISO image to fluctuate. Because the ISO keeps changing, the ISO attachment process frequently fails, throwing “ISO is not ready” errors. the team is relying on a manual process to create and apply these secrets to bypass the failures. To fix this, we need to finalize our automated secret management strategy. We need an automated way to pull these secrets, integrate them with Vault for proper password rotation, and reliably replicate them down to the managed clusters without breaking the deployment flow.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.56888+00	2026-05-27 04:42:57.427825+00	summarized	2026-05-26
9593e551-b537-4eca-b44f-e6ad21289da8	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777717100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777717100.000000", "text": "Hey team,\\n\\nfor the ones who are off tomorrow, I hope you all manage to switch off and rest :vacation_relax:\\nfor the ones off on Monday, I'll resend this message tomorrow :upside_down_face:\\nimage.png Philip Jones  [5:45 PM]\\n[Isovalent Update]\\n\\nLargely just confirming the version that we'll be installing for the POC phase 2. \\nLast time all the clusters were agent based installations so I've suggested that this time we build one ACM cluster and build the second cluster from that instead. This should more closely represent the build process HSBC will use for the majority of their clusters.\\nWill need to provide some info in POCDOC to assist with ACM install etc.", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.513867+00	2026-05-27 04:46:26.559666+00	summarized	2026-05-26
3251777b-6fec-45ae-ba8d-f73732bd2ac1	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777712400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777712400.000000", "text": "[XFS Corruption internal meeting]\\nEngineering is chasing the XFS repair failures root cause as a kernel mismatch between the RHEL 7 source VMs and the RHEL 10 conversion appliance environment. Because the filesystems are mounted read-only during the conversion, critical on-disk format repairs cannot be completed, causing the process to fail.\\n\\nDuring our upcoming debug session with the customer, we will test two specific approaches:\\n\\nOption A (Custom Image): Use a modified virt-v2v image provided by Engineering that explicitly skips the XFS repair step. @Philip Jones I need help to upload this to Nexus, I have it already in my VDI, but not sure how to use it in Nexus to use it in Forklift as this:\\noc patch ForkliftController -n openshift-mtv forklift-controller --type=merge -p '{\\"spec\\": {\\"virt_v2v_image_fqin\\":\\"quay.io/mnecas0/forklift-virt-v2v:xfs_repair\\"}}'\\n\\nOption B (Raw Copy Mode): Use raw copy mode to entirely circumvent the conversion issues (though this will require manual post-migration performance tuning by the customer).\\n\\nTo capture data in the VM, an ISO is being generated, but I am not sure if we will have enough time to test this.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.144198+00	2026-05-26 21:20:23.429531+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e449132b-113e-4ef6-9076-35223f0cb201	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777700900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777700900.000000", "text": "[VM triage process] we need to propose a triage process to the back as this is clearly not moving. @Shebi @janine, here is an idea:\\n\\nwhen a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back and the migrated VM is put in triage.\\nusing MTV, VM is moved from a production cluster/namespace to triage cluster/namespace\\nuse virtctl guestfs to manipulate the VM OS and\\n    a. change the VM IP to something compatible with the triage environment\\n    b. enable a local account with root capability\\n\\nconfirm that the VM can start correct and local account works\\n5 delete original migrated VM\\n\\ntroubleshoot the VM\\n7 once the resolution is confirmed, delete the VM\\n\\nplease mentally verify these steps for both Linux and Windows OSes.\\n\\n@Rydekull I know you are mostly focused on security, but we could use your input too here. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.696369+00	2026-05-27 04:49:39.177205+00	summarized	2026-05-26
930dbd62-8c70-4329-8f76-62784a9b6901	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777718600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777718600.000000", "text": "Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\\n\\n\\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\\n\\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\\n\\n\\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\\n\\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\\n\\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\\n\\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}]	{U_SAM_F28235E5}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.597895+00	2026-05-27 04:53:07.706668+00	summarized	2026-05-26
f406aa46-e1d2-4c70-b872-39234e1d7792	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702900.000000", "text": "[Bulk Migration Testing with AAP]: Latency & AAP Platform: Magnus confirmed that a latency of around 400ms is acceptable, meaning no architectural changes to the AAP platform are required right now. We have also increased the UK database CPU to 18 and applied Red Hat’s fine-tuning recommendations.\\n\\nMigration SLAs & Strategy: The acceptable duration for VM migrations is set between 45 minutes and 1 hour 15 minutes. Our target split is 80% via storage offloading and 20% via cold migration.\\n\\nResource Consumption Testing: Because the Hong Kong lab is still under construction, Nitesh and Abhishek will conduct the next round of testing in the UK environment. We need to measure exact CPU, memory, and disk consumption during both Linux and Windows migrations to accurately calculate capacity needs.\\n\\nFuture Re-IP Scenarios: @janine told that future migrations requiring IP changes will involve additional pre- and post-migration automation tasks, taking longer. We will measure both standard and re-IP migration patterns and add safety buffers for unexpected scenarios.\\n\\nRecent Test Results: Abhishek confirmed that the recent 52 migrations had some failures, but they were not Ansible-related. The team is fixing these issues and will avoid problematic VM scenarios in the upcoming tests.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_1166B4A9"}]	{U_RAFFAE_1166B4A9}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.870895+00	2026-05-26 22:34:48.317938+00	summarized	2026-05-26
406c5a3d-2c05-4eb1-9286-686916454ca6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777701100.000000	7777701101.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777701100.000000", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\n\\nTeam I had a sync with Maj this morning and we talked mainly about Ny/Mx trip (only praises to our team here) and status of hadware.\\n\\n@pdelashe I want to sync with you about how this hardware plan is linked to ACN migration plans.\\n@Natasha Ghoojamanian we will need to link this then to staffing planning.\\n@rspazzol @Shebi - you don't have any PM support for the NY DC migration approach / testing. I'm wondering whether a PM should be involved in this or not yet? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_35CC3553"}, {"ts": "7777701101.000000", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\n\\nMexico:\\n\\nFabric delivery to Enginpresents a significant challenge.\\n\\n\\nIndia:\\n\\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\\n\\n\\nDMZ (General):\\n\\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\\nThis issue also affects the UK.\\n\\n\\nHong Kong (HK):\\n\\nReprioritization work is complete.\\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\\n\\n\\nUnited States (US):\\n\\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\\nNote: EOS is their second priority.", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C", "thread_ts": "7777701100.000000"}]	{U_GOOGLE_35CC3553,U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.721348+00	2026-05-27 04:56:00.965878+00	summarized	2026-05-26
2880ca72-9fde-4318-8da7-c733217615ba	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777718800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777718800.000000", "text": "Isovalent Update:\\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\\n\\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.\\nScreenshot 2026-05-06 at 15.39.09.png James Force  [5:12 PM]\\n@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}]	{U_PHILIP_740C6823}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.609427+00	2026-05-27 04:58:13.570345+00	summarized	2026-05-26
6d99cd6b-34d2-4612-a13b-be5256340cd5	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219331.000171	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219331.000171", "text": "can you help answer this question? @Anne @Carina Almeida", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.562048+00	2026-05-09 13:32:58.950964+00	pending_retry	\N
fee31afb-88af-4f38-8f37-16ba5a1871dd	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708100.000000", "text": "[mexico meetings summary] the ITSO crowd in mexico was much more active and interested. Overall it looks like this country is fine with participating to this program.\\nWith regards to the DMZ discussion, the issue is essentially solved and it comes down to verifying that there are enough ports in the existing switches. Mexico will fall in line with the global guidelines.\\nLooking at capacity we discovered that the initial purchases for the new kits led by Maj did not take into account the capability fragmentation introduced by the DMZ architecture ( [customer|utility|non-prod\\\\extranet]x[edmx|idmz]x[TLDC|CLDL] (extranet does not have edmz). Recalling that the guidelines from global is that each cluster must be self-contained in zone, this yields (4x2-1)x2=14 clusters for a minimum of 42 nodes (only 16 have been purchased). We have this misalignment in all the regions. Maj is aware.Philip Jones  [11:45 AM]\\nIssue for Monday: the SRE team have discovered that a tech preview setting has been applied to all clusters including prod. This relates to OCP virt and virtio video adapters. \\n\\nHopefully we can switch this off on the prod clusters and there won't be any issue with upgrades or support in the future.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.778207+00	2026-05-27 00:26:07.493983+00	summarized	2026-05-26
49039253-65ea-4d1f-9e23-e3ee1a5497a3	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777701400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777701400.000000", "text": "[Migration Failure Process Workshop]\\nGoal: Improve the failure management as it is not clear who needs to do what, and in particular SLAs\\nGoal2: Vinay has asked ACN to be more proactive on the initial Triage\\nWe reviewed the process drafted by ACN (Image on Teams) and modified some responsabilities and SLAs\\nActions:\\na) All Miox Logs posted in Splunk should be available for the team that is doing the triage\\nb) ACN to review a Confluence Knowledgebase of Miox Errors = Solutions or whom to call\\nc) Escalate to the Program what to do if ITSOs do not respond in the agreed time (30') either rollback or move to hypercare, or someone to talk to ITSO to clarify the importance of responding in time\\nd) Red Hat (me) to send our proposal on how we want to collaborate with the Command Center and support triageRaffaele Spazzoli  [2:10 PM]\\n[metrics and acm] Enterprise architecture and the run team are starting to take a look at the otel integration and are raising some objections (the same I was raising at the beginning: not all metrics are being forwarded). next steps: a demo of what exist today will be given. Onkar will demo the otel piece, redhat will demo in platform observability. I volunteered, but I have some travel time in front of me and I might have to delegate. @Shebi @Shebi. in the horizon there is the fact that the run team and the Enterprise architecture team bith like the idea of using the product feature when it comes to operationalization. so we might be asked to enabled ACM observability. This was a hard no from Vinay, so we'll se how the conversation evolves. Aside from @ricardo gregorio who has been following this we need and architect to follow this.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.746001+00	2026-05-27 05:07:37.526169+00	summarized	2026-05-26
f3c8eedd-6866-4948-80a6-f6576da29589	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777719400.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777719400.000000", "text": "The day when im done with this project, I will cherish the sweet knowledge of knowing my VDI will be destroyed and not surpass my existence in this cruel world.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}]	{U_ALEXAN_D03599F6}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.646764+00	2026-05-27 05:09:52.197542+00	summarized	2026-05-26
a1c4951b-4400-4234-88cf-ce2d1cd6b471	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777711900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777711900.000000", "text": "[phase 2 design] @rspazzol @Shebi @Rydekull one question came up regarding how to best utilize different storage arrays in one cluster (non-stretched setup spanning multiple pods). With Pure and px-csi, there seems to be 2 options: one is 1 storage cluster with multiple storage arrays, the storage class or PVC specifying the respective array [1], at provisioning time they need to account for storage capacity to determine which storage class to use. The other would be to utilize CSI topologies [2], woudl still require to determine a storage class at provisioning time.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JANINE_71F80BBD"}]	{U_JANINE_71F80BBD}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.110524+00	2026-05-27 01:22:58.146791+00	summarized	2026-05-26
2c71d014-e2a1-4818-acb2-69c188e7e727	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777701800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777701800.000000", "text": "[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\\n\\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?", "type": "message", "user": "U_NICK_CA725671"}]	{U_NICK_CA725671}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.777196+00	2026-05-27 05:12:41.584615+00	summarized	2026-05-26
4aabf1b6-978d-4c70-b93d-dfa62d1e9831	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777720000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777720000.000000", "text": "@rspazzol in the ClusterVersion resource is there a reason why we have an image specified?\\n\\ne.g. https://github.com/redhat-developer/openshift-virtualization-gitops/blob/main/clusters/etl4/overlays/openshift-config/cluster-version.yaml#L11\\n\\nWe're thinking of removing this if not needed, surely the version param is sufficient? anything we're missing here?  : https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.15/html/config_apis/clusterversion-config-openshift-io-v1#spec-desiredupdate\\ndocs.redhat.comChapter 6. ClusterVersion [config.openshift.io/v1] | Config APIs | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.15 | Red Hat DocumentationChapter 6. ClusterVersion [config.openshift.io/v1] | Config APIs | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.15 | Red Hat DocumentationRaffaele Spazzoli  [2:23 PM]\\n[ess] from how the cases are being handled, I can  see that ESS is still not handling them. Do we know when this is going start? @Carina Almeida @Anne", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.674412+00	2026-05-27 05:15:06.298509+00	summarized	2026-05-26
9bb838ae-cfb5-4fcf-b3b3-671d27c2e745	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777702700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777702700.000000", "text": "[TSR - Review]\\nThe first draft of the TSR is available (we still need to update amother must-gather) but I've seen that it complains because of certificates expiration date. Can anyone review if this is correct? Or a false positive?image.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [11:39 AM]\\n[Migration Pilot2 update]\\nUpdated the \\"on call\\" team for the 1st week to include Janine&Alex as Shebi will be in us/MX\\nStart date has been pushed to May 5th (as there is a quite period that finishes on May 4th)\\nLooks like some of the VMs with RDM disks are sitting on HP storage that does not support storage offload, so they will be moved to either Pure or Dell before migrating, which will imply > 10m down time\\nThey are thinking to create a new Change Request Category to accelerate the ITSO response time (I think they are using Patching now, which doesn't sound much urgent)Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [12:11 PM]\\n[RCA Meeting]\\nTo schedule the meeting to discuss our RCA proposal, what is your availability Architects? And Raffa proposed to include Narender, Natty and John Davis. Anyone else?Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:18 PM]\\n[dell scalability testing] dell tests cordon and drain with an average of 10 VM and 2 disks per node. this means 20 volumes per node. This test is not realistic, we have asked to rerun the test with 120 volumes per node, which is what the bank expects.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PLEASE_802C7AFD"}]	{U_PLEASE_802C7AFD}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.854282+00	2026-05-27 05:17:56.639484+00	summarized	2026-05-26
b20ffba8-e154-4a86-aac6-088b43564409	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777720800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777720800.000000", "text": "Good news!!\\n\\nI asked Alex from the OC mirror dev team, the following:\\nAt the moment our customer has issues with either their Nexus or Proxy server that limits us to running oc-mirror with --parallel-images=1 and --paralllel-layers=1. Needless to say, it's painful! We had sync running over 30 hrs earlier this week and the current run is now over 24hrs.\\nWe need a way in which we can sync specific operators or elements faster. Right now, were we to try and sync a small image-set-config, we'd end up with a tiny catalog. Is there no way to have it merge a catalog update with an existing catalog, rather than re-publish a new one?\\nI.e. we really need to get hold of MTV 2.11.6 without waiting a LONG time for a full sync.\\n\\nHe's responded that it's coming in oc-mirror 4.22 :slightly_smiling_face: So we should have a means to cherry pick (when needed) and merge with an existing catalog, rather than replace it. In essence, we can run a minimal sync when needed, to grab a specific update, rather than needing to always mirror the full image-set-config.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}]	{U_PHILIP_740C6823}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.708672+00	2026-05-27 05:20:07.795828+00	summarized	2026-05-26
6961321a-47f1-4390-8506-e3158a4c7efd	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708300.000000", "text": "[Update reuired]\\n\\nTeam,\\nWe need last update on the following item, who can help with this? @janine @Shebi @Rydekull @jfeind @atolani @Petros @pdelashe\\n\\nPS, I already asked TAM / ESS to get cases updates as well.\\n\\n1. VIB Version Mismatch (Compliance Blocker)\\nMTV automatically upgrades the VIB from version 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 during migration. As a regulated financial institution, we are required to obtain security approval before releasing any new package into our environment. This auto-upgrade behaviour bypasses our internal compliance process and cannot be permitted without prior approval. We need MTV to support our existing VIB version (0.2.0) or provide a controlled upgrade path.\\n\\n2. Concurrent Migrations from the Same ESXi Host\\nWhen multiple VMs residing on the same ESXi host are migrated concurrently, storage offloading fails consistently. We have no control over VM-to-host placement within our estate, making this condition unavoidable. The current workaround of retrying migrations repeatedly is operationally unsustainable at our scale.\\n\\n3. VMs with More Than 10 Disks\\nVMs with more than 10 attached disks fail storage offloading consistently, and retries do not resolve the issue. Over 3,000 VMs in our estate fall into this category and are currently completely blocked from migration with no available workaround.\\n\\n4. QEMU issue\\n\\n5 . Not getting IP issue (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.790941+00	2026-05-27 06:16:10.760496+00	summarized	2026-05-26
df6f34a1-f98a-475f-9575-07fdfc4d7b9c	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778204632.000232	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778204632.000232", "text": "[Delivery Report]\\nPlease have a look and complete the gaps as this will be send out in 20 minutes\\nThanks", "type": "message", "user": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}]	{"Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.342247+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.268311+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3367cc56-c0c1-4057-85f8-fc2534d979ff	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703300.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703300.000000", "text": "[architecture documentation] with regards to this thread https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C099TDJDDKL/p1776434503713569 , I hope everyone is making progress. Here is my update:\\n@janine has been helping me creating teh documentation that was assigned by Vijay to Michele, we should be in decent spot enough to keep Vijay happy. @janine will keep working with Michele in my absence.\\n@Carina Almeida please keep people accountable to complete their documentation. the deadline is Friday 5/1\\n\\nPS: I have been in many projects in which red hat has been in defect because we didn't deliver the documentation. Let's make sure this is not one of those.\\n[arch documentation] we need to finish the following pieces of architecture docs in two weeks. Please let's sure we deliver on this, as red hatter we are notoriously slow/bad at this part..:\\n\\ncompute design for non-hic, status: empty, assigned: Michele, Raf and now @janine \\nsecurity: status: Natty populated it: @Rydekull to review, lean and filter. This is the piece that concerns Vijay\\ndata architecture (i.e. labels and annotation): populated by Gareth. @Shebi to review and approve. @Shebi since you are also following teh migration track, let';s make sure this guidance is implemented. I have not seen those labels on the migrated VMs. I could be wrong though.\\nTertiary Vault: sta… \\nThread in proj-eos-mvp | Apr 17th | View messageRaffaele Spazzoli  [3:38 PM]\\n[bsod] this is teh list of well-knon bsod scenarios @Shebi @pdelashe @Petros please share this with the customer so they can build detection rules in the pre-flight automation.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:51.999238+00	2026-05-27 05:25:08.505762+00	summarized	2026-05-26
20d625d6-3031-4cc8-aeea-32d33bb28eeb	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777722000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777722000.000000", "text": "@channel Let's try it again... :guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\\n\\nTo help us get through this programme and customer's build/migration blockers, we’ve officially started a team Spotify playlist: https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\\n\\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote on Wednesday after our internal stand-up :wink:\\n\\nIn the meantime, keep the beat on! :headphones: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.811181+00	2026-05-27 05:27:05.727231+00	summarized	2026-05-26
20a47681-fb21-4f43-96da-9841bcd0c546	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709000.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709000.000000", "text": "[HIC Design Followup] HIC Design Workshop Follow-up (Compute/Storage Design Sync)\\n\\nVijay led the meeting today. I jumped in to support Michele, and I plan to continue supporting this track until I receive formal notification otherwise.\\n\\nCluster Footprint & Node Sizing: We discussed downsizing the Control plane node on the 3rd site, and optimizing the overall cluster footprint. The goal is to reduce hardware expenses by finding the right balance of cluster sizes versus the number of control plane nodes. (against what Dennis said last time)\\n\\nDR & Stretched Patterns: Phil, Gareth, and Michele reviewed stretched patterns to ease DR requirements. A questionnaire has been sent out to all HIC ITSOs to gather feedback on their specific needs. AFAIK the only need is to provide active/standby functionality. I raised the question again today in the round.\\n\\nHA Patterns & RPO/RTO: We are aligning documentation around specific HA app patterns (Linux, Windows, SQL Always On, VCS Always On). The “Platform DR” patterns are already labeled, I have not seen such a documentation yet.\\n\\n A specific question was directed to me regarding Isovalent’s scalability and its limitations/impact on etcd when managing a large number of control planes (because of the cluster mesh solution). @janine I think you can take that one with you", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.823539+00	2026-05-27 06:22:31.090744+00	summarized	2026-05-26
484803bb-966a-469b-8238-a4ea77e44c67	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778196544.000064	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778196544.000064", "text": "[RCA analysis update]\\nWe need to wait. Looks like the \\"Defect\\" that was created is not correct, and they will need to re-create it. As soon as de \\"Defect\\" tikect is correct and landed in the appropiate \\"SRE\\" SNOW group, they  will initiate the RCA analysis. Then we can use the ticket as a communication means", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.050545+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.273475+00	delivered	2026-05-09
da6a8302-18fd-465a-a89b-002ee667c367	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703500.000000", "text": "[US/MX Workshops]: We have a request for the workshop to clarify our support engagement in both pilots (Test Migrations) and production migration (Volume Migrations). I need help from @Anne @Carina Almeida , @pdelashe, even @Nikos if you have any slides, ideas, workflows, screenshots, documents, share it them here and I will create a slide out of this. My understanding is the following about both process:\\n\\nPilot Migrations (Consulting-Led)\\nDuring the pilot phase, Red Hat Consulting will be heavily involved in the execution and troubleshooting. The goal here is to establish our baseline and refine our automation.\\n\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution.\\nExecution: Consulting is involved in the communication structure of the migration (we are passive listeners here).\\nFailure Handling (The New RCA Proposal): If a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back in VMware. The failed OpenShift VM is then moved to an isolated “Quarantine/Triage” environment. (Note: This isolation environment is not currently in place; we will officially propose building this during the upcoming workshops).\\nResolution: Consulting performs Root Cause Analysis (RCA) in the triage environment, finds the issue and ask for the fixes the underlying automation (Narender), and places the VM back into the backlog to be rescheduled for a future migration wave.\\n\\n\\n2. Volume / Production Migrations (Support-Led)\\n\\nOnce we move into bulk production migrations, the execution and issue resolution will shift entirely to our Support organization.\\n\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution to ensure global readiness.\\nExecution & Failure Handling: Handled 100% by Red Hat Support. This will leverage our Technical Account Managers (TAMs) across the different timezones to ensure “follow-the-sun” coverage, alongside the recently onboarded ESS team.\\nResolution: The Support and ESS teams will drive immediate break/fix resolutions and coordinate any necessary escalations directly.\\n\\n\\nPlease review this logic and let me know your thoughts or if you see any gaps.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PER_F4CE6A9D"}]	{U_PER_F4CE6A9D}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.033853+00	2026-05-27 05:29:56.718931+00	summarized	2026-05-26
e29e9493-a62c-4105-8697-33ecb6b15843	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777722200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777722200.000000", "text": "Reminder :slightly_smiling_face: https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C099TDJDDKL/p1779108201943439\\n@channel Let's try it again... :guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\\n\\nTo help us get through this programme andn.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\\n\\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote on Wednesday after our internal stand-up :wink:\\n\\nThread in proj-eos-mvp | May 18th | View messageJames Force  [11:49 AM]\\n@Shebi can you post that KCS you were showing earlier? It seems MutatingAdmissionPolicy(probably the most easiest and elegant solution here) isn't GA yet :disappointed: seems in still under TechPreviewNoUpgrade  see https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.21/html/postinstallation_configuration/post-install-cluster-tasks#nod[…]asks\\ndocs.redhat.comChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/solutions/7135435\\nRed Hat Customer PortalMTV Migrations fails as virt-v2v appliance runs out of memory - Red Hat Customer PortalConversion of Virtual Machine to OpenShift Virtualization fails with out of memory error. oom-killer is invoked during migration of Virtual Machine to OpenShift VirtualizationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\\nThere you go", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_35CC3553"}]	{U_GOOGLE_35CC3553}	2026-05-25 11:51:53.820561+00	2026-05-27 05:32:44.523705+00	summarized	2026-05-26
ec7065ca-2fc1-48c0-bdca-362a3a8ee1f9	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778208579.000099	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778208579.000099", "text": "@Carina Almeida I'll go to the US/MX meeting. My request for the TAMs is that they create a slide with a timeline with when all of the blocker issues under CAP will be released and with the OCP releases.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.642892+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.277872+00	delivered	2026-05-09
1112e06b-a51e-4818-b7a7-87d344e75f74	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777703800.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777703800.000000", "text": "[OTEL vs OCP out of the box demo today]\\n\\nTeam, Ravi booked a OTEL vs OCP demo for today at 10.30 am BST - Objective attached.\\nHe invited Raffa who's out, is there anyone available, who can demo the RH side of things? or should I ask to postpone this?\\n\\n@ricardo gregorio were you aware of this?\\n@Rydekull @janine @Shebi do you have time and the skills to help with this?\\n@Nikos would we have an SSP by change who could support this kind of demo in future?\\n\\nThanks (edited) \\nimage.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [10:20 AM]\\n[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\nVMs in scope 212; from 230 in initial scope, some dropped because they’re in the demise path, inventory errors and descoped: 23 ITSOs haven’t responded yet.\\nPlan:\\nMay 5th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 46 VMs\\nMay 5th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 47 VMs\\nMay 6th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 49 VMs\\nMay 6th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 42 VMs\\nMay 7th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 28 VMs\\n\\nUK Pilot:\\nNo delays on the UK Pilot plan; new clusters to be built on track\\nPlan:\\nMay 13th -> June 15th - Dev & UAT & OAT\\nJune 17 -> End of July - Contingency and Prod - Weekdays & WeekendsAlexander Rydekull  [10:50 AM]\\n[Wildcard certificates] Oh, right, so there's a meeting in 40 minutes on the topic of Wildcard certs, and it seems like Engineering is making up excuses from wht I can gather. They seem to claim that they cannot rotate wildcard/api certs without affecting VMs running on the platform.", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}]	{U_CARINA_D5667D0C}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.076002+00	2026-05-27 08:48:17.976805+00	summarized	2026-05-27
9d12aae5-9b79-431d-8ec4-090fda323911	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704200.000000	7777704201.000000	2	[{"ts": "7777704200.000000", "text": "[Build update]\\n\\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it. \\nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}, {"ts": "7777704201.000000", "text": "[Build Update]:\\n\\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel. \\n421 channel work is underway as well.\\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully. \\nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\\n\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823", "thread_ts": "7777704200.000000"}]	{U_PHILIP_740C6823}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.140773+00	2026-05-27 05:45:47.419757+00	summarized	2026-05-26
b6e1ed5c-f217-46f5-9955-9717fa7e4125	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777704600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777704600.000000", "text": "[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\\n\\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\\n\\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\\n\\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\\n\\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\\n\\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}]	{U_SAM_F28235E5}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.241702+00	2026-05-27 05:48:23.367625+00	summarized	2026-05-26
995d10dd-d1a2-4fd4-a345-ba5252a6b2eb	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778197625.000065	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778197625.000065", "text": "And @rspazzol Vinay has asked for you to stay away of all the migration issues; he said that they know what the RCA is and they are working with the ITSO to see how to fix it. And it is the second time he says so, so please, all your concerns about how we are dealing with migrations, please keep them inside Red Hat", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.063891+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.28515+00	delivered	2026-05-09
3073de0a-6815-4e6c-8c65-50fe14bf55a6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777705500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777705500.000000", "text": "[HIC - Workshop - Summary]: I am now on my way to NYC, and as I like to communicate much, I decided to create a summary of my impressions of the workshop; and along with what ATL will share, we will have a good idea on how the workshop was, and what it will come next, I have created a file on Google Docs with more details, I would like your comments over there so I we can correct or amend anything:  --> :use-thread:", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}]	{U_SEBAST_AC383055}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.380096+00	2026-05-27 05:50:09.263004+00	summarized	2026-05-26
c7390b0e-e621-4f82-a8f8-b0c967055d94	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209516.000256	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209516.000256", "text": "@Rydekull can you cover the GitOps meeting or do you rather want to join the migration call ?", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}]	{"Janine Eichler"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.605284+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.316158+00	delivered	2026-05-09
547a2d95-c37a-4f21-b711-33bf6fca1193	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777706600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777706600.000000", "text": "[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\\n\\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\\n\\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.559323+00	2026-05-27 05:54:15.730914+00	summarized	2026-05-26
ff1e8694-0b77-4831-a521-5cb1743a01f3	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778197470.000270	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778197470.000270", "text": "[Delivery Report]\\nPlease, don't forget to add your input here, by EOD today: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g39a69ff70c8_3_0#slide=id.g39a69ff70c8_3_0\\nGoogle Drive", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.740075+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.294353+00	delivered	2026-05-09
