92eb024e-d4d1-4ede-81b2-baf5630701ec	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778224601.000281	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778224601.000281", "text": "@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.838083+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.350216+00	delivered	2026-05-09
