69ad1d3d-fe10-41a4-9086-2c2b1c8ad116	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778232490.000130	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778232490.000130", "text": "[hyper-care] we need a slide on how the hyper-care works at a high level (for us/mx deck). We also need a low-level description of the process in agreement with the customer. @Anne @Carina Almeida @pdelashe I expect this to come from you but do let me know if I am wrong. We need clarification on the following:\\nhow does the customer engage with us when a migration fails\\nwho is available and response time. Is the OS a matter in this decision.\\ntroubleshooting environment (we cannot/should not access production) and level of collaboration with the migration team and service owners.. (RACI)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.039935+00	2026-05-09 14:24:00.407711+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
e41941cf-5490-4cf0-a0a5-b9bde2d6ed1d	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778247372.000132	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778247372.000132", "text": "[VM triage process] we need to propose a triage process to the back as this is clearly not moving. @Shebi @janine, here is an idea:\\nwhen a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back and the migrated VM is put in triage.\\nusing MTV, VM is moved from a production cluster/namespace to triage cluster/namespace\\nuse virtctl guestfs to manipulate the VM OS and\\n    a. change the VM IP to something compatible with the triage environment\\n    b. enable a local account with root capability\\nconfirm that the VM can start correct and local account works\\n5 delete original migrated VM\\ntroubleshoot the VM\\n7 once the resolution is confirmed, delete the VM\\nplease mentally verify these steps for both Linux and Windows OSes.\\n@Rydekull I know you are mostly focused on security, but we could use your input too here. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.061294+00	2026-05-09 14:30:00.16881+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
51efbb33-6c08-4b28-8d6d-ad1c652d1611	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778250553.000133	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778250553.000133", "text": "[build - network build issue] something to be aware of... the network folks have made an error in the build out of  everything outside the immediate lab. The tldr is LACP hasn't been configured on the switch side, thus right now we're essentially only leveraging single ports. Michael and Rushi are aware and will sort it out so hopefully all in hand, but just sharing for visibility if the topic comes up.", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.082747+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.489965+00	delivered	2026-05-09
