027aa07a-8cc4-4740-a27f-3c8e90f1dc03	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778235929.000149	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778235929.000149", "text": "[VM Migration]\\nSrinath and Abhishek are interested in NUMA aware VMs regarding their high performance applications.\\nMain question is how their current NUMA mappings on VMware would be translated to OCP+V.\\nI am currently go through the docs and sources regarding the current state of kubeVirt\\nhttps://kubevirt.io/user-guide/compute/numa/\\netc\\nIf anyone of you is deep in the matter, a short exchange would be appreciated.\\nOverall I asked that this would be perfect match for a testcase, they agreed and would need to organize such a VM into the current environment for us to migrate. (edited) \\nkubevirt.io\\nNUMA - KubeVirt user guide\\nDocumentation for KubeVirt", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.269594+00	2026-05-09 15:30:59.775279+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
b60e85bb-18c1-461d-b4f9-58679b070681	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778243670.000150	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778243670.000150", "text": "a bit of good news, today HSBC deployed three more clusters. minor non blocking automation issues reported, they will be addressed.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.278091+00	2026-05-09 15:36:00.34592+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
f1d19b54-76e5-45b3-8c38-218fbe365adf	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778244751.000151	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778244751.000151", "text": "[Bulk Migrations] :books:\\nAlso from me a bit of good news.\\nFirst iteration of bulk migrations was done.\\nBefore I share some numbers, I share one issue: from the 200 VMs they promised we have just around 60 available now, because 128 have been deleted due to some internal compliance issue on how those VMs have been deployed internally. Bit of a nuisance, I got promised they will bring them back asap, I hope so, until then we have to work with what we got.\\nThe Bulk Migration itself is run over MIO-X to get it as real as possible.\\nTest Case No 1 was done as cold and direct migration (storage offloading is currently not available as a feature in MIO-X, due it can not make sure that both source and target storage maps are the same and storage offload activated. I had a conversation with the team and Abhishek is now taken care of this to be implemented.)\\nSo, now some numbers:\\n61 VMs Migrated with 1 VM per Migrationplan :arrow_forward:\\n59 VMs with disksize of 100-150 GB, mix of Linux and Windows OS\\n- 52 VMs migrated successfully within a total timeframe of 43 (earliest) to 120 min (latest). :white_check_mark:\\n- 7 VMs failed through a freak configuration on VMware which said: 2 sockets and 1 cpu, this translates into 0.5 sockets, while the manifest actually expects an integer >=1 for the sockets value. :x:\\nThis has been identified and fixed, also Srinath mentioned this happend when the testing VMs have been created and should not re-occur within the production VMs. :check:\\n- 2 running into a MIO-X timeout (currently set to approx 3 hours) but those had 1,5 TB disk which took 5 hours and finished successfully :white_check_mark:\\nI will share in the Red Hat Teams channel the official Confluence page on this bulk migration test.\\nA lot more to come, especially looking forward to have 200 VMs with storage offload and various migration plan sizings. Good thing is that VM Migration and Testops Team works now together really well. We plan to have a bulk migration status call now two times a week.\\nObservability while we migrate is in the making by Srinath and will hopefully be gathered on the next iteration. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.289065+00	2026-05-09 15:42:00.201576+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
f63ff5e0-c571-4e65-8372-c19ddd122781	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778194052.000152	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778194052.000152", "text": "Related to migration projects, but a bit too late for us: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iDqlo42vOXs", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.299433+00	2026-05-09 15:48:00.0221+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
