162f84e1-6b4b-41ec-a862-57b4ccf8fcdf	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778226848.000188	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778226848.000188", "text": "[observability]\\n- customer wants to find a way of 'observing' the cluster build lifecycle, i.e., capturing/monitoring the build phases/progress/failures. This is because over the weekend 4x worker nodes out of 48x did not join a cluster that was built. Unsure how this can be done, so currently researching this. Thank you for helping @janine\\n- checked with Cyber team. Cluster 104, last 24h ingested 33.6 million events ~ 59.2G. It seems that they have not checked the contents in regards of what is useful, what is sensitive, etc\\n- reviewing Confluence doc in regards to OCP-V Security Requirement Matrix (defined by customer)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.790954+00	2026-05-09 17:07:00.568254+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
86d7495c-f7dc-41b5-b40a-a737654424fb	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227029.000189	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227029.000189", "text": "[Migration velocity]\\n@janine @Shebi @Rydekull iIn our call with ACN today, we agreed to document the specific challenges and constraints that can impact migration velocity.\\nWhile the document @Anne prepared outlines our advice to achieve velocity, we now need to explicitly list the challenges and constraints. Could you please add your input to that document? - Go Faster ideas\\nACN also raised a question regarding potential Miox restrictions. They were informed that Miox can only migrate 40 VMs in parallel. Are you aware of this limitation, or do you have a views on whether this is accurate?\\nThank you so much.\\nPS. @Nikos  and @rspazzol for info.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.80525+00	2026-05-09 17:13:00.298977+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
233f269f-b642-4c83-8fbe-375527f7147e	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227990.000190	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227990.000190", "text": "[team availability]\\nTeam for info we will start to send weekly team availability info to Vinay and his team. here is a print scren of this week's email.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.815333+00	2026-05-09 17:19:00.017179+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
0b4e5a6c-bf86-4453-bd3f-de762115ab61	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778243171.000191	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778243171.000191", "text": "[build]\\nSpoke with Mike on the LACP issue we came accross recently, they will add some checks on their side to mitigate this, but  he was curious if there was anything we can do on our side, I mentioned the lack of metrics in this area but he seemed happy about the upstream conversation and was curious to know if something did get added to node_exporter upstream when would that land in openshift\\nQuick call on the ACM prorogation policies and then created an issue on the backlog to attempt to remove dependency on ACM after the initial seed... I will try to pick this up when I get some time\\nRuishi dragged me into a call to discuss security policies and then went around the circles of gatekeeper, kyverno VAPs etc..  I circ led it back to the point of that VAPs were decided and work was already started here,,, I think there is a clear need for a proper backlog and planning of work as things feel a bit all over the place\\nRushi called me again on the gitops approach and his want to move to something completely different (this binary artefact approach). I told him again this won't work, but he wants to allign with some 'deploycontol' approaches of their... @janine I've pinged you on the links in the teams chat.. maybe can you help me here? I think we just need to educate here on our controls for gitops and route to live process. IIRC you were working on something around this area?\\nMTU... all our clusters MTU is just at 1400 (default)... this is probably a driver in the why live migrations are 'slow'....  @Rydekull I your help tomorrow on this to understand your last comment on the jump frames GH issue on upping this value to 9000\\nPure upgrade troubleshooting\\nSnapshot issue (102) - I've just sent the operator log to pure for 102 on the pending failed upgrade due to snapshots... hopefully they can script up something to address that ... however.... if their approach is to manually delete records out of etcd using etcdctl... not sure I really like that, doesn't exactly feel elegant!\\nVolume mapping (104)  - unfortunately the horrible idea I had the other day to manually remap volumes looks like it is a reality and the only way forward... albeit they provided us with a more elegant way to get the required info we need, and also let us know we don't need to define the targets in the purevolume resource", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.826559+00	2026-05-09 17:24:00.621968+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
41f46b77-280d-48f3-9c5a-bfdc1ea45693	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777708600.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777708600.000000", "text": "[VM Migration RDM to LUN issue]\\nTalked to engineering about the issue of MigrationPlan spec.rdmAsLun=true not setting the LUN type interface to SCSI and did open a bug for it:\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5387\\nThis should then finally allow us to discard the whole post-hook/ansible logic doing that atm.:jira: MTV-5387 [New] : MigrationPlan flag \\"rdmAsLun=true\\" does not change the interface typeAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerAlexander Rydekull  [11:23 AM]\\nI am just flabbergasted... I think I can currently count 10 people involved in a request to add \\"api.crowdstrike.com\\" into an allowlist for a proxy", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}]	{U_JENS_9E9831E8}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.804754+00	2026-05-27 06:19:45.65984+00	summarized	2026-05-26
