0e32af9c-ab8b-48ac-be19-4c4b7c125129	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209540.000220	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209540.000220", "text": "@Carina Almeida, @janine, @Rosemary Lynch and @James Force, for info the customer is still having issues with cluster hkoclu307. Specifically, that three nodes aren't able to register, having built successfully via ACM.\\nI've exhausted my troubleshooting on this and did request a few days ago that they capture all the diagnostic and debug info from myself and their networking team and then raise a RH support ticket.\\nWe can ssh into the problem nodes. I've checked the br-ex and it looks good. Both interfaces in the bond are good. It can nslookup and curl other endpoints e.g the default ingress controller. It just can't build a route to the API IP. No route to host and a tcpdump show arp requests being sent with no response. Their networking team is saying there's no issues on their side...", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.217842+00	2026-05-09 17:36:00.238958+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
205682b0-9e9d-4fee-8664-0914d51bff0f	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778216923.000223	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778216923.000223", "text": "Hi all,\\nI think it was mentioned last year, by @rspazzol @Sam Marland, in the other eos channel about demo of Network Observability. During the Sheffield workshops @Nikos mentioned \\"Network Observability Operator to be used for Non-HIC and data to be fed to HSBC cyber team\\".\\nWhat is the plan for this?\\nI need to read, but does anyone know what extra it provides (compare to the current node network metrics available)???", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.259991+00	2026-05-09 17:42:00.238741+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
