1e5eb3e3-df59-4127-8c55-680bb1b41eaf	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219517.000237	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219517.000237", "text": "Hey team,\\nfor the ones who are off tomorrow, I hope you all manage to switch off and rest :vacation_relax:\\nfor the ones off on Monday, I'll resend this message tomorrow :upside_down_face:", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.391293+00	2026-05-09 18:32:59.746306+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
dd588b43-46a8-4961-b433-33c659f72378	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778237700.000240	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778237700.000240", "text": "[VM Migration Debugging Session]\\nToday Martin Necas from engineering joined us to debug a variety of issues.\\nForemost the topic around migrating VMs with Shared Disks not take over their IP:\\nSuccessful workaround applied to the customer environment by making sure the VM is actually running before migration so the forklift controller can catch its metadata (this is done for all the VMs of the targeted VSphere), it stays in in-memory cache before the controller or its pod restarts (current caveat), a verbose warning is to be implemented to make the user aware of this process pattern.\\nWe migrated the VMs with their IPs preserved then. :check:\\nNext, a constant pita was solved by a new flag in the Migration Plans:\\nspec.rdmAsLun=true\\nThats really great as it was something important pending at the customer, as they do not need change the disks any longer manually, or by a post-hook. :check:\\nAlso, what is currently ongoing is that qemu-guest-agent sometimes not installs on Windows Servers, we gathered logs which have some hot leads to be followed up by engineering. :gear:\\nCase: https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\nRegarding the VMware Tools Cleanup, there is a much more smooth and stable option on the horizon now, its an early dev-preview and therefore no where documented so far, but with 2.11.4 we can enable this featureGate in MTV:\\noc patch ForkliftController  -n openshift-mtv forklift-controller  --type=merge -p '{\\"spec\\": {\\"feature_vsphere_vmware_driver_removal\\": \\"true\\"}}'\\nIt contains most of the famous VMware removal script from Github including other findings from Red Hat to cleanup the VMs. Sudhir and the team agreed to start testing it with the ultimate goals of removing all the post-hook removal scripts currently scrubbing VMware Tools. :check:\\nRegarding the Windows Failover Cluster issue to initialize and consume the shared disks we are still on going, with quite a range of potential error sources. Martin will now take it as priority and investigate in our RH labs. :wrench:\\nAt this point I want to highlight Martins amazing dedication to our HSBC project! He stayed with us in a marathon call for many hours answering and tackling wide range of customer questions until 11:00 pm at night in his timezone. Customer team was really impressed and pleased by that. If you got a few reward zone points to spare, Martin definitely deserves it :slightly_smiling_face: :+1: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.427418+00	2026-05-09 18:38:00.362463+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
ef21c9b8-eb6c-45b8-9f0c-ec8a1ac5798c	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778230357.000037	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778230357.000037", "text": "[SRE Qs]\\n- Suppress info alerts in the alertmanager config [Kuldeep has a PR with Receiver: null]. Need to investigate if this is the best way to achieve this\\n- They raised a support ticket for Insights alerts. I mentioned that this is is disconnected cluster and cannot go out. I will review some KBs about how to deal with these rules in disconnected clusters.\\n- They asked about collecting hardware metrics. I mentioned that what I had found is not much and already shared with Onkar. They should look into querying/exporting data from iDRAC (Onkar is aware of this).\\n- There is an alert about system memory reservation (they've got a support ticket open). Basically the kubeletconfig CR has a paremeter configured in the wrong level (openshift-config app).\\n- They asked about SLI/SLO, which I mentioned I could not find any \\"template\\" guidance with our ROSA SRE Team. These vary from business to business. Thresholds have to be meaningful and achievable. For once reached and action should take place.\\n- There seem to be some overlap/miscomm between SRE and OBS team as to who owns what (alerts + HW metrics)\\n[observability]\\n- pushed new metrics and collector endpoint to cluster 102.\\n- setup cyber Splunk  endpoint to forward audit logs. Validate data flow with cyber splunk team.\\n- added a filter to remove get/list/watch verbs. Will review that with cyber Splunk team tomorrow.\\n- Create a variable to tie otel collector LB endpoint to region (will review this with Raffa)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:22.583253+00	2026-05-09 19:06:00.233344+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
