d5030652-31c4-47ca-83a9-62116e71e8a7	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219373.000093	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219373.000093", "text": "Question for architects: I've just updated ACM to 2.16 on 101 and this now includes some new features including:\\nCentralised Observability for Virtual Machines including right sizing recommendations: https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga#\\nAbility to manage VM's centrally from ACM search across all managed clusters.\\nShould we look to propose switching these features on for the customer? I know they have their own observability solution.\\nRed Hat Developer\\nAdvanced Cluster Management 2.16 right-sizing recommendation GA | Red Hat Developer\\nAnnouncing the Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management 2.16 general availability (GA) of namespace and virtualization right-sizing recommendations\\nMar 17th\\nhttps://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.538335+00	2026-05-09 19:39:59.870536+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
5bd25fa7-3d49-48da-bdea-439615b7c3fa	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778210681.000101	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778210681.000101", "text": "[tam meeeting] slide deck shared, https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-Eqtb1k1oDZYRs8MxZ-wyF_mT4H0DyEO3rEpek-GVFE/edit?slide=id.g5d5641e02e_4_6#slide=id.g5d5641e02e_4_6", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.674993+00	2026-05-09 19:45:00.287268+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
8f9ea98c-20c0-4d50-a671-f04264cdfdd4	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778220157.000277	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778220157.000277", "text": "[Entra change on Monday 11 at 5pm BST]\\nTeam there's an Entra change happening to Prod on Monday at 5pm BST and HSBC is asking for RH support.\\nI'll get more info about this change and share it. Meanwhile who could support this? - @rspazzol my first thought is you since this will be compatible with US hours... :thinking_face:", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.797884+00	2026-05-09 19:56:59.680938+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
a6f8d5a9-7d79-4cce-bef9-77be87db9161	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709100.000000", "text": "[Question for the Build Team]\\nmust-gather is not working on some of the Prod Clusters, and we need those for the migration proactive cases. Can anyone check the case to see what is mieeing in the clusters and see if it can be fixed for future builds?: https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04445461", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.830184+00	2026-05-27 06:25:04.279838+00	summarized	2026-05-26
8ff1b5f9-f879-4274-a7ee-fbdab111119d	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778219565.000105	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778219565.000105", "text": "[build] I'm suggesting we go quite aggressive on the no_proxy configuration i.e. set things like 128.0.0.0/8 to cover whole address spaces... as we've had a couple of issues now where building clusters and the install never happens and gets stuck as ironic gets a proxy issue (expected) as it tries to speak to the public address... they are using IP addresses (for say nodes) that are actually public address privately i.e. not in standard with RFC-1918 so this is bound to happen. Does anyone have any concerns/feedback here? @Rydekull @rspazzol @Philip Jones?", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.726682+00	2026-05-09 19:51:00.100445+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
b5c58945-edc3-4e79-9097-a758b3ce93a4	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778198273.000113	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778198273.000113", "text": "[Migration Update]\\nPilot Phase 2 includes only DEV, UAT and OAT (Operational Acceptance Test) VMS and will be run during mornings (UK Time) so no need to follow-the-sun model yet\\nDetailed plan covering Pilot Phase #2 and Country Pilot (UK) will be shared on the Red Hat Channel on Teams - plan covers almost 3000 VMs migrated by Mid June. This plan assumes that 2 more clusters will be ready by mid and end of may for fabrics 113 and 122. By June 15th everything should be ready to start migrating Contingency and Production VMs.\\nAs soon as we have the “committed” dates for HK clusters for the selected fabrics, the planning for HK should start\\nHypercare: There is a meeting today between Chris, Vinay & ACN to discuss Hypercare. We have intentionally been left out of this meeting\\nReminders:\\n@Shebi  to send the list of “common issues found during migrations” that he extracted from support cases to the VM Migration Workstream\\n@pdelashe to share with Damon and Viky the analysis of failure ratios in other projects (to be reviewed by Brenna first)", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.816496+00	2026-05-09 20:02:00.258419+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
3eccf105-e18a-4302-8a52-f87638cb9b36	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228406.000126	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228406.000126", "text": "[observability]\\nadded couple of namespaces and a message keyword to the existing filter setup in the logforwarder resource;\\nteam work with @Philip Jones to get the dell powermax metrics available;\\nadded couple of powermax metrics to the otel configuration on 104. observability team with validate data flowing into splunk tomorrow.\\nenabled, manually on 104, servicemonitor to make Trident-metrics available. At quick glance could not work out array capacity;\\nthanks @Philip Jones for pulling metrics list from 104 manually;\\nraised PR to enable custom alerts to monitor OTEL Collector health, message queue usage and failure of messages not queuing locally or not sending to the OTEL Collector Gateway.", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}]	{"Ricardo Gregorio"}	2026-05-08 17:54:23.988742+00	2026-05-09 20:07:59.81188+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
ae6e893d-28d0-4cea-98bd-fd10548306ab	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778228767.000127	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778228767.000127", "text": "@Rydekull @Shebi\\nSo regarding Sudhirs request on the failed migration of Windows Failover Cluster we made some progress over the day:\\nProblem 1 solved: The migration itself is now successfull with all PVCs being available to both VMs. :check:\\nMulti rooted issues, the migration plan execution order and configuration. Also the disks have been there once and then recreated as copy-[pvc-name..] which led to the VMs had different set of disks mounted.\\nProblem 2 solved: The VMs do boot up now successfully after the Migration. :check:\\nIssue was wrong NAD mappings and one NAD missing in the destination namespace.\\nNew problem: The Windows Failover Cluster itself fails, I have some experience with Windows Server from 10+ years ago, nevertheless I wondered where do we draw the line in supporting applications after the migration.\\nAnyway, when trying to bring the disks online it just says device i/o error, the Windows OS does see the disks but can not communicate... totally sounds like the good old SCSI3-PR issue has another place in the spotlight... ?", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}]	{"Jens Feind"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.004082+00	2026-05-09 20:13:00.287147+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
28d73445-005b-47a1-a01a-d7d6affcea7c	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778201235.000135	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778201235.000135", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\nTeam I had a sync with Maj this morning and we talked mainly about Ny/Mx trip (only praises to our team here) and status of hadware.\\n@pdelashe I want to sync with you about how this hardware plan is linked to ACN migration plans.\\n@Natasha Ghoojamanian we will need to link this then to staffing planning.\\n@rspazzol @Shebi - you don't have any PM support for the NY DC migration approach / testing. I'm wondering whether a PM should be involved in this or not yet? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.108204+00	2026-05-09 20:18:59.951318+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
e3cb35b6-0598-40a9-b216-3c7619ebe9cd	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778221525.000145	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778221525.000145", "text": "[Resourcing call with Vinay and Programme team]\\nTeam,\\nAnne and I met with Vinay and the Programme Team today. While the objective was to position the new staff, the discussion evolved into a broader conversation regarding team allocation.\\nWe walked them through our Governance and Work Distribution slides, which have now been shared with them for reference.\\nA key request from Vinay is that our team maintains an 80% dedication to ENG work. This means ENG tasks take priority over all other activities. In case you have a conflict in priorities, please notify Rose, Patricia, or myself immediately so we can coordinate with ENG for prioritisation. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.229048+00	2026-05-09 20:24:00.339293+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
605d449d-f521-4bfe-b6aa-fcf97e29450b	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709200.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709200.000000", "text": "[Question on parallell VM Migration limits]\\nI've posted it also in VM Migration Teams Channel -> Is there a real limit on parallel VMMigration? In One Plan? In many Plans? Iḿ asking because there is a miscommunication between Eng, SRE and MigraitonPlanning Teams, and some of them are concerned that if we migrate 44VMs in parallel this afternoon, something will crashCarina Almeida  [11:35 AM]\\n:exclamation-circle: [RH Delivery Team Updates]\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nWe have new members joining us next week and in June, alongside some internal shuffling. You can find the full details of these transitions in the Team Changes - May/June 2026.\\n\\nWhat to expect:\\n\\nChannel Access: New members will be added to the relevant Slack channels by the end of this week.\\nIntro Calls: Please keep an eye on your calendars; some of you will receive invites for introductory calls on Friday afternoon and Monday.\\nPeering: Starting next week, we will be asking some team members to begin peering with our new joiners to help with their onboarding.\\n\\n\\nPlease help us to welcome our new team members :relaxed: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.837677+00	2026-05-27 06:28:37.443617+00	summarized	2026-05-26
68951069-1c42-4ea5-9700-1b27a98ee254	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778227840.000160	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778227840.000160", "text": "PJ Build Update:\\nPortworx CSI driver updated to 26.1.1 on all lab clusters.\\nLargely successful, but 102 cluster has a MAJOR issue with snapshots... There are >4700 vm snapshots and volumesnapshotcontent resources present, but there are 0 volumesnapshots! This problem is breaking the CSI migration pods and causing them to fail :(\\nWe don't have an easy solution or explanation. If we manually create a snapshot, no new snapshot instance is created, just the content and the virtmachine upgrades.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.419266+00	2026-05-09 20:29:59.885045+00	pending_retry	2026-05-09
5385496f-47c0-4869-869a-50512d1cdaf9	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778204507.000167	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778204507.000167", "text": "[Migration Pilot2 update]\\nUpdated the \\"on call\\" team for the 1st week to include Janine&Alex as Shebi will be in us/MX\\nStart date has been pushed to May 5th (as there is a quite period that finishes on May 4th)\\nLooks like some of the VMs with RDM disks are sitting on HP storage that does not support storage offload, so they will be moved to either Pure or Dell before migrating, which will imply > 10m down time\\nThey are thinking to create a new Change Request Category to accelerate the ITSO response time (I think they are using Patching now, which doesn't sound much urgent)", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.516424+00	2026-05-12 05:07:55.496384+00	delivered	2026-05-09
bb1ccb20-beb0-4ac7-a3d6-216c201ce193	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709500.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709500.000000", "text": "[HK hardware analysis] I have a request to confirm support for servers in HK, @Philip Jones @Rydekull can I delegate this request to you?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}]	{U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.856176+00	2026-05-27 06:30:51.102219+00	summarized	2026-05-26
747ddf18-b946-49bd-a1c7-a1f4668b896a	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778235536.000176	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778235536.000176", "text": "[build]\\ntroubleshooted the pure issues making progress root cause, session with pure on monday\\nspent the majority of my time today time with Suhas and Sourav on going over the remaining custom compliance operator rules, the final remaing things are not from the CIS KubeVirt benchmarks but custom HSBC AI invented ones so some not relevant/unclear, but think we're close to wrapping this piece of work up\\nwent over next steps for the remote worker piece with Vinayak - it's a bit slow going but the priority on this has seemed to get lower so somewhat expected\\nclarified the kubeletconfig changes required for the SRE team ... again, but the point/approach has stuck now as they've raised a PR for it now\\nbonus: there is a bit of traction again on getting LACP link aggregation metrics for node exporter after prompting it... fingers crossed as this would be a nice addition and with a prom alert this could be quite informative and useful https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/issues/1604#issuecomment-4299123571\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.630228+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.115143+00	embedded	2026-05-09
0fc65802-22ad-47c6-b766-13e3010b7bee	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778220518.000278	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778220518.000278", "text": "[VIB Update] Roy and @janine joined a call with Abhishek and we agreed actions. The summary is that HSBC will try to get to 0.3.0, in the meantime Roy will share a script for Abhi to test if there is still a failure through parallelism execution and RH team will update documentation to reflect the VIB requirements.", "type": "message", "user": "Nikolaos Goulias"}]	{"Nikolaos Goulias"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.811153+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.198043+00	embedded	2026-05-09
b900b3de-0140-40eb-801d-1e645e893534	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709700.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709700.000000", "text": "[2 urgent things for today]\\nIf they are not solved yet...\\nMTV 2.11.6 Installed in Lab so customer can test the infamous \\"VIB Issue\\"\\nProduction clusters being able to generate must-gathers. Starting today we are going to migrate VMs to different clusters, and we have to be able to upload must-gathers to the cases\\n[1 not so urgent]\\nI need to know who is responsible for adding Pre-Checks to MIoX, so they can add one related to XFS repair issue, that can prevent VMs in such a state to be migrated at all, reducing the number of failures\\n[Reminder]\\nRicardo and Arpit are supporting the war rooms today. I'll ping them if they are requiredRosemary Lynch  [10:20 AM]\\n[Delivery Report] Will be sent at noon today covering last Thursday to close of business Wednesday. @Rydekull can you provide an update for Security please. @Shebi can you add the latest for the Design elements please? @Philip Jones, @James Force @atolani @jfeind @ricardo gregorio can you provide any relevant update from the build side please. @Petros & @pdelashe can you add the Migration updated please? All updates before 11am GMT if you can", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}]	{U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.866701+00	2026-05-26 01:52:00.298107+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
bc2fb5dc-7c14-4026-b108-84637d1fa161	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778199675.000195	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778199675.000195", "text": "[OTEL vs OCP out of the box demo today]\\nTeam, Ravi booked a OTEL vs OCP demo for today at 10.30 am BST - Objective attached.\\nHe invited Raffa who's out, is there anyone available, who can demo the RH side of things? or should I ask to postpone this?\\n@ricardo gregorio were you aware of this?\\n@Rydekull @janine @Shebi do you have time and the skills to help with this?\\n@Nikos would we have an SSP by change who could support this kind of demo in future?\\nThanks (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:24.883601+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.293251+00	embedded	2026-05-09
3585597e-b4c6-4909-b1c3-5d6101315b03	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778197232.000212	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778197232.000212", "text": "[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}]	{"Sam Marland"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.131512+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.384725+00	embedded	2026-05-09
53ad599e-0a34-48c2-9ee7-2ff0b508f7b5	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209119.000219	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209119.000219", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\nMexico:\\nFabric delivery to Engineering (ENG) expected around May 15th.\\nFull migration planned for October, though the DMZ presents a significant challenge.\\nIndia:\\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\\nDMZ (General):\\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\\nThis issue also affects the UK.\\nHong Kong (HK):\\nReprioritization work is complete.\\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\\nUnited States (US):\\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\\nNote: EOS is their second priority.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.201332+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.488208+00	embedded	2026-05-09
d96b534a-4778-40c5-9296-b0cefaaf43de	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777709900.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777709900.000000", "text": "[Build: PJ]\\n\\nGood meeting to discuss the HSBC git control and commit strategy. \\nContinued with documenting the new release and cluster upgrade processes.\\n... 90% sure there won't be stretch clusters, but final decision is pending...\\nSome queries raised from Cisco relating to customisations to OCP Virt. \\nThey're asking if they could change OCP Virt to run virt handler pods to in host networking mode. This is to ensure that live migration traffic is sent via the management interface, now they're able to split traffic across multiple interfaces e.g. management bond and a VM bond. This is impacting their ability to offer live migrations with the current build.\\n\\nWe need to review the ACM cluster and ensure it can deploy new clusters with Cilium networking enabled.\\nI will be away from Fri 22nd, returning Wed 27th and will need someone to cover the Isovalent calls in my absence.  @janine, are you okay to cover these days? Not sure we need to cover the recharge day?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}]	{U_PHILIP_740C6823}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.877098+00	2026-05-26 01:48:00.027275+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
9f98300d-8ba8-4c39-909e-c2201b86b1ed	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778201584.000244	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778201584.000244", "text": "[HIC - Workshop - Summary]: I am now on my way to NYC, and as I like to communicate much, I decided to create a summary of my impressions of the workshop; and along with what ATL will share, we will have a good idea on how the workshop was, and what it will come next, I have created a file on Google Docs with more details, I would like your comments over there so I we can correct or amend anything:  --> :use-thread:", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}]	{"Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.479267+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.655263+00	embedded	2026-05-09
6f4405e9-d67e-4c2a-8ea0-085de9b4652d	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778210589.000249	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778210589.000249", "text": "[pure storage driver upgrade issue] @Philip Jones @James Force I am trying to figure out where we are with all the email on the subject. Would it be fair to say that we fixed the issues in 104 and 102? Do we have a plan for future upgrades?", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}]	{"Raffaele Spazzoli"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.53582+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.746404+00	embedded	2026-05-09
6cb92bdb-e977-46a7-a865-5b23f0716042	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778225770.000250	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778225770.000250", "text": "[Consulting Support Model during Migrations]\\nI've put together mi ideas and what I've proposed to ACN and HSBC as our support during migrations & hipercare in a Presentation format here: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1BJE9tmRgpDlAWTAtbRugZffAxIpJP6a7zkQKb75plWA/edit?slide=id.p1#slide=id.p1 (edited) \\nGoogle Slides", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.542729+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.886868+00	embedded	2026-05-09
bcd532d0-386d-4098-b0a2-8b2f30f1f20b	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778196971.000251	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778196971.000251", "text": "[302 pure storage error] I think James Force is aware of it (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}]	{"Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.549608+00	2026-05-09 21:09:11.97588+00	embedded	2026-05-09
87c1d536-5125-410d-a953-47ab87d85ba1	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778199672.000252	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778199672.000252", "text": "Team, Anne, Nickos, David and I are in a whole day workshop today. Please shout if you need any of us.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}]	{"Carina Almeida"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.55833+00	2026-05-09 21:09:12.060981+00	embedded	2026-05-09
a68c5dec-128a-43d1-9fca-d706b7335163	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778222547.000267	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778222547.000267", "text": "Hmm, Andrews mail about ongoing training\\nHi, unfortunately the Red Hat SME was again unable to join the Day 2 Q&A Session today, we now have several Red Hat Technical Questions I need feedback on.\\nWho's supposed to be joining?", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}]	{"Alexander Rydekull"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.711158+00	2026-05-09 21:09:12.15044+00	embedded	2026-05-09
316eeabb-2c2f-4fac-8a64-84d92cd16959	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778209056.000276	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778209056.000276", "text": "@Rydekull @janine do you know where the point around workloads running on control plane nodes (schedulable masters) ended up with Natti? The folks writing/reviewing the security polcies (VAPs and Compliance rules etc) are asking", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}]	{"James Force"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.787869+00	2026-05-09 21:09:13.202817+00	embedded	2026-05-09
fa2cc904-3b94-4b55-9dee-f4c8d02ff612	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778222800.000280	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778222800.000280", "text": "Isovalent Update:\\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}]	{"Philip Jones"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.830813+00	2026-05-09 21:09:13.342049+00	embedded	2026-05-09
109b1564-1e36-41d1-8393-c4c0ea848c09	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778202091.000271	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778202091.000271", "text": "[VIB Version Issue] @Rydekull @janine Abhishek reached out to me to get more help about this. Based on his message, he does not fully understand the need of specific VIB versions and their relation to MTV versions. Can you please help him with a way forward? Roy is also engaged on this in case we need engineering support.\\nLet me know if I can somehow help, I want to give him a clear way forward process-wise. He does not get answers so he reached out to everyone in Red Hat (he thought Roy was support :grimacing:). (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Nikolaos Goulias"}]	{"Nikolaos Goulias"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.74888+00	2026-05-09 21:09:13.489636+00	embedded	2026-05-09
92c7fadf-8f51-405c-8de9-07ea2cab746e	T01EOS001	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	1778201864.000284	\N	1	[{"ts": "1778201864.000284", "text": "[Descheduler] turns out the descheduler's AffinityAndTaints Profile doesn't take preferred scheduling into consideration, only requiredDuringScheduling. existing RFE: https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7370. @Rydekull @Shebi @rspazzol - anyone got other ideas to get the workloads re-balanced to their preferred sites in the HIC  scenario (site A is lost, VMs are started on site B, at some point site A is back) other than using external automation?", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}]	{"Janine Eichler"}	2026-05-08 17:54:25.864773+00	2026-05-09 21:09:13.602681+00	embedded	2026-05-09
2c5b5159-3d48-4e51-813f-80dcf7d63bf6	T_EOS_MVP	153c4abb-b8f9-4e4b-8be0-c6e189ffd9b0	7777710100.000000	\N	1	[{"ts": "7777710100.000000", "text": "[build/security etcd encryption]\\nSo... Sourav has been working with security on all things compliance related and commvault etcd backups and.. it's seemingly been decided (by security) that etcd needs to be encrypted. I know we wanted to push doing this until 4.22 when that KMS integration comes in.. but seems they want to do something in the interim... so it looks like we'll have to turn on etcd encryption and the commvault backups will backup the db and keys to the same place (daft we know, but security was okay with this).. defiantly feels a box ticking exercise, but I'm not that opposed to push back on this too much as it does't really have any negative impact too much (just seems a little silly)... thoughts? @rspazzol @Rydekull @janine", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}]	{U_JAMES_F3856179}	2026-05-25 11:51:52.889853+00	2026-05-26 02:22:59.983314+00	pending_retry	2026-05-25
