cc6e5f37-b16a-430c-990b-2fe41fae3f4d	ec6a32ee-dfb0-4162-97da-cc5057ded35a	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on the migration project, noting that the initial support period passed without issues. The first pilot phase is ongoing with one server, and the team will review the results later this week.\\n\\nThere is currently a disagreement regarding the speed of the next phase. Vinay wants to speed up the process by skipping standard approval steps and safety protocols to begin moving data immediately. However, Damon is pushing back on this, as he believes moving too quickly without proper checks creates unnecessary risk for the project.", "headline": "Update on migration progress and internal discussions regarding project speed and safety.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Escalate support needs to the technical account managers.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Lead a project review meeting by the end of the week.", "Vinay: Confirm the timeline for the remaining pilot locations."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reports that the Hypercare period concluded with no activity, prompting the escalation of proactive support cases to TAMs. Pilot Phase 1 remains active with a single VM, with a retrospective scheduled for the end of the week.\\n\\nRegarding Pilot Phase 2, there is internal friction regarding scope and velocity. Vinay is advocating for an accelerated migration path by bypassing ITSO approvals and standard Accenture-defined processes for Fabric 111 categories 1-3. Damon is actively resisting this approach to mitigate the risks associated with at-scale migration at this maturity level.", "headline": "Migration project status update covering Hypercare, Pilot phases, and scope acceleration risks.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Share proactive support case with TAMs.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Conduct Pilot Phase 1 retrospective by end of week.", "Vinay: Provide availability dates for the 3 fabrics in the Country Pilot."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on the migration project, noting that the initial support period passed without issues. The first pilot phase is ongoing with one server, and the team will review the results later this week.\\n\\nThere is currently a disagreement regarding the speed of the next phase. Vinay wants to speed up the process by skipping standard approval steps and safety protocols to begin moving data immediately. However, Damon is pushing back on this, as he believes moving too quickly without proper checks creates unnecessary risk for the project.", "headline": "Update on migration progress and internal discussions regarding project speed and safety.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Escalate support needs to the technical account managers.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Lead a project review meeting by the end of the week.", "Vinay: Confirm the timeline for the remaining pilot locations."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reports that the Hypercare period concluded with no activity, prompting the escalation of proactive support cases to TAMs. Pilot Phase 1 remains active with a single VM, with a retrospective scheduled for the end of the week.\\n\\nRegarding Pilot Phase 2, there is internal friction regarding scope and velocity. Vinay is advocating for an accelerated migration path by bypassing ITSO approvals and standard Accenture-defined processes for Fabric 111 categories 1-3. Damon is actively resisting this approach to mitigate the risks associated with at-scale migration at this maturity level.", "headline": "Migration project status update covering Hypercare, Pilot phases, and scope acceleration risks.", "action_items": ["Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Share proactive support case with TAMs.", "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia: Conduct Pilot Phase 1 retrospective by end of week.", "Vinay: Provide availability dates for the 3 fabrics in the Country Pilot."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:55.478665+00
73978113-7518-42a4-9683-c4754964494f	c1712ff9-d9de-4d49-8470-d59661a3d518	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reported that the team successfully moved the virtual machine for the Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev service today. After the move, the team performed checks to ensure the service is working correctly, and all tests passed.\\n\\nLooking ahead, the team is preparing for the next stage of the project. A larger migration involving 9 virtual machines is scheduled to take place on Wednesday, April 15th.", "headline": "The first phase of the virtual machine migration project is successfully underway.", "action_items": ["Complete the migration of 9 additional virtual machines on April 15th."], "key_decisions": ["The initial migration test was successful.", "The next set of migrations is set for Wednesday, April 15th."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed the successful migration of the VM associated with the Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev service as part of the Migration Event Pilot Phase 1 #2. Post-migration service validation was executed and verified as successful.\\n\\nThe project is now transitioning to the next phase of the migration schedule. The subsequent migration event is confirmed for Wednesday, April 15th, with a scope increase to 9 VMs.", "headline": "Successful completion of Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev VM migration during Phase 1 pilot.", "action_items": ["Execute migration of 9 VMs on Wednesday, April 15th."], "key_decisions": ["Migration of Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev VM completed successfully.", "Next migration event scheduled for Wednesday, April 15th."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia reported that the team successfully moved the virtual machine for the Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev service today. After the move, the team performed checks to ensure the service is working correctly, and all tests passed.\\n\\nLooking ahead, the team is preparing for the next stage of the project. A larger migration involving 9 virtual machines is scheduled to take place on Wednesday, April 15th.", "headline": "The first phase of the virtual machine migration project is successfully underway.", "action_items": ["Complete the migration of 9 additional virtual machines on April 15th."], "key_decisions": ["The initial migration test was successful.", "The next set of migrations is set for Wednesday, April 15th."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed the successful migration of the VM associated with the Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev service as part of the Migration Event Pilot Phase 1 #2. Post-migration service validation was executed and verified as successful.\\n\\nThe project is now transitioning to the next phase of the migration schedule. The subsequent migration event is confirmed for Wednesday, April 15th, with a scope increase to 9 VMs.", "headline": "Successful completion of Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev VM migration during Phase 1 pilot.", "action_items": ["Execute migration of 9 VMs on Wednesday, April 15th."], "key_decisions": ["Migration of Enterprise-Telephony-UK-Dev VM completed successfully.", "Next migration event scheduled for Wednesday, April 15th."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:55.520385+00
ba9ab4c6-1be6-49e5-9b5b-14f159a1b254	11ee8c1c-1804-4a42-a51f-371adf38fe62	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull shared that the team is meeting to discuss whether to use 'wildcard' security certificates for our systems. These certificates are a way to manage website security across multiple addresses at once.\\n\\nAlexander Rydekull mentioned that Natti is currently explaining and defending the reasoning behind this approach. We are waiting for more information on the final decision and how it might affect our current setup.", "headline": "The team is currently reviewing the use of wildcard security certificates.", "action_items": ["Alexander Rydekull to share the results of the discussion once the meeting concludes."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull initiated a status update regarding the ongoing architectural evaluation of wildcard certificate deployment. The discussion is centered on the security implications and operational feasibility of utilizing wildcard certificates within the existing SSL/TLS infrastructure.\\n\\nAlexander Rydekull noted that Natti is currently leading the technical defense of the wildcard approach, addressing potential security concerns and architectural requirements during the meeting. Further technical specifications and implementation details are expected to follow.", "headline": "Evaluation of wildcard certificate implementation for SSL/TLS infrastructure currently in progress.", "action_items": ["Alexander Rydekull to provide an update on the outcome of the wildcard certificate implementation meeting."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull shared that the team is meeting to discuss whether to use 'wildcard' security certificates for our systems. These certificates are a way to manage website security across multiple addresses at once.\\n\\nAlexander Rydekull mentioned that Natti is currently explaining and defending the reasoning behind this approach. We are waiting for more information on the final decision and how it might affect our current setup.", "headline": "The team is currently reviewing the use of wildcard security certificates.", "action_items": ["Alexander Rydekull to share the results of the discussion once the meeting concludes."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull initiated a status update regarding the ongoing architectural evaluation of wildcard certificate deployment. The discussion is centered on the security implications and operational feasibility of utilizing wildcard certificates within the existing SSL/TLS infrastructure.\\n\\nAlexander Rydekull noted that Natti is currently leading the technical defense of the wildcard approach, addressing potential security concerns and architectural requirements during the meeting. Further technical specifications and implementation details are expected to follow.", "headline": "Evaluation of wildcard certificate implementation for SSL/TLS infrastructure currently in progress.", "action_items": ["Alexander Rydekull to provide an update on the outcome of the wildcard certificate implementation meeting."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.625444+00
