9c8e4911-7198-40fa-9843-067f28e8f48e	b6d6d770-c7ed-45f9-93dc-0f1bc4ff8c78	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio has reached out to the team to understand which AI tools are currently being used for work tasks outside of our standard customer-facing systems.\\n\\nThis information is being collected to get a better sense of how the team is utilizing AI to improve their daily productivity and to ensure we have visibility into the tools being used.", "headline": "Ricardo Gregorio is surveying the team on their use of external AI tools.", "action_items": ["Team members to share which AI tools they are using with Ricardo Gregorio."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio initiated a discovery thread to audit the current landscape of AI tool adoption among team members. The query specifically targets the utilization of external AI-driven software solutions that operate outside of the established customer-facing environment.\\n\\nThis request serves as a preliminary data-gathering step to assess the current tech stack and potential shadow IT risks associated with third-party AI tool usage.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding external AI tool integration and usage patterns outside the customer environment.", "action_items": ["Team members to provide documentation or feedback regarding their current external AI tool usage to Ricardo Gregorio."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio has reached out to the team to understand which AI tools are currently being used for work tasks outside of our standard customer-facing systems.\\n\\nThis information is being collected to get a better sense of how the team is utilizing AI to improve their daily productivity and to ensure we have visibility into the tools being used.", "headline": "Ricardo Gregorio is surveying the team on their use of external AI tools.", "action_items": ["Team members to share which AI tools they are using with Ricardo Gregorio."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio initiated a discovery thread to audit the current landscape of AI tool adoption among team members. The query specifically targets the utilization of external AI-driven software solutions that operate outside of the established customer-facing environment.\\n\\nThis request serves as a preliminary data-gathering step to assess the current tech stack and potential shadow IT risks associated with third-party AI tool usage.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding external AI tool integration and usage patterns outside the customer environment.", "action_items": ["Team members to provide documentation or feedback regarding their current external AI tool usage to Ricardo Gregorio."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.123936+00
a66075c7-0167-44df-a117-f4acf8dc0181	e2c001cf-5bdd-42ff-9878-dbf5d5e01a9e	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has identified a problem with a customer's project involving moving data from HPE storage systems to Dell storage systems. Although the process is designed to work between different brands, the migration is currently failing.\\n\\nBecause the project is urgent and Raffaele Spazzoli will be away on leave, he is handing the task over to Janine. They plan to meet today to ensure Janine has all the necessary information to resolve the issue for the customer.", "headline": "Urgent assistance needed for a storage migration project between different hardware vendors.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli and Janine to meet today to discuss the migration issue.", "Janine to take over the project from Raffaele Spazzoli."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reports a failure in an 'any-to-any' storage offload migration workflow specifically involving a transition from HPE to Dell hardware. The issue persists despite the expectation of vendor-agnostic interoperability.\\n\\nDue to the urgency of the migration and Raffaele Spazzoli’s upcoming PTO, the issue is being escalated. Engineering support from Roy has been delayed due to PTO, necessitating a handoff to Janine to ensure continuity and technical resolution.", "headline": "Interoperability failure reported during cross-vendor storage offload migration from HPE to Dell.", "action_items": ["Janine to sync with Raffaele Spazzoli regarding the HPE to Dell migration issue.", "Janine to assume ownership of the migration support case from Raffaele Spazzoli."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has identified a problem with a customer's project involving moving data from HPE storage systems to Dell storage systems. Although the process is designed to work between different brands, the migration is currently failing.\\n\\nBecause the project is urgent and Raffaele Spazzoli will be away on leave, he is handing the task over to Janine. They plan to meet today to ensure Janine has all the necessary information to resolve the issue for the customer.", "headline": "Urgent assistance needed for a storage migration project between different hardware vendors.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli and Janine to meet today to discuss the migration issue.", "Janine to take over the project from Raffaele Spazzoli."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reports a failure in an 'any-to-any' storage offload migration workflow specifically involving a transition from HPE to Dell hardware. The issue persists despite the expectation of vendor-agnostic interoperability.\\n\\nDue to the urgency of the migration and Raffaele Spazzoli’s upcoming PTO, the issue is being escalated. Engineering support from Roy has been delayed due to PTO, necessitating a handoff to Janine to ensure continuity and technical resolution.", "headline": "Interoperability failure reported during cross-vendor storage offload migration from HPE to Dell.", "action_items": ["Janine to sync with Raffaele Spazzoli regarding the HPE to Dell migration issue.", "Janine to assume ownership of the migration support case from Raffaele Spazzoli."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.217438+00
a878f3cb-7589-4d0e-8ee1-78450f9363e0	86d58448-dc99-4ab5-90fc-0c3a31a6f1ca	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Rosemary Lynch has asked the team to provide an update on their current build tasks. This information is needed to ensure that the project report being prepared for Rushi is accurate and up to date.\\n\\nShebi, James Force, and Philip Jones have been tasked with updating the project spreadsheet. This needs to be completed by the end of the day to ensure the team is ready for the upcoming review.", "headline": "Team requested to update project status spreadsheet by end of day.", "action_items": ["Shebi, James Force, and Philip Jones to update the project status spreadsheet by the end of the day."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Rosemary Lynch has initiated a request for a status update regarding current build tasks. The objective is to synchronize the project tracking spreadsheet to ensure data integrity for reporting to Rushi.\\n\\nShebi, James Force, and Philip Jones are required to perform a data entry update on the designated tracking document. This action is critical for maintaining accurate project metrics and reporting transparency by the end of the current business day.", "headline": "Request for build task status synchronization for stakeholder reporting.", "action_items": ["Shebi, James Force, and Philip Jones to update the build task spreadsheet by EOD."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Rosemary Lynch has asked the team to provide an update on their current build tasks. This information is needed to ensure that the project report being prepared for Rushi is accurate and up to date.\\n\\nShebi, James Force, and Philip Jones have been tasked with updating the project spreadsheet. This needs to be completed by the end of the day to ensure the team is ready for the upcoming review.", "headline": "Team requested to update project status spreadsheet by end of day.", "action_items": ["Shebi, James Force, and Philip Jones to update the project status spreadsheet by the end of the day."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Rosemary Lynch has initiated a request for a status update regarding current build tasks. The objective is to synchronize the project tracking spreadsheet to ensure data integrity for reporting to Rushi.\\n\\nShebi, James Force, and Philip Jones are required to perform a data entry update on the designated tracking document. This action is critical for maintaining accurate project metrics and reporting transparency by the end of the current business day.", "headline": "Request for build task status synchronization for stakeholder reporting.", "action_items": ["Shebi, James Force, and Philip Jones to update the build task spreadsheet by EOD."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.357465+00
04798cd9-1d82-48da-916d-1b99e9ade6c8	17033358-4349-481a-8d3b-bdce08e8b16f	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones has recommended a change to how the project's computer systems are set up for the second phase of the proof-of-concept. Instead of installing each system individually, the team will set up one main management system to automatically build and oversee the second system.\\n\\nThis change ensures that the project's technical setup more closely mirrors the real-world environment the client uses, making the results more relevant. Philip Jones will be updating the project documentation to include instructions on how to perform this new setup process.", "headline": "Updating the infrastructure setup process to better match client standards.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to update the project documentation with new setup instructions."], "key_decisions": ["Switch to a centralized management system for building project clusters."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones has proposed a shift in the infrastructure deployment strategy for POC Phase 2, moving away from the previous agent-based installation method. The new approach involves deploying a primary ACM (Advanced Cluster Management) cluster, which will then be utilized to provision the secondary cluster.\\n\\nThis architectural change is intended to better align the POC environment with the standard cluster lifecycle management processes utilized by HSBC. Philip Jones noted that documentation updates in the POCDOC will be required to support the ACM installation procedures.", "headline": "Transitioning POC Phase 2 to ACM-based cluster deployment architecture.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to update POCDOC with ACM installation requirements."], "key_decisions": ["Adopt ACM-based deployment for POC Phase 2 instead of agent-based installation."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones has recommended a change to how the project's computer systems are set up for the second phase of the proof-of-concept. Instead of installing each system individually, the team will set up one main management system to automatically build and oversee the second system.\\n\\nThis change ensures that the project's technical setup more closely mirrors the real-world environment the client uses, making the results more relevant. Philip Jones will be updating the project documentation to include instructions on how to perform this new setup process.", "headline": "Updating the infrastructure setup process to better match client standards.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to update the project documentation with new setup instructions."], "key_decisions": ["Switch to a centralized management system for building project clusters."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones has proposed a shift in the infrastructure deployment strategy for POC Phase 2, moving away from the previous agent-based installation method. The new approach involves deploying a primary ACM (Advanced Cluster Management) cluster, which will then be utilized to provision the secondary cluster.\\n\\nThis architectural change is intended to better align the POC environment with the standard cluster lifecycle management processes utilized by HSBC. Philip Jones noted that documentation updates in the POCDOC will be required to support the ACM installation procedures.", "headline": "Transitioning POC Phase 2 to ACM-based cluster deployment architecture.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones to update POCDOC with ACM installation requirements."], "key_decisions": ["Adopt ACM-based deployment for POC Phase 2 instead of agent-based installation."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.40243+00
effbf6f9-bfd4-497f-9dde-8832cc314d3b	0acc7785-d98f-493b-9c49-b27fb915d177	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones provided an update on infrastructure maintenance, noting that the latest Dell storage software cannot be installed because it is looking for files in the wrong location. Despite following the official documentation, the software is unable to locate the necessary images in our mirrored storage. Philip indicated that this is likely a vendor issue that will require a fix from Dell.\\n\\nOn the maintenance front, Philip successfully updated the documentation for the image mirroring process. The team is now focusing on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, and they are preparing to delete older version 4.19 files to free up space. Additionally, Philip has requested that Durga look into problems involving the management of virtual machine sets.", "headline": "Updates on storage module deployment issues and OpenShift maintenance progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate reported issues with virtual machine sets.", "Philip Jones to proceed with deleting outdated 4.19 files once ready."], "key_decisions": ["The team will focus mirroring efforts on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Old version 4.19 files will be removed from the system to save space."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones reported a blocker regarding the latest Dell Container Storage Module (CSM) deployment. The module is failing to pull images due to incorrect pathing, specifically a mismatch between the expected 'dell' namespace and the mirrored 'dell-emc' registry path, compounded by an unexpected appended folder name. Philip has confirmed that the mirrored images align with the official support matrix, necessitating a potential vendor-side fix.\\n\\nIn parallel, Philip confirmed the successful merge of the updated oc-mirror documentation. The mirroring process is now restricted to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, with plans to execute 'oc-mirror delete' to prune version 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces. Additionally, Philip has escalated an investigation into OpenShift machinesets and machines to Durga.", "headline": "Dell CSM deployment blocked by image pathing issues and oc-mirror cleanup progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate issues regarding OpenShift machinesets and machines.", "Execute 'oc-mirror delete' to remove 4.19 images from Nexus and local storage."], "key_decisions": ["Restricted oc-mirror scope to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Initiated pruning of OpenShift 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones provided an update on infrastructure maintenance, noting that the latest Dell storage software cannot be installed because it is looking for files in the wrong location. Despite following the official documentation, the software is unable to locate the necessary images in our mirrored storage. Philip indicated that this is likely a vendor issue that will require a fix from Dell.\\n\\nOn the maintenance front, Philip successfully updated the documentation for the image mirroring process. The team is now focusing on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, and they are preparing to delete older version 4.19 files to free up space. Additionally, Philip has requested that Durga look into problems involving the management of virtual machine sets.", "headline": "Updates on storage module deployment issues and OpenShift maintenance progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate reported issues with virtual machine sets.", "Philip Jones to proceed with deleting outdated 4.19 files once ready."], "key_decisions": ["The team will focus mirroring efforts on OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Old version 4.19 files will be removed from the system to save space."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones reported a blocker regarding the latest Dell Container Storage Module (CSM) deployment. The module is failing to pull images due to incorrect pathing, specifically a mismatch between the expected 'dell' namespace and the mirrored 'dell-emc' registry path, compounded by an unexpected appended folder name. Philip has confirmed that the mirrored images align with the official support matrix, necessitating a potential vendor-side fix.\\n\\nIn parallel, Philip confirmed the successful merge of the updated oc-mirror documentation. The mirroring process is now restricted to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21, with plans to execute 'oc-mirror delete' to prune version 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces. Additionally, Philip has escalated an investigation into OpenShift machinesets and machines to Durga.", "headline": "Dell CSM deployment blocked by image pathing issues and oc-mirror cleanup progress.", "action_items": ["Durga to investigate issues regarding OpenShift machinesets and machines.", "Execute 'oc-mirror delete' to remove 4.19 images from Nexus and local storage."], "key_decisions": ["Restricted oc-mirror scope to OpenShift versions 4.20 and 4.21.", "Initiated pruning of OpenShift 4.19 from Nexus and local workspaces."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.451475+00
e890cea4-a497-4164-95fc-fdc3ea871b41	a28201c7-555f-4a51-9059-c45e4a137462	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Carina Almeida has shared the draft presentation slides and the collaborative Miro board for the RH Gov & WOW project. She is asking the team to review these materials to ensure everything is accurate and ready for the client.\\n\\nPlease provide any suggestions or corrections by Monday morning. Carina will then meet with Anne to finalize the documents before sending them to the customer.", "headline": "Feedback requested on the RH Gov & WOW project proposal materials.", "action_items": ["Team to review proposal slides and Miro board.", "Team to submit feedback to Carina Almeida by Monday 10am GMT.", "Carina Almeida to review the proposal with Anne."], "key_decisions": ["Feedback deadline established for Monday at 10:00 AM GMT."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Carina Almeida has circulated the RH Gov & WOW slide deck and associated Miro board for internal stakeholder review. This documentation serves as the primary deliverable for the upcoming client-facing proposal.\\n\\nFeedback is requested to ensure alignment before the scheduled review with Anne. Following the internal validation phase, the finalized assets will be transitioned to the client.", "headline": "Review of RH Gov & WOW proposal slides and Miro board architecture initiated.", "action_items": ["Team to review RH Gov & WOW slides and Miro board.", "Team to provide feedback to Carina Almeida by Monday 10am GMT.", "Carina Almeida to review materials with Anne post-deadline."], "key_decisions": ["Internal review deadline set for Monday at 10:00 AM GMT."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Carina Almeida has shared the draft presentation slides and the collaborative Miro board for the RH Gov & WOW project. She is asking the team to review these materials to ensure everything is accurate and ready for the client.\\n\\nPlease provide any suggestions or corrections by Monday morning. Carina will then meet with Anne to finalize the documents before sending them to the customer.", "headline": "Feedback requested on the RH Gov & WOW project proposal materials.", "action_items": ["Team to review proposal slides and Miro board.", "Team to submit feedback to Carina Almeida by Monday 10am GMT.", "Carina Almeida to review the proposal with Anne."], "key_decisions": ["Feedback deadline established for Monday at 10:00 AM GMT."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Carina Almeida has circulated the RH Gov & WOW slide deck and associated Miro board for internal stakeholder review. This documentation serves as the primary deliverable for the upcoming client-facing proposal.\\n\\nFeedback is requested to ensure alignment before the scheduled review with Anne. Following the internal validation phase, the finalized assets will be transitioned to the client.", "headline": "Review of RH Gov & WOW proposal slides and Miro board architecture initiated.", "action_items": ["Team to review RH Gov & WOW slides and Miro board.", "Team to provide feedback to Carina Almeida by Monday 10am GMT.", "Carina Almeida to review materials with Anne post-deadline."], "key_decisions": ["Internal review deadline set for Monday at 10:00 AM GMT."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.500433+00
2a226400-10fa-4edf-865f-42e2dd632204	6004aa6f-8afc-4391-ba23-b03c3d9faf4a	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones provided an update on maintenance activities for the lab clusters. He is currently working with Sourav to determine the best approach for managing security settings on cluster102, balancing customer control with the need for manual upkeep. Philip also resolved a technical issue causing image errors on cluster105.\\n\\nPhilip completed a review of all automated deployment applications across the lab, creating a list of necessary fixes to address tomorrow. Furthermore, he updated the system to include necessary Dell storage software images and requested network access for security monitoring tools that were previously blocked.", "headline": "Updates on system security, image management, and maintenance tasks for lab clusters.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones: Follow up with Sourav on security profile preferences", "Philip Jones: Fix identified issues in the deployment applications", "Philip Jones: Configure security monitoring tools to work through the network proxy"], "key_decisions": ["Decided to manage security settings centrally through the system's code repository"]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones reported progress on cluster102, specifically updating the tlsSecurityProfile and evaluating the trade-offs between custom profiles and centralized Git-managed configurations. Philip also diagnosed an Image Stream failure on cluster105, attributing it to a misconfigured dataimportcron.\\n\\nAdditionally, Philip completed a comprehensive audit of ArgoCD applications across Lab clusters, identifying a backlog of remediation tasks. Infrastructure updates included syncing OC mirror to include missing Dell CSM images and preparing the corresponding ConfigMap. A request was submitted to enable CrowdStrike via proxy to resolve image mirroring limitations for the operator.", "headline": "Cluster infrastructure maintenance updates covering TLS security, image stream resolution, and ArgoCD synchronization.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones: Await feedback from Sourav regarding custom TLS security profiles", "Philip Jones: Remediate identified issues across Lab cluster ArgoCD applications", "Philip Jones: Enable CrowdStrike through proxy for operator image access"], "key_decisions": ["Centralized management of TLS security profiles via Git", "Integration of Dell CSM images into the OC mirror sync"]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones provided an update on maintenance activities for the lab clusters. He is currently working with Sourav to determine the best approach for managing security settings on cluster102, balancing customer control with the need for manual upkeep. Philip also resolved a technical issue causing image errors on cluster105.\\n\\nPhilip completed a review of all automated deployment applications across the lab, creating a list of necessary fixes to address tomorrow. Furthermore, he updated the system to include necessary Dell storage software images and requested network access for security monitoring tools that were previously blocked.", "headline": "Updates on system security, image management, and maintenance tasks for lab clusters.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones: Follow up with Sourav on security profile preferences", "Philip Jones: Fix identified issues in the deployment applications", "Philip Jones: Configure security monitoring tools to work through the network proxy"], "key_decisions": ["Decided to manage security settings centrally through the system's code repository"]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones reported progress on cluster102, specifically updating the tlsSecurityProfile and evaluating the trade-offs between custom profiles and centralized Git-managed configurations. Philip also diagnosed an Image Stream failure on cluster105, attributing it to a misconfigured dataimportcron.\\n\\nAdditionally, Philip completed a comprehensive audit of ArgoCD applications across Lab clusters, identifying a backlog of remediation tasks. Infrastructure updates included syncing OC mirror to include missing Dell CSM images and preparing the corresponding ConfigMap. A request was submitted to enable CrowdStrike via proxy to resolve image mirroring limitations for the operator.", "headline": "Cluster infrastructure maintenance updates covering TLS security, image stream resolution, and ArgoCD synchronization.", "action_items": ["Philip Jones: Await feedback from Sourav regarding custom TLS security profiles", "Philip Jones: Remediate identified issues across Lab cluster ArgoCD applications", "Philip Jones: Enable CrowdStrike through proxy for operator image access"], "key_decisions": ["Centralized management of TLS security profiles via Git", "Integration of Dell CSM images into the OC mirror sync"]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:57.567451+00
