nt of Rydekull's during a training engagement focused on OpenShift 3 architecture.\\n\\nThe integration of this team member suggests a pre-existing professional rapport and potential familiarity with legacy container orchestration workflows established during the OpenShift 3 training period.", "headline": "Alexander Rydekull reports a former trainee from an OpenShift 3 engagement has joined the project.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:59.766821+00
03d0e957-a3ed-4625-8daf-3a49caa7d3c3	dd7635d0-7b56-494e-a958-87d46d46eb3b	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio provided an update on efforts to improve how the system monitors performance and logs data. This includes adding new automated alerts to the system, thanks to contributions from James Force, and expanding the scope of data being collected into new areas.\\n\\nRicardo also adjusted the settings for how data is sent to the security reporting tool (Splunk) to ensure better visibility, noting that 18GB of data was processed over the last day. Upcoming work involves updating the system's connection settings to support secure metrics, which will be coordinated with James Force.", "headline": "Improvements to system monitoring and data logging processes.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to meet with Rijo to review recent logging changes.", "Ricardo Gregorio to update system connection settings for secure metrics.", "Ricardo Gregorio to sync with James Force on upcoming configuration tasks."], "key_decisions": ["Updated logging settings to capture more data and removed previous restrictions.", "Added new automated alerts to the system monitoring tools."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio reported progress on observability infrastructure, specifically the integration of new alert rules into the OpenTelemetry (Otel) Collector, credited to James Force. Additionally, Ricardo updated logging configurations to include extra namespaces and removed existing filters targeting the cyber Splunk instance.\\n\\nRicardo noted a data ingestion volume of 18GB from 104 sources over the last 24 hours while filters were active. Future technical requirements include modifying the Trident configuration to support https-metrics, with a pending consultation scheduled with James Force.", "headline": "Updates to OpenTelemetry collector alerting and logging infrastructure configurations.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to review Splunk filter changes with Rijo.", "Ricardo Gregorio to modify Trident configuration for https-metrics support.", "Ricardo Gregorio to coordinate with James Force regarding Trident configuration updates."], "key_decisions": ["Removed existing filters targeting cyber Splunk for logging.", "Expanded logging configuration to include additional namespaces."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio provided an update on efforts to improve how the system monitors performance and logs data. This includes adding new automated alerts to the system, thanks to contributions from James Force, and expanding the scope of data being collected into new areas.\\n\\nRicardo also adjusted the settings for how data is sent to the security reporting tool (Splunk) to ensure better visibility, noting that 18GB of data was processed over the last day. Upcoming work involves updating the system's connection settings to support secure metrics, which will be coordinated with James Force.", "headline": "Improvements to system monitoring and data logging processes.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to meet with Rijo to review recent logging changes.", "Ricardo Gregorio to update system connection settings for secure metrics.", "Ricardo Gregorio to sync with James Force on upcoming configuration tasks."], "key_decisions": ["Updated logging settings to capture more data and removed previous restrictions.", "Added new automated alerts to the system monitoring tools."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Ricardo Gregorio reported progress on observability infrastructure, specifically the integration of new alert rules into the OpenTelemetry (Otel) Collector, credited to James Force. Additionally, Ricardo updated logging configurations to include extra namespaces and removed existing filters targeting the cyber Splunk instance.\\n\\nRicardo noted a data ingestion volume of 18GB from 104 sources over the last 24 hours while filters were active. Future technical requirements include modifying the Trident configuration to support https-metrics, with a pending consultation scheduled with James Force.", "headline": "Updates to OpenTelemetry collector alerting and logging infrastructure configurations.", "action_items": ["Ricardo Gregorio to review Splunk filter changes with Rijo.", "Ricardo Gregorio to modify Trident configuration for https-metrics support.", "Ricardo Gregorio to coordinate with James Force regarding Trident configuration updates."], "key_decisions": ["Removed existing filters targeting cyber Splunk for logging.", "Expanded logging configuration to include additional namespaces."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:04:59.835443+00
