57fec2bb-0d38-4936-9a5f-95d104b4efc2	c61d9f22-9991-418d-b73e-305a0cab47cd	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia shared an update on the second phase of the server migration. The total number of servers to be moved has been adjusted to 212, down from the original 230, due to some servers being retired and others requiring further clarification from the IT support teams. The migration work is scheduled to take place over three days, from May 5th to May 7th.\\n\\nAdditionally, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that the UK project is on track. The team will focus on testing and development environments from mid-May through mid-June, with the final production rollout scheduled to run from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Update on server migration plans and upcoming project timelines.", "action_items": ["Contact the 23 IT support staff members who have not yet responded to confirm their server details."], "key_decisions": ["Reduced the number of servers in the current migration phase to 212.", "Confirmed the migration schedule for early May.", "Confirmed the timeline for the UK project through the end of July."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on Pilot Phase 2, confirming a scope adjustment to 212 VMs. The reduction from the initial 230 VMs is attributed to decommissioning paths, inventory reconciliation, and pending responses from 23 ITSOs. The migration execution is scheduled across three days, May 5th through May 7th, with specific hourly batching for the 212 VMs.\\n\\nRegarding the UK Pilot, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that cluster provisioning remains on schedule. The deployment lifecycle is mapped from May 13th through June 15th for Dev, UAT, and OAT environments, followed by a transition to contingency and production phases from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Infrastructure Migration Pilot Phase 2 scheduling and UK cluster deployment roadmap finalized.", "action_items": ["Follow up with 23 non-responsive ITSOs regarding VM inventory."], "key_decisions": ["Finalized Pilot Phase 2 scope at 212 VMs.", "Established migration execution window for May 5th-7th.", "Defined UK Pilot deployment timeline from May 13th through July."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia shared an update on the second phase of the server migration. The total number of servers to be moved has been adjusted to 212, down from the original 230, due to some servers being retired and others requiring further clarification from the IT support teams. The migration work is scheduled to take place over three days, from May 5th to May 7th.\\n\\nAdditionally, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that the UK project is on track. The team will focus on testing and development environments from mid-May through mid-June, with the final production rollout scheduled to run from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Update on server migration plans and upcoming project timelines.", "action_items": ["Contact the 23 IT support staff members who have not yet responded to confirm their server details."], "key_decisions": ["Reduced the number of servers in the current migration phase to 212.", "Confirmed the migration schedule for early May.", "Confirmed the timeline for the UK project through the end of July."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia provided an update on Pilot Phase 2, confirming a scope adjustment to 212 VMs. The reduction from the initial 230 VMs is attributed to decommissioning paths, inventory reconciliation, and pending responses from 23 ITSOs. The migration execution is scheduled across three days, May 5th through May 7th, with specific hourly batching for the 212 VMs.\\n\\nRegarding the UK Pilot, Patricia de las Heras Granaglia confirmed that cluster provisioning remains on schedule. The deployment lifecycle is mapped from May 13th through June 15th for Dev, UAT, and OAT environments, followed by a transition to contingency and production phases from June 17th through the end of July.", "headline": "Infrastructure Migration Pilot Phase 2 scheduling and UK cluster deployment roadmap finalized.", "action_items": ["Follow up with 23 non-responsive ITSOs regarding VM inventory."], "key_decisions": ["Finalized Pilot Phase 2 scope at 212 VMs.", "Established migration execution window for May 5th-7th.", "Defined UK Pilot deployment timeline from May 13th through July."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.283151+00
4bcfd673-2bf6-4349-9244-bcd291141f99	db8bbd61-5f55-4a37-b9af-40682111c261	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported that a recent network change has caused a major outage across three of our production systems. In two of the systems, the background servers have crashed, though the management interface is still working. In the third system, the entire service is currently offline and inaccessible.\\n\\nThe team has decided to restart the servers to get the services back online as quickly as possible, following advice from previous support tickets. Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga expressed hesitation with this approach, as it prioritizes immediate recovery over identifying the specific cause of the crashes.", "headline": "Production system outage caused by recent network configuration updates.", "action_items": ["Restart servers in clusters 311, 312, and 314."], "key_decisions": ["Restart the servers to restore service access."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reports a critical outage across three production clusters (311, 312, and 314) following recent LACP configuration changes. Clusters 311 and 312 are experiencing total worker node failure, though the Web Console and API remain reachable. Cluster 314 is experiencing a complete loss of service, with both worker nodes and management interfaces (Web Console/API) currently inaccessible.\\n\\nSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga notes that the team is currently executing node reboots based on previous support recommendations. Sebastian expressed concern regarding this reactive recovery strategy, noting that rebooting obscures the root cause analysis of the LACP-induced instability.", "headline": "Production cluster outage following LACP configuration changes impacting worker node stability.", "action_items": ["Perform node reboots on clusters 311, 312, and 314 to restore service."], "key_decisions": ["Initiate node reboots across affected clusters (311, 312, 314) to restore service availability."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported that a recent network change has caused a major outage across three of our production systems. In two of the systems, the background servers have crashed, though the management interface is still working. In the third system, the entire service is currently offline and inaccessible.\\n\\nThe team has decided to restart the servers to get the services back online as quickly as possible, following advice from previous support tickets. Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga expressed hesitation with this approach, as it prioritizes immediate recovery over identifying the specific cause of the crashes.", "headline": "Production system outage caused by recent network configuration updates.", "action_items": ["Restart servers in clusters 311, 312, and 314."], "key_decisions": ["Restart the servers to restore service access."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reports a critical outage across three production clusters (311, 312, and 314) following recent LACP configuration changes. Clusters 311 and 312 are experiencing total worker node failure, though the Web Console and API remain reachable. Cluster 314 is experiencing a complete loss of service, with both worker nodes and management interfaces (Web Console/API) currently inaccessible.\\n\\nSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga notes that the team is currently executing node reboots based on previous support recommendations. Sebastian expressed concern regarding this reactive recovery strategy, noting that rebooting obscures the root cause analysis of the LACP-induced instability.", "headline": "Production cluster outage following LACP configuration changes impacting worker node stability.", "action_items": ["Perform node reboots on clusters 311, 312, and 314 to restore service."], "key_decisions": ["Initiate node reboots across affected clusters (311, 312, 314) to restore service availability."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.298354+00
