nt to manage how these systems communicate.\\n\\nTo ensure stability and reliability, the setup will be spread across three different locations. Two of these locations will handle the primary computing tasks, while the third location will act as a tie-breaker to keep the system running smoothly if issues arise.", "headline": "Plan established for the second phase of the technical proof-of-concept project.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["The project will proceed with a two-cluster setup using Isovalent technology.", "The infrastructure will be distributed across three physical or logical sites."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Philip Jones outlined the architectural roadmap for POC Phase 2, which utilizes a standard cluster with OVN for ACM management and a secondary cluster leveraging Isovalent Cilium. The deployment strategy involves a multi-site configuration distributed across three distinct sites.\\n\\nThe topology consists of a high-availability-style split: Site 1 and Site 2 will each host one master node and 1-2 worker nodes, while Site 3 is designated for an Arbiter Node to manage cluster quorum.", "headline": "Architectural definition for POC Phase 2 involving multi-site Isovalent Cilium cluster deployment.", "action_items": [], "key_decisions": ["POC Phase 2 will utilize a two-cluster architecture with Isovalent Cilium.", "Deployment will be split across three sites, including an Arbiter Node in the third site."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.88476+00
