elayed until November.", "action_items": ["Shebi to verify the updated delivery date for the security features."], "key_decisions": ["The delivery of the Cilium security features has been moved to November."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported that, based on the Sheffield meeting minutes, the Cilium integration for WAF and IDS functionality will not meet the original delivery timeline. The projected availability has been pushed to November.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli has advised Nikos to consider re-evaluating OVN as an alternative implementation strategy in light of this delay. Shebi has been requested to verify these findings and confirm the updated project schedule.", "headline": "Cilium WAF and IDS feature delivery delayed until November.", "action_items": ["Shebi to confirm the accuracy of the November delivery timeline for Cilium WAF/IDS."], "key_decisions": ["Cilium WAF and IDS delivery date shifted to November."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.532389+00
632990bf-79ff-4b94-9a0f-bf93c1ee9e35	b82eb3de-678e-43af-8fbc-b73256cf56f6	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull has asked the team to confirm the current setup process for new OpenShift clusters. He observed that the settings used to grant remote access (SSH keys) to the system administrator account appear to be disabled in the project's configuration files.\\n\\nRydekull is asking the project team to clarify whether this is a deliberate security choice or if the configuration needs to be updated to allow for proper system access.", "headline": "Clarification requested on security access settings for new OpenShift clusters.", "action_items": ["The engineering team needs to confirm if the current method for accessing the cluster is intentional or requires a change."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull initiated a query regarding the current OpenShift cluster deployment configuration, specifically noting that the SSH key injection for the 'core' user appears to be commented out within the existing Infrastructure as Code (IaC) repository files. \\n\\nRydekull is seeking verification from the engineering team—specifically James Force, Philip Jones, Rspazzol, and Janine—to confirm if this omission is intentional or a configuration oversight in the current deployment pipeline.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding SSH key injection for OpenShift core user during cluster provisioning.", "action_items": ["James Force, Philip Jones, Rspazzol, and Janine to verify if the exclusion of SSH keys for the 'core' user in the Git configuration is intentional."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull has asked the team to confirm the current setup process for new OpenShift clusters. He observed that the settings used to grant remote access (SSH keys) to the system administrator account appear to be disabled in the project's configuration files.\\n\\nRydekull is asking the project team to clarify whether this is a deliberate security choice or if the configuration needs to be updated to allow for proper system access.", "headline": "Clarification requested on security access settings for new OpenShift clusters.", "action_items": ["The engineering team needs to confirm if the current method for accessing the cluster is intentional or requires a change."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Alexander Rydekull initiated a query regarding the current OpenShift cluster deployment configuration, specifically noting that the SSH key injection for the 'core' user appears to be commented out within the existing Infrastructure as Code (IaC) repository files. \\n\\nRydekull is seeking verification from the engineering team—specifically James Force, Philip Jones, Rspazzol, and Janine—to confirm if this omission is intentional or a configuration oversight in the current deployment pipeline.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding SSH key injection for OpenShift core user during cluster provisioning.", "action_items": ["James Force, Philip Jones, Rspazzol, and Janine to verify if the exclusion of SSH keys for the 'core' user in the Git configuration is intentional."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.547153+00
d9a021fb-ea95-473b-a600-6852c6771e03	d4e2e550-18af-4594-a768-f7d917b239bb	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported that changing the network addresses for virtual machines in Hong Kong will be difficult. Based on recent challenges faced in the New York office, the team has realized that simply updating the server addresses causes several other connected systems to stop working.\\n\\nKey services like shared network storage, secure remote access (VPNs), and web traffic handlers are all linked to these specific addresses. Because these systems rely on the current setup, the team must carefully plan how to update them to avoid service disruptions.", "headline": "Planned server address changes in Hong Kong are more complex than anticipated.", "action_items": ["Review all connected systems and services before proceeding with the Hong Kong server address changes."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli identified significant architectural blockers regarding the proposed re-IPing of virtual machines in the Hong Kong environment. Drawing from recent experiences in the NY data center, Spazzoli highlighted that IP changes trigger cascading failures across several tightly coupled dependencies.\\n\\nSpecifically, the migration is complicated by OS-mounted NAS storage, VPN tunnel configurations, and proxy server settings. These components are currently hard-coded or statically bound to existing IP addresses, necessitating a comprehensive audit before any network re-addressing can proceed.", "headline": "VM IP migration in Hong Kong faces critical infrastructure dependency challenges.", "action_items": ["Conduct dependency audit for OS-mounted NAS, VPNs, and proxies prior to HK VM migration."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported that changing the network addresses for virtual machines in Hong Kong will be difficult. Based on recent challenges faced in the New York office, the team has realized that simply updating the server addresses causes several other connected systems to stop working.\\n\\nKey services like shared network storage, secure remote access (VPNs), and web traffic handlers are all linked to these specific addresses. Because these systems rely on the current setup, the team must carefully plan how to update them to avoid service disruptions.", "headline": "Planned server address changes in Hong Kong are more complex than anticipated.", "action_items": ["Review all connected systems and services before proceeding with the Hong Kong server address changes."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli identified significant architectural blockers regarding the proposed re-IPing of virtual machines in the Hong Kong environment. Drawing from recent experiences in the NY data center, Spazzoli highlighted that IP changes trigger cascading failures across several tightly coupled dependencies.\\n\\nSpecifically, the migration is complicated by OS-mounted NAS storage, VPN tunnel configurations, and proxy server settings. These components are currently hard-coded or statically bound to existing IP addresses, necessitating a comprehensive audit before any network re-addressing can proceed.", "headline": "VM IP migration in Hong Kong faces critical infrastructure dependency challenges.", "action_items": ["Conduct dependency audit for OS-mounted NAS, VPNs, and proxies prior to HK VM migration."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:00.584888+00
