3df4d67f-73f7-45a0-af80-407327934438	ffada008-fe4c-47a9-b7b7-49292595dc7b	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Kevin Rizza shared an update regarding the project to update the OAuth proxy system. The team is currently reviewing the technical requirements and potential issues to ensure a smooth rollout. The current plan is to complete the update for the upcoming 5.0 version first, and then apply those changes to the older 4.22 version.\\n\\nProgress is being tracked in a central project management ticket, OCPSTRAT-3174. Kevin Rizza will post regular weekly updates there so stakeholders can monitor the progress and timeline.", "headline": "Plans to update the security login system for older software versions.", "action_items": ["Kevin Rizza to provide weekly progress updates in the project tracking system."], "key_decisions": ["The team will update the security login system for version 4.22 after the 5.0 release is finished."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Kevin Rizza provided an update on the OAuth proxy implementation, noting that the team is currently assessing edge cases and scope requirements. The current strategy involves finalizing the implementation for the 5.0 release cycle before initiating a backport to the 4.22 release stream.\\n\\nAll development efforts and progress tracking are centralized in Jira ticket OCPSTRAT-3174. Kevin Rizza committed to providing recurring weekly status updates within that ticket to ensure transparency regarding the backport timeline.", "headline": "OAuth proxy backport strategy targeting OCP 4.22 following 5.0 release.", "action_items": ["Kevin Rizza to provide weekly updates in OCPSTRAT-3174."], "key_decisions": ["Target the OAuth proxy backport for OCP 4.22.", "Prioritize the 5.0 release implementation before backporting."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Kevin Rizza shared an update regarding the project to update the OAuth proxy system. The team is currently reviewing the technical requirements and 