ops. The goal is to gather all information in one place first, so the team can organize and clean up the details later.\\n\\nSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga encourages the team to be thorough and include as much information as possible, even if it is currently unorganized, to ensure nothing from the workshops is lost.", "headline": "New shared document created for Sheffield HIC project workshop notes.", "action_items": ["All team members: Add your workshop notes and screenshots to the shared document."], "key_decisions": ["The team will use a specific Google Doc to store all workshop-related notes and images."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga has initiated a centralized documentation repository for the Sheffield HIC project design workshops. The objective is to aggregate raw data, including screenshots and unstructured notes, into a single Google Doc instance to facilitate subsequent information architecture and knowledge management structuring.\\n\\nSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga emphasizes a 'capture-all' approach to ensure comprehensive data retention before formalizing the documentation schema. This repository will serve as the primary source of truth for the workshop outputs.", "headline": "Centralization of Sheffield HIC design workshop documentation via shared Google Doc.", "action_items": ["All project participants: Upload workshop notes and relevant screenshots to the provided Google Doc."], "key_decisions": ["Establishment of a centralized Google Doc as the primary repository for Sheffield HIC design workshop documentation."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:02.659573+00
