 registry for all migration-related error tracking."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has created a shared document to keep track of all errors occurring during the migration process. This system is designed to ensure that different teams are not accidentally working on the same problems at the same time, which helps prevent confusion and wasted effort.\\n\\nBy using this central list, the team can clearly see who is responsible for each issue and where the fixes need to be applied. This will help keep the project organized and ensure that everyone is working from the same information.", "headline": "New shared tracking system launched to coordinate migration error fixes.", "action_items": ["Team members are requested to add, update, or remove migration errors in the shared spreadsheet as they work."], "key_decisions": ["A shared spreadsheet will now serve as the official tool for tracking migration errors."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has initiated a centralized tracking mechanism for migration-related errors to mitigate redundant efforts and potential race conditions during remediation. By consolidating error logs into a shared spreadsheet, the team aims to establish a single source of truth for issue assessment and architectural solution deployment.\\n\\nThe initiative focuses on cross-team coordination to ensure that migration errors are systematically mapped to the appropriate workstreams. This approach is intended to prevent parallel, conflicting fixes and streamline the resolution lifecycle for identified migration anomalies.", "headline": "Centralized tracking implementation for migration error remediation and cross-team synchronization.", "action_items": ["All team members to utilize the shared spreadsheet for logging, tracking, and updating the status of migration errors."], "key_decisions": ["Establishment of a centralized Google Sheets registry for all migration-related error tracking."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:01.532842+00
339d1a02-ac5f-4d69-a015-4036d053e8b9	bda1b95b-0bc8-49fd-90a5-e3c691858ef4	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias has sent a reminder to the team regarding the deadline for submitting time-tracking information. To ensure payroll and project billing are processed correctly, all staff must complete their entries in the required systems today.\\n\\nSpecifically, please ensure your time sheets are updated in the Clarity system and Consulting Cloud by noon. Additionally, Red Hat time cards must be finalized before the end of the business day.", "headline": "Reminder to submit all time sheets and hours by end of day.", "action_items": ["All team members: Submit time sheets in Clarity and Consulting Cloud by 12:00 PM.", "All team members: Submit Red Hat time cards by the end of the day."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias issued a compliance notification regarding time-reporting workflows. The directive requires the synchronization of billable hours across multiple platforms, specifically mandating Clarity entries by 12:00 PM and Red Hat time card submissions by EOD.\\n\\nFurthermore, the workflow requires concurrent data entry into the Consulting Cloud environment to ensure alignment with bank-side reporting requirements. All project resources must adhere to these specific system-level deadlines to maintain payroll and billing integrity.", "headline": "Mandatory submission deadlines for Clarity and Consulting Cloud time-tracking systems.", "action_items": ["All team members: Submit Clarity time sheets by 12:00 PM.", "All team members: Submit Red Hat time cards by close of business.", "All team members: Enter hours into Consulting Cloud by 12:00 PM."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias has sent a reminder to the team regarding the deadline for submitting time-tracking information. To ensure payroll and project billing are processed correctly, all staff must complete their entries in the required systems today.\\n\\nSpecifically, please ensure your time sheets are updated in the Clarity system and Consulting Cloud by noon. Additionally, Red Hat time cards must be finalized before the end of the business day.", "headline": "Reminder to submit all time sheets and hours by end of day.", "action_items": ["All team members: Submit time sheets in Clarity and Consulting Cloud by 12:00 PM.", "All team members: Submit Red Hat time cards by the end of the day."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias issued a compliance notification regarding time-reporting workflows. The directive requires the synchronization of billable hours across multiple platforms, specifically mandating Clarity entries by 12:00 PM and Red Hat time card submissions by EOD.\\n\\nFurthermore, the workflow requires concurrent data entry into the Consulting Cloud environment to ensure alignment with bank-side reporting requirements. All project resources must adhere to these specific system-level deadlines to maintain payroll and billing integrity.", "headline": "Mandatory submission deadlines for Clarity and Consulting Cloud time-tracking systems.", "action_items": ["All team members: Submit Clarity time sheets by 12:00 PM.", "All team members: Submit Red Hat time cards by close of business.", "All team members: Enter hours into Consulting Cloud by 12:00 PM."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:01.628535+00
cea1a07b-c8fc-4039-be5f-923aa5b0bfc5	fccaa7d9-514e-44ac-adb3-1f40e6ee74a1	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged a serious issue where customers are experiencing system crashes (Blue Screen of Death) when using our virtualization software. This problem is affecting multiple clients, and the severity has already caused at least one customer to stop using our product.\\n\\nOur engineering team is currently working to identify the source of the problem to determine if it is a fault in our software or an issue related to Windows updates.", "headline": "Urgent investigation underway for system crashes affecting Windows virtual machines.", "action_items": ["Engineering to investigate the cause of the system crashes and report findings."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported a critical regression causing Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) events on Windows guest operating systems within OpenShift Virtualization environments. The issue is currently impacting multiple customers, with at least one client terminating their deployment due to the instability.\\n\\nEngineering teams are actively investigating whether the root cause stems from a regression within the OpenShift Virtualization product stack or an underlying incompatibility introduced by recent Windows updates.", "headline": "Investigation initiated into critical BSOD regressions affecting OpenShift Virtualization deployments.", "action_items": ["Engineering to conduct root cause analysis to determine if the BSOD is caused by product regression or Windows environment changes."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has flagged a serious issue where customers are experiencing system crashes (Blue Screen of Death) when using our virtualization software. This problem is affecting multiple clients, and the severity has already caused at least one customer to stop using our product.\\n\\nOur engineering team is currently working to identify the source of the problem to determine if it is a fault in our software or an issue related to Windows updates.", "headline": "Urgent investigation underway for system crashes affecting Windows virtual machines.", "action_items": ["Engineering to investigate the cause of the system crashes and report findings."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli reported a critical regression causing Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) events on Windows guest operating systems within OpenShift Virtualization environments. The issue is currently impacting multiple customers, with at least one client terminating their deployment due to the instability.\\n\\nEngineering teams are actively investigating whether the root cause stems from a regression within the OpenShift Virtualization product stack or an underlying incompatibility introduced by recent Windows updates.", "headline": "Investigation initiated into critical BSOD regressions affecting OpenShift Virtualization deployments.", "action_items": ["Engineering to conduct root cause analysis to determine if the BSOD is caused by product regression or Windows environment changes."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:01.743638+00
db14ec20-bc75-456c-9466-fa4078ebae2b	a7b5f218-c456-4884-aeef-15d6399918f9	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported on a recent project meeting, noting that the team needs to better align their internal work priorities with the bank's actual business needs. By syncing these expectations, the team aims to ensure they are focusing their efforts on the most impactful tasks.\\n\\nAdditionally, the team is working to better utilize the Technical Account Managers (TAMs). To help them be more effective, the team plans to provide them with more detailed background information on the project. They also decided to hold regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests to ensure nothing important is overlooked.", "headline": "Improving Project Alignment and Team Collaboration for the EOSBank Account", "action_items": ["Carina Almeida: Organize a meeting for next week to brief the TAMs on the project's technical background.", "Nikos and Rspazzol: Review the meeting notes and add any missing details."], "key_decisions": ["Set up regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests.", "Improve the training process for new TAMs to help them understand the project better."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga summarized the CAP-978 EOSBank sync, highlighting a misalignment between internal engineering priorities and the client's impact requirements. The team identified a need to recalibrate the development roadmap to ensure it reflects the bank's current architectural and business objectives.\\n\\nFurthermore, the integration of Technical Account Managers (TAMs) requires an accelerated onboarding process focused on deep-dive architectural context. Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga noted that providing this technical depth is essential for TAMs to effectively manage the RFE and support case lifecycle, necessitating a more structured cadence for ongoing alignment.", "headline": "Alignment of CAP-978 Engineering Priorities and TAM Architectural Integration", "action_items": ["Carina Almeida: Schedule a call for next week to facilitate architectural knowledge transfer to TAMs.", "Nikos and Rspazzol: Review and provide additional input on the proposed alignment strategy."], "key_decisions": ["Establish a recurring cadence for RFE and support case alignment meetings.", "Formalize the onboarding process for TAMs to include deep-dive architectural context."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga reported on a recent project meeting, noting that the team needs to better align their internal work priorities with the bank's actual business needs. By syncing these expectations, the team aims to ensure they are focusing their efforts on the most impactful tasks.\\n\\nAdditionally, the team is working to better utilize the Technical Account Managers (TAMs). To help them be more effective, the team plans to provide them with more detailed background information on the project. They also decided to hold regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests to ensure nothing important is overlooked.", "headline": "Improving Project Alignment and Team Collaboration for the EOSBank Account", "action_items": ["Carina Almeida: Organize a meeting for next week to brief the TAMs on the project's technical background.", "Nikos and Rspazzol: Review the meeting notes and add any missing details."], "key_decisions": ["Set up regular meetings to review support cases and feature requests.", "Improve the training process for new TAMs to help them understand the project better."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga summarized the CAP-978 EOSBank sync, highlighting a misalignment between internal engineering priorities and the client's impact requirements. The team identified a need to recalibrate the development roadmap to ensure it reflects the bank's current architectural and business objectives.\\n\\nFurthermore, the integration of Technical Account Managers (TAMs) requires an accelerated onboarding process focused on deep-dive architectural context. Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga noted that providing this technical depth is essential for TAMs to effectively manage the RFE and support case lifecycle, necessitating a more structured cadence for ongoing alignment.", "headline": "Alignment of CAP-978 Engineering Priorities and TAM Architectural Integration", "action_items": ["Carina Almeida: Schedule a call for next week to facilitate architectural knowledge transfer to TAMs.", "Nikos and Rspazzol: Review and provide additional input on the proposed alignment strategy."], "key_decisions": ["Establish a recurring cadence for RFE and support case alignment meetings.", "Formalize the onboarding process for TAMs to include deep-dive architectural context."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:01.811344+00
a65f1881-1a69-4547-959b-f7779d596441	3c2fbaf0-15c0-43a1-ae84-aa12c82fbcf1	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sam Marland shared an update regarding ongoing issues with the system's authentication proxy. Because the current setup is no longer meeting project needs, the team is exploring a workaround that involves adding a new configuration setting to the authentication system.\\n\\nWhile the team is working on a permanent fix, they are currently determining which versions of the software will receive this update. It is unlikely to be available for version 4.22, but the team is confident it will be included in the 4.23 release.", "headline": "Update on resolving authentication proxy issues for the current cluster setup.", "action_items": ["Engineering team to finalize the update and confirm which software versions will receive the fix."], "key_decisions": ["The team will move forward with a new configuration setting to fix the authentication proxy issue."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sam Marland reported on discussions regarding RFE-7054, noting that current cluster-wide proxy configurations are insufficient for the project's requirements. The proposed architectural resolution involves extending the OAuth object with a new property to facilitate custom proxy configuration.\\n\\nEngineering stakeholders expressed uncertainty regarding the feasibility of backporting this change to version 4.22. However, they indicated high confidence in the ability to backport the implementation to version 4.23.", "headline": "Proposed OAuth object property extension to resolve RFE-7054 authentication proxy limitations.", "action_items": ["Engineering team to evaluate backport feasibility for 4.22 and 4.23."], "key_decisions": ["Proposed solution for RFE-7054 is to add a new property to the OAuth object."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Sam Marland shared an update regarding ongoing issues with the system's authentication proxy. Because the current setup is no longer meeting project needs, the team is exploring a workaround that involves adding a new configuration setting to the authentication system.\\n\\nWhile the team is working on a permanent fix, they are currently determining which versions of the software will receive this update. It is unlikely to be available for version 4.22, but the team is confident it will be included in the 4.23 release.", "headline": "Update on resolving authentication proxy issues for the current cluster setup.", "action_items": ["Engineering team to finalize the update and confirm which software versions will receive the fix."], "key_decisions": ["The team will move forward with a new configuration setting to fix the authentication proxy issue."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Sam Marland reported on discussions regarding RFE-7054, noting that current cluster-wide proxy configurations are insufficient for the project's requirements. The proposed architectural resolution involves extending the OAuth object with a new property to facilitate custom proxy configuration.\\n\\nEngineering stakeholders expressed uncertainty regarding the feasibility of backporting this change to version 4.22. However, they indicated high confidence in the ability to backport the implementation to version 4.23.", "headline": "Proposed OAuth object property extension to resolve RFE-7054 authentication proxy limitations.", "action_items": ["Engineering team to evaluate backport feasibility for 4.22 and 4.23."], "key_decisions": ["Proposed solution for RFE-7054 is to add a new property to the OAuth object."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:02.736819+00
