nvironment. The objective is to facilitate package management and deployment operations directly from the bastion host.\\n\\nNo specific path or pre-installed binary has been identified or confirmed by the team at this stage of the thread.", "headline": "Inquiry regarding Helm binary availability on Linux bastion host.", "action_items": ["Identify or provision a Helm binary for use on the Linux bastion host."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:02.105823+00
b0bba08b-0276-4f1a-8f39-48c347e2f0c4	cb9ec78e-3d82-41d6-b5eb-5f07b1761fd3	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has identified the requirements for the second phase of the virtual machine migration pilot. The team is narrowing down a list of 230 machines to those that are independent, not shared across multiple services, and located on specific network segments.\\n\\nThis phase will include both Windows and Linux systems. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that the final list of machines to be moved must be reviewed and confirmed by the IT Service Owners (ITSOs) to ensure accuracy before proceeding.", "headline": "Planning the next phase of the virtual machine migration project", "action_items": ["Collaborate with IT Service Owners to finalize the list of machines for migration (Assigned: Patricia de las Heras Granaglia)"], "key_decisions": ["Established specific criteria to filter which virtual machines are eligible for the migration pilot."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has outlined the scope for Migration Pilot Phase #2, targeting a subset of 230 VMs. The selection criteria specify non-HIC, single-service VMs located on fabrics 111, 113, and 122, encompassing both Windows and Linux OS environments. \\n\\nThe migration will utilize patterns C1, C2, C3, C4, and C9. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has indicated that the current candidate list requires further validation and refinement in collaboration with ITSOs.", "headline": "Defining scope and criteria for Migration Pilot Phase #2", "action_items": ["Refine the current list of candidate VMs with ITSOs (Assigned: Patricia de las Heras Granaglia)"], "key_decisions": ["Defined VM pilot criteria: non-HIC, single-service, fabrics 111/113/122, and patterns C1-C4/C9."]}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has identified the requirements for the second phase of the virtual machine migration pilot. The team is narrowing down a list of 230 machines to those that are independent, not shared across multiple services, and located on specific network segments.\\n\\nThis phase will include both Windows and Linux systems. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia noted that the final list of machines to be moved must be reviewed and confirmed by the IT Service Owners (ITSOs) to ensure accuracy before proceeding.", "headline": "Planning the next phase of the virtual machine migration project", "action_items": ["Collaborate with IT Service Owners to finalize the list of machines for migration (Assigned: Patricia de las Heras Granaglia)"], "key_decisions": ["Established specific criteria to filter which virtual machines are eligible for the migration pilot."]}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has outlined the scope for Migration Pilot Phase #2, targeting a subset of 230 VMs. The selection criteria specify non-HIC, single-service VMs located on fabrics 111, 113, and 122, encompassing both Windows and Linux OS environments. \\n\\nThe migration will utilize patterns C1, C2, C3, C4, and C9. Patricia de las Heras Granaglia has indicated that the current candidate list requires further validation and refinement in collaboration with ITSOs.", "headline": "Defining scope and criteria for Migration Pilot Phase #2", "action_items": ["Refine the current list of candidate VMs with ITSOs (Assigned: Patricia de las Heras Granaglia)"], "key_decisions": ["Defined VM pilot criteria: non-HIC, single-service, fabrics 111/113/122, and patterns C1-C4/C9."]}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:02.172087+00
