4deec379-fdf6-4fb7-8f41-961a6108c26a	f97b02c9-d5f5-485e-8a63-983c815bd937	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Jens Feind has raised a concern regarding a request from the customer's team (Nitesh and Srinath) about using experimental or early-access software features in their live production system. This requires a formal agreement between our company and the customer to ensure it meets project standards.\\n\\nJens Feind is asking if this has already been discussed or decided, as the customer is waiting for a formal written confirmation before proceeding.", "headline": "Clarification needed on using experimental software features in the customer's live environment.", "action_items": ["Determine if a decision has been made regarding the use of experimental features.", "Draft a written response for the customer confirming the governance policy."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Jens Feind has flagged an inquiry from Nitesh and Srinath regarding the formal governance policy for utilizing DevPreview or Upstream features, specifically citing the 'MTV-wait-hook', within production environments. The current architectural stance requires a joint decision between HSBC and Red Hat.\\n\\nJens Feind is seeking clarification on whether this topic is currently under active deliberation or if a formal consensus has already been reached, as the customer is requesting a written conclusion to validate the supportability of these features in production.", "headline": "Governance requirements for deploying DevPreview and Upstream features in production environments.", "action_items": ["Clarify current status of governance discussions regarding DevPreview/Upstream features with the customer.", "Provide a written conclusion to Nitesh and Srinath regarding production usage of non-GA features."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Jens Feind has raised a concern regarding a request from the customer's team (Nitesh and Srinath) about using experimental or early-access software features in their live production system. This requires a formal agreement between our company and the customer to ensure it meets project standards.\\n\\nJens Feind is asking if this has already been discussed or decided, as the customer is waiting for a formal written confirmation before proceeding.", "headline": "Clarification needed on using experimental software features in the customer's live environment.", "action_items": ["Determine if a decision has been made regarding the use of experimental features.", "Draft a written response for the customer confirming the governance policy."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Jens Feind has flagged an inquiry from Nitesh and Srinath regarding the formal governance policy for utilizing DevPreview or Upstream features, specifically citing the 'MTV-wait-hook', within production environments. The current architectural stance requires a joint decision between HSBC and Red Hat.\\n\\nJens Feind is seeking clarification on whether this topic is currently under active deliberation or if a formal consensus has already been reached, as the customer is requesting a written conclusion to validate the supportability of these features in production.", "headline": "Governance requirements for deploying DevPreview and Upstream features in production environments.", "action_items": ["Clarify current status of governance discussions regarding DevPreview/Upstream features with the customer.", "Provide a written conclusion to Nitesh and Srinath regarding production usage of non-GA features."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:05.573282+00
7e5b57e1-2f65-4f1f-93fb-4fc8000714ba	3a920f12-d855-4567-ba8d-05f9b3422a8b	064f2b1a-841c-4113-a5fd-d14ee3573d6b	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli expressed frustration regarding a recent meeting where four architects were present with Michele without a clear purpose. He noted that this represents an inefficient use of the team's time and requested that the group find a way to prevent similar situations in the future.\\n\\nThe team is looking to improve how they manage client interactions to ensure that staff time is spent productively. The focus is on ensuring that only necessary personnel attend meetings and that there is a clear reason for every session.", "headline": "Improving meeting efficiency and preventing unnecessary staff attendance.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli, Rydekull, and Shebi to create a process to better manage meeting attendance and ensure clear agendas."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has raised a concern regarding the over-allocation of architectural resources in client meetings. Specifically, four architects were present in a session with Michele, despite a lack of clear agenda or technical necessity for such a high-density presence.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli is advocating for a more rigorous gatekeeping process to prevent inefficient utilization of technical staff. The goal is to establish a protocol that ensures architectural participation is justified by the meeting's scope and technical requirements.", "headline": "Optimization of architectural resource allocation during client-facing meetings.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli, Rydekull, and Shebi to define a protocol for meeting attendance and agenda validation."], "key_decisions": []}}	{"plainSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli expressed frustration regarding a recent meeting where four architects were present with Michele without a clear purpose. He noted that this represents an inefficient use of the team's time and requested that the group find a way to prevent similar situations in the future.\\n\\nThe team is looking to improve how they manage client interactions to ensure that staff time is spent productively. The focus is on ensuring that only necessary personnel attend meetings and that there is a clear reason for every session.", "headline": "Improving meeting efficiency and preventing unnecessary staff attendance.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli, Rydekull, and Shebi to create a process to better manage meeting attendance and ensure clear agendas."], "key_decisions": []}, "technicalSummary": {"body": "Raffaele Spazzoli has raised a concern regarding the over-allocation of architectural resources in client meetings. Specifically, four architects were present in a session with Michele, despite a lack of clear agenda or technical necessity for such a high-density presence.\\n\\nRaffaele Spazzoli is advocating for a more rigorous gatekeeping process to prevent inefficient utilization of technical staff. The goal is to establish a protocol that ensures architectural participation is justified by the meeting's scope and technical requirements.", "headline": "Optimization of architectural resource allocation during client-facing meetings.", "action_items": ["Raffaele Spazzoli, Rydekull, and Shebi to define a protocol for meeting attendance and agenda validation."], "key_decisions": []}}	[]	approved	\N	2026-05-12 05:07:35.053672+00	2026-05-12 05:05:05.731491+00
