429d6154-34e4-405d-9fc9-931a8005bf6c	cb9ec78e-3d82-41d6-b5eb-5f07b1761fd3	1778225376.000036	Patricia de las Heras Granaglia	[Migration Pilot Phase #2]\nScope of VMS: 230 -> Number of VMs that match the Pilot criteria: non-hic, vms that a re not shared by two or more services, vms that are on fabrics 111,113 and 122, migration patterns C1,C2,C3,C4 and C9\nBoth windows and linux\nThat list of VMs need to be refined with ITSOs	{"ts": "1778225376.000036", "text": "[Migration Pilot Phase #2]\\nScope of VMS: 230 -> Number of VMs that match the Pilot criteria: non-hic, vms that a re not shared by two or more services, vms that are on fabrics 111,113 and 122, migration patterns C1,C2,C3,C4 and C9\\nBoth windows and linux\\nThat list of VMs need to be refined with ITSOs", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}
760e58c8-5719-40bb-956c-9fa60811301f	ef21c9b8-eb6c-45b8-9f0c-ec8a1ac5798c	1778230357.000037	Ricardo Gregorio	[SRE Qs]\n- Suppress info alerts in the alertmanager config [Kuldeep has a PR with Receiver: null]. Need to investigate if this is the best way to achieve this\n- They raised a support ticket for Insights alerts. I mentioned that this is is disconnected cluster and cannot go out. I will review some KBs about how to deal with these rules in disconnected clusters.\n- They asked about collecting hardware metrics. I mentioned that what I had found is not much and already shared with Onkar. They should look into querying/exporting data from iDRAC (Onkar is aware of this).\n- There is an alert about system memory reservation (they've got a support ticket open). Basically the kubeletconfig CR has a paremeter configured in the wrong level (openshift-config app).\n- They asked about SLI/SLO, which I mentioned I could not find any "template" guidance with our ROSA SRE Team. These vary from business to business. Thresholds have to be meaningful and achievable. For once reached and action should take place.\n- There seem to be some overlap/miscomm between SRE and OBS team as to who owns what (alerts + HW metrics)\n[observability]\n- pushed new metrics and collector endpoint to cluster 102.\n- setup cyber Splunk  endpoint to forward audit logs. Validate data flow with cyber splunk team.\n- added a filter to remove get/list/watch verbs. Will review that with cyber Splunk team tomorrow.\n- Create a variable to tie otel collector LB endpoint to region (will review this with Raffa)	{"ts": "1778230357.000037", "text": "[SRE Qs]\\n- Suppress info alerts in the alertmanager config [Kuldeep has a PR with Receiver: null]. Need to investigate if this is the best way to achieve this\\n- They raised a support ticket for Insights alerts. I mentioned that this is is disconnected cluster and cannot go out. I will review some KBs about how to deal with these rules in disconnected clusters.\\n- They asked about collecting hardware metrics. I mentioned that what I had found is not much and already shared with Onkar. They should look into querying/exporting data from iDRAC (Onkar is aware of this).\\n- There is an alert about system memory reservation (they've got a support ticket open). Basically the kubeletconfig CR has a paremeter configured in the wrong level (openshift-config app).\\n- They asked about SLI/SLO, which I mentioned I could not find any \\"template\\" guidance with our ROSA SRE Team. These vary from business to business. Thresholds have to be meaningful and achievable. For once reached and action should take place.\\n- There seem to be some overlap/miscomm between SRE and OBS team as to who owns what (alerts + HW metrics)\\n[observability]\\n- pushed new metrics and collector endpoint to cluster 102.\\n- setup cyber Splunk  endpoint to forward audit logs. Validate data flow with cyber splunk team.\\n- added a filter to remove get/list/watch verbs. Will review that with cyber Splunk team tomorrow.\\n- Create a variable to tie otel collector LB endpoint to region (will review this with Raffa)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}
