9b46f781-93e6-4bb9-8592-7558e67b8664	d5030652-31c4-47ca-83a9-62116e71e8a7	1778219373.000093	Philip Jones	Question for architects: I've just updated ACM to 2.16 on 101 and this now includes some new features including:\nCentralised Observability for Virtual Machines including right sizing recommendations: https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga#\nAbility to manage VM's centrally from ACM search across all managed clusters.\nShould we look to propose switching these features on for the customer? I know they have their own observability solution.\nRed Hat Developer\nAdvanced Cluster Management 2.16 right-sizing recommendation GA | Red Hat Developer\nAnnouncing the Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management 2.16 general availability (GA) of namespace and virtualization right-sizing recommendations\nMar 17th\nhttps://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga	{"ts": "1778219373.000093", "text": "Question for architects: I've just updated ACM to 2.16 on 101 and this now includes some new features including:\\nCentralised Observability for Virtual Machines including right sizing recommendations: https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga#\\nAbility to manage VM's centrally from ACM search across all managed clusters.\\nShould we look to propose switching these features on for the customer? I know they have their own observability solution.\\nRed Hat Developer\\nAdvanced Cluster Management 2.16 right-sizing recommendation GA | Red Hat Developer\\nAnnouncing the Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management 2.16 general availability (GA) of namespace and virtualization right-sizing recommendations\\nMar 17th\\nhttps://developers.redhat.com/articles/2026/03/17/advanced-cluster-management-216-right-sizing-recommendation-ga", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
