5faf6f50-775a-411c-be8d-c90bbd0ca52d	21426b22-78fa-4fd1-a7ed-fb6a667b7227	1778216844.000144	Nick Evans	[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?	{"ts": "1778216844.000144", "text": "[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?", "type": "message", "user": "Nick Evans"}
