b71b4181-22d2-4c71-a075-3ceccc0883e2	6e907dfb-5bfa-4900-af5f-90553efa4488	1778193343.000163	Sam Marland	Had this ping from the PM team for auth proxy as they try and prioritize. My view is we need this feature for 4.22 unless someone else says otherwise. @rspazzol @Rydekull @Nikos @Nick Evans\nWallace Lewis\nHi Sam!  I hope this message finds you well.\nI'm an engineering director in OpenShift and the requirement to provide https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7054 for HSBC is on our list for planning our next release.  I'm trying to gather more details on timeline so we can prioritize this appropriately.  I've been told the plan is to have HSBC on 4.22 (now dev complete for us) until moving to 5.2 next year.  Can you confirm that's the plan and/or do you see a need to have this auth proxy feature available prior to our 5.2 release?  If this would be better to discuss in a short meeting, feel free to grab a time on my calendar that works for you.  Thanks in advance!\nFrom a private conversation | Apr 23rd	{"ts": "1778193343.000163", "text": "Had this ping from the PM team for auth proxy as they try and prioritize. My view is we need this feature for 4.22 unless someone else says otherwise. @rspazzol @Rydekull @Nikos @Nick Evans\\nWallace Lewis\\nHi Sam!  I hope this message finds you well.\\nI'm an engineering director in OpenShift and the requirement to provide https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7054 for HSBC is on our list for planning our next release.  I'm trying to gather more details on timeline so we can prioritize this appropriately.  I've been told the plan is to have HSBC on 4.22 (now dev complete for us) until moving to 5.2 next year.  Can you confirm that's the plan and/or do you see a need to have this auth proxy feature available prior to our 5.2 release?  If this would be better to discuss in a short meeting, feel free to grab a time on my calendar that works for you.  Thanks in advance!\\nFrom a private conversation | Apr 23rd", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
