f00dab21-b779-4e98-a384-8678f713296b	cd33e312-f3de-4c01-9dda-29b46e053970	1778195282.000182	Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga	[US/MX Workshops]: We have a request for the workshop to clarify our support engagement in both pilots (Test Migrations) and production migration (Volume Migrations). I need help from @Anne @Carina Almeida , @pdelashe, even @Nikos if you have any slides, ideas, workflows, screenshots, documents, share it them here and I will create a slide out of this. My understanding is the following about both process:\nPilot Migrations (Consulting-Led)\nDuring the pilot phase, Red Hat Consulting will be heavily involved in the execution and troubleshooting. The goal here is to establish our baseline and refine our automation.\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution.\nExecution: Consulting is involved in the communication structure of the migration (we are passive listeners here).\nFailure Handling (The New RCA Proposal): If a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back in VMware. The failed OpenShift VM is then moved to an isolated “Quarantine/Triage” environment. (Note: This isolation environment is not currently in place; we will officially propose building this during the upcoming workshops).\nResolution: Consulting performs Root Cause Analysis (RCA) in the triage environment, finds the issue and ask for the fixes the underlying automation (Narender), and places the VM back into the backlog to be rescheduled for a future migration wave.\n2. Volume / Production Migrations (Support-Led)\nOnce we move into bulk production migrations, the execution and issue resolution will shift entirely to our Support organization.\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution to ensure global readiness.\nExecution & Failure Handling: Handled 100% by Red Hat Support. This will leverage our Technical Account Managers (TAMs) across the different timezones to ensure “follow-the-sun” coverage, alongside the recently onboarded ESS team.\nResolution: The Support and ESS teams will drive immediate break/fix resolutions and coordinate any necessary escalations directly.\nPlease review this logic and let me know your thoughts or if you see any gaps.\nThis message was deleted.	{"ts": "1778195282.000182", "text": "[US/MX Workshops]: We have a request for the workshop to clarify our support engagement in both pilots (Test Migrations) and production migration (Volume Migrations). I need help from @Anne @Carina Almeida , @pdelashe, even @Nikos if you have any slides, ideas, workflows, screenshots, documents, share it them here and I will create a slide out of this. My understanding is the following about both process:\\nPilot Migrations (Consulting-Led)\\nDuring the pilot phase, Red Hat Consulting will be heavily involved in the execution and troubleshooting. The goal here is to establish our baseline and refine our automation.\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution.\\nExecution: Consulting is involved in the communication structure of the migration (we are passive listeners here).\\nFailure Handling (The New RCA Proposal): If a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back in VMware. The failed OpenShift VM is then moved to an isolated “Quarantine/Triage” environment. (Note: This isolation environment is not currently in place; we will officially propose building this during the upcoming workshops).\\nResolution: Consulting performs Root Cause Analysis (RCA) in the triage environment, finds the issue and ask for the fixes the underlying automation (Narender), and places the VM back into the backlog to be rescheduled for a future migration wave.\\n2. Volume / Production Migrations (Support-Led)\\nOnce we move into bulk production migrations, the execution and issue resolution will shift entirely to our Support organization.\\nProactive Support Case: Created prior to execution to ensure global readiness.\\nExecution & Failure Handling: Handled 100% by Red Hat Support. This will leverage our Technical Account Managers (TAMs) across the different timezones to ensure “follow-the-sun” coverage, alongside the recently onboarded ESS team.\\nResolution: The Support and ESS teams will drive immediate break/fix resolutions and coordinate any necessary escalations directly.\\nPlease review this logic and let me know your thoughts or if you see any gaps.\\nThis message was deleted.", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}
