2b253543-e114-4408-84b9-7252713c8e13	0b4e5a6c-bf86-4453-bd3f-de762115ab61	1778243171.000191	James Force	[build]\nSpoke with Mike on the LACP issue we came accross recently, they will add some checks on their side to mitigate this, but  he was curious if there was anything we can do on our side, I mentioned the lack of metrics in this area but he seemed happy about the upstream conversation and was curious to know if something did get added to node_exporter upstream when would that land in openshift\nQuick call on the ACM prorogation policies and then created an issue on the backlog to attempt to remove dependency on ACM after the initial seed... I will try to pick this up when I get some time\nRuishi dragged me into a call to discuss security policies and then went around the circles of gatekeeper, kyverno VAPs etc..  I circ led it back to the point of that VAPs were decided and work was already started here,,, I think there is a clear need for a proper backlog and planning of work as things feel a bit all over the place\nRushi called me again on the gitops approach and his want to move to something completely different (this binary artefact approach). I told him again this won't work, but he wants to allign with some 'deploycontol' approaches of their... @janine I've pinged you on the links in the teams chat.. maybe can you help me here? I think we just need to educate here on our controls for gitops and route to live process. IIRC you were working on something around this area?\nMTU... all our clusters MTU is just at 1400 (default)... this is probably a driver in the why live migrations are 'slow'....  @Rydekull I your help tomorrow on this to understand your last comment on the jump frames GH issue on upping this value to 9000\nPure upgrade troubleshooting\nSnapshot issue (102) - I've just sent the operator log to pure for 102 on the pending failed upgrade due to snapshots... hopefully they can script up something to address that ... however.... if their approach is to manually delete records out of etcd using etcdctl... not sure I really like that, doesn't exactly feel elegant!\nVolume mapping (104)  - unfortunately the horrible idea I had the other day to manually remap volumes looks like it is a reality and the only way forward... albeit they provided us with a more elegant way to get the required info we need, and also let us know we don't need to define the targets in the purevolume resource	{"ts": "1778243171.000191", "text": "[build]\\nSpoke with Mike on the LACP issue we came accross recently, they will add some checks on their side to mitigate this, but  he was curious if there was anything we can do on our side, I mentioned the lack of metrics in this area but he seemed happy about the upstream conversation and was curious to know if something did get added to node_exporter upstream when would that land in openshift\\nQuick call on the ACM prorogation policies and then created an issue on the backlog to attempt to remove dependency on ACM after the initial seed... I will try to pick this up when I get some time\\nRuishi dragged me into a call to discuss security policies and then went around the circles of gatekeeper, kyverno VAPs etc..  I circ led it back to the point of that VAPs were decided and work was already started here,,, I think there is a clear need for a proper backlog and planning of work as things feel a bit all over the place\\nRushi called me again on the gitops approach and his want to move to something completely different (this binary artefact approach). I told him again this won't work, but he wants to allign with some 'deploycontol' approaches of their... @janine I've pinged you on the links in the teams chat.. maybe can you help me here? I think we just need to educate here on our controls for gitops and route to live process. IIRC you were working on something around this area?\\nMTU... all our clusters MTU is just at 1400 (default)... this is probably a driver in the why live migrations are 'slow'....  @Rydekull I your help tomorrow on this to understand your last comment on the jump frames GH issue on upping this value to 9000\\nPure upgrade troubleshooting\\nSnapshot issue (102) - I've just sent the operator log to pure for 102 on the pending failed upgrade due to snapshots... hopefully they can script up something to address that ... however.... if their approach is to manually delete records out of etcd using etcdctl... not sure I really like that, doesn't exactly feel elegant!\\nVolume mapping (104)  - unfortunately the horrible idea I had the other day to manually remap volumes looks like it is a reality and the only way forward... albeit they provided us with a more elegant way to get the required info we need, and also let us know we don't need to define the targets in the purevolume resource", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}
