6a6c91ee-fb3d-4e4f-be63-9b4fb7f5cd89	20983bf9-df7c-4b68-ac3e-64313cb55d2f	1778220565.000205	Philip Jones	Isovalent POC Phase 2 is about to kick off... Is there an architect who wants to be involved in this? Originally Alex was involved, handing over to Shebi towards the end of the last POC. Regardless, I will take some notes and share here.\nThe new POC is to validate the latest features and changes in the new version os Isovalent Cilium. This is on the critical path for the customer to support HIC clusters.	{"ts": "1778220565.000205", "text": "Isovalent POC Phase 2 is about to kick off... Is there an architect who wants to be involved in this? Originally Alex was involved, handing over to Shebi towards the end of the last POC. Regardless, I will take some notes and share here.\\nThe new POC is to validate the latest features and changes in the new version os Isovalent Cilium. This is on the critical path for the customer to support HIC clusters.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
8d693911-5931-4a16-80c3-f5fd8bf80bf5	25b89273-9b19-4b35-bc4f-25f7dfa00bc8	1778228606.000206	Janine Eichler	[Storage Offloading] RH Engineering provided infos on how to configure storage offloading from Dell --> Pure. will be tested once 104 is back to healthy. this is not a migration pattern that's included in the upcoming pilot phase 2	{"ts": "1778228606.000206", "text": "[Storage Offloading] RH Engineering provided infos on how to configure storage offloading from Dell --> Pure. will be tested once 104 is back to healthy. this is not a migration pattern that's included in the upcoming pilot phase 2", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}
8757cecf-d337-474b-8ae8-c2567c6c6559	0b6bf832-f7ef-49ba-9e4d-689c445adb2b	1778228787.000207	Janine Eichler	[Observability] Seems the initial sizing calculation they did for storing (filtered) metrics in splunk (which was an order of magnitude higher than what we saw in overall disk usage in OpenShift) wasn't the storage consumed in splunk, but kafka. in splunk it actually looked okay today from what they showed us, got to ask for the specific number, but Onkar was not concerned at all anymore, they'll doublecheck, but looks like it's not actually an issue.	{"ts": "1778228787.000207", "text": "[Observability] Seems the initial sizing calculation they did for storing (filtered) metrics in splunk (which was an order of magnitude higher than what we saw in overall disk usage in OpenShift) wasn't the storage consumed in splunk, but kafka. in splunk it actually looked okay today from what they showed us, got to ask for the specific number, but Onkar was not concerned at all anymore, they'll doublecheck, but looks like it's not actually an issue.", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}
edc69828-41ca-4f21-9250-ee8793946688	33f87bfa-ab21-4b07-a6dd-65a5960ecd0e	1778229628.000208	Philip Jones	[Build update]\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it.\nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\n(edited)	{"ts": "1778229628.000208", "text": "[Build update]\\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it.\\nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
a65e1254-5aa4-4745-a20a-8a01d2514157	db8bbd61-5f55-4a37-b9af-40682111c261	1778276189.000209	Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga	[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessible\nThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)	{"ts": "1778276189.000209", "text": "[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessible\\nThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}
ed45010e-dbef-424c-b7a5-43154c144ba3	bb837ec7-8433-44c0-bb6d-1280c72b8d4f	1778195490.000210	Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga	[Sheffield - HIC Design Workshops notes]: Please all the notes here, include screenshots or whatever you want and later we can add structure, is better to have excess in this case: https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/edit?tab=t.0\nGoogle Docs	{"ts": "1778195490.000210", "text": "[Sheffield - HIC Design Workshops notes]: Please all the notes here, include screenshots or whatever you want and later we can add structure, is better to have excess in this case: https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/edit?tab=t.0\\nGoogle Docs", "type": "message", "user": "Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga"}
a61451a0-4c07-431e-b9e1-1ba3f07b9365	3c2fbaf0-15c0-43a1-ae84-aa12c82fbcf1	1778196871.000211	Sam Marland	[RFE-7054 - Auth Proxy] - I had a call two people in engineering about the auth proxy last night. I explained to them that we have a workaround at the moment but at some point, we might need to configure a different proxy and the cluster wide proxy doesn't work for us anymore. The proposed solution is to add a new property to the oauth object. THey're not sure if they will be able to backport it to 4.22 but they were confident on a backport to 4.23. @Shebi @Rydekull @James Force @rspazzol @Philip Jones	{"ts": "1778196871.000211", "text": "[RFE-7054 - Auth Proxy] - I had a call two people in engineering about the auth proxy last night. I explained to them that we have a workaround at the moment but at some point, we might need to configure a different proxy and the cluster wide proxy doesn't work for us anymore. The proposed solution is to add a new property to the oauth object. THey're not sure if they will be able to backport it to 4.22 but they were confident on a backport to 4.23. @Shebi @Rydekull @James Force @rspazzol @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
585d6e14-1eea-4ae4-98a2-8c9120183fa1	7446d1f6-999b-4bf9-9fe7-7b04315e4704	1778222246.000266	Philip Jones	Isovalent Update:\nCurrent plan for POC Phase 2:\nOne standard cluster (with OVN) to run ACM and deploy the second cluster (this may not be the case initially).\n2 cluster (with Isovalent Cilium).\n Split across three "sites"\nFirst Site - 1 master & 1 or 2 worker\nSecond Site - 1 master and 1 or 2 workers\nThird Site - Arbiter Node	{"ts": "1778222246.000266", "text": "Isovalent Update:\\nCurrent plan for POC Phase 2:\\nOne standard cluster (with OVN) to run ACM and deploy the second cluster (this may not be the case initially).\\n2 cluster (with Isovalent Cilium).\\n Split across three \\"sites\\"\\nFirst Site - 1 master & 1 or 2 worker\\nSecond Site - 1 master and 1 or 2 workers\\nThird Site - Arbiter Node", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
a4d3d05f-62ad-424e-84c1-24a099c72b00	3585597e-b4c6-4909-b1c3-5d6101315b03	1778197232.000212	Sam Marland	[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.	{"ts": "1778197232.000212", "text": "[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
d708e98e-06c7-403e-a97e-04831672d310	add80429-c955-4029-88ca-2a8954979511	1778197353.000213	Sam Marland	[Windows restarts] Vinay mentioned they've noticed Windows VMs restarting up to 20 times as part of the migration. Any context on this? Is it expected behavior? Is there something that can be done to improve the situation?	{"ts": "1778197353.000213", "text": "[Windows restarts] Vinay mentioned they've noticed Windows VMs restarting up to 20 times as part of the migration. Any context on this? Is it expected behavior? Is there something that can be done to improve the situation?", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
90fab272-6f97-4061-9672-68774ba8956a	0de681bd-aed0-4382-9919-d76e07cf3942	1778198614.000214	Patricia de las Heras Granaglia	[Migration update]\nPilot Phase 2:\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th	{"ts": "1778198614.000214", "text": "[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}
905d5e79-53f3-42c4-9fbd-0259cdcd267b	1bdfa3af-f844-497e-ba24-973b7ed6d3a3	1778199275.000215	Philip Jones	Just a quick reminder that I have a dentists appointment today. Should hopefully be back online before 10:00	{"ts": "1778199275.000215", "text": "Just a quick reminder that I have a dentists appointment today. Should hopefully be back online before 10:00", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
ff074e3d-8d92-4246-bf0e-3779a827838c	1636213e-537f-4f6d-873e-bcbcafcc9c3e	1778201856.000216	Rosalia Suarez Mejias	[Delivery Report]\nHi team,  Can you all please put in your updates from last Thursday to today to the template: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0#slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0 I will be sending this out at 11am tomorrow. Please ensure that you update the main body by close of business today. Thank you all.	{"ts": "1778201856.000216", "text": "[Delivery Report]\\nHi team,  Can you all please put in your updates from last Thursday to today to the template: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0#slide=id.g3d367ed5e9f_0_0 I will be sending this out at 11am tomorrow. Please ensure that you update the main body by close of business today. Thank you all.", "type": "message", "user": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}
