199ae1a9-ee61-4d44-9874-a3665d9a8ccb	ea651e64-a7cc-4af5-9bef-5db1960969d7	1778206298.000218	Janine Eichler	@Shebi @Rydekull we know why there's a site preference for workloads in stretched clusters?	{"ts": "1778206298.000218", "text": "@Shebi @Rydekull we know why there's a site preference for workloads in stretched clusters?", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}
89b8c794-3d2f-4d5a-bd6c-1cdad1d77693	53ad599e-0a34-48c2-9ee7-2ff0b508f7b5	1778209119.000219	Carina Almeida	[Maj/Carina sync]\nMexico:\nFabric delivery to Engineering (ENG) expected around May 15th.\nFull migration planned for October, though the DMZ presents a significant challenge.\nIndia:\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\nDMZ (General):\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\nThis issue also affects the UK.\nHong Kong (HK):\nReprioritization work is complete.\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\nUnited States (US):\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\nNote: EOS is their second priority.	{"ts": "1778209119.000219", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\nMexico:\\nFabric delivery to Engineering (ENG) expected around May 15th.\\nFull migration planned for October, though the DMZ presents a significant challenge.\\nIndia:\\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\\nDMZ (General):\\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\\nThis issue also affects the UK.\\nHong Kong (HK):\\nReprioritization work is complete.\\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\\nUnited States (US):\\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\\nNote: EOS is their second priority.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}
9b42102d-1bc9-4ac8-abd7-375cfee0bb31	1f02ead8-d86f-4f99-9e0d-696f5b21d237	7777721900.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	I's been more than 1 hour since I started calling people to join	{"ts": "7777721900.000000", "text": "I's been more than 1 hour since I started calling people to join", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
40ccbada-0ac3-4de1-9a15-69cdd0248dc3	0e32af9c-ab8b-48ac-be19-4c4b7c125129	1778209540.000220	Philip Jones	@Carina Almeida, @janine, @Rosemary Lynch and @James Force, for info the customer is still having issues with cluster hkoclu307. Specifically, that three nodes aren't able to register, having built successfully via ACM.\nI've exhausted my troubleshooting on this and did request a few days ago that they capture all the diagnostic and debug info from myself and their networking team and then raise a RH support ticket.\nWe can ssh into the problem nodes. I've checked the br-ex and it looks good. Both interfaces in the bond are good. It can nslookup and curl other endpoints e.g the default ingress controller. It just can't build a route to the API IP. No route to host and a tcpdump show arp requests being sent with no response. Their networking team is saying there's no issues on their side...	{"ts": "1778209540.000220", "text": "@Carina Almeida, @janine, @Rosemary Lynch and @James Force, for info the customer is still having issues with cluster hkoclu307. Specifically, that three nodes aren't able to register, having built successfully via ACM.\\nI've exhausted my troubleshooting on this and did request a few days ago that they capture all the diagnostic and debug info from myself and their networking team and then raise a RH support ticket.\\nWe can ssh into the problem nodes. I've checked the br-ex and it looks good. Both interfaces in the bond are good. It can nslookup and curl other endpoints e.g the default ingress controller. It just can't build a route to the API IP. No route to host and a tcpdump show arp requests being sent with no response. Their networking team is saying there's no issues on their side...", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
6f0e4da9-c36b-4222-80a4-a3c9a8cc4244	f92708ff-72d3-4597-8b25-ab71e2beb54c	1778209541.000221	Philip Jones	So they're talking about raising a blocker if this isn't fixed by the end of the day.	{"ts": "1778209541.000221", "text": "So they're talking about raising a blocker if this isn't fixed by the end of the day.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
