1f1b94fe-969a-4de2-af9e-07c490df941d	205682b0-9e9d-4fee-8664-0914d51bff0f	1778216923.000223	Ricardo Gregorio	Hi all,\nI think it was mentioned last year, by @rspazzol @Sam Marland, in the other eos channel about demo of Network Observability. During the Sheffield workshops @Nikos mentioned "Network Observability Operator to be used for Non-HIC and data to be fed to HSBC cyber team".\nWhat is the plan for this?\nI need to read, but does anyone know what extra it provides (compare to the current node network metrics available)???	{"ts": "1778216923.000223", "text": "Hi all,\\nI think it was mentioned last year, by @rspazzol @Sam Marland, in the other eos channel about demo of Network Observability. During the Sheffield workshops @Nikos mentioned \\"Network Observability Operator to be used for Non-HIC and data to be fed to HSBC cyber team\\".\\nWhat is the plan for this?\\nI need to read, but does anyone know what extra it provides (compare to the current node network metrics available)???", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}
6079680a-1918-4c52-8388-c3a34f0ec415	12da03aa-8039-427e-9f70-c31b58575297	1778217944.000224	Rosalia Suarez Mejias	Delivery Report]\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)	{"ts": "1778217944.000224", "text": "Delivery Report]\\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}
9a6c6e3d-46d6-413b-962b-16da1639a33e	ce35ac1b-34cf-4866-8415-cc0e20927050	1778220285.000225	Alexander Rydekull	[Due to their internal network setup missing firewalls...] We're being asked if we can prevent who can talk to the nodes and the kube api. Many ways to skin a cat. Stupid that it is required and not solved with a traditional firewall.\nAny thoughts?	{"ts": "1778220285.000225", "text": "[Due to their internal network setup missing firewalls...] We're being asked if we can prevent who can talk to the nodes and the kube api. Many ways to skin a cat. Stupid that it is required and not solved with a traditional firewall.\\nAny thoughts?", "type": "message", "user": "Alexander Rydekull"}
ab8f5c19-5608-4c68-9061-e329f4251c4f	0695dc1b-ff8c-4c0b-8c9c-d2837e0940b5	1778225086.000226	Jens Feind	[VM Migration]\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.\nAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler	{"ts": "1778225086.000226", "text": "[VM Migration]\\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \\n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.\\nAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}
f5920398-c6eb-463c-a4fb-d0c389830f25	17033358-4349-481a-8d3b-bdce08e8b16f	1778226538.000238	Philip Jones	[Isovalent Update]\nLargely just confirming the version that we'll be installing for the POC phase 2.\nLast time all the clusters were agent based installations so I've suggested that this time we build one ACM cluster and build the second cluster from that instead. This should more closely represent the build process HSBC will use for the majority of their clusters.\nWill need to provide some info in POCDOC to assist with ACM install etc.	{"ts": "1778226538.000238", "text": "[Isovalent Update]\\nLargely just confirming the version that we'll be installing for the POC phase 2.\\nLast time all the clusters were agent based installations so I've suggested that this time we build one ACM cluster and build the second cluster from that instead. This should more closely represent the build process HSBC will use for the majority of their clusters.\\nWill need to provide some info in POCDOC to assist with ACM install etc.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
183b4bbb-0672-44cb-8b54-a60ff034d83e	d8119474-0406-4ff2-a628-21be7123fab6	1778228507.000227	Philip Jones	[build]\nWe have restored cluster 104 this morning. It's now at least as good as it was before the storage update :wink:\nCluster 102 pure storage update now successfully completed after we ran a cleanup script to remove stale entries in the pure storage cluster kvdb.\nTake away from this is that the storage cluster had a lot of volume snapshots it thought it was managing that didn't actually exist on the flasharray. This was likely triggered by stress testing back in Feb.\nWe still see a LOT of volume snapshots associated with non-existent, previously deleted pvc's. These are for the most case the same stale volumes the script removed from kvdb. We will need to create our own script to remove them and complete the cleanup.\nIssues impacting hkoclu307 and the three nodes that refused to register now tracked to a Cisco switch issue. A ticket is being raised with Cisco to debug.\nIsovalent call postponed for today.	{"ts": "1778228507.000227", "text": "[build]\\nWe have restored cluster 104 this morning. It's now at least as good as it was before the storage update :wink:\\nCluster 102 pure storage update now successfully completed after we ran a cleanup script to remove stale entries in the pure storage cluster kvdb.\\nTake away from this is that the storage cluster had a lot of volume snapshots it thought it was managing that didn't actually exist on the flasharray. This was likely triggered by stress testing back in Feb.\\nWe still see a LOT of volume snapshots associated with non-existent, previously deleted pvc's. These are for the most case the same stale volumes the script removed from kvdb. We will need to create our own script to remove them and complete the cleanup.\\nIssues impacting hkoclu307 and the three nodes that refused to register now tracked to a Cisco switch issue. A ticket is being raised with Cisco to debug.\\nIsovalent call postponed for today.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
57c7d7d7-d2a7-41fa-9083-8ed73ad5a620	2ca1cf33-7dc8-4176-a2c7-90777050f2bc	1778229768.000228	Ricardo Gregorio	[observability]\ninvestigating whether info from the assisted-service pod logs can help with monitoring the managed-cluster build progress. I will share some findings with @janine\nworking on SIEM log requirements (will catch up with @Rydekull tomorrow)	{"ts": "1778229768.000228", "text": "[observability]\\ninvestigating whether info from the assisted-service pod logs can help with monitoring the managed-cluster build progress. I will share some findings with @janine\\nworking on SIEM log requirements (will catch up with @Rydekull tomorrow)", "type": "message", "user": "Ricardo Gregorio"}
a4e5515b-9f9c-45a0-9a2b-65131fca1f25	f79942ba-525a-4bd0-b85d-5022bfc74418	1778276029.000229	Arpit Tolani	{Migration}\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has "Windows Server" or not.. If it has, patch it\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\n --type merge\n -p '{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"domain":{"devices":{"video":{"type":"virtio"}}}}}}}'\nBut with automation i have few questions.\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...	{"ts": "1778276029.000229", "text": "{Migration}\\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has \\"Windows Server\\" or not.. If it has, patch it\\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\\n --type merge\\n -p '{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"domain\\":{\\"devices\\":{\\"video\\":{\\"type\\":\\"virtio\\"}}}}}}}'\\nBut with automation i have few questions.\\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...", "type": "message", "user": "Arpit Tolani"}
9135f7bc-a0e0-4be3-bbc0-0547827acdb9	72dada6b-e189-454d-b38f-6f9a026d130e	1778201810.000230	Rosalia Suarez Mejias	Delivery Report]\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)	{"ts": "1778201810.000230", "text": "Delivery Report]\\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Rosalia Suarez Mejias"}
b22edcbe-5c53-4980-8a2a-c0f025ea36f8	17530c3e-20e5-47e0-90cb-e20aee05020a	1778203371.000231	Patricia de las Heras Granaglia	[Migration Update]\nPilot Phase 2:\nStart date confirmed May 5th\n4 VMs may drop of scope (due RDM)\nStill some issues in MIoX integrations with CRQ, may delay a bit the change approval (holidays 1 and 4)\nTODO: Proactive Support Case\nPilot Mexico:\nConfirmed availability dates for Fabric Mid June; Vimal to provide cluster readiness dates\nTODO: Confirm with ACN the migration window for MX\n(edited)	{"ts": "1778203371.000231", "text": "[Migration Update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\nStart date confirmed May 5th\\n4 VMs may drop of scope (due RDM)\\nStill some issues in MIoX integrations with CRQ, may delay a bit the change approval (holidays 1 and 4)\\nTODO: Proactive Support Case\\nPilot Mexico:\\nConfirmed availability dates for Fabric Mid June; Vimal to provide cluster readiness dates\\nTODO: Confirm with ACN the migration window for MX\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Patricia de las Heras Granaglia"}
