f750b089-2491-4335-b890-343b3e2eb227	a998ae29-3336-4367-8c10-315b85e5fc7b	1778217622.000262	Raffaele Spazzoli	[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)	{"ts": "1778217622.000262", "text": "[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}
