f389ce2e-f212-4f87-a95c-f000cf810c21	e6d70d7f-5c75-4792-99da-fbd563c46fb8	1778230049.000269	Sam Marland	Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.	{"ts": "1778230049.000269", "text": "Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
