b0ecade2-df10-440f-bc6d-ec193407320d	fa2cc904-3b94-4b55-9dee-f4c8d02ff612	1778222800.000280	Philip Jones	Isovalent Update:\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.	{"ts": "1778222800.000280", "text": "Isovalent Update:\\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
41dacd95-1dad-4349-8e3d-5069b476795a	92eb024e-d4d1-4ede-81b2-baf5630701ec	1778224601.000281	James Force	@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?	{"ts": "1778224601.000281", "text": "@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?", "type": "message", "user": "James Force"}
c0291f4f-060c-416d-b754-17df99f9fce3	ffada008-fe4c-47a9-b7b7-49292595dc7b	1778245662.000282	Sam Marland	Update on the plan for oauth proxy.\nKevin Rizza\nhey Sam, we are still assessing all the work that needs to happen. at this point we believe that making this change for the oauth stack is something we will target to backport to 4.22. we are still looking at all the edge cases, so we don't have a firm commitment on exactly what date it would land, but we're trying to get this done in the 5.0 release timeframe and then work on a backport once that's done.\nwe're tracking all that effort here https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/OCPSTRAT-3174, and I'll keep regular weekly updates in that ticket\nFrom a private conversation | May 6th	{"ts": "1778245662.000282", "text": "Update on the plan for oauth proxy.\\nKevin Rizza\\nhey Sam, we are still assessing all the work that needs to happen. at this point we believe that making this change for the oauth stack is something we will target to backport to 4.22. we are still looking at all the edge cases, so we don't have a firm commitment on exactly what date it would land, but we're trying to get this done in the 5.0 release timeframe and then work on a backport once that's done.\\nwe're tracking all that effort here https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/OCPSTRAT-3174, and I'll keep regular weekly updates in that ticket\\nFrom a private conversation | May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
