26cd2f93-2218-4905-9b76-c2e2d5c17ef4	7584e75d-2aab-4709-8586-7a08e831f9e1	1778210510.000290	Jens Feind	[Missing IPs after Migration]\n@janine @Rydekull et al\nThere is a support case regarding this issue, Amrut attached the log of virt-v2v pod of the affected VMs migration plan. If you got other findings or artifacts this would be a good central place to store and follow up.\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04435341 (edited)	{"ts": "1778210510.000290", "text": "[Missing IPs after Migration]\\n@janine @Rydekull et al\\nThere is a support case regarding this issue, Amrut attached the log of virt-v2v pod of the affected VMs migration plan. If you got other findings or artifacts this would be a good central place to store and follow up.\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04435341 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}
a1203653-c9dd-4483-8a86-02d61d55d5c3	a03183ef-2f19-4bdc-909d-751fee6923b4	1778219271.000291	Janine Eichler	[US Migrations] @Shebi current status:\ngenerally: they expect to have to report stauts / progress more often beginning next week. seems they get some mgmt attention.\nJune got pointed to another repo where he shall put his playbook and where another pb sits that he should invoke. nothing to do from our side here.\nThey asked if you had started anything on the multi NIC linux use case.\nThey asked us to kickstart the re-IPing automation for windows VMs. I';ve reached out to the windows team, will need to file a "formal" request to the program lead so we can get a peek into what the Widnwos team did when they re-IPed VMs. @Carina Almeida pinging you here, if you could let me know how this request to the pgrogram leads works, I'd be eternally grateful :slightly_smiling_face:\nThey seem focussed on the VM side of things, who's responsible for the other necessary things (LB, DNS, app config, etc.)?	{"ts": "1778219271.000291", "text": "[US Migrations] @Shebi current status:\\ngenerally: they expect to have to report stauts / progress more often beginning next week. seems they get some mgmt attention.\\nJune got pointed to another repo where he shall put his playbook and where another pb sits that he should invoke. nothing to do from our side here.\\nThey asked if you had started anything on the multi NIC linux use case.\\nThey asked us to kickstart the re-IPing automation for windows VMs. I';ve reached out to the windows team, will need to file a \\"formal\\" request to the program lead so we can get a peek into what the Widnwos team did when they re-IPed VMs. @Carina Almeida pinging you here, if you could let me know how this request to the pgrogram leads works, I'd be eternally grateful :slightly_smiling_face:\\nThey seem focussed on the VM side of things, who's responsible for the other necessary things (LB, DNS, app config, etc.)?", "type": "message", "user": "Janine Eichler"}
3d056f46-3469-400a-bb6d-dbbd69de30bd	3d8250e2-15bd-433c-9fe1-0c2c2e427cde	1778224792.000292	Philip Jones	[Build Update]:\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel.\n421 channel work is underway as well.\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully.\nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\n(edited)	{"ts": "1778224792.000292", "text": "[Build Update]:\\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel.\\n421 channel work is underway as well.\\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully.\\nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Philip Jones"}
82e0f58c-09f4-4031-9480-617b8f5103af	e26b7c3e-2836-4ab6-adea-241802ff5c53	1778226113.000293	Raffaele Spazzoli	[VIB memory still failing] hello, Abhishek is reaching out to me stating that storage offloads migration are still failing due to memory issues at the ESXi hosts level. Do we have anyone looking into it? @pdelashe @janine I think you are the closest to this issue. Roy Golan should guide us through the resolution.	{"ts": "1778226113.000293", "text": "[VIB memory still failing] hello, Abhishek is reaching out to me stating that storage offloads migration are still failing due to memory issues at the ESXi hosts level. Do we have anyone looking into it? @pdelashe @janine I think you are the closest to this issue. Roy Golan should guide us through the resolution.", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}
51c7431b-a9b1-4e6a-b26d-574bbae91dc6	38a84f05-ac1a-44bf-8b8d-5d3f1c0485de	1778228034.000294	Carina Almeida	[Migration team cover for the next two weeks]\n@pdelashe – I  mentioned we would address this on Monday, but I’ve moved it up as I realised there is a bank holiday in Germany next week.\nTeam,\nNext week, the bank is planning to migrate approximately 230 VMs across Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. Since Thursday is a bank holiday in Germany, we need to ensure coverage. @atolani @ricardo gregorio @rspazzol @Rydekull do you have availability to cover for @Shebi and @jfeind? We need one arch and one Consultant for Thursday.\nMay 22nd is a Red Hat Recharge Day. We are currently coordinating with ESS to see if they can cover migrations that day. However, I would like to know if anyone is interested in a day swap: working on the 22nd and taking your Recharge Day at another date. This would help us with coordination.\nPlease let me know your availability for the cover and the swap by lunch time tomorrow. :pray:\nTagging who's not tagged yet: @janine @James Force @Philip Jones @Petros\nShebi-Openshift-Alerting\nAPP  18:11\nwas added to proj-eos-mvp by Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga\n.	{"ts": "1778228034.000294", "text": "[Migration team cover for the next two weeks]\\n@pdelashe – I  mentioned we would address this on Monday, but I’ve moved it up as I realised there is a bank holiday in Germany next week.\\nTeam,\\nNext week, the bank is planning to migrate approximately 230 VMs across Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. Since Thursday is a bank holiday in Germany, we need to ensure coverage. @atolani @ricardo gregorio @rspazzol @Rydekull do you have availability to cover for @Shebi and @jfeind? We need one arch and one Consultant for Thursday.\\nMay 22nd is a Red Hat Recharge Day. We are currently coordinating with ESS to see if they can cover migrations that day. However, I would like to know if anyone is interested in a day swap: working on the 22nd and taking your Recharge Day at another date. This would help us with coordination.\\nPlease let me know your availability for the cover and the swap by lunch time tomorrow. :pray:\\nTagging who's not tagged yet: @janine @James Force @Philip Jones @Petros\\nShebi-Openshift-Alerting\\nAPP  18:11\\nwas added to proj-eos-mvp by Sebastian Rodriguez Isaziga\\n.", "type": "message", "user": "Carina Almeida"}
33ee8660-cfd7-4b8c-b4d1-d7365c725c21	c559155b-5faf-4bc3-9b1c-b1b1701e3f1a	1778257915.000295	Raffaele Spazzoli	[vibe coding] it turned out that all the nice tools that Vinay teams is coming out with are partially vibe coded by Vinay himself. So we started talking a bit about spec-driven development and I shared my methodology (bmad) . Michael P. will now develop an operator, Vinay will try it. @Shebi was already coding away. All in all, the world is changing, take a look at what is happening and learn the new methodologies. you can do it for free for now as long as red hat is paying for your tokens... (edited)	{"ts": "1778257915.000295", "text": "[vibe coding] it turned out that all the nice tools that Vinay teams is coming out with are partially vibe coded by Vinay himself. So we started talking a bit about spec-driven development and I shared my methodology (bmad) . Michael P. will now develop an operator, Vinay will try it. @Shebi was already coding away. All in all, the world is changing, take a look at what is happening and learn the new methodologies. you can do it for free for now as long as red hat is paying for your tokens... (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "Raffaele Spazzoli"}
b6358df2-6498-40a9-81e9-b733e8e250eb	359e3467-1f43-427f-b9cc-6c2b50398856	1778193356.000296	Sam Marland	Case - https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04442406\nAbhishek has raised this case over night. It appears linked to the issue from yesterday with the machine with many disks. My intention is to share this ASAP in the migration-blockers-nda-customer channel for focus. It is going to be difficult to get focus with everyone about to travel to Summit. @Rydekull I think you're closest to this from a debug perspective. Can you share any more context you've seen during debugging so we can help engineering?	{"ts": "1778193356.000296", "text": "Case - https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04442406\\nAbhishek has raised this case over night. It appears linked to the issue from yesterday with the machine with many disks. My intention is to share this ASAP in the migration-blockers-nda-customer channel for focus. It is going to be difficult to get focus with everyone about to travel to Summit. @Rydekull I think you're closest to this from a debug perspective. Can you share any more context you've seen during debugging so we can help engineering?", "type": "message", "user": "Sam Marland"}
