abe667ca-81f4-4a0f-b01f-4e99525f3351	e9d8a216-b620-4860-a59f-1dc59981dbc8	1778213641.000301	Jens Feind	[Update 104 to 4.21]\n@Philip Jones technically speaking, would we be ready to roll 104 to 4.21 soon? (SCSI3-PR, shared disk topic), I saw you gave updates on Operators regarding 4.21 in the build channel, thanks for that.\n@rspazzol you had a brief sync with Rushikesh on this, that and why we need it?\nHe is not replying on the Build Team Channel, it is a bit annoying, at some point I would expect green light from him, or not.\nIn context: There is ongoing demand mounting up to proceed with the Windows Failover Cluster VM shared disk issues.\nI have been asked to write an Email to Vinay and Narender by today on what our proposed next step is, I guess Sudhir is getting tons of pressure...\nI want to support him and if we tell them we update 104 to 4.21 soon to continue debug this, we have a positive spin here. (edited) \nMessage proj-eos-mvp	{"ts": "1778213641.000301", "text": "[Update 104 to 4.21]\\n@Philip Jones technically speaking, would we be ready to roll 104 to 4.21 soon? (SCSI3-PR, shared disk topic), I saw you gave updates on Operators regarding 4.21 in the build channel, thanks for that.\\n@rspazzol you had a brief sync with Rushikesh on this, that and why we need it?\\nHe is not replying on the Build Team Channel, it is a bit annoying, at some point I would expect green light from him, or not.\\nIn context: There is ongoing demand mounting up to proceed with the Windows Failover Cluster VM shared disk issues.\\nI have been asked to write an Email to Vinay and Narender by today on what our proposed next step is, I guess Sudhir is getting tons of pressure...\\nI want to support him and if we tell them we update 104 to 4.21 soon to continue debug this, we have a positive spin here. (edited) \\nMessage proj-eos-mvp", "type": "message", "user": "Jens Feind"}
