b833fa73-c76b-41a7-9331-42be09e65db8	49039253-65ea-4d1f-9e23-e3ee1a5497a3	7777701400.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Migration Failure Process Workshop]\nGoal: Improve the failure management as it is not clear who needs to do what, and in particular SLAs\nGoal2: Vinay has asked ACN to be more proactive on the initial Triage\nWe reviewed the process drafted by ACN (Image on Teams) and modified some responsabilities and SLAs\nActions:\na) All Miox Logs posted in Splunk should be available for the team that is doing the triage\nb) ACN to review a Confluence Knowledgebase of Miox Errors = Solutions or whom to call\nc) Escalate to the Program what to do if ITSOs do not respond in the agreed time (30') either rollback or move to hypercare, or someone to talk to ITSO to clarify the importance of responding in time\nd) Red Hat (me) to send our proposal on how we want to collaborate with the Command Center and support triageRaffaele Spazzoli  [2:10 PM]\n[metrics and acm] Enterprise architecture and the run team are starting to take a look at the otel integration and are raising some objections (the same I was raising at the beginning: not all metrics are being forwarded). next steps: a demo of what exist today will be given. Onkar will demo the otel piece, redhat will demo in platform observability. I volunteered, but I have some travel time in front of me and I might have to delegate. @Shebi @Shebi. in the horizon there is the fact that the run team and the Enterprise architecture team bith like the idea of using the product feature when it comes to operationalization. so we might be asked to enabled ACM observability. This was a hard no from Vinay, so we'll se how the conversation evolves. Aside from @ricardo gregorio who has been following this we need and architect to follow this.	{"ts": "7777701400.000000", "text": "[Migration Failure Process Workshop]\\nGoal: Improve the failure management as it is not clear who needs to do what, and in particular SLAs\\nGoal2: Vinay has asked ACN to be more proactive on the initial Triage\\nWe reviewed the process drafted by ACN (Image on Teams) and modified some responsabilities and SLAs\\nActions:\\na) All Miox Logs posted in Splunk should be available for the team that is doing the triage\\nb) ACN to review a Confluence Knowledgebase of Miox Errors = Solutions or whom to call\\nc) Escalate to the Program what to do if ITSOs do not respond in the agreed time (30') either rollback or move to hypercare, or someone to talk to ITSO to clarify the importance of responding in time\\nd) Red Hat (me) to send our proposal on how we want to collaborate with the Command Center and support triageRaffaele Spazzoli  [2:10 PM]\\n[metrics and acm] Enterprise architecture and the run team are starting to take a look at the otel integration and are raising some objections (the same I was raising at the beginning: not all metrics are being forwarded). next steps: a demo of what exist today will be given. Onkar will demo the otel piece, redhat will demo in platform observability. I volunteered, but I have some travel time in front of me and I might have to delegate. @Shebi @Shebi. in the horizon there is the fact that the run team and the Enterprise architecture team bith like the idea of using the product feature when it comes to operationalization. so we might be asked to enabled ACM observability. This was a hard no from Vinay, so we'll se how the conversation evolves. Aside from @ricardo gregorio who has been following this we need and architect to follow this.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
