81d2d38b-9226-45cc-82f6-fc90ba9bc70b	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700600.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\nadded couple of namespaces and a message keyword to the existing filter setup in the logforwarder resource;\nteam work with @Philip Jones to get the dell powermax metrics available;\nadded couple of powermax metrics to the otel configuration on 104. observability team with validate data flowing into splunk tomorrow.\nenabled, manually on 104, servicemonitor to make Trident-metrics available. At quick glance could not work out array capacity;\nthanks @Philip Jones for pulling metrics list from 104 manually;\nraised PR to enable custom alerts to monitor OTEL Collector health, message queue usage and failure of messages not queuing locally or not sending to the OTEL Collector Gateway.	{"ts": "7777700600.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nadded couple of namespaces and a message keyword to the existing filter setup in the logforwarder resource;\\nteam work with @Philip Jones to get the dell powermax metrics available;\\nadded couple of powermax metrics to the otel configuration on 104. observability team with validate data flowing into splunk tomorrow.\\nenabled, manually on 104, servicemonitor to make Trident-metrics available. At quick glance could not work out array capacity;\\nthanks @Philip Jones for pulling metrics list from 104 manually;\\nraised PR to enable custom alerts to monitor OTEL Collector health, message queue usage and failure of messages not queuing locally or not sending to the OTEL Collector Gateway.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D"}
46a3d551-c439-46a6-9f98-59968be5f0e7	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700601.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\nPR to add alert rules to Otel Collector - thank you @James Force \nPR to add extra namespaces in logging\nRemoved filters in CLF targetting cyber Splunk. Will review this with Rijo tomorrow. Last 24h with filters in place: data ingestion of 18G from 104\nNeed to mod. Trident config to allow for https-metrics. Might have a catch up with @James Force if/when available next.	{"ts": "7777700601.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nPR to add alert rules to Otel Collector - thank you @James Force \\nPR to add extra namespaces in logging\\nRemoved filters in CLF targetting cyber Splunk. Will review this with Rijo tomorrow. Last 24h with filters in place: data ingestion of 18G from 104\\nNeed to mod. Trident config to allow for https-metrics. Might have a catch up with @James Force if/when available next.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
1464ee5e-644a-4e4b-ba19-ac0a572d8970	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700602.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\nadded netapp-trident namespace to log-forwarder filter + added regex patterns to message filter\nsimulated a kustomize patch definition for the region based endpoints in anticipation for live changes next week\nworking with Onkar to provide powermax metrics to stor team	{"ts": "7777700602.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\nadded netapp-trident namespace to log-forwarder filter + added regex patterns to message filter\\nsimulated a kustomize patch definition for the region based endpoints in anticipation for live changes next week\\nworking with Onkar to provide powermax metrics to stor team", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
fe219511-b17c-442f-bca7-902cc0b0c636	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700603.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n- customer wants to find a way of 'observing' the cluster build lifecycle, i.e., capturing/monitoring the build phases/progress/failures. This is because over the weekend 4x worker nodes out of 48x did not join a cluster that was built. Unsure how this can be done, so currently researching this. Thank you for helping @janine\n- checked with Cyber team. Cluster 104, last 24h ingested 33.6 million events ~ 59.2G. It seems that they have not checked the contents in regards of what is useful, what is sensitive, etc\n- reviewing Confluence doc in regards to OCP-V Security Requirement Matrix (defined by customer)Carina Almeida  [5:54 PM]\n[Migration velocity]\n\n@janine @Shebi @Rydekull iIn our call with ACN today, we agreed to document the specific challenges and constraints that can impact migration velocity.\n\nWhile the document @Anne prepared outlines our advice to achieve velocity, we now need to explicitly list the challenges and constraints. Could you please add your input to that document? - Go Faster ideas\n\nACN also raised a question regarding potential Miox restrictions. They were informed that Miox can only migrate 40 VMs in parallel. Are you aware of this limitation, or do you have a views on whether this is accurate?\n\nThank you so much.\n\nPS. @Nikos  and @rspazzol for info.	{"ts": "7777700603.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n- customer wants to find a way of 'observing' the cluster build lifecycle, i.e., capturing/monitoring the build phases/progress/failures. This is because over the weekend 4x worker nodes out of 48x did not join a cluster that was built. Unsure how this can be done, so currently researching this. Thank you for helping @janine\\n- checked with Cyber team. Cluster 104, last 24h ingested 33.6 million events ~ 59.2G. It seems that they have not checked the contents in regards of what is useful, what is sensitive, etc\\n- reviewing Confluence doc in regards to OCP-V Security Requirement Matrix (defined by customer)Carina Almeida  [5:54 PM]\\n[Migration velocity]\\n\\n@janine @Shebi @Rydekull iIn our call with ACN today, we agreed to document the specific challenges and constraints that can impact migration velocity.\\n\\nWhile the document @Anne prepared outlines our advice to achieve velocity, we now need to explicitly list the challenges and constraints. Could you please add your input to that document? - Go Faster ideas\\n\\nACN also raised a question regarding potential Miox restrictions. They were informed that Miox can only migrate 40 VMs in parallel. Are you aware of this limitation, or do you have a views on whether this is accurate?\\n\\nThank you so much.\\n\\nPS. @Nikos  and @rspazzol for info.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
4d084968-74f4-4837-a413-28afa76dcdad	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700604.000000	U_JANINE_71F80BBD	[Observability] Seems the initial sizing calculation they did for storing (filtered) metrics in splunk (which was an order of magnitude higher than what we saw in overall disk usage in OpenShift) wasn't the storage consumed in splunk, but kafka. in splunk it actually looked okay today from what they showed us, got to ask for the specific number, but Onkar was not concerned at all anymore, they'll doublecheck, but looks like it's not actually an issue.	{"ts": "7777700604.000000", "text": "[Observability] Seems the initial sizing calculation they did for storing (filtered) metrics in splunk (which was an order of magnitude higher than what we saw in overall disk usage in OpenShift) wasn't the storage consumed in splunk, but kafka. in splunk it actually looked okay today from what they showed us, got to ask for the specific number, but Onkar was not concerned at all anymore, they'll doublecheck, but looks like it's not actually an issue.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JANINE_71F80BBD", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
15079622-7a45-4bb5-8c5e-73c518a6d79a	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700605.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\ninvestigating whether info from the assisted-service pod logs can help with monitoring the managed-cluster build progress. I will share some findings with @janine \nworking on SIEM log requirements (will catch up with @Rydekull tomorrow)	{"ts": "7777700605.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ninvestigating whether info from the assisted-service pod logs can help with monitoring the managed-cluster build progress. I will share some findings with @janine \\nworking on SIEM log requirements (will catch up with @Rydekull tomorrow)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
909db714-a7c9-447f-b965-78ebb837e2ed	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700606.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\ntemporarily forwarding infra/audit logs to SIEM Splunk Pre-Prod instance, via 102;\nshared intentional ssh attempt failures and selfsubjectaccessreviews resource events with the SIEM team;	{"ts": "7777700606.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ntemporarily forwarding infra/audit logs to SIEM Splunk Pre-Prod instance, via 102;\\nshared intentional ssh attempt failures and selfsubjectaccessreviews resource events with the SIEM team;", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
0edbfaf5-d461-4899-b93f-80ccef350163	09755a8d-eb1e-4636-a1b5-1e5ca7efea10	7777700607.000000	U_RICARD_02F5C49D	[observability]\n\ncreated changes (with new staff) for logging & otel configs to target GB/HK lab clusters;\nworking on of alert rules for logging to eal with silent failures, etc\nworking on SIEM use cases for tomorrow's PM meeting	{"ts": "7777700607.000000", "text": "[observability]\\n\\ncreated changes (with new staff) for logging & otel configs to target GB/HK lab clusters;\\nworking on of alert rules for logging to eal with silent failures, etc\\nworking on SIEM use cases for tomorrow's PM meeting", "type": "message", "user": "U_RICARD_02F5C49D", "thread_ts": "7777700600.000000"}
541ac244-0bd6-4273-a9a9-a1e2e816d992	70296ee0-af61-4ea8-af53-b0eb59e691bb	7777700700.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[hyper-care] we need a slide on how the hyper-care works at a high level (for us/mx deck). We also need a low-level description of the process in agreement with the customer. @Anne @Carina Almeida @pdelashe I expect this to come from you but do let me know if I am wrong. We need clarification on the following:\n\nhow does the customer engage with us when a migration fails\nwho is available and response time. Is the OS a matter in this decision.\ntroubleshooting environment (we cannot/should not access production) and level of collaboration with the migration team and service owners.. (RACI)	{"ts": "7777700700.000000", "text": "[hyper-care] we need a slide on how the hyper-care works at a high level (for us/mx deck). We also need a low-level description of the process in agreement with the customer. @Anne @Carina Almeida @pdelashe I expect this to come from you but do let me know if I am wrong. We need clarification on the following:\\n\\nhow does the customer engage with us when a migration fails\\nwho is available and response time. Is the OS a matter in this decision.\\ntroubleshooting environment (we cannot/should not access production) and level of collaboration with the migration team and service owners.. (RACI)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
90867f97-96f8-4895-9889-16f05d947cfe	79fea343-0bb2-4e1e-aa93-93701e4deda7	7777700800.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[netapp and storage offload] just a heads up, customer tried to do storage offload with netapp. this of course does not work. netapp has its own tool called shift toolkit. We have communicated the situation,	{"ts": "7777700800.000000", "text": "[netapp and storage offload] just a heads up, customer tried to do storage offload with netapp. this of course does not work. netapp has its own tool called shift toolkit. We have communicated the situation,", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
df421604-f89f-45ce-9cef-165991183e96	e449132b-113e-4ef6-9076-35223f0cb201	7777700900.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[VM triage process] we need to propose a triage process to the back as this is clearly not moving. @Shebi @janine, here is an idea:\n\nwhen a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back and the migrated VM is put in triage.\nusing MTV, VM is moved from a production cluster/namespace to triage cluster/namespace\nuse virtctl guestfs to manipulate the VM OS and\n    a. change the VM IP to something compatible with the triage environment\n    b. enable a local account with root capability\n\nconfirm that the VM can start correct and local account works\n5 delete original migrated VM\n\ntroubleshoot the VM\n7 once the resolution is confirmed, delete the VM\n\nplease mentally verify these steps for both Linux and Windows OSes.\n\n@Rydekull I know you are mostly focused on security, but we could use your input too here. (edited)	{"ts": "7777700900.000000", "text": "[VM triage process] we need to propose a triage process to the back as this is clearly not moving. @Shebi @janine, here is an idea:\\n\\nwhen a VM migration fails, the VM is rolled back and the migrated VM is put in triage.\\nusing MTV, VM is moved from a production cluster/namespace to triage cluster/namespace\\nuse virtctl guestfs to manipulate the VM OS and\\n    a. change the VM IP to something compatible with the triage environment\\n    b. enable a local account with root capability\\n\\nconfirm that the VM can start correct and local account works\\n5 delete original migrated VM\\n\\ntroubleshoot the VM\\n7 once the resolution is confirmed, delete the VM\\n\\nplease mentally verify these steps for both Linux and Windows OSes.\\n\\n@Rydekull I know you are mostly focused on security, but we could use your input too here. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
c5ec7645-b568-4ca8-85f4-42f4975f7557	26c772bd-7146-4349-b6cb-0f4bfdd5e2a7	7777701000.000000	U_JAMES_F3856179	[build - network build issue] something to be aware of... the network folks have made an error in the build out of  everything outside the immediate lab. The tldr is LACP hasn't been configured on the switch side, thus right now we're essentially only leveraging single ports. Michael and Rushi are aware and will sort it out so hopefully all in hand, but just sharing for visibility if the topic comes up.	{"ts": "7777701000.000000", "text": "[build - network build issue] something to be aware of... the network folks have made an error in the build out of  everything outside the immediate lab. The tldr is LACP hasn't been configured on the switch side, thus right now we're essentially only leveraging single ports. Michael and Rushi are aware and will sort it out so hopefully all in hand, but just sharing for visibility if the topic comes up.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JAMES_F3856179"}
1bccfeba-4ee9-431d-ba06-cad10693d102	406c5a3d-2c05-4eb1-9286-686916454ca6	7777701100.000000	U_GOOGLE_35CC3553	[Maj/Carina sync]\n\nTeam I had a sync with Maj this morning and we talked mainly about Ny/Mx trip (only praises to our team here) and status of hadware.\n\n@pdelashe I want to sync with you about how this hardware plan is linked to ACN migration plans.\n@Natasha Ghoojamanian we will need to link this then to staffing planning.\n@rspazzol @Shebi - you don't have any PM support for the NY DC migration approach / testing. I'm wondering whether a PM should be involved in this or not yet? (edited)	{"ts": "7777701100.000000", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\n\\nTeam I had a sync with Maj this morning and we talked mainly about Ny/Mx trip (only praises to our team here) and status of hadware.\\n\\n@pdelashe I want to sync with you about how this hardware plan is linked to ACN migration plans.\\n@Natasha Ghoojamanian we will need to link this then to staffing planning.\\n@rspazzol @Shebi - you don't have any PM support for the NY DC migration approach / testing. I'm wondering whether a PM should be involved in this or not yet? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_35CC3553"}
c8d82602-4968-432e-9cd8-e33cf8a41da5	9a24c4a7-68c1-4629-bffd-b44ccac4fd4c	7777715400.000000	U_THIS_09302691	Greetings team,\n\nI hope you all had a good weekend :sunglasses:\n\n@atolani can you please liaise with our team and ask Prerana or Kuldip help to get you access to console, git etc? - sorry I tried to get Vimal to help with this but had no success	{"ts": "7777715400.000000", "text": "Greetings team,\\n\\nI hope you all had a good weekend :sunglasses:\\n\\n@atolani can you please liaise with our team and ask Prerana or Kuldip help to get you access to console, git etc? - sorry I tried to get Vimal to help with this but had no success", "type": "message", "user": "U_THIS_09302691"}
7bccb81d-793b-4285-aec5-5be573ac7fdb	406c5a3d-2c05-4eb1-9286-686916454ca6	7777701101.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	[Maj/Carina sync]\n\nMexico:\n\nFabric delivery to Enginpresents a significant challenge.\n\n\nIndia:\n\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\n\n\nDMZ (General):\n\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\nThis issue also affects the UK.\n\n\nHong Kong (HK):\n\nReprioritization work is complete.\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\n\n\nUnited States (US):\n\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\nNote: EOS is their second priority.	{"ts": "7777701101.000000", "text": "[Maj/Carina sync]\\n\\nMexico:\\n\\nFabric delivery to Enginpresents a significant challenge.\\n\\n\\nIndia:\\n\\nHandover to ENG anticipated around May 7th.\\n\\n\\nDMZ (General):\\n\\nThe DMZ is a major roadblock, especially for Mexico.\\nA solution for the DMZ could take up to a year.\\nThis issue also affects the UK.\\n\\n\\nHong Kong (HK):\\n\\nReprioritization work is complete.\\nHeading towards the pilot phase around May 10th.\\n\\n\\nUnited States (US):\\n\\nServer rack/stack is a one-month process, so testing should begin around the third week of May.\\nEarliest target for pilot is July.\\nServers would then be converted to Production (Prod), leading to the pilot in July.\\nNote: EOS is their second priority.", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C", "thread_ts": "7777701100.000000"}
