67f36230-2aac-4837-bd3a-50c3bc04eb76	50d7c306-f3f7-401f-8377-c4cd4fa83f34	7777701600.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[cilium cluster mesh] mike presented cilium's way of propagating workload identity to be able to make network policy decision. very cool, I wish we had something like that in OCP. it seems it could have scalability issues if many clusters are part of the mesh or teh workload density is very high.	{"ts": "7777701600.000000", "text": "[cilium cluster mesh] mike presented cilium's way of propagating workload identity to be able to make network policy decision. very cool, I wish we had something like that in OCP. it seems it could have scalability issues if many clusters are part of the mesh or teh workload density is very high.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
7d54c414-e37a-470e-83ec-a8b9c5e41bbe	05bba4d3-2151-4f69-8e49-af5ba53a7fbe	7777701700.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[audit logs to SIEM] the pipeline is proved, thanks @ricardo gregorio. security team now has to verify they understand what they get (@Rydekullassigned to help), provide feedback on whether it is too much or too little, write security breach detection rules. (edited)	{"ts": "7777701700.000000", "text": "[audit logs to SIEM] the pipeline is proved, thanks @ricardo gregorio. security team now has to verify they understand what they get (@Rydekullassigned to help), provide feedback on whether it is too much or too little, write security breach detection rules. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
fe1bc078-0a4d-48bf-ae24-150d313f432d	2c71d014-e2a1-4818-acb2-69c188e7e727	7777701800.000000	U_NICK_CA725671	[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\n\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?	{"ts": "7777701800.000000", "text": "[Proxy RFE] Myself, @Rydekull and @Nikos discussed with OAuth PM and Eng'g about this no_proxy RFE and have had it explained why the best case scenario for this is GA in 5.1. This is due to a couple of key factors:\\n\\n4.22 branch is already closed and 5.0 branch close is late July so earliest is 5.0 for TP then 5.1 for GA.\\nAs this is an API change that is fundamental to O/shift it will a full suite of tests to be developed which is non-trivial task.\\nIt was also mentioned that due to the workload associated with major release 5.0 upcoming ultimate prioritisation is still a bit fluid and this may move to a 5.1 TP with 5.2 GA. PM to keep us updated on that.\\nIt was also stated that this could potentially be backported to 4.2x when it does go GA but that is all dependant upon the engineering work getting done and clearing QE appropriately in due course.\\nPlease keep me honest if I have missed anything @Rydekull or @Nikos?", "type": "message", "user": "U_NICK_CA725671"}
11dd7cb8-0501-46e2-8e49-d4c7181ad113	c353832b-3022-4167-a2f5-426b136c2055	7777701900.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	[Resourcing call with Vinay and Programme team]\n\nTeam,\n\nAnne and I met with Vinay and the Programme Team today. While the objective was to position the new staff, the discussion evolved into a broader conversation regarding team allocation.\n\nWe walked them through our Governance and Work Distribution slides, which have now been shared with them for reference.\n\nA key request from Vinay is that our team maintains an 80% dedication to ENG work. This means ENG tasks take priority over all other activities. In case you have a conflict in priorities, please notify Rose, Patricia, or myself immediately so we can coordinate with ENG for prioritisation. (edited)	{"ts": "7777701900.000000", "text": "[Resourcing call with Vinay and Programme team]\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nAnne and I met with Vinay and the Programme Team today. While the objective was to position the new staff, the discussion evolved into a broader conversation regarding team allocation.\\n\\nWe walked them through our Governance and Work Distribution slides, which have now been shared with them for reference.\\n\\nA key request from Vinay is that our team maintains an 80% dedication to ENG work. This means ENG tasks take priority over all other activities. In case you have a conflict in priorities, please notify Rose, Patricia, or myself immediately so we can coordinate with ENG for prioritisation. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
8867d60b-13e1-45e4-b42b-136333f8398a	8c4c71ae-600b-425f-bc41-bf17e1ed968c	7777702000.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[OS drivers] @atolani @jfeind there is an email thread from Abhishek to which I am being added about issues that we are still having with the OS drivers for windows. This typically means that we are not making progress. Can you summarize the issue and the plan to resolve it. Also anything you need?	{"ts": "7777702000.000000", "text": "[OS drivers] @atolani @jfeind there is an email thread from Abhishek to which I am being added about issues that we are still having with the OS drivers for windows. This typically means that we are not making progress. Can you summarize the issue and the plan to resolve it. Also anything you need?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
b47fc542-f21c-4b1f-8c93-e2b565dec59b	da84b8f5-7088-49fc-815f-187d8989fbaa	7777702100.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[VM Migration]\nSrinath and Abhishek are interested in NUMA aware VMs regarding their high performance applications.\nMain question is how their current NUMA mappings on VMware would be translated to OCP+V.\nI am currently go through the docs and sources regarding the current state of kubeVirt\nhttps://kubevirt.io/user-guide/compute/numa/\netc\nIf anyone of you is deep in the matter, a short exchange would be appreciated.\nOverall I asked that this would be perfect match for a testcase, they agreed and would need to organize such a VM into the current environment for us to migrate. (edited) \nkubevirt.ioNUMA - KubeVirt user guideDocumentation for KubeVirtRaffaele Spazzoli  [10:32 PM]\na bit of good news, today HSBC deployed three more clusters. minor non blocking automation issues reported, they will be addressed.	{"ts": "7777702100.000000", "text": "[VM Migration]\\nSrinath and Abhishek are interested in NUMA aware VMs regarding their high performance applications.\\nMain question is how their current NUMA mappings on VMware would be translated to OCP+V.\\nI am currently go through the docs and sources regarding the current state of kubeVirt\\nhttps://kubevirt.io/user-guide/compute/numa/\\netc\\nIf anyone of you is deep in the matter, a short exchange would be appreciated.\\nOverall I asked that this would be perfect match for a testcase, they agreed and would need to organize such a VM into the current environment for us to migrate. (edited) \\nkubevirt.ioNUMA - KubeVirt user guideDocumentation for KubeVirtRaffaele Spazzoli  [10:32 PM]\\na bit of good news, today HSBC deployed three more clusters. minor non blocking automation issues reported, they will be addressed.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
e2f7f8b9-6584-45f2-b468-701d05feee23	da84b8f5-7088-49fc-815f-187d8989fbaa	7777702101.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[VM Migration]\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\n\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.Added by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerPhilip Jones  [6:18 PM]\n[build]\n\nWe have restored cluster 104 this morning. It's now at least as good as it was before the storage update :wink:\nCluster 102 pure storage update now successfully completed after we ran a cleanup script to remove stale entries in the pure storage cluster kvdb. \nTake away from this is that the storage cluster had a lot of volume snapshots it thought it was managing that didn't actually exist on the flasharray. This was likely triggered by stress testing back in Feb.\nWe still see a LOT of volume snapshots associated with non-existent, previously deleted pvc's. These are for the most case the same stale volumes the script removed from kvdb. We will need to create our own script to remove them and complete the cleanup.\n\nIssues impacting hkoclu307 and the three nodes that refused to register now tracked to a Cisco switch issue. A ticket is being raised with Cisco to debug. \nIsovalent call postponed for today.	{"ts": "7777702101.000000", "text": "[VM Migration]\\n@Shebi Today I was following up the issue with Windows Failover Clusters not being able to start after migration.\\nI see it as a multi-layered issue. First one is that the VMs do not migrate their IPs, thats due the fact that they are powered off before migration, which is currently a dependency of MTV for VMs with shared disks, before it gives green light for the Migration Plan to run.\\nI reflected this issue with Martin Necas and created a bug\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5235\\nA Solution/Workaround  is to be provided by us, until then those VMs have to be excluded from the upcoming Migrations. I will draft a statement on this for Narender tomorrow and will share it here for feedback.\\n\\nI also supported Sudhir and Nitesh on\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04432578\\nand the VMware Tools cleanup topic (see Sam's thread), both are rolling atm. (edited) \\n:jira: MTV-5235 [New] : VMs with shared disks do not transfer static IPs as they must be powered off to migrate.Added by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerPhilip Jones  [6:18 PM]\\n[build]\\n\\nWe have restored cluster 104 this morning. It's now at least as good as it was before the storage update :wink:\\nCluster 102 pure storage update now successfully completed after we ran a cleanup script to remove stale entries in the pure storage cluster kvdb. \\nTake away from this is that the storage cluster had a lot of volume snapshots it thought it was managing that didn't actually exist on the flasharray. This was likely triggered by stress testing back in Feb.\\nWe still see a LOT of volume snapshots associated with non-existent, previously deleted pvc's. These are for the most case the same stale volumes the script removed from kvdb. We will need to create our own script to remove them and complete the cleanup.\\n\\nIssues impacting hkoclu307 and the three nodes that refused to register now tracked to a Cisco switch issue. A ticket is being raised with Cisco to debug. \\nIsovalent call postponed for today.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8", "thread_ts": "7777702100.000000"}
a39bff7c-5e1b-45e1-9a39-712fb84d578d	195b1177-70c5-4953-8fef-bb6ae753c247	7777702800.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[any to any storage offload migrations] any to any means between different storage vendors. This should work, but it seems not to. I have involved Roy from engineering but he has be slow to answer as he was on PTO. Customer is attempting migration from HPE to Dell. There is a certain urgency on this and I am about to go on PTO. @janine can you pick this up? Let's sync on this today before I disappear.	{"ts": "7777702800.000000", "text": "[any to any storage offload migrations] any to any means between different storage vendors. This should work, but it seems not to. I have involved Roy from engineering but he has be slow to answer as he was on PTO. Customer is attempting migration from HPE to Dell. There is a certain urgency on this and I am about to go on PTO. @janine can you pick this up? Let's sync on this today before I disappear.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
9df49299-eff1-4fbb-a8f9-6953b55497c0	d1c8dedd-5467-4096-8064-05957d352634	7777721400.000000	U_SUNNY_0D526D2F	Hello Everyone...Excited to be part of the Team!!	{"ts": "7777721400.000000", "text": "Hello Everyone...Excited to be part of the Team!!", "type": "message", "user": "U_SUNNY_0D526D2F"}
0482551c-4d8c-46da-85f5-93331e82e28f	215173c3-3fba-4973-93d5-3eedecbd5d93	7777702200.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[Bulk Migrations] :books:\nAlso from me a bit of good news.\nFirst iteration of bulk migrations was done.\nBefore I share some numbers, I share one issue: from the 200 VMs they promised we have just around 60 available now, because 128 have been deleted due to some internal compliance issue on how those VMs have been deployed internally. Bit of a nuisance, I got promised they will bring them back asap, I hope so, until then we have to work with what we got.\nThe Bulk Migration itself is run over MIO-X to get it as real as possible.\nTest Case No 1 was done as cold and direct migration (storage offloading is currently not available as a feature in MIO-X, due it can not make sure that both source and target storage maps are the same and storage offload activated. I had a conversation with the team and Abhishek is now taken care of this to be implemented.)\n\nSo, now some numbers:\n\n61 VMs Migrated with 1 VM per Migrationplan :arrow_forward:\n59 VMs with disksize of 100-150 GB, mix of Linux and Windows OS\n- 52 VMs migrated successfully within a total timeframe of 43 (earliest) to 120 min (latest). :white_check_mark:\n- 7 VMs failed through a freak configuration on VMware which said: 2 sockets and 1 cpu, this translates into 0.5 sockets, while the manifest actually expects an integer >=1 for the sockets value. :x:\nThis has been identified and fixed, also Srinath mentioned this happend when the testing VMs have been created and should not re-occur within the production VMs. :check:\n- 2 running into a MIO-X timeout (currently set to approx 3 hours) but those had 1,5 TB disk which took 5 hours and finished successfully :white_check_mark:\n\nI will share in the Red Hat Teams channel the official Confluence page on this bulk migration test.\nA lot more to come, especially looking forward to have 200 VMs with storage offload and various migration plan sizings. Good thing is that VM Migration and Testops Team works now together really well. We plan to have a bulk migration status call now two times a week.\n\nObservability while we migrate is in the making by Srinath and will hopefully be gathered on the next iteration. (edited)	{"ts": "7777702200.000000", "text": "[Bulk Migrations] :books:\\nAlso from me a bit of good news.\\nFirst iteration of bulk migrations was done.\\nBefore I share some numbers, I share one issue: from the 200 VMs they promised we have just around 60 available now, because 128 have been deleted due to some internal compliance issue on how those VMs have been deployed internally. Bit of a nuisance, I got promised they will bring them back asap, I hope so, until then we have to work with what we got.\\nThe Bulk Migration itself is run over MIO-X to get it as real as possible.\\nTest Case No 1 was done as cold and direct migration (storage offloading is currently not available as a feature in MIO-X, due it can not make sure that both source and target storage maps are the same and storage offload activated. I had a conversation with the team and Abhishek is now taken care of this to be implemented.)\\n\\nSo, now some numbers:\\n\\n61 VMs Migrated with 1 VM per Migrationplan :arrow_forward:\\n59 VMs with disksize of 100-150 GB, mix of Linux and Windows OS\\n- 52 VMs migrated successfully within a total timeframe of 43 (earliest) to 120 min (latest). :white_check_mark:\\n- 7 VMs failed through a freak configuration on VMware which said: 2 sockets and 1 cpu, this translates into 0.5 sockets, while the manifest actually expects an integer >=1 for the sockets value. :x:\\nThis has been identified and fixed, also Srinath mentioned this happend when the testing VMs have been created and should not re-occur within the production VMs. :check:\\n- 2 running into a MIO-X timeout (currently set to approx 3 hours) but those had 1,5 TB disk which took 5 hours and finished successfully :white_check_mark:\\n\\nI will share in the Red Hat Teams channel the official Confluence page on this bulk migration test.\\nA lot more to come, especially looking forward to have 200 VMs with storage offload and various migration plan sizings. Good thing is that VM Migration and Testops Team works now together really well. We plan to have a bulk migration status call now two times a week.\\n\\nObservability while we migrate is in the making by Srinath and will hopefully be gathered on the next iteration. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
4b142233-ce19-48a8-925d-5ad2086f3888	bc7ac5c9-2d47-4244-ad91-9d114134f9bb	7777702300.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Migration Support and Hypercare Thread]\nI am opening this thread to keep all ideas together as I need to send our proposal by end of this week. Bear in mind that we can't invent a new process and need to adapt to what they have already defined (remember this is a Bank and they follow ITIL proceses), and their SLAs: While migrating a VM there are only 15minutes limit to decide to roll back, so all the ideas you are proposing IMO should be in a separate section of RCA . I'm putting everything together here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vYMFbZpGRjLOltrKqecQh06cpCp-8tkKLprEdCQwUAo/edit?tab=t.1q40s08up9xd#heading=h.wd3rd5djgvwy	{"ts": "7777702300.000000", "text": "[Migration Support and Hypercare Thread]\\nI am opening this thread to keep all ideas together as I need to send our proposal by end of this week. Bear in mind that we can't invent a new process and need to adapt to what they have already defined (remember this is a Bank and they follow ITIL proceses), and their SLAs: While migrating a VM there are only 15minutes limit to decide to roll back, so all the ideas you are proposing IMO should be in a separate section of RCA . I'm putting everything together here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vYMFbZpGRjLOltrKqecQh06cpCp-8tkKLprEdCQwUAo/edit?tab=t.1q40s08up9xd#heading=h.wd3rd5djgvwy", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
fb192168-b660-4f1e-81b9-15397938f2be	7029f740-3d03-4587-a954-a40d0b77373d	7777702400.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[US DC migration] we learned that there is a program level DC migration and we need to sync with them to understand what the process is. The VM migration tool/automation with need to be harmonized with that process. likely they will take care of the network devices (DNS, Loadbalacer, firewall) configuration at the program level, but teh modalities are unknown at this point. Next week there will be a meeting with the DC migration program team to get some insight. @Shebi will follow this part and create a proposal on how the VM migration process will integrate with the larger DC migration process.	{"ts": "7777702400.000000", "text": "[US DC migration] we learned that there is a program level DC migration and we need to sync with them to understand what the process is. The VM migration tool/automation with need to be harmonized with that process. likely they will take care of the network devices (DNS, Loadbalacer, firewall) configuration at the program level, but teh modalities are unknown at this point. Next week there will be a meeting with the DC migration program team to get some insight. @Shebi will follow this part and create a proposal on how the VM migration process will integrate with the larger DC migration process.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
495acd34-fd65-482d-990b-7e43d3414434	6598f042-3ad9-4a7c-a225-6d9b13769770	7777702500.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[bsod] MTV 2.11.4-2 seems to solve most of teh bsod-related problems that other customers have been experiencing by installing the latest VirtIO-Win 1.9.57 drivers. It would be grate if we could upgrade top this version. @Philip Jones	{"ts": "7777702500.000000", "text": "[bsod] MTV 2.11.4-2 seems to solve most of teh bsod-related problems that other customers have been experiencing by installing the latest VirtIO-Win 1.9.57 drivers. It would be grate if we could upgrade top this version. @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
