d19a9034-8e26-457d-b32b-782f6724c7d6	9bb838ae-cfb5-4fcf-b3b3-671d27c2e745	7777702700.000000	U_PLEASE_802C7AFD	[TSR - Review]\nThe first draft of the TSR is available (we still need to update amother must-gather) but I've seen that it complains because of certificates expiration date. Can anyone review if this is correct? Or a false positive?image.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [11:39 AM]\n[Migration Pilot2 update]\nUpdated the "on call" team for the 1st week to include Janine&Alex as Shebi will be in us/MX\nStart date has been pushed to May 5th (as there is a quite period that finishes on May 4th)\nLooks like some of the VMs with RDM disks are sitting on HP storage that does not support storage offload, so they will be moved to either Pure or Dell before migrating, which will imply > 10m down time\nThey are thinking to create a new Change Request Category to accelerate the ITSO response time (I think they are using Patching now, which doesn't sound much urgent)Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [12:11 PM]\n[RCA Meeting]\nTo schedule the meeting to discuss our RCA proposal, what is your availability Architects? And Raffa proposed to include Narender, Natty and John Davis. Anyone else?Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:18 PM]\n[dell scalability testing] dell tests cordon and drain with an average of 10 VM and 2 disks per node. this means 20 volumes per node. This test is not realistic, we have asked to rerun the test with 120 volumes per node, which is what the bank expects.	{"ts": "7777702700.000000", "text": "[TSR - Review]\\nThe first draft of the TSR is available (we still need to update amother must-gather) but I've seen that it complains because of certificates expiration date. Can anyone review if this is correct? Or a false positive?image.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [11:39 AM]\\n[Migration Pilot2 update]\\nUpdated the \\"on call\\" team for the 1st week to include Janine&Alex as Shebi will be in us/MX\\nStart date has been pushed to May 5th (as there is a quite period that finishes on May 4th)\\nLooks like some of the VMs with RDM disks are sitting on HP storage that does not support storage offload, so they will be moved to either Pure or Dell before migrating, which will imply > 10m down time\\nThey are thinking to create a new Change Request Category to accelerate the ITSO response time (I think they are using Patching now, which doesn't sound much urgent)Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [12:11 PM]\\n[RCA Meeting]\\nTo schedule the meeting to discuss our RCA proposal, what is your availability Architects? And Raffa proposed to include Narender, Natty and John Davis. Anyone else?Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:18 PM]\\n[dell scalability testing] dell tests cordon and drain with an average of 10 VM and 2 disks per node. this means 20 volumes per node. This test is not realistic, we have asked to rerun the test with 120 volumes per node, which is what the bank expects.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PLEASE_802C7AFD"}
