ff731817-7fdd-441e-94af-f25fc9ac3a51	1112e06b-a51e-4818-b7a7-87d344e75f74	7777703800.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	[OTEL vs OCP out of the box demo today]\n\nTeam, Ravi booked a OTEL vs OCP demo for today at 10.30 am BST - Objective attached.\nHe invited Raffa who's out, is there anyone available, who can demo the RH side of things? or should I ask to postpone this?\n\n@ricardo gregorio were you aware of this?\n@Rydekull @janine @Shebi do you have time and the skills to help with this?\n@Nikos would we have an SSP by change who could support this kind of demo in future?\n\nThanks (edited) \nimage.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [10:20 AM]\n[Migration update]\nPilot Phase 2:\nVMs in scope 212; from 230 in initial scope, some dropped because they’re in the demise path, inventory errors and descoped: 23 ITSOs haven’t responded yet.\nPlan:\nMay 5th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 46 VMs\nMay 5th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 47 VMs\nMay 6th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 49 VMs\nMay 6th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 42 VMs\nMay 7th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 28 VMs\n\nUK Pilot:\nNo delays on the UK Pilot plan; new clusters to be built on track\nPlan:\nMay 13th -> June 15th - Dev & UAT & OAT\nJune 17 -> End of July - Contingency and Prod - Weekdays & WeekendsAlexander Rydekull  [10:50 AM]\n[Wildcard certificates] Oh, right, so there's a meeting in 40 minutes on the topic of Wildcard certs, and it seems like Engineering is making up excuses from wht I can gather. They seem to claim that they cannot rotate wildcard/api certs without affecting VMs running on the platform.	{"ts": "7777703800.000000", "text": "[OTEL vs OCP out of the box demo today]\\n\\nTeam, Ravi booked a OTEL vs OCP demo for today at 10.30 am BST - Objective attached.\\nHe invited Raffa who's out, is there anyone available, who can demo the RH side of things? or should I ask to postpone this?\\n\\n@ricardo gregorio were you aware of this?\\n@Rydekull @janine @Shebi do you have time and the skills to help with this?\\n@Nikos would we have an SSP by change who could support this kind of demo in future?\\n\\nThanks (edited) \\nimage.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [10:20 AM]\\n[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\nVMs in scope 212; from 230 in initial scope, some dropped because they’re in the demise path, inventory errors and descoped: 23 ITSOs haven’t responded yet.\\nPlan:\\nMay 5th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 46 VMs\\nMay 5th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 47 VMs\\nMay 6th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 49 VMs\\nMay 6th from 13:00 -> 16:00 - 42 VMs\\nMay 7th from 10:00 -> 13:00 - 28 VMs\\n\\nUK Pilot:\\nNo delays on the UK Pilot plan; new clusters to be built on track\\nPlan:\\nMay 13th -> June 15th - Dev & UAT & OAT\\nJune 17 -> End of July - Contingency and Prod - Weekdays & WeekendsAlexander Rydekull  [10:50 AM]\\n[Wildcard certificates] Oh, right, so there's a meeting in 40 minutes on the topic of Wildcard certs, and it seems like Engineering is making up excuses from wht I can gather. They seem to claim that they cannot rotate wildcard/api certs without affecting VMs running on the platform.", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
