4ac7e202-eccd-47c0-ab7e-ec34f133e799	e51d43cf-8e3f-436a-92c4-dee16242fa85	7777704100.000000	U_JANINE_71F80BBD	[Storage Offloading] RH Engineering provided infos on how to configure storage offloading from Dell --> Pure. will be tested once 104 is back to healthy. this is not a migration pattern that's included in the upcoming pilot phase 2	{"ts": "7777704100.000000", "text": "[Storage Offloading] RH Engineering provided infos on how to configure storage offloading from Dell --> Pure. will be tested once 104 is back to healthy. this is not a migration pattern that's included in the upcoming pilot phase 2", "type": "message", "user": "U_JANINE_71F80BBD"}
8f87cc25-18b0-41a4-9a38-34e21c5fb3d2	9d12aae5-9b79-431d-8ec4-090fda323911	7777704200.000000	U_PHILIP_740C6823	[Build update]\n\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it. \nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\n(edited)	{"ts": "7777704200.000000", "text": "[Build update]\\n\\nProvided some suggestions to Kuldeep to automate the silencing of alerts when building new clusters.\\nSupporting Vinayak with some questions around exporting the compliance reports and how to convert the xml to csv format.\\nWork is continuing with network support to identify the cause of issues for three cluster nodes being unable to join 307 cluster.\\nOngoing issues primarily with cluster 104. Pure has provided two scripts, one to cleanup 102, the second to try and re-map volumes on 104. We can test the former tomorrow and will need it to complete successfully before we sync the new operator version again. The latter was developed entirely with iSCSI connections in mind, whilst 104 is using FC. Pure are going to rework the script for tomorrow and we hope to restore the cluster to normal. Huge thanks and kudos to James as well for his work on scripting an alternative solution should we need it. \\nIsovalent phase 2 poc is now getting underway. The plan is to target 4.20 rather than 4.21 or 22. The customer has indicated they may jump to 4.22 and skip 4.21. It'll be a while before all operators etc required will be available for 4.22 so it makes sense to stick with 4.20.\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}
2805253e-1c06-4ec5-a67f-132f78b47ce8	9d12aae5-9b79-431d-8ec4-090fda323911	7777704201.000000	U_PHILIP_740C6823	[Build Update]:\n\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel. \n421 channel work is underway as well.\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully. \nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\n\n(edited)	{"ts": "7777704201.000000", "text": "[Build Update]:\\n\\nPrep completed for Operator upgrades to clusters managed by original git repo. This has revealed a few items of signaficance in the release notes. I've detailed these via Teams in the build channel. \\n421 channel work is underway as well.\\nHK entra change and proxy change was applied today. 3/5 managed clusters are now down completely. We can't even ping the nodes, though drac shows the interfaces as up and the nodes are booting successfully. \\nThe proxy config applied to 302 (which works) and 307 (which is offline) appears the same!\\nIt's almost like a firewall has been switched on, or a switch has failed...\\nWe did see switch problems were the cause behind three nodes not joining 307 previously, so it's possible something has broken... Maybe a default route?\\nUPDATE: It's suggested the problems relate to a mis-communicated LACP change the network team are completing tomorrow.\\n\\n(edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823", "thread_ts": "7777704200.000000"}
4c876294-5111-4208-a95d-c21aa402e185	f4f8e853-ee74-4557-b70f-c2f0ca6bbd0a	7777704300.000000	U_SEBAST_AC383055	[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessibleThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)	{"ts": "7777704300.000000", "text": "[More issues on Prod cluster due to the LACP change]:\\n2 clusters -- 311, 312 --- worker node all crashed /down - Web Console and API are accessible\\n1 cluster -- 314 -- all worker nodes crashed /down - Web Console and api not accessibleThe team is just rebooting the nodes as per the support recommendation from the issue we had yesterday. (I don’t like to reboot, because you won’t see what actually caused the issue, but I guess the important thing here is to bring the service back up)", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}
c5411334-418b-450b-b085-ded02c333d71	8fc01cfd-3cb3-4203-8893-1716391c67d7	7777704400.000000	U_SEBAST_AC383055	[Sheffield - HIC Design Workshops notes]: Please all the notes here, include screenshots or whatever you want and later we can add structure, is better to have excess in this case: https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/edit?tab=t.0	{"ts": "7777704400.000000", "text": "[Sheffield - HIC Design Workshops notes]: Please all the notes here, include screenshots or whatever you want and later we can add structure, is better to have excess in this case: https://docs.google.com/document/d/13HYEJrLKXtP-FxkLz7WPSa_oUCMWYXODyGEZj4juuNI/edit?tab=t.0", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}
b03657b7-6019-44d8-8ee7-b1cd2e852897	d8c7d8c5-2a85-40bf-9eec-f4aeedafc3a0	7777704500.000000	U_GOOGLE_2764FAE5	[RFE-7054 - Auth Proxy] - I had a call two people in engineering about the auth proxy last night. I explained to them that we have a workaround at the moment but at some point, we might need to configure a different proxy and the cluster wide proxy doesn't work for us anymore. The proposed solution is to add a new property to the oauth object. THey're not sure if they will be able to backport it to 4.22 but they were confident on a backport to 4.23. @Shebi @Rydekull @James Force @rspazzol @Philip Jones	{"ts": "7777704500.000000", "text": "[RFE-7054 - Auth Proxy] - I had a call two people in engineering about the auth proxy last night. I explained to them that we have a workaround at the moment but at some point, we might need to configure a different proxy and the cluster wide proxy doesn't work for us anymore. The proposed solution is to add a new property to the oauth object. THey're not sure if they will be able to backport it to 4.22 but they were confident on a backport to 4.23. @Shebi @Rydekull @James Force @rspazzol @Philip Jones", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_2764FAE5"}
55b63b89-318d-4524-9566-b957b6e9b87d	b6e1ed5c-f217-46f5-9955-9717fa7e4125	7777704600.000000	U_SAM_F28235E5	[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\n\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\n\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\n\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\n\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\n\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.	{"ts": "7777704600.000000", "text": "[Vinay/Brian Call] I had a 15 minute call with Vinay yesterday focussed on the DLL issue. As an aside he's not been well this week and was out a chunk on Monday.\\n\\nHe said they've upgraded the library that was causing the issue and they've now successfully migrated the machine. They've done a readacross their estate and believe that this issue affects over 5K windows machines.\\n\\nHe also raised frustration on VMWare tooling not being properly removed from Windows machines. I know this has come up a few times here. What's our current view on the situation and remediation we're putting in place? Is there something that MTV or other teams are working on to improve the success rate?\\n\\nI've been added to the weekly Thursday case review to help move things along.\\n\\nThey both asked if there's a way for Red Hat to bring issues we're seeing elsewhere more proactively to the customer so they can catch them before they become a problem and put in proactive remediations. I pinged @Ed Keen about it last night but didn't get a resposne.\\n\\nAt the end I asked how their confidence was on the program. They both said they had high confidence on the technology working and the risk remained in the process side. He called out specific areas of focus being the coordination of change and deciding if something needs a service migration vs VM migration.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}
4fae9f3e-43ba-47d4-9b17-5272ed71cc11	8fdea01e-2e24-4270-9276-500e42b9e45c	7777704700.000000	U_SAM_F28235E5	[Windows restarts] Vinay mentioned they've noticed Windows VMs restarting up to 20 times as part of the migration. Any context on this? Is it expected behavior? Is there something that can be done to improve the situation?	{"ts": "7777704700.000000", "text": "[Windows restarts] Vinay mentioned they've noticed Windows VMs restarting up to 20 times as part of the migration. Any context on this? Is it expected behavior? Is there something that can be done to improve the situation?", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}
d1732ceb-3e60-4bd2-b707-54390259eea3	be96b70d-c128-4676-901e-3963c0a9eb32	7777704800.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Migration update]\nPilot Phase 2:\n\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\n\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th	{"ts": "7777704800.000000", "text": "[Migration update]\\nPilot Phase 2:\\n\\nNetwork outage affected all OCP clusters, including those that are part of Pilot Phase 2.\\nNetwork changes are going to be reapplied during the weekend, expected 30hr of downtime\\nThis affects the Cluster Readiness and puts the target date of May 5th at risk\\n\\nVMX changes in VMware Clusters have not been applied yet\\nSome issues in Miox are also preventing to create the migration plans and start running the pre-checks at T-2\\nThere is also a “Reptational Risk” with ITSOs as the plan was to “impose” the change window for Pilot & Scale migrations, and we may not be able to comply with the migration dates -> >Meeting later today to agree on how ITSO comms should be handled to prevent this\\nWe still maintain next week as Migration week, but the start date may be pushed to May 6th", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
