6b0db2b2-3249-43b4-acd4-a87fc537e74b	e420c85e-c022-4389-8449-37efe77b7ec6	7777706100.000000	U_IMAGE_3227E706	[RBAC (Manifest & VNC Access)] @Shebi in Build status call toady Praveen asked for an update on the proposed solution that you committed to outline. Has this been sent & he missed it? It's around secret management and password rotation on local accounts using Hashi Vault. I've asked @janine if she can take this over from you as you will be away from desk for most of this week.	{"ts": "7777706100.000000", "text": "[RBAC (Manifest & VNC Access)] @Shebi in Build status call toady Praveen asked for an update on the proposed solution that you committed to outline. Has this been sent & he missed it? It's around secret management and password rotation on local accounts using Hashi Vault. I've asked @janine if she can take this over from you as you will be away from desk for most of this week.", "type": "message", "user": "U_IMAGE_3227E706"}
04d76678-3643-4a30-b33f-3fb8874fe7a3	3cbe94c8-8127-42ad-895b-c5392b00e638	7777706200.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[Performance]\n@Shebi @Rydekull\nToday I got a preview on a document to be shared with us, which shows performance differences on a VM migrated to 104. It is a Oracle DB on RHEL 9 and there are quit some drops on Cluster 104 vs the Vsphere.\nThe VMs in question are gbl25239315 and gbl25239316.	{"ts": "7777706200.000000", "text": "[Performance]\\n@Shebi @Rydekull\\nToday I got a preview on a document to be shared with us, which shows performance differences on a VM migrated to 104. It is a Oracle DB on RHEL 9 and there are quit some drops on Cluster 104 vs the Vsphere.\\nThe VMs in question are gbl25239315 and gbl25239316.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
f98768d7-97d7-49d5-a597-bc87b8cd23f6	9639d4c1-76bd-49a9-b3aa-765747f8e8f7	7777706300.000000	U_SUDHIR_58B5FB81	[Build of OpenShift Clusters] @James Force @Philip Jones @rspazzol @janine Question, when we deploy the clusters today, we dont add a ssh-key to the core user, do we? It seems commented out in the git files.	{"ts": "7777706300.000000", "text": "[Build of OpenShift Clusters] @James Force @Philip Jones @rspazzol @janine Question, when we deploy the clusters today, we dont add a ssh-key to the core user, do we? It seems commented out in the git files.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SUDHIR_58B5FB81"}
1285cd06-4b46-4035-953e-7937c1b8f9b1	587e8d0d-d5e1-4e8d-9cc0-e6fd02d76471	7777706400.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[HK and re-ip] Vinay yesterday casually dropped that some VMs in HK will need Re-iping. We are learning how hard it is to re-ip here in NY. couple of things that came out yesterday that we didn't think about: OS-mounted NAS, VPNs, proxies. they are all also affected by the VM's IP change. (edited)	{"ts": "7777706400.000000", "text": "[HK and re-ip] Vinay yesterday casually dropped that some VMs in HK will need Re-iping. We are learning how hard it is to re-ip here in NY. couple of things that came out yesterday that we didn't think about: OS-mounted NAS, VPNs, proxies. they are all also affected by the VM's IP change. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
01723342-02c2-4e99-8b0f-1380ce0714b6	547a2d95-c37a-4f21-b711-33bf6fca1193	7777706600.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\n\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\n\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)	{"ts": "7777706600.000000", "text": "[NY meetings] yesterday the meetings were mostly with technical people around the re-ip problem. After several hours of conversations I don't feel much more reassured. We were able to surface several problems that will need to be solved, hopefully we surfaced most of them. But the lack of automation and the lack of commitment from the local teams is still an issue. In general service owners will be given this choices:\\n\\nre-provision in VMWare, if they are willing to start now.\\nre-provision in openshift, soon a date will be set after which no more provisioning in VMWare will be possible.\\nmigrate. the preferred migration approach will be from VMWare to OCP using storage offload over the network. Other possibilities will also be considered.\\nWhen it comes to the re-iping strategy, the discovery of the impact of re-iping will be two fold:\\n\\nquestionnaires to the service owners to discover dependencies.\\nqueries (called scrubs) to firewalls and LB.\\nAside for those we also found out that we need to consider NAS configurations, VPNs and proxy configurations....\\nWhen it comes to how the new configurations will be done and who is responsible for doing them, there is a lack of clarity and accountability.\\nSome people expects that the service owners will submit servicenow requests. Vinay wants automation. We are with Vinay of course, however it looks like automation will be available only for DNS and @Philip Jones knows hows that project was hard to concretize and I am not sure it will come to fruition by when its needed. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
