e5ff778d-3457-4a16-bcb5-38634b6c7f86	196c562f-bbcf-4c3c-a4af-bfba37710e32	7777708200.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Qemu Issue URGENT]\nWe need to help support troubleshoot what is happening with the QEMU installation, so we need to a) identify in which Windos OS it works and it doesn.'t -> to see it it is related to OS version b) If it is not OS related, try to figure out similarities that may be causig the errorRosemary Lynch  [10:05 AM]\n[Time Card entry] Happy Monday team, can you log your RH time cards urgently for last week please? I need to send out the burndown report by noon. Please have your time cards in before 11am GMT. If you have not yet logged your Bank Clarity time sheets please do so at the same time. Those missing: @jfeind  @Rydekull @Anne @Carina Almeida @James Force  @ricardo gregorio @Shebi	{"ts": "7777708200.000000", "text": "[Qemu Issue URGENT]\\nWe need to help support troubleshoot what is happening with the QEMU installation, so we need to a) identify in which Windos OS it works and it doesn.'t -> to see it it is related to OS version b) If it is not OS related, try to figure out similarities that may be causig the errorRosemary Lynch  [10:05 AM]\\n[Time Card entry] Happy Monday team, can you log your RH time cards urgently for last week please? I need to send out the burndown report by noon. Please have your time cards in before 11am GMT. If you have not yet logged your Bank Clarity time sheets please do so at the same time. Those missing: @jfeind  @Rydekull @Anne @Carina Almeida @James Force  @ricardo gregorio @Shebi", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
494d1f1a-2efe-4633-b2e1-3eb7488c7e6b	5a304454-4c79-4815-88a7-51a9f639ce24	7777707901.000000	U_TC_ACAFE313	[Time Reporting]\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Philip Jones  [11:19 AM]\nHas Red Hat ever considered providing Quay as a SaaS offering? This could be cloud hosted and customers could have their own private VPN or direct connect option to reach it.\n\nIt could provide the a full mirror of content for OCP, Operators, etc etc. Customers could have some limited admin capabilities to sync specific additional images, setup their preferred image scanner etc...\n\nThat way, they have a performant, reliable solution with all the content available immediately. Something like this might work for many customers who don't want to use a public registry and prefer to have their own image scanning etc in place.	{"ts": "7777707901.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Philip Jones  [11:19 AM]\\nHas Red Hat ever considered providing Quay as a SaaS offering? This could be cloud hosted and customers could have their own private VPN or direct connect option to reach it.\\n\\nIt could provide the a full mirror of content for OCP, Operators, etc etc. Customers could have some limited admin capabilities to sync specific additional images, setup their preferred image scanner etc...\\n\\nThat way, they have a performant, reliable solution with all the content available immediately. Something like this might work for many customers who don't want to use a public registry and prefer to have their own image scanning etc in place.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TC_ACAFE313", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}
