4c30e9a3-32aa-46d3-8188-c6d6fde19172	5a304454-4c79-4815-88a7-51a9f639ce24	7777707903.000000	U_PATRIC_460B8EAB	[Time Reporting]\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:08 PM]\n@pdelashe I'm available for the next 3 hours if you need some coverage in the was room. I assume many other have taken recharge day	{"ts": "7777707903.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nDont forget to enter your Timecards in Consulting Cloud and your hours in Clarity before noon!Raffaele Spazzoli  [12:08 PM]\\n@pdelashe I'm available for the next 3 hours if you need some coverage in the was room. I assume many other have taken recharge day", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_460B8EAB", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}
43f2ce40-6a5b-4634-bd60-0d1fc5e830ca	5a304454-4c79-4815-88a7-51a9f639ce24	7777707904.000000	U_TIME_3519BFBB	[Time Reporting]\nIf you have not done so already please log your time sheets in Clarity (was due Friday) and your Red Hat time card in PSA please before 11am.Raffaele Spazzoli  [9:35 AM]\n[platform tasks] I have been catching up with Rushi. There are several platform tasks pending. not sure if they have made progress recently. These tasks are being managed by @Rosemary Lynch so perhaps @Rosemary Lynch we should have a stand up dedicated just to these tasks. I'll add here the discussion I had with Rushi on them.\n\nEntra and service accounts -- @Shebi -- a final explanation/diagram is missing. In particular something tat shows that a user with certain entitlement can only get the sa token of the cluster they are entitled to.\nCIS compliance -- not sure who is assigned to this -- hsbc is not apply because the OCP CIS v1.9.0 and the OCP-V CIS v.1.0.0 have been released but the compliance operator is not capable of reporting on teh new checks. HSBC does not want to go the custom checks route. So I believe the only option is to open an RFE to the compliance operator team to get those checks updated. There is also apparently a discrepancy between in the TLS check between what the operator expects and what the suggested configuration does.\nuse case write up  for remote workers -- @rspazzol \nVNC access via SA. Additional checks must be added when using this approach. We have to checks that the user has entitlements on that VM and that there is a change request open. @rspazzol to talk with Shwetali and design this.\nGitops workflow documentation -- @Philip Jones -- the workflow that hsbc wants to use on the gitops repo is still not fully fleshed out. @Philip Jones I'd like to get a status o what you have done so far. I'll also talk to Shwetali and Prerana to understand what use cases they want to support.\nLab cluster instabilities -- @Philip Jones -- I assume this is a continuous learning task. we need a status update.\n\n\nthere were more open items, but Rushi was not worried about them. (edited)	{"ts": "7777707904.000000", "text": "[Time Reporting]\\nIf you have not done so already please log your time sheets in Clarity (was due Friday) and your Red Hat time card in PSA please before 11am.Raffaele Spazzoli  [9:35 AM]\\n[platform tasks] I have been catching up with Rushi. There are several platform tasks pending. not sure if they have made progress recently. These tasks are being managed by @Rosemary Lynch so perhaps @Rosemary Lynch we should have a stand up dedicated just to these tasks. I'll add here the discussion I had with Rushi on them.\\n\\nEntra and service accounts -- @Shebi -- a final explanation/diagram is missing. In particular something tat shows that a user with certain entitlement can only get the sa token of the cluster they are entitled to.\\nCIS compliance -- not sure who is assigned to this -- hsbc is not apply because the OCP CIS v1.9.0 and the OCP-V CIS v.1.0.0 have been released but the compliance operator is not capable of reporting on teh new checks. HSBC does not want to go the custom checks route. So I believe the only option is to open an RFE to the compliance operator team to get those checks updated. There is also apparently a discrepancy between in the TLS check between what the operator expects and what the suggested configuration does.\\nuse case write up  for remote workers -- @rspazzol \\nVNC access via SA. Additional checks must be added when using this approach. We have to checks that the user has entitlements on that VM and that there is a change request open. @rspazzol to talk with Shwetali and design this.\\nGitops workflow documentation -- @Philip Jones -- the workflow that hsbc wants to use on the gitops repo is still not fully fleshed out. @Philip Jones I'd like to get a status o what you have done so far. I'll also talk to Shwetali and Prerana to understand what use cases they want to support.\\nLab cluster instabilities -- @Philip Jones -- I assume this is a continuous learning task. we need a status update.\\n\\n\\nthere were more open items, but Rushi was not worried about them. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_TIME_3519BFBB", "thread_ts": "7777707900.000000"}
c46f0699-0bfa-476d-864c-324ddf1787ed	ddffd8c9-386b-4489-98df-82d894338472	7777708000.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[Update 104 to 4.21]\n@Philip Jones technically speaking, would we be ready to roll 104 to 4.21 soon? (SCSI3-PR, shared disk topic), I saw you gave updates on Operators regarding 4.21 in the build channel, thanks for that.\n@rspazzol you had a brief sync with Rushikesh on this, that and why we need it?\nHe is not replying on the Build Team Channel, it is a bit annoying, at some point I would expect green light from him, or not.\nIn context: There is ongoing demand mounting up to proceed with the Windows Failover Cluster VM shared disk issues.\nI have been asked to write an Email to Vinay and Narender by today on what our proposed next step is, I guess Sudhir is getting tons of pressure...\nI want to support him and if we tell them we update 104 to 4.21 soon to continue debug this, we have a positive spin here. (edited)	{"ts": "7777708000.000000", "text": "[Update 104 to 4.21]\\n@Philip Jones technically speaking, would we be ready to roll 104 to 4.21 soon? (SCSI3-PR, shared disk topic), I saw you gave updates on Operators regarding 4.21 in the build channel, thanks for that.\\n@rspazzol you had a brief sync with Rushikesh on this, that and why we need it?\\nHe is not replying on the Build Team Channel, it is a bit annoying, at some point I would expect green light from him, or not.\\nIn context: There is ongoing demand mounting up to proceed with the Windows Failover Cluster VM shared disk issues.\\nI have been asked to write an Email to Vinay and Narender by today on what our proposed next step is, I guess Sudhir is getting tons of pressure...\\nI want to support him and if we tell them we update 104 to 4.21 soon to continue debug this, we have a positive spin here. (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
59acc781-10ed-42ab-8f90-d6fb11248e84	fee31afb-88af-4f38-8f37-16ba5a1871dd	7777708100.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[mexico meetings summary] the ITSO crowd in mexico was much more active and interested. Overall it looks like this country is fine with participating to this program.\nWith regards to the DMZ discussion, the issue is essentially solved and it comes down to verifying that there are enough ports in the existing switches. Mexico will fall in line with the global guidelines.\nLooking at capacity we discovered that the initial purchases for the new kits led by Maj did not take into account the capability fragmentation introduced by the DMZ architecture ( [customer|utility|non-prod\\extranet]x[edmx|idmz]x[TLDC|CLDL] (extranet does not have edmz). Recalling that the guidelines from global is that each cluster must be self-contained in zone, this yields (4x2-1)x2=14 clusters for a minimum of 42 nodes (only 16 have been purchased). We have this misalignment in all the regions. Maj is aware.Philip Jones  [11:45 AM]\nIssue for Monday: the SRE team have discovered that a tech preview setting has been applied to all clusters including prod. This relates to OCP virt and virtio video adapters. \n\nHopefully we can switch this off on the prod clusters and there won't be any issue with upgrades or support in the future.	{"ts": "7777708100.000000", "text": "[mexico meetings summary] the ITSO crowd in mexico was much more active and interested. Overall it looks like this country is fine with participating to this program.\\nWith regards to the DMZ discussion, the issue is essentially solved and it comes down to verifying that there are enough ports in the existing switches. Mexico will fall in line with the global guidelines.\\nLooking at capacity we discovered that the initial purchases for the new kits led by Maj did not take into account the capability fragmentation introduced by the DMZ architecture ( [customer|utility|non-prod\\\\extranet]x[edmx|idmz]x[TLDC|CLDL] (extranet does not have edmz). Recalling that the guidelines from global is that each cluster must be self-contained in zone, this yields (4x2-1)x2=14 clusters for a minimum of 42 nodes (only 16 have been purchased). We have this misalignment in all the regions. Maj is aware.Philip Jones  [11:45 AM]\\nIssue for Monday: the SRE team have discovered that a tech preview setting has been applied to all clusters including prod. This relates to OCP virt and virtio video adapters. \\n\\nHopefully we can switch this off on the prod clusters and there won't be any issue with upgrades or support in the future.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
3e678a05-6afd-4c53-9f09-a54e60cf119b	6961321a-47f1-4390-8506-e3158a4c7efd	7777708300.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	[Update reuired]\n\nTeam,\nWe need last update on the following item, who can help with this? @janine @Shebi @Rydekull @jfeind @atolani @Petros @pdelashe\n\nPS, I already asked TAM / ESS to get cases updates as well.\n\n1. VIB Version Mismatch (Compliance Blocker)\nMTV automatically upgrades the VIB from version 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 during migration. As a regulated financial institution, we are required to obtain security approval before releasing any new package into our environment. This auto-upgrade behaviour bypasses our internal compliance process and cannot be permitted without prior approval. We need MTV to support our existing VIB version (0.2.0) or provide a controlled upgrade path.\n\n2. Concurrent Migrations from the Same ESXi Host\nWhen multiple VMs residing on the same ESXi host are migrated concurrently, storage offloading fails consistently. We have no control over VM-to-host placement within our estate, making this condition unavoidable. The current workaround of retrying migrations repeatedly is operationally unsustainable at our scale.\n\n3. VMs with More Than 10 Disks\nVMs with more than 10 attached disks fail storage offloading consistently, and retries do not resolve the issue. Over 3,000 VMs in our estate fall into this category and are currently completely blocked from migration with no available workaround.\n\n4. QEMU issue\n\n5 . Not getting IP issue (edited)	{"ts": "7777708300.000000", "text": "[Update reuired]\\n\\nTeam,\\nWe need last update on the following item, who can help with this? @janine @Shebi @Rydekull @jfeind @atolani @Petros @pdelashe\\n\\nPS, I already asked TAM / ESS to get cases updates as well.\\n\\n1. VIB Version Mismatch (Compliance Blocker)\\nMTV automatically upgrades the VIB from version 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 during migration. As a regulated financial institution, we are required to obtain security approval before releasing any new package into our environment. This auto-upgrade behaviour bypasses our internal compliance process and cannot be permitted without prior approval. We need MTV to support our existing VIB version (0.2.0) or provide a controlled upgrade path.\\n\\n2. Concurrent Migrations from the Same ESXi Host\\nWhen multiple VMs residing on the same ESXi host are migrated concurrently, storage offloading fails consistently. We have no control over VM-to-host placement within our estate, making this condition unavoidable. The current workaround of retrying migrations repeatedly is operationally unsustainable at our scale.\\n\\n3. VMs with More Than 10 Disks\\nVMs with more than 10 attached disks fail storage offloading consistently, and retries do not resolve the issue. Over 3,000 VMs in our estate fall into this category and are currently completely blocked from migration with no available workaround.\\n\\n4. QEMU issue\\n\\n5 . Not getting IP issue (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
77a88e90-db27-4405-b9fc-e3bea11cdc28	fea5757a-f0c8-48c2-bf31-af84a8e9f29b	7777708400.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[VIB Issue]\nIn todays checkpoint they asked for the latest status of this issue. AFAIK looks like MTV2.11 needs VIB 0.3.0 and it is installing it "on the fly", failing in some ESXs (due to concurrency?). However, I've read somewhere that even with VIB 0.3.0 migrations are failing. Can you help me identifying who said it? So we can push that info in the support case because I think no one is looking into it. All I can find in the support case is that it fails for VMs with lots of disks. Are you aware of any other scenario? (edited)	{"ts": "7777708400.000000", "text": "[VIB Issue]\\nIn todays checkpoint they asked for the latest status of this issue. AFAIK looks like MTV2.11 needs VIB 0.3.0 and it is installing it \\"on the fly\\", failing in some ESXs (due to concurrency?). However, I've read somewhere that even with VIB 0.3.0 migrations are failing. Can you help me identifying who said it? So we can push that info in the support case because I think no one is looking into it. All I can find in the support case is that it fails for VMs with lots of disks. Are you aware of any other scenario? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
09680c29-54e6-49ec-a247-3ef4409eece0	5349d03e-e4a5-478a-8399-263e2a4d6d9b	7777708500.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[VMTools not being unintsalled issue]\n@jfeind If I recall correctly, you said that you had enambeld something in 104 (forklift something??) to make sure the tools were unisntalled and it was pending re-testing. Am I right?	{"ts": "7777708500.000000", "text": "[VMTools not being unintsalled issue]\\n@jfeind If I recall correctly, you said that you had enambeld something in 104 (forklift something??) to make sure the tools were unisntalled and it was pending re-testing. Am I right?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
ac40dc9a-ea2a-4543-aa6e-c09587cbde0e	41f46b77-280d-48f3-9c5a-bfdc1ea45693	7777708600.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	[VM Migration RDM to LUN issue]\nTalked to engineering about the issue of MigrationPlan spec.rdmAsLun=true not setting the LUN type interface to SCSI and did open a bug for it:\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5387\nThis should then finally allow us to discard the whole post-hook/ansible logic doing that atm.:jira: MTV-5387 [New] : MigrationPlan flag "rdmAsLun=true" does not change the interface typeAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerAlexander Rydekull  [11:23 AM]\nI am just flabbergasted... I think I can currently count 10 people involved in a request to add "api.crowdstrike.com" into an allowlist for a proxy	{"ts": "7777708600.000000", "text": "[VM Migration RDM to LUN issue]\\nTalked to engineering about the issue of MigrationPlan spec.rdmAsLun=true not setting the LUN type interface to SCSI and did open a bug for it:\\nhttps://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/MTV-5387\\nThis should then finally allow us to discard the whole post-hook/ansible logic doing that atm.:jira: MTV-5387 [New] : MigrationPlan flag \\"rdmAsLun=true\\" does not change the interface typeAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerAlexander Rydekull  [11:23 AM]\\nI am just flabbergasted... I think I can currently count 10 people involved in a request to add \\"api.crowdstrike.com\\" into an allowlist for a proxy", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
