f6dcf6fe-27e6-4365-bd41-0f0ea91ba812	fe75b1c7-b352-4d05-83e6-1299b45b576d	7777708800.000000	U_ALEXAN_D03599F6	[When / if re-IP of a VM occurs] Unicorn will need to be updated, since its central to so many other tools. I believe Unicorn will be updated without us needing to do anything. But just writing this so you remember that this needs to be done for any VM that changes IP (regardless if its US or HK or wherever).\n\nUnicorn is apparently the source of info for IPs for other tools, or in fact, ODS is, that pull from Unicorn.	{"ts": "7777708800.000000", "text": "[When / if re-IP of a VM occurs] Unicorn will need to be updated, since its central to so many other tools. I believe Unicorn will be updated without us needing to do anything. But just writing this so you remember that this needs to be done for any VM that changes IP (regardless if its US or HK or wherever).\\n\\nUnicorn is apparently the source of info for IPs for other tools, or in fact, ODS is, that pull from Unicorn.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}
f80be536-e31e-42f7-a61d-3702fe4a9c00	e46f4c2f-a349-4a99-a74c-1ae9daeb753d	7777708900.000000	U_SEBAST_AC383055	[Issues escalated to ESS - TAM]: We escalated today 4 issues impacting the migration:\n\nCase 04408443 and related RHEL-165220\nCase 04442406 and related MTV-5368\nCase 04432578 and related MTV-5349\nCase 04435341\nI created one ACE escalation to gather attention from engineering to get the issues solved before the next migration next week.\nOur escalations are currently missing project timelines. We must clearly document the project impact and exact timelines in these cases so Engineering can see the immediate dependencies and prioritize fixes accordingly. @pdelashe I am not sure about this, I think we have communicated timelines with ESS/TAM, but I am not sure.\nTo bypass support delays, the team is mandated to gather logs proactively for these failing scenarios. I asked them to request the logs directly in the support case, so the customer gets familiar with the process.\nA new dedicated Slack channel has been created for rapid communication and incident management for these specific EOS critical cases.\nKathinka created with my help this document to share with engineering about the support cases being escalated: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LACIffqYUWCgC4NtIVyDEcfEWvC0LIPbpu8tjp12fao/edit?tab=t.0\n:jira: RHEL-165220 [Integration] : virt-v2v with sun partition table and Veritas storage failed with: parted exited with status 1: Warning: The disk CHS geometry reported by the operating system does not match the geometry stored on the disk labelAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler:jira: MTV-5368 [New] : Copy-offload: VMs with many disks fail with "failed to get the VIB version" due to unthrottled concurrent esxcli callsAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [6:16 PM]\n[US Migration Workstream]:\nTimeline Alignment (Project ECB): Srinath is scheduling a sync with Nitesh and the US team to align our remaining development efforts (IP changes, DNS, LB, Firewall, Unicorn, etc) with the official ECB migration dates.\nMulti-NIC Re-IP Automation: We need Ansible support (@Petros / @atolani) to finalize the automation for VMs with multiple network interfaces. We are looking at using the QEMU guest agent or OS cmdlets to push the IP changes, but we need to validate this against our existing pipelines.	{"ts": "7777708900.000000", "text": "[Issues escalated to ESS - TAM]: We escalated today 4 issues impacting the migration:\\n\\nCase 04408443 and related RHEL-165220\\nCase 04442406 and related MTV-5368\\nCase 04432578 and related MTV-5349\\nCase 04435341\\nI created one ACE escalation to gather attention from engineering to get the issues solved before the next migration next week.\\nOur escalations are currently missing project timelines. We must clearly document the project impact and exact timelines in these cases so Engineering can see the immediate dependencies and prioritize fixes accordingly. @pdelashe I am not sure about this, I think we have communicated timelines with ESS/TAM, but I am not sure.\\nTo bypass support delays, the team is mandated to gather logs proactively for these failing scenarios. I asked them to request the logs directly in the support case, so the customer gets familiar with the process.\\nA new dedicated Slack channel has been created for rapid communication and incident management for these specific EOS critical cases.\\nKathinka created with my help this document to share with engineering about the support cases being escalated: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LACIffqYUWCgC4NtIVyDEcfEWvC0LIPbpu8tjp12fao/edit?tab=t.0\\n:jira: RHEL-165220 [Integration] : virt-v2v with sun partition table and Veritas storage failed with: parted exited with status 1: Warning: The disk CHS geometry reported by the operating system does not match the geometry stored on the disk labelAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurler:jira: MTV-5368 [New] : Copy-offload: VMs with many disks fail with \\"failed to get the VIB version\\" due to unthrottled concurrent esxcli callsAdded by assisted-installer-jira-unfurlerSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [6:16 PM]\\n[US Migration Workstream]:\\nTimeline Alignment (Project ECB): Srinath is scheduling a sync with Nitesh and the US team to align our remaining development efforts (IP changes, DNS, LB, Firewall, Unicorn, etc) with the official ECB migration dates.\\nMulti-NIC Re-IP Automation: We need Ansible support (@Petros / @atolani) to finalize the automation for VMs with multiple network interfaces. We are looking at using the QEMU guest agent or OS cmdlets to push the IP changes, but we need to validate this against our existing pipelines.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}
d4a8702b-0ca6-4708-9242-1c3aff849ec4	20a47681-fb21-4f43-96da-9841bcd0c546	7777709000.000000	U_SEBAST_AC383055	[HIC Design Followup] HIC Design Workshop Follow-up (Compute/Storage Design Sync)\n\nVijay led the meeting today. I jumped in to support Michele, and I plan to continue supporting this track until I receive formal notification otherwise.\n\nCluster Footprint & Node Sizing: We discussed downsizing the Control plane node on the 3rd site, and optimizing the overall cluster footprint. The goal is to reduce hardware expenses by finding the right balance of cluster sizes versus the number of control plane nodes. (against what Dennis said last time)\n\nDR & Stretched Patterns: Phil, Gareth, and Michele reviewed stretched patterns to ease DR requirements. A questionnaire has been sent out to all HIC ITSOs to gather feedback on their specific needs. AFAIK the only need is to provide active/standby functionality. I raised the question again today in the round.\n\nHA Patterns & RPO/RTO: We are aligning documentation around specific HA app patterns (Linux, Windows, SQL Always On, VCS Always On). The “Platform DR” patterns are already labeled, I have not seen such a documentation yet.\n\n A specific question was directed to me regarding Isovalent’s scalability and its limitations/impact on etcd when managing a large number of control planes (because of the cluster mesh solution). @janine I think you can take that one with you	{"ts": "7777709000.000000", "text": "[HIC Design Followup] HIC Design Workshop Follow-up (Compute/Storage Design Sync)\\n\\nVijay led the meeting today. I jumped in to support Michele, and I plan to continue supporting this track until I receive formal notification otherwise.\\n\\nCluster Footprint & Node Sizing: We discussed downsizing the Control plane node on the 3rd site, and optimizing the overall cluster footprint. The goal is to reduce hardware expenses by finding the right balance of cluster sizes versus the number of control plane nodes. (against what Dennis said last time)\\n\\nDR & Stretched Patterns: Phil, Gareth, and Michele reviewed stretched patterns to ease DR requirements. A questionnaire has been sent out to all HIC ITSOs to gather feedback on their specific needs. AFAIK the only need is to provide active/standby functionality. I raised the question again today in the round.\\n\\nHA Patterns & RPO/RTO: We are aligning documentation around specific HA app patterns (Linux, Windows, SQL Always On, VCS Always On). The “Platform DR” patterns are already labeled, I have not seen such a documentation yet.\\n\\n A specific question was directed to me regarding Isovalent’s scalability and its limitations/impact on etcd when managing a large number of control planes (because of the cluster mesh solution). @janine I think you can take that one with you", "type": "message", "user": "U_SEBAST_AC383055"}
25962c4a-e5d8-4269-a61a-afaf90df7463	a6f8d5a9-7d79-4cce-bef9-77be87db9161	7777709100.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Question for the Build Team]\nmust-gather is not working on some of the Prod Clusters, and we need those for the migration proactive cases. Can anyone check the case to see what is mieeing in the clusters and see if it can be fixed for future builds?: https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04445461	{"ts": "7777709100.000000", "text": "[Question for the Build Team]\\nmust-gather is not working on some of the Prod Clusters, and we need those for the migration proactive cases. Can anyone check the case to see what is mieeing in the clusters and see if it can be fixed for future builds?: https://access.redhat.com/support/cases/#/case/04445461", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
84cf756b-7f75-4e27-b6a2-b465b867713d	605d449d-f521-4bfe-b6aa-fcf97e29450b	7777709200.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[Question on parallell VM Migration limits]\nI've posted it also in VM Migration Teams Channel -> Is there a real limit on parallel VMMigration? In One Plan? In many Plans? Iḿ asking because there is a miscommunication between Eng, SRE and MigraitonPlanning Teams, and some of them are concerned that if we migrate 44VMs in parallel this afternoon, something will crashCarina Almeida  [11:35 AM]\n:exclamation-circle: [RH Delivery Team Updates]\n\nTeam,\n\nWe have new members joining us next week and in June, alongside some internal shuffling. You can find the full details of these transitions in the Team Changes - May/June 2026.\n\nWhat to expect:\n\nChannel Access: New members will be added to the relevant Slack channels by the end of this week.\nIntro Calls: Please keep an eye on your calendars; some of you will receive invites for introductory calls on Friday afternoon and Monday.\nPeering: Starting next week, we will be asking some team members to begin peering with our new joiners to help with their onboarding.\n\n\nPlease help us to welcome our new team members :relaxed: (edited)	{"ts": "7777709200.000000", "text": "[Question on parallell VM Migration limits]\\nI've posted it also in VM Migration Teams Channel -> Is there a real limit on parallel VMMigration? In One Plan? In many Plans? Iḿ asking because there is a miscommunication between Eng, SRE and MigraitonPlanning Teams, and some of them are concerned that if we migrate 44VMs in parallel this afternoon, something will crashCarina Almeida  [11:35 AM]\\n:exclamation-circle: [RH Delivery Team Updates]\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nWe have new members joining us next week and in June, alongside some internal shuffling. You can find the full details of these transitions in the Team Changes - May/June 2026.\\n\\nWhat to expect:\\n\\nChannel Access: New members will be added to the relevant Slack channels by the end of this week.\\nIntro Calls: Please keep an eye on your calendars; some of you will receive invites for introductory calls on Friday afternoon and Monday.\\nPeering: Starting next week, we will be asking some team members to begin peering with our new joiners to help with their onboarding.\\n\\n\\nPlease help us to welcome our new team members :relaxed: (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
560fa3cf-6745-4a7f-b1d9-545099cef249	3d5a8944-1ac8-4aee-b654-b2ab00cc4581	7777709300.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[dinner with hsbc] Vinay has reiterated how much he likes to work with redhat. He likes something about our transparency and openness that he does not get from the other vendors. Let's continue this way.\nThey also shared that likely n a few weeks the NDA will be lifted. As soon as we get to the point where communication of this project will be given to hundred of ITSO, there is no point in continuing with the NDA.\nThey also shared that once the NDA is lifted, there is an intention to open source MIO-X. The modalities still have to be defined, stay tuned....Carina Almeida  [1:31 PM]\n:guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\n\nTo help us get through this programme and customer's build/migration blockers, we’ve officially started a team Spotify playlist: https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\n\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote tomorrow after our internal stand-up :wink:\n\nIn the meantime, keep the beat on! :headphones:	{"ts": "7777709300.000000", "text": "[dinner with hsbc] Vinay has reiterated how much he likes to work with redhat. He likes something about our transparency and openness that he does not get from the other vendors. Let's continue this way.\\nThey also shared that likely n a few weeks the NDA will be lifted. As soon as we get to the point where communication of this project will be given to hundred of ITSO, there is no point in continuing with the NDA.\\nThey also shared that once the NDA is lifted, there is an intention to open source MIO-X. The modalities still have to be defined, stay tuned....Carina Almeida  [1:31 PM]\\n:guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\\n\\nTo help us get through this programme and customer's build/migration blockers, we’ve officially started a team Spotify playlist: https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\\n\\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote tomorrow after our internal stand-up :wink:\\n\\nIn the meantime, keep the beat on! :headphones:", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
79525fd3-8964-4798-abc3-4d56dc06cd64	736d4693-2694-4a86-9bab-5585c203354a	7777709400.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	[Maj / Carina sync]\n\nUS: The US session was very quiet as most participants joined remotely; only one person attended in person.\nThe deep dive session re. re-IP was highly successful, though significant work remains. I noted that we are looking into bringing a consultant to help with this.  Maj suggests hiring a consultant who can work UK hours to better align with the majority of the team.\n\nMexico: The Mexico team is ready to begin and even attended sessions on their day off.\nA list of required trainees has been compiled during the visit, including a request for Spanish speakers. Maj has identified 24 names, which match the ATL list. Maj will liaise with ATL and explain the request. Carina needs to double check with GLS about the Spanish speaker instructor.Jens Feind  [3:24 PM]\n[Bulk Migration]\nToday we had several runs with Bulk Migration holding approx 57 VMs per Migration Plan.\n12-16 VMs do migrate successfully while the others fail.\nIts an interesting topic, as the variation of error says:\n"No VSphereXcopyVolumePopulator CR found - populator may not have been created or was deleted"\nor\n"populator pod failed"\nThe latter error message in the populator pod log actually complains "failed to ensure VIB is installed"\nChecked with Devdatt that the ESXi hosts in question are all running on VIB 0.3.0\n\nThe second issue might be tackle with 2.11.6 release as it states in its notes:\nhttps://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/migration_toolkit_for_virtualization/2.11/html-single/release_notes/index#ref_resolved-issues-2-11-6_release-notes\n\nDevdatt is creating a support case now, I will highlight it to the TAM team.\ndocs.redhat.comRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRaffaele Spazzoli  [4:38 PM]\n@Philip Jones I need your help in understanding something. we were thinking on re-purposing 102 to hic deployment. probably 2 cluster each of 6 nodes. of course the biggest change is the deployment of cilium and teh configuration of BGP. Michael said this is not possible without bringing in new HW (specifically a netscaler router) to handle the VTEP. But my understanding is that the VTEP is only needed when stretching the networks, not strictly when enabling BGP. What is your point of view?	{"ts": "7777709400.000000", "text": "[Maj / Carina sync]\\n\\nUS: The US session was very quiet as most participants joined remotely; only one person attended in person.\\nThe deep dive session re. re-IP was highly successful, though significant work remains. I noted that we are looking into bringing a consultant to help with this.  Maj suggests hiring a consultant who can work UK hours to better align with the majority of the team.\\n\\nMexico: The Mexico team is ready to begin and even attended sessions on their day off.\\nA list of required trainees has been compiled during the visit, including a request for Spanish speakers. Maj has identified 24 names, which match the ATL list. Maj will liaise with ATL and explain the request. Carina needs to double check with GLS about the Spanish speaker instructor.Jens Feind  [3:24 PM]\\n[Bulk Migration]\\nToday we had several runs with Bulk Migration holding approx 57 VMs per Migration Plan.\\n12-16 VMs do migrate successfully while the others fail.\\nIts an interesting topic, as the variation of error says:\\n\\"No VSphereXcopyVolumePopulator CR found - populator may not have been created or was deleted\\"\\nor\\n\\"populator pod failed\\"\\nThe latter error message in the populator pod log actually complains \\"failed to ensure VIB is installed\\"\\nChecked with Devdatt that the ESXi hosts in question are all running on VIB 0.3.0\\n\\nThe second issue might be tackle with 2.11.6 release as it states in its notes:\\nhttps://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/migration_toolkit_for_virtualization/2.11/html-single/release_notes/index#ref_resolved-issues-2-11-6_release-notes\\n\\nDevdatt is creating a support case now, I will highlight it to the TAM team.\\ndocs.redhat.comRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRelease notes | Migration Toolkit for Virtualization | 2.11 | Red Hat DocumentationRaffaele Spazzoli  [4:38 PM]\\n@Philip Jones I need your help in understanding something. we were thinking on re-purposing 102 to hic deployment. probably 2 cluster each of 6 nodes. of course the biggest change is the deployment of cilium and teh configuration of BGP. Michael said this is not possible without bringing in new HW (specifically a netscaler router) to handle the VTEP. But my understanding is that the VTEP is only needed when stretching the networks, not strictly when enabling BGP. What is your point of view?", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
a48b543e-3f11-4c6d-9fef-c39600c93b04	bb1ccb20-beb0-4ac7-a3d6-216c201ce193	7777709500.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[HK hardware analysis] I have a request to confirm support for servers in HK, @Philip Jones @Rydekull can I delegate this request to you?	{"ts": "7777709500.000000", "text": "[HK hardware analysis] I have a request to confirm support for servers in HK, @Philip Jones @Rydekull can I delegate this request to you?", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
f769b04a-b1c1-4c61-a91a-ede854c8ece7	916a590b-ae74-4761-bba3-bd95c6e2cbd5	7777709600.000000	U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E	[wibdows sql server performance] @jfeind I believe you were seeing windows sqlserver performance degradation. Please take a loom at this doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BeJ-eOc4lqpkU-apddFAfekUSxAFKSuVkrC3XHLQPjw/edit?tab=t.0 if it applies, please sanitize jpmc name and share it with the customer.	{"ts": "7777709600.000000", "text": "[wibdows sql server performance] @jfeind I believe you were seeing windows sqlserver performance degradation. Please take a loom at this doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BeJ-eOc4lqpkU-apddFAfekUSxAFKSuVkrC3XHLQPjw/edit?tab=t.0 if it applies, please sanitize jpmc name and share it with the customer.", "type": "message", "user": "U_RAFFAE_9DC03E2E"}
421d3a43-a796-4cd2-a9f4-48de37d5e93d	b900b3de-0140-40eb-801d-1e645e893534	7777709700.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	[2 urgent things for today]\nIf they are not solved yet...\nMTV 2.11.6 Installed in Lab so customer can test the infamous "VIB Issue"\nProduction clusters being able to generate must-gathers. Starting today we are going to migrate VMs to different clusters, and we have to be able to upload must-gathers to the cases\n[1 not so urgent]\nI need to know who is responsible for adding Pre-Checks to MIoX, so they can add one related to XFS repair issue, that can prevent VMs in such a state to be migrated at all, reducing the number of failures\n[Reminder]\nRicardo and Arpit are supporting the war rooms today. I'll ping them if they are requiredRosemary Lynch  [10:20 AM]\n[Delivery Report] Will be sent at noon today covering last Thursday to close of business Wednesday. @Rydekull can you provide an update for Security please. @Shebi can you add the latest for the Design elements please? @Philip Jones, @James Force @atolani @jfeind @ricardo gregorio can you provide any relevant update from the build side please. @Petros & @pdelashe can you add the Migration updated please? All updates before 11am GMT if you can	{"ts": "7777709700.000000", "text": "[2 urgent things for today]\\nIf they are not solved yet...\\nMTV 2.11.6 Installed in Lab so customer can test the infamous \\"VIB Issue\\"\\nProduction clusters being able to generate must-gathers. Starting today we are going to migrate VMs to different clusters, and we have to be able to upload must-gathers to the cases\\n[1 not so urgent]\\nI need to know who is responsible for adding Pre-Checks to MIoX, so they can add one related to XFS repair issue, that can prevent VMs in such a state to be migrated at all, reducing the number of failures\\n[Reminder]\\nRicardo and Arpit are supporting the war rooms today. I'll ping them if they are requiredRosemary Lynch  [10:20 AM]\\n[Delivery Report] Will be sent at noon today covering last Thursday to close of business Wednesday. @Rydekull can you provide an update for Security please. @Shebi can you add the latest for the Design elements please? @Philip Jones, @James Force @atolani @jfeind @ricardo gregorio can you provide any relevant update from the build side please. @Petros & @pdelashe can you add the Migration updated please? All updates before 11am GMT if you can", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
