f3b620cb-32b6-4357-9f49-abdfa597a446	9bd4656e-0aa4-41cf-843d-5c8448ed4141	7777713900.000000	U_ALEXAN_D03599F6	@Philip Jones @James Force im curious, for one release of OCP how many images are actually synced in this environment?\nAlso, how many images have we synced in total with the different versions? (edited)	{"ts": "7777713900.000000", "text": "@Philip Jones @James Force im curious, for one release of OCP how many images are actually synced in this environment?\\nAlso, how many images have we synced in total with the different versions? (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ALEXAN_D03599F6"}
b46a3bf1-2eac-4c05-81ce-c530eb7b03e2	265cb088-8c86-4132-8be9-54b4cfa1d346	7777714000.000000	U_PHILIP_740C6823	Build Update\n\nDELL CSM Updated on 104\nNow includes OTEL metrics, credit to @ricardo gregorio \nMeeting to be scheduled by Dell for next week to discuss operator improvements.\n\nLatest EntraID issue identified and fix is pending a proxy change for cluster 301. \nPortworx operator upgrade prepared. We are just waiting on some required images to mirror now.	{"ts": "7777714000.000000", "text": "Build Update\\n\\nDELL CSM Updated on 104\\nNow includes OTEL metrics, credit to @ricardo gregorio \\nMeeting to be scheduled by Dell for next week to discuss operator improvements.\\n\\nLatest EntraID issue identified and fix is pending a proxy change for cluster 301. \\nPortworx operator upgrade prepared. We are just waiting on some required images to mirror now.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}
79b7e9e8-2d9d-4b82-9a53-66a26e07d8af	c68ccdb7-a0b0-49c0-825c-4146d83d4410	7777715200.000000	U_SAM_F28235E5	Had this ping from the PM team for auth proxy as they try and prioritize. My view is we need this feature for 4.22 unless someone else says otherwise. @rspazzol @Rydekull @Nikos @Nick Evans\nHi Sam!  I hope this message finds you well.\n\nI'm an engineering director in OpenShift and the requirement to provide https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7054 for HSBC is on our list for planning our next release.  I'm trying to gather more details on timeline so we can prioritize this appropriately.  I've been told the plan is to have HSBC on 4.22 (now dev complete for us) until moving to 5.2 next year.  Can you confirm that's the plan and/or do you see a need to have this auth proxy feature available prior to our 5.2 release?  If this would be better to discuss in a short meeting, feel free to grab a time on my calendar that works for you.  Thanks in advance!\nFrom a private conversation | Apr 23rdNick Evans  [9:32 AM]\n@Sam Marland if there is in fact a pathway to this being achieved then that would be great :+1::skin-tone-2:	{"ts": "7777715200.000000", "text": "Had this ping from the PM team for auth proxy as they try and prioritize. My view is we need this feature for 4.22 unless someone else says otherwise. @rspazzol @Rydekull @Nikos @Nick Evans\\nHi Sam!  I hope this message finds you well.\\n\\nI'm an engineering director in OpenShift and the requirement to provide https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RFE-7054 for HSBC is on our list for planning our next release.  I'm trying to gather more details on timeline so we can prioritize this appropriately.  I've been told the plan is to have HSBC on 4.22 (now dev complete for us) until moving to 5.2 next year.  Can you confirm that's the plan and/or do you see a need to have this auth proxy feature available prior to our 5.2 release?  If this would be better to discuss in a short meeting, feel free to grab a time on my calendar that works for you.  Thanks in advance!\\nFrom a private conversation | Apr 23rdNick Evans  [9:32 AM]\\n@Sam Marland if there is in fact a pathway to this being achieved then that would be great :+1::skin-tone-2:", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}
36fa4380-b718-49e7-8316-7cc0f9fb2a89	6d275b1e-32e4-4067-a712-c20bdf775566	7777714100.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	@Rydekull @Shebi\nSo regarding Sudhirs request on the failed migration of Windows Failover Cluster we made some progress over the day:\nProblem 1 solved: The migration itself is now successfull with all PVCs being available to both VMs. :check:\nMulti rooted issues, the migration plan execution order and configuration. Also the disks have been there once and then recreated as copy-[pvc-name..] which led to the VMs had different set of disks mounted.\nProblem 2 solved: The VMs do boot up now successfully after the Migration. :check:\nIssue was wrong NAD mappings and one NAD missing in the destination namespace.\n\nNew problem: The Windows Failover Cluster itself fails, I have some experience with Windows Server from 10+ years ago, nevertheless I wondered where do we draw the line in supporting applications after the migration.\nAnyway, when trying to bring the disks online it just says device i/o error, the Windows OS does see the disks but can not communicate... totally sounds like the good old SCSI3-PR issue has another place in the spotlight... ?Arpit Tolani  [6:34 PM]\nI was pulled into a call regarding Microsoft Entra ID authentication failing on one cluster. On that cluster, the customer had a production proxy configured, and authentication was not working.\nThe same Entra ID setup was configured on another cluster using a different proxy, where authentication was working as expected.\nDuring debugging, I found that the non-working cluster was unable to reach Microsoft Graph (graph.microsoft.com), which was being blocked by the proxy.\nAs a temporary workaround, I suggested allowing access to that endpoint. I also advised the customer to open a support case with Microsoft or obtain an official list of required URLs. Since dependencies may change (for example, due to outages or load balancing across different endpoints), relying on a single allowed domain may not be sufficient—it's better to follow Microsoft’s documented and supported endpoint list.Carina Almeida  [7:10 PM]\nAnd why are you working at this time @atolani? 'go home' and speak to you tomorrow :wink:	{"ts": "7777714100.000000", "text": "@Rydekull @Shebi\\nSo regarding Sudhirs request on the failed migration of Windows Failover Cluster we made some progress over the day:\\nProblem 1 solved: The migration itself is now successfull with all PVCs being available to both VMs. :check:\\nMulti rooted issues, the migration plan execution order and configuration. Also the disks have been there once and then recreated as copy-[pvc-name..] which led to the VMs had different set of disks mounted.\\nProblem 2 solved: The VMs do boot up now successfully after the Migration. :check:\\nIssue was wrong NAD mappings and one NAD missing in the destination namespace.\\n\\nNew problem: The Windows Failover Cluster itself fails, I have some experience with Windows Server from 10+ years ago, nevertheless I wondered where do we draw the line in supporting applications after the migration.\\nAnyway, when trying to bring the disks online it just says device i/o error, the Windows OS does see the disks but can not communicate... totally sounds like the good old SCSI3-PR issue has another place in the spotlight... ?Arpit Tolani  [6:34 PM]\\nI was pulled into a call regarding Microsoft Entra ID authentication failing on one cluster. On that cluster, the customer had a production proxy configured, and authentication was not working.\\nThe same Entra ID setup was configured on another cluster using a different proxy, where authentication was working as expected.\\nDuring debugging, I found that the non-working cluster was unable to reach Microsoft Graph (graph.microsoft.com), which was being blocked by the proxy.\\nAs a temporary workaround, I suggested allowing access to that endpoint. I also advised the customer to open a support case with Microsoft or obtain an official list of required URLs. Since dependencies may change (for example, due to outages or load balancing across different endpoints), relying on a single allowed domain may not be sufficient—it's better to follow Microsoft’s documented and supported endpoint list.Carina Almeida  [7:10 PM]\\nAnd why are you working at this time @atolani? 'go home' and speak to you tomorrow :wink:", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
