efd1fa1c-1269-45b8-946a-0f501870dfc2	6261ab7e-528c-4be3-aa6d-a655da1a7990	7777714500.000000	U_JENS_9E9831E8	@Rydekull I followed up on your idea which you mentioned to Ansell regarding installing qemu-guest-agent on Windows VMs as a pre-hook to reduce the number of reboots. Srinath sees it as a red flag currently installing anything on the VMs before the migration in case of a rollback. Nevertheless I think the idea is not bad, we agreed that I write a proposal to Abhishek to create a new testcase with a VM being migrated that has qemu-agent installed and a vanilla one to see what the time difference would make.	{"ts": "7777714500.000000", "text": "@Rydekull I followed up on your idea which you mentioned to Ansell regarding installing qemu-guest-agent on Windows VMs as a pre-hook to reduce the number of reboots. Srinath sees it as a red flag currently installing anything on the VMs before the migration in case of a rollback. Nevertheless I think the idea is not bad, we agreed that I write a proposal to Abhishek to create a new testcase with a VM being migrated that has qemu-agent installed and a vanilla one to see what the time difference would make.", "type": "message", "user": "U_JENS_9E9831E8"}
