29431735-646f-409a-99d2-ac44b62327eb	27c72c54-bbe3-4608-8464-f0f948036bb9	7777716800.000000	U_ARPIT_8F539902	{Migration}\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has "Windows Server" or not.. If it has, patch it\n\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\n --type merge\n -p '{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"domain":{"devices":{"video":{"type":"virtio"}}}}}}}'\n\nBut with automation i have few questions.\n\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...Rosalia Suarez Mejias  [10:53 AM]\nDelivery Report]\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)	{"ts": "7777716800.000000", "text": "{Migration}\\nI am working on an ansible script to patch all the windows VM after migration with their correct display driver.\\nIt should be straight forward, Check on VMI for that VM if .status.guestOSInfo.prettyName has \\"Windows Server\\" or not.. If it has, patch it\\n\\noc patch vm {{ vm_name }} -n {{ namespace }}\\n --type merge\\n -p '{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"domain\\":{\\"devices\\":{\\"video\\":{\\"type\\":\\"virtio\\"}}}}}}}'\\n\\nBut with automation i have few questions.\\n\\nHow are we connecting the OCP? Which module are we using?\\nThis entire workflow assumes that VM is running after migration & after patching we can reboot the VM\\nI dont have much details but is there a way in our migration plan we can fetch what all VM got migrated & which are Windows.. so we can do it just after  migration?\\nAlso where am I going to get the list of VM's which I have to look into...Rosalia Suarez Mejias  [10:53 AM]\\nDelivery Report]\\nThis is due to go out by tomorrow noon. Please start to update it so we can have it ready to sent on time. Can the following review & update by tomorrow 11am please?\\nPlatform slide still empty  @Rydekull, @rspazzol, @Shebi, @janine, @Philip Jones, @James Force ,@ricardo gregorio, @Petros ,@pdelashe appreciate it. https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AZG2KXxtiPZAKWUXIVvEu9h8F1UjaLIB/edit?slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13#slide=id.g38b58e86daa_0_13 (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_ARPIT_8F539902"}
