99680b85-58e3-4737-a5e9-1d4fb68b4423	930dbd62-8c70-4329-8f76-62784a9b6901	7777718600.000000	U_SAM_F28235E5	Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\n\n\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\n\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\n\n\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\n\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\n\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\n\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.	{"ts": "7777718600.000000", "text": "Looking at the information on today’s migrations it looks like we have 4 issues:\\n\\n\\nOne machine failed to restart due to VMWare tooling not being removed cleanly\\nXFS Filesystem issues caught by MTV\\nVIB version upgrade causing two issues:\\nv0.3.0 of the VIB not being certified by HSBC\\nThe upgrade from 0.2.0 to 0.3.0 causing pressure on the host which caused migrations to fail\\n\\nAn suspected LVM related failure.\\n\\n\\nThere was a separate MioX issue which appears unrelated to MTV or Red Hat tech.\\n\\nPlease can people validate that list as accurate.\\n\\nI’d also like to understand ASAP (so we can report to Stefanie -> Frank) what our proposed solution is to each of those points.\\n\\nI think @Nikos has asked @Roy Golan (rgolan) to give more information on the VIB issue.", "type": "message", "user": "U_SAM_F28235E5"}
dab93006-4e9e-428b-8959-6489811c767e	a164e8d0-b50b-46a8-8dbb-d32adcdf2b11	7777718700.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	Team, for info, the bank is currently tracking the following 'issues' assigened to RH - who's working on each one of this? (edited) \nimage.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [12:14 PM]\n[Migration completed]\n1 VM failed during migration\n3 VM failed in postchecks\ni'M JOINING THE ZOOM BRIDGE NOWJames Force  [12:53 PM]\n@Rydekull @janine do you know where the point around workloads running on control plane nodes (schedulable masters) ended up with Natti? The folks writing/reviewing the security polcies (VAPs and Compliance rules etc) are asking	{"ts": "7777718700.000000", "text": "Team, for info, the bank is currently tracking the following 'issues' assigened to RH - who's working on each one of this? (edited) \\nimage.png Patricia de las Heras Granaglia  [12:14 PM]\\n[Migration completed]\\n1 VM failed during migration\\n3 VM failed in postchecks\\ni'M JOINING THE ZOOM BRIDGE NOWJames Force  [12:53 PM]\\n@Rydekull @janine do you know where the point around workloads running on control plane nodes (schedulable masters) ended up with Natti? The folks writing/reviewing the security polcies (VAPs and Compliance rules etc) are asking", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
dae5bf04-1b14-46f6-9b8f-586c9ca0c7ea	2880ca72-9fde-4318-8da7-c733217615ba	7777718800.000000	U_PHILIP_740C6823	Isovalent Update:\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\n\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.\nScreenshot 2026-05-06 at 15.39.09.png James Force  [5:12 PM]\n@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?	{"ts": "7777718800.000000", "text": "Isovalent Update:\\nThe intent (for now) is to mimic the third site re-using the site 2 fabric (just to save on resources). As discussed yesterday, the plan is to have a full control plane / master node in site 3, rather than just an arbiter.\\n\\nPlans agreed to re-create a HIC NSX cluster as well. I suspect builds will be kicking off soon.\\nScreenshot 2026-05-06 at 15.39.09.png James Force  [5:12 PM]\\n@rspazzol - question for you on the gitops operator... so right now this is operator is installed not via an operatorpolicy (for good reasons to help bootstrap the cluster config)... however, I'm concerned about the management of this operator from there on out... every other operator has a succinct version managed by the operator policy.. makes it very clear to control versions, whereas with the gitops operator it just installs latest at the time and then auto updates (if there are no blockers in the openshift-operators namespace that is)... I was thinking to introduce an operatorpolicy resource for this later on that would pickup and manage the operator after the initial bootstra.. but the issues with that would be matching the versions... so we'd have to introduce a specific CSV in the sub and turn off auto upgrades, and also have that in the operator policy so they would marry up... do you have any other ideas/approaches here?", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}
ded26d61-b09d-4f5a-bd03-7f709a667979	389b1ae0-cbac-4c55-b63d-fcc4fdffb094	7777721500.000000	U_JANINE_71F80BBD	@rspazzol the "private network bit" Vijay mentioned is the question Michael asked: "can a CUDN be stretched across clusters?"	{"ts": "7777721500.000000", "text": "@rspazzol the \\"private network bit\\" Vijay mentioned is the question Michael asked: \\"can a CUDN be stretched across clusters?\\"", "type": "message", "user": "U_JANINE_71F80BBD"}
