1b0bd01a-c989-47b1-b5e4-e703b5a3d7e7	b20ffba8-e154-4a86-aac6-088b43564409	7777720800.000000	U_PHILIP_740C6823	Good news!!\n\nI asked Alex from the OC mirror dev team, the following:\nAt the moment our customer has issues with either their Nexus or Proxy server that limits us to running oc-mirror with --parallel-images=1 and --paralllel-layers=1. Needless to say, it's painful! We had sync running over 30 hrs earlier this week and the current run is now over 24hrs.\nWe need a way in which we can sync specific operators or elements faster. Right now, were we to try and sync a small image-set-config, we'd end up with a tiny catalog. Is there no way to have it merge a catalog update with an existing catalog, rather than re-publish a new one?\nI.e. we really need to get hold of MTV 2.11.6 without waiting a LONG time for a full sync.\n\nHe's responded that it's coming in oc-mirror 4.22 :slightly_smiling_face: So we should have a means to cherry pick (when needed) and merge with an existing catalog, rather than replace it. In essence, we can run a minimal sync when needed, to grab a specific update, rather than needing to always mirror the full image-set-config.	{"ts": "7777720800.000000", "text": "Good news!!\\n\\nI asked Alex from the OC mirror dev team, the following:\\nAt the moment our customer has issues with either their Nexus or Proxy server that limits us to running oc-mirror with --parallel-images=1 and --paralllel-layers=1. Needless to say, it's painful! We had sync running over 30 hrs earlier this week and the current run is now over 24hrs.\\nWe need a way in which we can sync specific operators or elements faster. Right now, were we to try and sync a small image-set-config, we'd end up with a tiny catalog. Is there no way to have it merge a catalog update with an existing catalog, rather than re-publish a new one?\\nI.e. we really need to get hold of MTV 2.11.6 without waiting a LONG time for a full sync.\\n\\nHe's responded that it's coming in oc-mirror 4.22 :slightly_smiling_face: So we should have a means to cherry pick (when needed) and merge with an existing catalog, rather than replace it. In essence, we can run a minimal sync when needed, to grab a specific update, rather than needing to always mirror the full image-set-config.", "type": "message", "user": "U_PHILIP_740C6823"}
