c3762472-dd8d-40d4-991a-c335726ff5c6	e29e9493-a62c-4105-8697-33ecb6b15843	7777722200.000000	U_GOOGLE_35CC3553	Reminder :slightly_smiling_face: https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C099TDJDDKL/p1779108201943439\n@channel Let's try it again... :guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\n\nTo help us get through this programme andn.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\n\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote on Wednesday after our internal stand-up :wink:\n\nThread in proj-eos-mvp | May 18th | View messageJames Force  [11:49 AM]\n@Shebi can you post that KCS you were showing earlier? It seems MutatingAdmissionPolicy(probably the most easiest and elegant solution here) isn't GA yet :disappointed: seems in still under TechPreviewNoUpgrade  see https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.21/html/postinstallation_configuration/post-install-cluster-tasks#nod[…]asks\ndocs.redhat.comChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\nhttps://access.redhat.com/solutions/7135435\nRed Hat Customer PortalMTV Migrations fails as virt-v2v appliance runs out of memory - Red Hat Customer PortalConversion of Virtual Machine to OpenShift Virtualization fails with out of memory error. oom-killer is invoked during migration of Virtual Machine to OpenShift VirtualizationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\nThere you go	{"ts": "7777722200.000000", "text": "Reminder :slightly_smiling_face: https://redhat-internal.slack.com/archives/C099TDJDDKL/p1779108201943439\\n@channel Let's try it again... :guitar:it's time for some fun! :guitar:\\n\\nTo help us get through this programme andn.spotify.com/playlist/5NxWiu4QgC0AavJqp6tMev?si=54cee70fd0d446f5\\n\\nThe catch? It’s currently untitled. We need a name that captures the chaos of the programme and brilliance of this team! Drop your funniest/best name ideas in this thread, and we’ll put them to a vote on Wednesday after our internal stand-up :wink:\\n\\nThread in proj-eos-mvp | May 18th | View messageJames Force  [11:49 AM]\\n@Shebi can you post that KCS you were showing earlier? It seems MutatingAdmissionPolicy(probably the most easiest and elegant solution here) isn't GA yet :disappointed: seems in still under TechPreviewNoUpgrade  see https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.21/html/postinstallation_configuration/post-install-cluster-tasks#nod[…]asks\\ndocs.redhat.comChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationChapter 4. Postinstallation cluster tasks | Postinstallation configuration | OpenShift Container Platform | 4.21 | Red Hat DocumentationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\\nhttps://access.redhat.com/solutions/7135435\\nRed Hat Customer PortalMTV Migrations fails as virt-v2v appliance runs out of memory - Red Hat Customer PortalConversion of Virtual Machine to OpenShift Virtualization fails with out of memory error. oom-killer is invoked during migration of Virtual Machine to OpenShift VirtualizationSebastian Rodriguez Isaziga  [11:50 AM]\\nThere you go", "type": "message", "user": "U_GOOGLE_35CC3553"}
6116ea3d-50e7-4ec4-aff7-b4b081a26949	a65fdd5e-ddc7-4678-b0bc-a34364b99435	7777722300.000000	U_PETROS_2EB3D870	The pre-check for a vm in the Automation Migration Pipeline.\nYou can also find it in the EOS Drawings in Miro. https://miro.com/app/board/uXjVGOH7PkE=/\n\nI am trying to clarify what is the purpose of the Mule ESB call and the call to another AAP Job which switches the inventory from localhost to the VM and does the OS checks using a shell script. This workflow seems to be time consuming. The shell script does simple checks which should not take more than 10 seconds.\n\nI want to believe my research on this is wrong but I highly doubt this :slightly_smiling_face:\nimage.png Carina Almeida  [3:30 PM]\n[gantt review]\n\n\nAll UK Phase 1 non-HIC hardware now handover to ENG to build OCPV platform.\nNo date / estimation for DMZ yet\nRelated to DMZ conversation - Chris noted that ENG asked for more people during bank's 1pm call \nHK seems to have delay to prep hardware and handover to ENG, some of them waiting on response / planning for smart orders\nTOM to be operational from November, i.e. expect HSBC team restructure happening then	{"ts": "7777722300.000000", "text": "The pre-check for a vm in the Automation Migration Pipeline.\\nYou can also find it in the EOS Drawings in Miro. https://miro.com/app/board/uXjVGOH7PkE=/\\n\\nI am trying to clarify what is the purpose of the Mule ESB call and the call to another AAP Job which switches the inventory from localhost to the VM and does the OS checks using a shell script. This workflow seems to be time consuming. The shell script does simple checks which should not take more than 10 seconds.\\n\\nI want to believe my research on this is wrong but I highly doubt this :slightly_smiling_face:\\nimage.png Carina Almeida  [3:30 PM]\\n[gantt review]\\n\\n\\nAll UK Phase 1 non-HIC hardware now handover to ENG to build OCPV platform.\\nNo date / estimation for DMZ yet\\nRelated to DMZ conversation - Chris noted that ENG asked for more people during bank's 1pm call \\nHK seems to have delay to prep hardware and handover to ENG, some of them waiting on response / planning for smart orders\\nTOM to be operational from November, i.e. expect HSBC team restructure happening then", "type": "message", "user": "U_PETROS_2EB3D870"}
f4311c5d-f0bc-450d-8a46-f90479b2978d	3957e4cd-66dc-4568-890a-79ccaf862027	7777722400.000000	U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB	replied to a thread:Apparently today they are migrating from Dell Storage and those VMs are also failing. But I need to confirm	{"ts": "7777722400.000000", "text": "replied to a thread:Apparently today they are migrating from Dell Storage and those VMs are also failing. But I need to confirm", "type": "message", "user": "U_PATRIC_80EFC8EB"}
