2eb93d38-c640-4860-a65a-44fcb0f2ab10	649c4906-e7c5-4c6e-be49-5e8619da788e	7777722700.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	:heart: A massive THANK YOU to this incredible team :heart:\n\nTeam,\n\nToday was one of those high-pressure days where escalations and queries were coming from all sides. But watching how this team responded made me incredibly proud and reminded me exactly why I love working at Red Hat.\n\nEvery single person; across Delivery, the Account Team, Engineering, TAM and Support; stayed focused, maintained professionalism, and handling the pressure.\n\nMore than just delivering technically, what amazed me most was how we supported each other. We didn't just collaborate professionally; we looked out for each other through a tough day. It is incredibly reassuring to know we have each other's backs like this.\n\nToday showed the absolute best of Red Hat. I feel incredibly lucky to work alongside such an amazing, dedicated group of people, and it’s teams like this that make us want to grow together.\n\nThank you all for your hard work, your resilience, and for being such a stellar team. Let's keep this amazing energy going! :pray:	{"ts": "7777722700.000000", "text": ":heart: A massive THANK YOU to this incredible team :heart:\\n\\nTeam,\\n\\nToday was one of those high-pressure days where escalations and queries were coming from all sides. But watching how this team responded made me incredibly proud and reminded me exactly why I love working at Red Hat.\\n\\nEvery single person; across Delivery, the Account Team, Engineering, TAM and Support; stayed focused, maintained professionalism, and handling the pressure.\\n\\nMore than just delivering technically, what amazed me most was how we supported each other. We didn't just collaborate professionally; we looked out for each other through a tough day. It is incredibly reassuring to know we have each other's backs like this.\\n\\nToday showed the absolute best of Red Hat. I feel incredibly lucky to work alongside such an amazing, dedicated group of people, and it’s teams like this that make us want to grow together.\\n\\nThank you all for your hard work, your resilience, and for being such a stellar team. Let's keep this amazing energy going! :pray:", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
f5bf760b-3e2d-4b39-92de-92a8d91a76b3	26a7e58a-6ad3-4210-a7a8-f277e22802d6	7777722800.000000	U_CARINA_D5667D0C	Mexico Pilot - estimated for 22nd June and Bucket 1 due to start on 29th June (edited)	{"ts": "7777722800.000000", "text": "Mexico Pilot - estimated for 22nd June and Bucket 1 due to start on 29th June (edited)", "type": "message", "user": "U_CARINA_D5667D0C"}
212fe612-0e57-48ba-a897-291d7151fce1	fcf5f04a-b5b1-451c-9b2d-be8aa6b4e9a1	7777723200.000000	U_ANNE_7F9C7274	:green_alert:\n\nNDA partly lifted internally in HSBC. Those on the NDA are now allowed to talk "carefully" about an Infrastructure Modernisation programme with those not on the NDA previously. The "why" they are doing the programme is still confidential for obvious reasons! External comms DO NOT change at present so from a RH perspective I suggest we stay as is	{"ts": "7777723200.000000", "text": ":green_alert:\\n\\nNDA partly lifted internally in HSBC. Those on the NDA are now allowed to talk \\"carefully\\" about an Infrastructure Modernisation programme with those not on the NDA previously. The \\"why\\" they are doing the programme is still confidential for obvious reasons! External comms DO NOT change at present so from a RH perspective I suggest we stay as is", "type": "message", "user": "U_ANNE_7F9C7274"}
375b4dbe-6048-4971-9bae-c9f20d4d5d35	a210ea9e-9386-40d4-89be-a3b2974b481c	7777723300.000000	U_ANNE_7F9C7274	:helpme:\n\nAppliances - who can join this chat with the customer and me - it came as an action out of Stefanie and Franks interlock this week.  "The ask would be to support us in understand options whereby our vendor provided appliances are not certified for use with OpenShift". Nikos is on holiday next week and i dont want a week of no movement\nimage001.png Raffaele Spazzoli  [1:37 PM]\nI can help.	{"ts": "7777723300.000000", "text": ":helpme:\\n\\nAppliances - who can join this chat with the customer and me - it came as an action out of Stefanie and Franks interlock this week.  \\"The ask would be to support us in understand options whereby our vendor provided appliances are not certified for use with OpenShift\\". Nikos is on holiday next week and i dont want a week of no movement\\nimage001.png Raffaele Spazzoli  [1:37 PM]\\nI can help.", "type": "message", "user": "U_ANNE_7F9C7274"}
bdc32dbe-1917-44d5-a44e-77628d1d0f63	8ffb9ba8-b83c-4aab-b56d-eac8224fe512	9999900001.000000	U_TEST1	We need to refactor the authentication module to support OIDC. The current JWT validation is too tightly coupled to our custom provider and will not work with Keycloak.	{"ts": "9999900001.000000", "text": "We need to refactor the authentication module to support OIDC. The current JWT validation is too tightly coupled to our custom provider and will not work with Keycloak.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST1"}
78716ebe-c508-405c-853b-2afce36c5937	8ffb9ba8-b83c-4aab-b56d-eac8224fe512	9999900002.000000	U_TEST2	Agreed. I looked into the Keycloak adapter and we can use passport-openidconnect. The main risk is session handling — we should keep stateless JWT but add token refresh support.	{"ts": "9999900002.000000", "text": "Agreed. I looked into the Keycloak adapter and we can use passport-openidconnect. The main risk is session handling — we should keep stateless JWT but add token refresh support.", "type": "message", "user": "U_TEST2", "thread_ts": "9999900001.000000"}
